window.FWN_DIMENSIONAL_KEEPER_ALL_MY_SKILLS_ARE_AT_LEVEL_100_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_DIMENSIONAL_KEEPER_ALL_MY_SKILLS_ARE_AT_LEVEL_100_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1801,"title":"Chapter 1801: Last Trial - 2","paragraphs":["A Max made of white-gold Genesis light stood in front of Max. A Revona formed before Revona. A Tamara stood before Tamara. A demonic Varkhon rose before Varkhon, and an abyssal Ervin appeared before Ervin. Their auras were not perfect copies, but they carried enough resemblance to make the meaning of the trial obvious.","[Genesis Reflections Awakened.]","[Defeat Your Reflection To Continue.]","[Warning: Reflections Will Adapt To Your Current Combat Style.]","Varkhon laughed loudly. \"Good. I like hitting myself.\"","His reflection rushed at him at the same time, and the two demonic figures collided with enough force to make the surrounding platform tremble. Varkhon’s raw strength erupted instantly, and he began trading heavy blows with his reflection, both of them smashing fists against fists until shockwaves rolled outward.","Tamara’s reflection raised a spear.","Tamara smiled coldly. \"A copy is still a soldier. I am the commander.\"","She stepped forward, war intent blazing, and her spear met the reflection’s spear in a direct clash.","Revona’s reflection opened its pale version of the Void Origin Eyes, and the space between the two women began to fade and reform continuously. Neither attacked recklessly. Their battle began in silence, with both trying to erase the other’s power before the first true strike landed.","Ervin looked at his abyssal reflection for a moment.","The reflection raised its spear.","Ervin raised his own.","Then both vanished.","The next instant, dozens of spear lights appeared across the platform, each one colliding with another in perfect silence. Their battle was the hardest to follow because both moved with terrifying precision and almost no wasted energy.","Max faced his own Genesis Reflection calmly.","The reflection held a white-gold version of Dragonheart, and faint seven-colored lightning moved around its body. It did not have Max’s true bloodline, true sword, or true foundation, but it had copied enough of his outward power from the previous trials to become dangerous. The reflection lifted its sword, and a pale version of Divine King Punishment flickered behind it.","Max looked at it and smiled faintly.","\"So you copied that.\"","The Genesis Reflection attacked.","Seven-colored lightning, paler and less destructive than Max’s true power, surged forward like a punishment storm. Max did not use Divine King Punishment in response. He stepped through the lightning with his Dimensional Sovereign Body reading every gap between the arcs, then swung Dragonheart once.","The first clash rang out.","The reflection blocked.","Its sword was strong, and its copied reaction speed was not weak, but Max immediately sensed the difference. The reflection could copy techniques, aura patterns, and battle rhythm, but it could not copy the true source of his power.","It did not have the real Storm King’s Inheritance essence. It did not have the real destructive and punishment nature of the seven-colored lightning. It did not have his Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline. It did not have his experiences, his rage, his will, or his path.","The reflection slashed again.","Max avoided it by half a step and struck its wrist.","The white-gold sword trembled.","The reflection immediately adapted, shifting from lightning to sword combat. A faint severing aura appeared around its blade, trying to imitate the Emotion Severing Path.","Max’s expression turned colder.","\"You should not copy that.\"","The Emotion Severing Path awakened around Max.","Silence descended.","The reflection’s imitation sword aura froze for a moment, as if the copied path itself had been severed from its foundation. Max stepped forward and slashed. Dragonheart passed through the reflection’s chest, and the white-gold figure split apart without even releasing a final attack.","The reflection dissolved into Genesis light.","Max looked toward the others.","Varkhon was still fighting brutally, but he was overpowering his reflection through sheer demonic strength. Tamara had already gained the advantage over her copy by using superior command of war intent.","Revona’s reflection was troublesome, but the real Revona’s Void Origin Eyes were far deeper, and the copied version gradually began fading under her gaze. Ervin’s battle ended almost at the same time as Max’s, with his black spear piercing the reflection’s throat after a sequence of exchanges too subtle for most people to understand.","One by one, the reflections fell.","[All Genesis Reflections Defeated.]","[Team Progress Preserved.]","[Ascent Continues.]","The pressure above them increased.","The Genesis Sovereign Platform shifted, and the next layers rose higher, steeper, and brighter. The throne at the top became slightly clearer, but it was still far away.","Max looked upward.","After the Genesis Reflections dissolved, the white-gold light they left behind did not disappear immediately.","Instead, it gathered beneath the feet of the five participants and formed five thin marks that sank into the platform. The Genesis Sovereign Platform responded with a deep hum, and the layer beneath them slowly rose like a massive cube elevator, carrying them higher into the starless sky.","The pressure surrounding them became heavier with each passing breath, and even though none of them had suffered serious injuries against their reflections, everyone understood that the final trial was only beginning to reveal its true nature.","A system prompt appeared before them.","[First Stage Cleared.]","[Reflection Assessment Completed.]","[Genesis Marks Temporarily Recorded.]","[Notice: Temporary Marks Will Be Finalized After The End Of Trial Three.]","[Ascent Continues.]","Varkhon rolled his shoulders, his demonic markings still burning faintly as he looked at the path above with a savage grin. \"Temporary marks? This trial is stingy.\"","Tamara glanced at him. \"It is testing whether we can keep climbing. If we fall before the end, the marks probably disappear.\"","Revona looked at the white-gold patterns under her feet with her Void Origin Eyes, and after a moment, she nodded. \"The trial is recording our performance, but it has not decided the final distribution yet. The Genesis Throne may change everything.\"","Ervin’s spear rested lightly in his hand, and his abyss-like eyes remained on the distant throne. \"Then the higher stages matter more than the lower ones.\"","Max did not speak. His Dimensional Sovereign Body was still active, quietly testing the pressure that descended from above. The suppression was becoming more complex. At first, it had only pressed down on flesh, energy, and will, but now it had begun to touch his paths, his bloodline, and even his memories.","It was subtle, not strong enough to cause any harm, but it was like invisible fingers searching through the foundation of his existence, trying to understand what kind of person was climbing toward the Genesis Throne.","That feeling made Max’s eyes turn slightly colder."]},{"number":1802,"title":"Chapter 1802: Last Trial - 3","paragraphs":["The platform rose again.","A new stretch of steps appeared ahead.","Unlike the lower layers, these steps were narrow and stretched across a vast open void. Each step floated separately, with gaps between them large enough to swallow an ordinary cultivator. White-gold mist moved between the gaps, and inside the mist, vague figures could be seen drifting silently.","They did not look like guardians at first. They looked like memories, shadows, or souls that had never fully formed.","Then the system prompt appeared.","[Second Stage: Genesis Will Corridor.]","[Objective: Cross The Corridor Without Losing Your Will.]","[Warning: The Corridor Will Manifest Regrets, Fears, Desires, And Attachments.]","[Warning: Participants May Assist One Another, But Cannot Bear Another Participant’s Trial Completely.]","[Warning: Individual Willpower Assessment Has Begun.]","The moment the prompt faded, the white-gold mist surged upward.","The world around them changed.","Max took the first step into the corridor, and the scenery before him blurred slightly. For a moment, the cubic platform, Revona, Tamara, Varkhon, and Ervin all faded from his senses. He still knew they were there, but the trial had placed a thin layer between each participant, separating their inner experiences while keeping their bodies on the same path.","Then Max heard a voice.","It was faint at first.","Then it became clearer.","\"Why did you survive?\"","Max’s footsteps paused for half a breath.","The mist before him formed a scene.","He saw a broken space, a fleeing child, golden light being torn out of a body, bloodline extraction chains, and a woman’s desperate scream that seemed to echo from a past he had not fully remembered with his own eyes.","The trial showed him fragments of the night his family had been destroyed. He saw his mother being restrained. He saw his father bleeding. He saw the forbidden formation extracting the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline from his young body. He saw a shadow carrying someone away through a collapsing spatial crack. He saw second faction elves standing above everything like judges.","The mist whispered again.","\"You survived while others suffered.\"","Max’s eyes became cold.","The pressure on his will deepened.","The scene tried to drag him into guilt, anger, confusion, and helplessness. It tried to make him ask why he had been spared, why his parents had remained imprisoned, why his sister had disappeared, why Caroline and the remnants of the third faction had suffered for so many years while he climbed step by step without knowing the truth.","It was not an illusion meant to trick his eyes. It was a manifestation aimed at the cracks in his heart.","Max stepped forward.","\"I survived,\" he said calmly, \"so I can settle the debt.\"","The mist trembled.","The voices grew louder.","\"Can you save them? Can you break the Celestial Thorn Abyss? Can you take back what was stolen? Can you face the Divine Son who carries your bloodline?\"","Max’s expression did not change.","Golden-black dragon scales faintly appeared beneath his skin, not because he needed their defense, but because his bloodline itself was reacting to the provocation. The little cursed eye on his shoulder blinked slowly, as if watching the memories with eerie interest.","The Emotion Severing Path stirred faintly in Max’s heart, but he did not fully release it. He did not want to sever this emotion. He wanted to remember this hatred.","He wanted to use it.","\"I do not need the trial to remind me,\" Max said softly. \"I already know who I have to kill.\"","With that, he took another step.","The memory before him split apart.","The mist retreated.","Max continued forward.","On another part of the corridor, Varkhon’s body trembled as the mist around him formed mountains of demon corpses and a throne made of broken horns. His expression twisted, but not from fear. It was from rage.","A giant demonic shadow stood before him, looking down with contempt, and the voice from the mist said something only he could hear. Varkhon roared, and his fist smashed forward, breaking the shadow apart with raw will as much as raw strength.","\"I do not kneel to dead demons,\" Varkhon snarled.","Farther away, Tamara walked through a battlefield of endless corpses.","Banners burned around her. Soldiers called her name. Some begged her to save them. Others accused her of leading them to death. The War God Palace had shaped her into a war lord, but war lords carried the weight of those who followed them.","Tamara’s grip tightened around her spear, and for a moment, her steps became slower. Then her war intent rose, not wild and violent, but firm like a commander refusing to collapse before the cries of the battlefield.","\"A commander remembers the dead,\" Tamara said, her voice heavy but steady. \"She does not die with them.\"","Her spear struck the ground.","The battlefield mist parted.","Revona’s trial was quieter.","She stood before a mirror of endless void.","Inside that mirror were countless eyes, each one identical to her Void Origin Eyes, watching her from every direction. The mist whispered that everything she erased would one day erase her in return.","It showed her a future where her eyes consumed her emotions, her connections, and even her own existence, leaving behind only a pair of void eyes floating in nothingness. Revona looked at the mirror in silence for a long time.","Then her Void Origin Eyes glowed softly.","The mirror began to vanish.","\"I decide what disappears,\" she said calmly. \"Not the void.\"","The mirror was erased.","Ervin’s mist was the strangest.","No one could see clearly what he faced.","Even Max, whose Dimensional Sovereign Body could vaguely sense the others through the trial’s separation, found Ervin’s side unusually difficult to read. The mist around him did not show a battlefield, family, sect, demon throne, or void mirror.","It showed darkness. Endless darkness. A deep abyss without sound, light, or direction. Ervin stood in front of it with his black spear in hand, and for the first time, his calm smile disappeared.","A faint voice came from the abyss.","\"Come back.\"","Ervin’s eyes remained still.","The abyss deepened.","\"Come back to where you belong.\"","His hand tightened around his spear.","For a few breaths, Ervin did not move. Then he slowly raised his spear and pointed it toward the darkness.","\"I have not reached the bottom yet. I have not fulfilled my goal\" he said softly. \"How can I come back?\"","The spear pierced forward.","A thin black-silver line cut through the abyss.","The darkness did not disappear completely, but a path opened through it, and Ervin walked forward without looking back."]},{"number":1803,"title":"Chapter 1803: Last Trial - 4","paragraphs":["The five continued through the Genesis Will Corridor.","The pressure increased again.","The mist tried different attacks as they climbed. It showed temptation. It showed fear. It showed victory. It showed loved ones. It showed enemies. It showed futures where they became kings, futures where they died forgotten, futures where they betrayed one another for Genesis Marks, and futures where one of them stood before the Genesis Throne while the others fell into the void.","But none of the five stopped for long. They were all monsters in their own way, and if their wills could be broken so easily, they would never have entered the Genesis Trial in the first place.","Still, the trial was not meaningless.","By the time they reached the end of the corridor, each person’s aura had changed slightly.","Tamara’s war intent became more compact.","Varkhon’s demonic pressure became more brutal.","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes became calmer and deeper.","Ervin’s abyss-like aura became quieter, but also more unnerving.","Max’s gaze became colder, and the promise inside his heart became firmer.","A system prompt appeared.","[Second Stage Cleared.]","[Willpower Assessment Completed.]","[All Participants Passed.]","[Individual Performance Recorded.]","The white-gold mist disappeared.","The five participants emerged onto a broad platform halfway up the Genesis Sovereign Platform. The Genesis Throne above them was much clearer now, but the pressure descending from it had become almost suffocating.","At this height, even standing still required strength. The white-gold patterns on the platform shone brighter, and countless cubic stars began gathering in the sky above them.","Then the platform split.","Five separate paths appeared ahead, each one leading toward the same upper layer but through different trials. At the junction where the paths began, a large system prompt appeared.","[Third Stage: Path Manifestation Ascent.]","[Objective: Manifest Your Path And Break Through The Trial Suppression.]","[Rules: Each Participant Must Take One Path.]","[Rules: Participants May Not Enter Another Participant’s Path Until The Final Convergence.]","[Warning: Path Strength, Path Stability, And Path Potential Will Be Assessed.]","[Warning: Weak Or Unstable Paths May Collapse Under Genesis Pressure.]","Varkhon grinned. \"Now we separate.\"","Tamara lifted her spear. \"Looks like it.\"","Revona glanced toward Max. \"This may decide who can stand before the throne.\"","Ervin looked at the five paths, then smiled faintly. \"Then we should all choose carefully.\"","Max examined the paths with his Dimensional Sovereign Body.","Each path felt different. One was heavy with battlefield pressure. One was filled with void fluctuations. One burned with demonic destruction. One sank into abyssal darkness. One was strange and unstable, shifting between sword, lightning, bloodline, space, and something deeper that seemed to respond to Max alone.","Max stepped toward that path.","The white-gold cubes beneath it trembled faintly as if recognizing him.","Tamara walked toward the path filled with battlefield pressure.","Varkhon chose the path burning with demonic destruction.","Revona moved toward the void path.","Ervin chose the abyssal path without hesitation.","Before stepping in, Tamara glanced at the others and said, \"The final stage only allows one before the throne. If we meet again there, do not expect mercy.\"","Varkhon laughed. \"I would be disappointed if you showed mercy.\"","Revona said calmly, \"Survive first.\"","Ervin looked at Max and smiled faintly. \"See you above.\"","Max nodded.","Then the five stepped onto their paths.","The moment Max entered his path, the world behind him vanished.","The platform around him stretched forward into a long white-gold road suspended in darkness. On both sides of the road, countless cubic mirrors appeared, each one reflecting a different version of him.","One mirror showed him wrapped in seven-colored lightning. Another showed him covered in golden-black dragon scales. Another showed him holding Dragonheart with Emotion Severing Path fully released.","Another showed him surrounded by spatial distortions. Another showed him shining with Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline. Another showed him standing in darkness with no emotion in his eyes.","Then the pressure descended.","[Path Manifestation Assessment Begins.]","[Participant Max Morgan.]","[Detected Path Fragments: Emotion Severing Path, Divine King Punishment, Dimensional Sovereign Body, Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline, Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline...]","[Warning: Multiple High-Level Foundations Detected.]","[Warning: Path Integration Difficulty Increased.]","Max’s eyes narrowed.","The white-gold road trembled violently.","Then, from the mirrors around him, five Genesis figures stepped out.","One held a sword filled with emotionless severing power.","One was covered in seven-colored lightning.","One had golden-black dragon scales.","One was surrounded by space.","One shone with Heavenly Luminance light.","Each one represented a part of Max’s power.","The trial was not asking him to defeat a single reflection anymore.","It was asking him to prove which of his powers belonged to his true path.","Max slowly raised Dragonheart.","His expression became calm.","\"So that is how it is.\"","The five Genesis figures attacked at once.","And Max stepped forward to meet them.","The five Genesis figures attacked Max at the same time.","The figure wrapped in seven-colored lightning moved first, releasing a storm of Divine King Punishment that filled the white-gold road with destructive thunder. The dragon-scaled figure followed, its body tearing through the storm with terrifying physical force.","The spatial figure vanished and reappeared behind Max, trying to cut off his retreat through layers of folded space. The Heavenly Luminance figure raised its hand and released golden divine light that sought to suppress Max’s bloodline, while the final figure, the one holding a sword filled with emotionless severing power, stood still for a breath before slowly lifting its blade.","Max’s eyes remained calm.","He did not immediately release all his strength. He watched them. He felt them. He allowed the trial’s pressure to show him what each figure represented, because this stage was no longer only a battle of power. It was an assessment of foundation, direction, and path. The Genesis Trial was asking him whether his strength was a pile of separate abilities or whether all of them could be controlled by one will.","The seven-colored lightning crashed down.","Max stepped through it.","His Dimensional Sovereign Body unfolded, and every arc of lightning became clear in his perception. He did not avoid all of them. Some lightning struck his body, making his golden-black dragon scales flicker beneath his skin, but none of it slowed him down.","He raised Dragonheart and cut through the center of the storm, splitting the destructive thunder apart before facing the dragon-scaled figure rushing toward him.","Boom!"]},{"number":1804,"title":"Chapter 1804: Last Trial - 5","paragraphs":["Their fists collided.","The white-gold road trembled.","The dragon-scaled figure possessed terrifying physical strength, and when it punched, it carried the power of Max’s own draconic body, but it lacked the true foundation behind that body. It possessed an image of strength, not the will that had forged it through battle.","Max activated the Vein of Strength, poured force through his arm, and shattered the figure’s fist before kicking it backward.","The spatial figure appeared behind him at the same time.","Its hand struck toward the back of Max’s head through a folded space, but Max turned without looking. His body shifted by half a step, and Dragonheart swept backward, cutting through the spatial fold and forcing the figure out of hiding.","The Heavenly Luminance figure then released a golden chain of divine light, trying to bind his body and bloodline together, but Max’s own Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline stirred faintly in response, and the chain trembled as if it had met a superior authority.","Max did not use it to overpower the chain.","He simply slashed.","The chain broke.","Only then did the sword figure move.","It was silent.","Too silent.","The moment it attacked, even the other four Genesis figures seemed to dim around it. Its blade carried the imitation of Emotion Severing Path, and although it was only an imitation, the aura still caused the entire white-gold road to become cold and still.","The trial had copied the concept of severing emotion, intent, connection, and existence, and among all the figures before him, this was the only one that made Max’s eyes sharpen with genuine seriousness.","Their swords met.","No explosion appeared.","No loud sound rang out.","Only a thin invisible ripple spread across the road, and several nearby cubic mirrors split apart in silence.","Max looked at the sword figure before him.","The sword figure looked back without emotion.","For several breaths, they clashed silently. Each slash was simple, clean, and terrifying. The figure tried to sever Max’s anger, but Max’s anger had already become part of his resolve. It tried to sever his killing intent, but Max’s killing intent did not need to roar to exist.","It tried to sever his connection to Dragonheart, but Dragonheart hummed in his hand as if answering him. It tried to sever his path from his heart, but that was where it failed completely.","Max stepped forward.","\"You can copy the aura,\" he said calmly. \"But you cannot copy why I walk this path.\"","Dragonheart descended.","The sword figure raised its blade to block, but Max’s Emotion Severing Path awakened fully.","The world became still.","The imitation severing aura around the Genesis figure was cut apart first. Then its sword split. Then its body split. The figure dissolved into white-gold light, and the moment it vanished, the other four figures froze as if the core of their coordination had been destroyed.","Max turned.","Divine King Punishment erupted once, destroying the lightning figure.","His golden-black dragon scales appeared, and one punch shattered the dragon-scaled figure.","His Dimensional Sovereign Body locked onto the real body of the spatial figure, and Dragonheart pierced through it before it could escape.","The Heavenly Luminance figure tried to retreat into a golden sun, but Max’s superior bloodline pressure descended, making its light tremble long enough for his sword to cut it in half.","All five figures vanished.","The white-gold road shook violently, then began to break apart into countless glowing cubes.","[Path Manifestation Assessment Completed.]","[Participant Max Morgan Has Passed.]","[Path Strength: Exceptional.]","[Path Stability: Exceptional.]","[Path Potential: Unknown.]","[Warning: Participant Possesses Multiple High-Level Foundations.]","[Genesis Throne Recognition Increased.]","Max looked at the final prompt, but before he could think further, the white-gold road beneath him rose sharply. The separate paths of the other participants appeared in the distance. Tamara was breaking through a battlefield of Genesis soldiers with her spear raised high. Varkhon was roaring as he crushed a demonic mountain of pressure with his fists.","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes were erasing layers of void mirrors one by one. Ervin was walking through a path of abyssal darkness, his spear cutting forward with frightening calm.","One by one, they reached the final convergence.","Max arrived first.","The platform at the top was vast and circular, floating directly beneath the Genesis Throne. The throne itself hovered above a staircase of colorless light, and the pressure descending from it was so terrifying that even Max felt his body sink slightly when he stepped onto the final platform.","A few breaths later, Ervin appeared, his black robe slightly torn but his expression still calm. Revona arrived after him, her eyes deeper than before. Tamara came next, her war intent compressed to the extreme. Varkhon arrived last, laughing despite the blood at the corner of his mouth.","All five stood beneath the Genesis Throne.","Then the final prompt appeared.","[Final Stage: Genesis Throne Recognition.]","[Only One Participant May Stand Before The Genesis Throne.]","[Participants May Challenge One Another.]","[Participants May Withdraw From The Final Throne Contest And Preserve Current Assessment.]","[Warning: Defeat At This Stage May Reduce Final Genesis Mark Reward.]","The moment the prompt appeared, the atmosphere changed.","Varkhon looked at the throne, then at the others. His eyes burned with desire, but after a few breaths, he clicked his tongue. \"I know when a fight is worth taking and when it is just asking to be crushed. I am not beating all of you here.\"","Tamara glanced at him. \"That is surprisingly honest.\"","Varkhon grinned. \"I am violent, not stupid.\"","Tamara looked toward the throne for a long moment, then slowly lowered her spear. \"My path is war. This throne does not call to me strongly enough to risk everything here. I withdraw.\"","[Participant Tamara Has Withdrawn From The Final Throne Contest.]","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes remained fixed on the Genesis Throne. Her gaze seemed to pierce into some hidden layer, but after a while, she also stepped back. \"This place is valuable, but not worth forcing beyond my current foundation.\"","[Participant Revona Has Withdrawn From The Final Throne Contest.]","Only Max and Ervin remained.","The two looked at each other.","Ervin’s abyss-like aura stirred faintly, and for the first time, the depth around him rose enough for everyone to feel a chill. It was vast, silent, and bottomless, as if the entire platform had been placed at the edge of an endless drop. His black spear rested in his hand, and his calm smile carried a rare seriousness."]},{"number":1805,"title":"Chapter 1805: Last Trial - 6","paragraphs":["\"You reached first,\" Ervin said softly. \"But first place is not decided by arrival alone.\"","Max nodded. \"I know.\"","Ervin lifted his spear.","Max raised Dragonheart.","Neither of them spoke again.","The battle began without warning.","Ervin’s spear thrust forward, and the abyssal aura around him collapsed into a single point. The attack did not feel fast in an ordinary sense. It felt unavoidable, as if the spear had been falling toward Max from the bottom of the abyss long before Ervin moved.","Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body expanded instantly, and he saw the path of the spear, but even seeing it did not make it easy to avoid.","Dragonheart met the spear.","The impact rang across the final platform.","Max’s body slid back half a step.","Ervin’s eyes flickered.","Max’s gaze sharpened.","The next exchange was faster.","Spear and sword collided again and again. Ervin’s spearmanship was monstrous, deeper than anything he had revealed in the earlier trials. Every thrust contained hidden changes, every sweep carried abyssal weight, and every retreat was actually a preparation for another killing angle.","His aura did not explode outward like Orion’s star power or Selene’s light. It swallowed. It pulled. It made the battlefield feel deeper than it should have been.","But Max did not fall into it.","His Dimensional Sovereign Body gave him a complete sense of the battlefield. His dragon-scaled body endured the pressure. Divine King Punishment tore through the abyssal pull whenever it tried to suppress him. Dragonheart cut through the hidden spear lines, and when Ervin tried to drag his movement into the abyssal rhythm, Max released Emotion Severing Path and cut the connection between himself and that rhythm.","Ervin’s expression changed slightly.","\"Your sword can sever even some crazy things.\"","Max stepped forward smiling.\"I know.\"","The two clashed one final time.","Ervin’s spear descended like a bottomless abyss.","Max’s sword rose in absolute silence.","The abyssal spear light and the Emotion Severing Path met in the center of the platform. For a breath, the entire Genesis Throne space trembled. Then the abyssal spear light split apart, not destroyed by force, but severed from the concept that allowed it to pull everything downward.","Ervin’s spear stopped a finger’s width from Max’s shoulder.","Dragonheart stopped at Ervin’s throat.","Silence fell.","Ervin looked at the blade near his neck, then slowly smiled.","\"I withdraw.\"","\"At the last moment, you could have defended, but you willingly didn’t,\" Max said, frowning. \"Why is that?\"","\"It looks like all my actions have been perceived by you.\" Ervin smiled wryly before shaking his head and looking at Max. \"I don’t want to release my full strength right now.\"","Max shrugged and didn’t ask much about it.","[Participant Ervin Has Withdrawn From The Final Throne Contest.]","[Final Throne Contest Winner: Max Morgan.]","The Genesis Throne released a colorless light that descended upon Max alone.","A pressure beyond all previous stages fell on him, but Max did not lower his head. He climbed the staircase of colorless light step by step, and every step made the throne clearer. When he finally reached the top, he stood before the Genesis Throne, and the entire trial space became silent.","[Genesis Throne Recognition Initiated.]","[Participant Max Morgan Has Obtained First Place In The Genesis Trial.]","[Final Genesis Marks Distribution Completed.]","[Max Morgan: 35 Genesis Marks From Trial Three.]","[Ervin: 18 Genesis Marks From Trial Three.]","[Revona: 8 Genesis Marks From Trial Three.]","[Tamara: 6 Genesis Marks From Trial Three.]","[Varkhon: 3 Genesis Marks From Trial Three.]","[Final Genesis Mark Totals:]","[Max Morgan: 56/100]","[Ervin: 33/100]","[Revona: 21/100]","[Tamara: 16/100]","[Varkhon: 9/100]","[Genesis Trial Completed.]","[Reward Phase Initiated.]","The Genesis Sovereign Platform dissolved.","All five participants appeared once again in a calm cubic chamber, but this time, the atmosphere was different. There was no pressure, no guardians, no trial sequence, and no competition. In front of each participant appeared several glowing doors, each one leading to a different reward chamber.","A system prompt appeared.","[Reward Chambers Available.]","[Reward Chamber Time Will Be Determined By Final Genesis Marks.]","[The More Genesis Marks A Participant Possesses, The Longer They May Remain In Their Chosen Reward Chamber.]","[Each Participant’s Reward Chamber Options Will Be Generated According To Their Paths, Foundations, Bloodlines, Talents, And Trial Performance.]","[Each Participant May Choose Only One Reward Chamber.]","Max looked at the prompt, then at the doors appearing before him.","Several doors flickered briefly, but in the end, only two remained stable.","The first door was wrapped in seven-colored lightning. A divine throne of thunder appeared faintly behind it, and the aura of destructive punishment rolled outward like a storm waiting to descend upon all things.","It was the reward chamber connected to Divine King Punishment, the Pseudo Cosmic Path he had created from the essence of the Storm King’s Inheritance and the destructive punishment nature of the seven-colored lightning.","The second door was silent.","There was no thunder.","No flames.","No dazzling light.","It was a plain dark-gray door with a single sword mark carved down its center. Yet the moment Max looked at it, the entire chamber seemed to become still. The emotions in the air thinned. The faint excitement from completing the trial, the lingering battle intent, the curiosity of the others, and even the subtle pressure of the Genesis reward phase all seemed to quiet down around that door.","Emotion Severing Path.","The system prompt appeared before Max.","[Reward Chamber Options Detected.]","[Option One: Divine King Punishment Chamber.]","[Effect: Improve comprehension, stability, and destructive authority of the Divine King Punishment Pseudo Cosmic Path.]","[Option Two: Emotion Severing Path Chamber.]","[Effect: Improve comprehension, stability, and severing authority of the Emotion Severing Path Pseudo Cosmic Path.]","[Final Genesis Marks: 56.]","[Reward Chamber Time Granted: 56 Days.]","[Please Choose One Reward Chamber.]","Max did not hesitate here.","Divine King Punishment was powerful. Its destructive force was terrifying, and it had already allowed him to suppress Selene’s light-based attacks. If he entered that chamber, his seven-colored lightning path would certainly grow stronger.","But Max knew himself clearly. Divine King Punishment was a weapon of destruction and punishment, while Emotion Severing Path was something deeper to him.","So the choice was obvious.","Max walked toward the second door.","\"I choose the Emotion Severing Path Chamber.\"","[Choice Confirmed.]","[Reward Chamber Selected: Emotion Severing Path Chamber.]","[Reward Time: 56 Days.]","The dark-gray door opened silently.","Inside was nothing but stillness.","No light came out.","No sound emerged.","Only a thin, invisible sword aura drifted from within, quiet enough to be missed by weaker people and terrifying enough to make every strong person present feel their heart tighten.","Max stepped toward it.","The others also chose their paths and entered in their respective chosen reward chambers."]},{"number":1806,"title":"Chapter 1806: A Shadow","paragraphs":["The moment Max stepped into the Emotion Severing Path Chamber, the door behind him closed without making even the faintest sound, sealing him inside a darkness that felt far more absolute than the absence of light.","There was no flash of brilliance, no grand welcome, and not even a system prompt explaining what he needed to do next. The chamber before him was completely dark, but this darkness was not ordinary darkness.","It was still, cold, and empty, as though sound, color, warmth, and even emotion itself had been severed from this place long before he arrived.","Max stood there in silence with Dragonheart in his hand, while the little cursed eye attached to his shoulder blinked once before becoming strangely quiet, as if even the Witch’s curse mark did not dare to move carelessly inside this chamber.","Max calmly looked around, but there was no sky above him, no ground beneath him that his eyes could see, no walls around him, and no visible end to the space. Even so, he could clearly feel that he was standing on something solid.","His Dimensional Sovereign Body spread outward by instinct, but the moment his perception touched the surrounding darkness, it returned to him in broken pieces. It had not been blocked by space, nor had it been suppressed by some ordinary formation. It had been cut apart by something far sharper.","At that moment, Max understood that this chamber did not belong to space. It belonged to the sword path he had chosen, the Emotion Severing Path.","After several breaths passed, Max finally saw something standing within the darkness far ahead of him. It was a black shadow with the shape of a man, but it had no face, no features, no clothes, and no clear body that could be seen.","It looked as if someone had cut a human silhouette out of the void itself and placed it before him. In its hand was a sword also made of shadow, and although the figure stood completely still, the aura around it made Max’s eyes narrow slightly.","That aura was not loud, nor was it oppressive in the usual sense. It simply made the world around it feel empty, as if everything close to it had already been cut away from meaning.","Max did not speak, and the black shadow did not speak either. For a while, the two of them simply stared at one another within the endless darkness, neither side moving first. Then Max slowly steadied his breathing, and the instant he did, the black shadow vanished from where it had been standing.","Max’s pupils narrowed a little as a sword appeared before him without warning, descending toward his neck in complete silence. It carried no killing intent, no anger, no warning, and no emotional fluctuation.","It simply arrived with the purest expression of the Emotion Severing Path, and the sword was not trying to cut his flesh first. It was trying to sever the reaction inside him, the fear that should have warned him, the instinct that should have made him move, and the connection between his mind and body.","\"He is also using the Emotion Severing Path?!\" Max was shocked. He quickly raised Dragonheart, and the same Emotion Severing Path erupted from his sword as he met the attack head-on. Their blades clashed in the darkness, yet no explosion rang out and no shockwave spread through the chamber.","Only the silence deepened. The two swords met, and the space around them seemed to lose another layer of existence. Max felt the shadow’s severing power enter through the clash, trying to cut through the anger, hatred, resolve, and purpose hidden inside his path.","At the same time, Max’s own Emotion Severing Path struck back, trying to sever the shadow’s sword intent, its rhythm, and the invisible connection between its blade and its body.","Neither side retreated, and in the next instant, they moved again. The black shadow slashed from the left, and Max answered from the right. The shadow thrust toward his heart, and Max turned the blade away before cutting toward the shadow’s shoulder.","The shadow shifted without making a sound, and its sword came from a blind angle that should not have existed, but Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body caught the distortion just before the blade arrived.","He stepped back, raised Dragonheart, and met the attack with his own severing sword force. Once again, their swords clashed, and once again, no sound appeared. Only the surrounding darkness became heavier.","Max immediately understood what this reward chamber truly was. It was not a simple comprehension room where he would sit quietly and absorb insights. It was a training chamber for the Emotion Severing Path, and the one training him was this black shadow.","More accurately, this shadow was not merely a mindless trial figure. Its sword was too pure, too sharp, and too complete. Every movement contained a version of the Emotion Severing Path that was more mature than his own, not necessarily stronger in raw power at every moment, but far deeper in understanding.","The black shadow attacked again, and Max responded without hesitation. One clash became ten, ten became a hundred, and a hundred became a thousand as time gradually lost all meaning inside the chamber.","Max did not know whether hours had passed or days had passed. There was no sunrise, no sunset, no system timer, and no voice telling him how much reward time remained. There was only the shadow, the sword, the stillness, and the endless collision between two Emotion Severing Paths.","Sometimes Max was forced back. Sometimes the shadow was forced back. Sometimes his sword severed the shadow’s attack before it reached him. Sometimes the shadow severed his rhythm and forced him to rebuild his stance from nothing.","The first thousand clashes taught Max one clear truth. His Emotion Severing Path was sharp, but it was not refined enough. He had used it to overwhelm many enemies because his foundation, sword, will, and killing intent were all terrifying. Against Seraphine, Fin, Morgana, and countless others, that had been enough."]},{"number":1807,"title":"Chapter 1807: Why Choose Emotion Severing Path?","paragraphs":["But against this black shadow, every flaw in his path became painfully visible. His severing power sometimes carried too much anger. Sometimes it carried too much intent to kill. Sometimes it moved with the hatred he held toward the second faction. Those emotions made the path strong, but they also created uneven edges that disrupted the purity of his sword.","The black shadow’s sword had none of that. It did not hate, it did not rage, and it did not judge. It simply severed. Max’s eyes grew colder as he understood this, but he did not try to remove his emotions completely.","That was not his way. Instead, he began compressing them. His anger became sharper, his hatred became quieter, and his resolve became cleaner. He no longer allowed those emotions to drag his sword out of line. He made them fuel the edge without disturbing the path of the blade.","Their swords clashed again, and this time, a faint change appeared on the black shadow. A thin line of gray emerged on its wrist, and Max noticed it instantly. The more they clashed, the more the shadow’s body began to reveal itself. At first, only its wrist became visible. Then part of its hand appeared.","After that, the fingers wrapped around its sword gradually became clear. The blackness covering it was not being torn away by brute force. It was being removed through understanding.","Every time Max grasped a deeper layer of the Emotion Severing Path, another part of the shadow was revealed, as if the chamber was rewarding his comprehension by showing him the true form of the one training him.","The clashes continued without pause. Ten thousand times passed, then fifty thousand, and then a hundred thousand. Max’s body should have grown exhausted long ago, but the reward chamber seemed to sustain him at the edge between strain and collapse. He could feel fatigue, but it never destroyed him.","He could feel pain in his arm, but it never reached the point where he could no longer lift Dragonheart. He could feel the pressure of the shadow’s path entering his mind again and again, but each time he resisted it, his own path became clearer than before.","The shadow’s sword became faster, while Max’s sword became quieter. The shadow’s severing force became deeper, while Max’s severing force became cleaner. The darkness around them became filled with sword marks that did not remain visible, yet never truly disappeared either.","Each sword mark represented a clash of severing authority, a moment where one path tried to cut through the other, and a moment where Max either failed, adapted, or surpassed the previous version of himself.","More of the shadow’s body appeared as the training continued. Its forearm emerged from the darkness, followed by its shoulder, its chest, its other hand, and finally its legs. Its face was still hidden, but the outline of a real person had already begun to emerge from beneath the black covering.","The figure no longer looked like a simple shadow. It looked like a man wrapped in layers of darkness, waiting to be fully uncovered by Max’s sword and understanding.","Then came the final series of clashes. Max no longer counted how many times their swords moved. It might have been tens of thousands more, or it might have been hundreds of thousands. In that place, numbers had become meaningless.","The only things that mattered were the edge of Dragonheart, the rhythm of his breathing, the stillness of his heart, and the growing understanding that the Emotion Severing Path was not about becoming emotionless.","It was about choosing which emotions could remain, which emotions needed to be cut away, and which emotions could be transformed into an edge that severed everything without hesitation.","At last, Max and the black shadow moved at the same time. Both of them used the Emotion Severing Path, and both swords drew silent lines through the darkness before meeting in the center. For the first time since the battle began, a sound rang out.","It was soft, clear, and distant, like the echo of a single sword cry breaking through countless layers of silence.","Clang.","The darkness around the shadow shattered like a broken shell, and its entire body was finally revealed.","Standing before Max was a middle-aged man with a strong presence. He wore plain dark robes, and his long black hair fell behind his shoulders. His face was calm, neither warm nor cold, while his eyes carried a depth that made it seem as if he had once severed countless things from himself and from the world.","There was no overwhelming killing intent around him, yet his presence made the chamber feel sharper than any battlefield Max had ever entered. He was not the projection of a random swordsman, nor was he a simple trial guardian. He was the first owner of the Emotion Severing Path.","The middle-aged man lowered his sword slightly and looked at Max.","For the first time since Max had entered the chamber, he finally spoke, and his voice was calm, yet every word seemed to cut through the darkness. \"Why did you choose Emotion Severing Path? There are countless severing path options. Severing space. Severing karma. Severing fate. Severing life. Severing death. Severing time. Severing cause and effect. Many of them sound greater, cleaner, and more direct. Why choose emotion?\"","Max held Dragonheart at his side and met the man’s gaze without looking away. For a few moments, he did not answer. Then he spoke calmly. \"I wanted the strongest severing force.\"","The middle-aged man’s eyes remained still, and Max continued, \"I wanted a severing force that could allow me to sever anything and everything that blocks my path. Body, soul, attacks, concepts, fate, karma, life, death, space, time, bloodline, hatred, fear, hesitation, and anything else standing before me.\"","The chamber became even quieter, and Max’s grip on Dragonheart tightened slightly as he added, \"So I chose emotion.\"","The middle-aged man looked at him without interrupting, and Max’s voice remained calm, but the resolve inside it was unmistakable. \"Because emotion is the root of everything I do. My anger tells me who I must kill. My hatred tells me what debt must be paid. My love tells me who I must protect. My regret tells me what I must never allow to happen again. My fear tells me what I must overcome. My hesitation tells me what I must cut away. If I can sever my own emotions, control them, sharpen them, and use them as the edge of my path, then I can sever everything else.\"","Max paused for a moment before continuing in the same steady voice. \"I did not choose Emotion Severing Path because I wanted to become emotionless. I chose it because I wanted to use my emotions to sever everything and create the strongest severing path.\""]},{"number":1808,"title":"Chapter 1808: A Forbidden Path","paragraphs":["The middle-aged man stared at Max in silence for a long while. Then, for the first time, a faint smile appeared on his face.","\"Good answer.\"","But then his expression became regretful.","\"However, did you know that Emotion Severing Path is one of the very few forbidden cosmic paths out there?\"","Max’s expression changed. \"What do you mean by forbidden? Am I walking some evil path?\"","The middle-aged man lowered his sword slightly.","\"Forbidden does not mean evil,\" he said. \"It means dangerous. Emotion Severing Path is forbidden because it is too strong, too unstable, and too volatile.\"","Max narrowed his eyes.","The middle-aged man continued, \"Most severing paths have a fixed target. Some sever space. Some sever karma. Some sever fate. Some sever life and death. But Emotion Severing Path is different. Emotion exists inside everything a living being does.\"","He looked at Max seriously.","\"Before a person kills, he hates. Before he protects, he loves. Before he runs, he fears. Before he climbs higher, he desires. Emotion is connected to will, memory, attachment, karma, and even the reason a person continues existing.\"","Max remained silent.","\"That is why this path is dangerous,\" the man said. \"At first, you sever fear so you can fight calmly. You sever hesitation so your sword becomes decisive. You sever pain so you do not collapse. This makes you stronger.\"","His eyes became colder.","\"But if you fail to control it, the path will not stop there.\"","The chamber became quieter.","\"It will begin severing emotions on its own. It will cut too much fear and make you reckless. It will cut hesitation completely and make you unable to stop. It will cut pity, mercy, regret, and restraint.\"","He paused for a moment.","\"When that happens, the user goes berserk.\"","Max’s gaze sharpened. He recalled the last few times he remained in his Emotion Severing state for a longer time than he intended because he simply couldn’t get out of that state. He wondered if it was because of this reason.","The middle-aged man said, \"A berserk user of Emotion Severing Path may not roar like a mad beast. Sometimes he becomes completely calm. Too calm. He kills without anger. He cuts without hesitation. He no longer knows the difference between enemy, stranger, or ally.\"","His voice turned heavy.","\"At that point, he is no longer a swordsman. He is a killing machine.\"","Max’s grip on Dragonheart tightened.","The man continued, \"That is why ancient forces feared this path. It can sever an enemy’s fighting intent, courage, hatred, loyalty, obsession, and even the emotional foundation behind karma or fate. But if it loses control, it can also sever the user’s own heart.\"","He looked directly at Max.","\"If you cannot control it, one day it may sever the very emotions that make you who you are.\"","Max was silent for a few breaths.","Then he asked, \"So that is why it is forbidden?\"","The man simply turned and waved his hand again. This time, an image appeared in the darkness. It showed a battlefield filled with countless warriors. They were not dead, but they stood frozen, their weapons lowered, their eyes empty.","Some had been charging forward with rage only moments earlier. Some had been protecting others with desperate courage. Some had been fighting for revenge. But after one silent sword passed through the battlefield, all of them had stopped.","\"They did not die immediately,\" the middle-aged man said. \"That was the first time the world called my path forbidden. I severed the hatred of an army, the loyalty of its generals, the courage of its vanguard, and the despair of its prisoners. The war ended in one sword. Everyone thought that was mercy at first.\"","His eyes became distant.","\"Then they realized the survivors could no longer live properly. The soldiers who lost hatred also lost the reason they had sharpened their blades for centuries. The generals who lost loyalty no longer cared for their kingdoms. The prisoners who lost despair no longer cared whether they were freed. Fathers looked at sons and felt nothing. Lovers held each other and felt nothing. A kingdom survived the war, but it became hollow.\"","The image faded.","Max’s fingers slowly tightened around Dragonheart.","The middle-aged man looked at him. \"That is why this path is forbidden. Because when Emotion Severing Path is used carelessly, it does not only defeat enemies. It hollows out worlds.\"","The chamber remained silent for several breaths.","Then Max asked, \"If it is that dangerous, why did you continue walking it?\"","The middle-aged man smiled bitterly. \"For the same reason you chose it.\"","Max’s gaze sharpened.","The man said softly, \"I also wanted to sever everything that blocked my path. I wanted a sword that could cut through fear, regret, fate, karma, and the chains of the heart. At first, I believed I could control it. I believed my will was strong enough to decide what should be cut and what should remain. And perhaps, for a time, I was right.\"","He paused.","\"But the more powerful the path became, the quieter my heart grew. That is the second reason it is forbidden. Emotion Severing Path does not only sever the enemy. It also tries to sever its owner.\"","Max’s eyes changed.","The middle-aged man tapped his own chest lightly.","\"Every time you use it, you draw the blade across your own heart first. You cut away fear so you can move. You cut away hesitation so you can kill. You cut away grief so you do not collapse. You cut away anger so your sword remains clean. You cut away love so your enemies cannot use it against you. At first, it feels like strength. It feels like clarity. It feels like freedom. But one day, if you are not careful, you will realize that you did not master the path. The path mastered you.\"","The darkness around him rippled.","His voice became lower.","\"You will stand above the corpses of your enemies and feel nothing. You will see the people you wanted to protect and feel nothing. You will remember your hatred and wonder why it once mattered. You will remember your love and find only an empty shape where warmth should have been. And if that day comes, your sword may become sharper than ever, but you will no longer know why you are swinging it.\""]},{"number":1809,"title":"Chapter 1809: The Final Obstacle of Emotion Severing Path","paragraphs":["Max remained still.","The middle-aged man stared at him with a grave expression. \"That is why the heavens reject it. That is why ancient forces sealed records of it. That is why sword lineages that discovered fragments of this path either destroyed them or buried them in forbidden grounds. Emotion Severing Path can become one of the strongest severing forces in existence, but it can also create a swordsman who is no longer truly alive. A blade without attachment. A will without warmth. A being who can sever worlds without hatred, without joy, without regret, and without stopping.\"","He lifted his sword slightly.","\"When such a person appears, the cosmos itself treats him as a calamity.\"","Max looked at him and asked, \"Did that happen to you?\"","The middle-aged man’s expression did not change, but the silence after the question was enough of an answer.","After a long time, he said, \"Almost.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly.","The middle-aged man looked into the endless darkness of the chamber, and for the first time, the calmness in his eyes seemed to carry a trace of old regret.","\"I was truly on the verge of creating the Cosmic Path of Emotion Severing Path,\" he said. \"But I never crossed that bridge. Or perhaps I should say, someone stopped me from crossing that bridge.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed as he heard him and a figure appeared in his mind.’","\"Was it the Sword Saint?\"","The middle-aged man turned his gaze back toward Max and nodded.","\"It was the Sword Saint.\"","The name caused the chamber to become even quieter.","\"One day, he appeared before me,\" the middle-aged man continued. \"There was no warning. There was no aura. There was no grand arrival. He simply stood in front of me, as if he had always been there. Then he told me to give up the path of Emotion Severing. He said it was one of the few forbidden cosmic paths and that if I truly completed it, I would not be creating a sword path. I would be creating a calamity.\"","Max listened silently.","The middle-aged man gave a faint bitter smile.","\"But back then, I was too arrogant. I respected the Sword Saint. In fact, I looked up to him. Every swordsman of my era did. But respect and obedience are two different things. I had already reached the final step of my path. I could see the bridge before me. I could feel the true Cosmic Path waiting beyond it. How could I turn away when I was already so close?\"","His grip on his sword tightened slightly.","\"So I refused him.\"","Max’s gaze sharpened.","\"That did not sit well with the Sword Saint,\" the middle-aged man said. \"He gave me one final chance. He told me that some paths could be pursued through talent, some through madness, and some through defiance. But Emotion Severing Path was different. He said this path contradicted the nature of the world itself.\"","The middle-aged man paused for a moment.","\"I still refused.\"","The darkness around them trembled faintly, as if even the chamber remembered what happened next.","\"In the end, we fought.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed. \"And?\"","\"I lost.\"","The middle-aged man’s answer was calm, but the weight behind it was terrifying.","\"In one sword.\"","Max’s expression changed slightly.","The middle-aged man did not seem ashamed as he said it. Instead, he sounded like someone stating an absolute truth that had long since settled in his heart.","\"I had spent my life creating the strongest severing path I could imagine. I had severed fear, hesitation, killing intent, hatred, courage, loyalty, obsession, and countless invisible threads that other sword paths could not even touch. I believed that even if I could not defeat the Sword Saint, I could at least make him draw out his true strength.\"","He lowered his eyes.","\"But I was wrong. His sword fell, and everything ended. My sword intent, my path, my ambition, my body, and the bridge I was about to cross were all cut apart in one strike.\"","Max remained silent.","The middle-aged man looked at him and continued, \"I died there without ever knowing the true potential of the path I wanted to follow. I never truly completed the Cosmic Path of Emotion Severing. I only stood before it.\"","The chamber grew colder.","\"But before my consciousness truly disappeared, I heard the Sword Saint say something.\"","Max looked at him seriously.","The middle-aged man’s voice became low.","\"He said Emotion Severing Path is the one path that truly contradicts the nature of the world. Because of that, he would appear every time someone starts to create the Cosmic Path of Emotion Severing Path.\"","Max’s expression finally changed.","\"What does that mean?\" he asked, clearly shocked by those last words. \"Does that mean he is not dead and has been alive all this time?\"","\"I do not know,\" the middle-aged man said, shaking his head.","Max frowned.","The middle-aged man continued, \"The Sword Saint, even in my time, was one of the most mysterious individuals in existence. Nobody knew which force he belonged to. Nobody knew where he came from. Nobody even knew what he truly looked like.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed further.","The middle-aged man said, \"Some claimed he was an ancient existence who had lived through many eras. Some said he was only a title passed from one supreme swordsman to another. Others believed he was not a person at all, but a will left behind by the sword itself. No one could prove anything.\"","He looked directly at Max.","\"But one thing I am sure of now.\"","Max did not speak.","The middle-aged man’s expression became solemn.","\"He will come after you.\"","The words fell into the darkness like a blade.","Max’s grip on Dragonheart tightened.","The middle-aged man continued, \"You have already formed the Pseudo Cosmic Path of Emotion Severing. You have not crossed the bridge yet, but you are walking toward it. The stronger your path becomes, the clearer your existence will appear to him. And if you truly reach the edge of creating the Cosmic Path of Emotion Severing, the Sword Saint will appear before you, just as he appeared before me. He will take your sword into his tomb just like he did with me and many others.\""]},{"number":1810,"title":"Chapter 1810 - 70 Million Points!","paragraphs":["Max stared at him. \"Then I will fight him.\"","The middle-aged man looked at Max for a long moment, then sighed softly.","\"That is exactly what I said back then.\"","Max did not look away.","The middle-aged man’s voice became heavier. \"Understand this, Max. I am not telling you this to make you afraid. I am telling you because you must know what waits at the end of this road. The danger of Emotion Severing Path is not only the path itself. It is also the one who guards the boundary before it becomes a true Cosmic Path.\"","Max’s eyes became cold and steady.","\"If he comes to stop me, then he becomes part of the path I need to sever.\"","For a moment, the middle-aged man said nothing.","Then a faint smile appeared on his face.","\"You truly are arrogant.\"","Max replied calmly, \"I have reasons to be.\"","The middle-aged man looked at him, and the regret in his eyes slowly faded, replaced by a sharper expression.","\"Good. Then before the Sword Saint comes, you need to become strong enough to survive one sword from him.\"","He raised his blade again.","\"Because I could not.\"","As he said those words, the silent severing aura around his sword began to fade.","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly.","The middle-aged man looked down at his own hand and saw it turning into golden particles. His fingers were disappearing first, then his wrist, then the edge of his sleeve. The process was slow and quiet, without pain or resistance, as if the final piece of consciousness he had left behind in this chamber had already completed its purpose.","Max frowned. \"You are disappearing.\"","The middle-aged man looked back at him and smiled faintly. \"Of course. I am not truly alive. What stands before you is only a remnant of my will, left behind in this reward chamber through the Genesis Trial. I existed here to test the one who chose the Emotion Severing Path Chamber, to warn him, and to see whether he was worthy of carrying this forbidden blade further.\"","His body continued dissolving into golden light.","Max tightened his grip on Dragonheart. \"You said you would teach me.\"","\"I did,\" the middle-aged man said calmly. \"And I already have.\"","Max’s expression did not change, but his gaze became sharper.","The man looked at him with calm eyes. \"You have already learned everything from our few exchanges of swords, so there is not much I can teach you here. Your comprehension is terrifying, Max. Each clash between us revealed a flaw in your path, and each time, you corrected it faster than I expected. By the time my true body was revealed, the chamber had already acknowledged that my sword could no longer guide you in the ordinary way.\"","Max remained silent.","The middle-aged man’s chest had already begun scattering into golden particles, but his presence did not weaken immediately. Instead, his gaze became even deeper.","\"What remains for you now is not something I can hand over with words. You must walk forward yourself. You must experience the danger of the path, control its volatility, resist the madness hidden within it, and face the Sword Saint when he comes. No one can do that in your place.\"","The golden particles drifted upward like fireflies in the darkness.","The man looked at Max and said softly, \"I just want you to see through the end of this path for me.\"","Those words made the chamber even quieter.","For a brief moment, Max did not answer. He simply looked at the man whose life had ended before he could truly complete the Cosmic Path of Emotion Severing. This man had been arrogant, talented, and brave enough to stand before the Sword Saint, but he had still fallen before reaching the end. Now, the last trace of his will was placing that unfinished path into Max’s hands.","Max slowly raised Dragonheart and gave a slight nod.","\"I will.\"","The middle-aged man’s smile became clearer.","\"Good.\"","His body finally dissolved completely.","The last thing to disappear was his face, and even as it faded, his eyes remained calm, regretful, and faintly hopeful. Then the golden particles scattered into the endless darkness, leaving behind only a silent sword mark in the air where he had stood.","Max remained in place for a long time.","The chamber did not immediately react.","There was no prompt.","No reward notification.","No congratulations.","There was only silence.","Max looked at the fading sword mark, then slowly lowered his gaze to Dragonheart. The Emotion Severing Path inside him had become quieter than before, but that quietness was not emptiness. It was control. It was a sharper boundary between emotion and madness, between severing and being severed, between wielding the blade and becoming the blade.","The middle-aged man was gone.","But his warning remained.","The Sword Saint would come.","And when that day arrived, Max would need to be strong enough to survive the sword that had killed the first owner of the Emotion Severing Path.","Max closed his eyes for a moment.","Then he opened them again.","His gaze was calm.","\"I will see the end of this path,\" he said softly.","With that Max’s time in the chamber ended and his body too disappeared from the scene.","In no moment, Max found himself standing outside the ruined castle he had destroyed himself.","\"I came back to this place?\" Max was surprised. He thought he would join the others and they would be teleported out together but it was clearly not the case.","\"Anyway, I should have been rewarded some good Killing Points.\" Max smiled and checked his Killing Points.","[Killing Points: 70 Million Killing Points]","[Rank: 4]","\"I am rank 4 even with 70 Million Killing Points?\" Max was shocked for the first time. This made him wondered just who were the top three.","With 70 million points, he should have at least reached top 3 but it was clear that he had underestimated the other top geniuses."]},{"number":1811,"title":"Chapter 1811: A Fiery Clash!","paragraphs":["Max flew away from the broken castle.","The ruined structure quickly became smaller beneath him, its collapsed towers and cracked walls fading into the distance as he moved through the sky. The wind rushed past his body, and the little cursed eye near his left shoulder shifted slightly before settling again, its red-black pupil blinking as if it had also sensed the change in his aura after the Genesis Trial.","Max ignored it as usual. His mind was still on the Emotion Severing Path Chamber, the middle-aged man’s warning, and the name of the Sword Saint.","However, before he could decide where to go next, a familiar system notification suddenly appeared in his vision.","[Cosmic Ascension Conference: First Round Status Update]","[Current Remaining Participants: 107]","[Notice: When The Number Of Remaining Participants Reaches 100, The First Round Will End.]","Max slowed down slightly in midair.","\"Only one hundred and seven left,\" he muttered.","The number made the situation clear.","The first round was almost over.","When the Cosmic Ascension Conference had begun, countless geniuses from different races, forces, clans, and worlds had entered this battlefield.","Some were supreme talents from first-rate forces. Some were descendants of ancient families. Some were demons, elves, humans, witches, beasts, and other strange races. Many of them had entered this world with confidence, believing that they could use the first round to build a strong foundation for the rest of the conference.","But now, only one hundred and seven remained.","That meant the weak had already been eliminated.","Even many strong participants had likely lost all their lives through ambushes, trials, beast territories, faction wars, and battles between geniuses. From this point onward, anyone who remained alive would not be simple. The first round had already filtered out almost everyone who relied on luck alone, and the final seven eliminations would likely happen very soon.","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly.","Seven more people.","Once seven more participants disappeared, the first round would end, and whatever came after it would begin.","He looked at the prompt for a moment longer before it faded from his vision.","The timing was interesting. He had just completed the Genesis Trial, strengthened his control over Emotion Severing Path, and learned about the Sword Saint. Now the system was telling him that the first round was close to ending. It felt less like a coincidence and more like the opening of the next stage.","\"It seems I have spent a lot more time in the reward chamber than it seems on the surface.\" Max glanced into the distance. He believed the number of participants fell this low because he might have spent too much time unknowingly in the rewards chamber.","Somewhere in this world, Caroline, Nancy, Jessica, and the remnants of the third faction were still trying to survive. Somewhere else, Revona, Tamara, Varkhon, and Ervin had likely returned from their own reward chambers.","Orion Starfall, Kaiden Voidmere, Princess Rosaline, the Divine Son of the second faction, the geniuses of Sword God Palace, and many others were still moving through this battlefield. Any one of them might become part of the final chaos before the first round ended.","Max’s expression remained calm.","\"Seven left,\" he said softly.","Then his speed increased again.","Golden light flashed beneath his feet as he flew across the sky, leaving the broken castle far behind. He did not know whether the final seven eliminations would happen through his hands or someone else’s, but it did not matter much.","The first round was nearing its end, and before it closed completely, Max wanted to see if anything else in this world was worth taking.","Just at that moment, Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body suddenly caught something, and he paused in the air.","Far away, violent ripples were tearing through the sky.","Max turned his head and saw two figures fighting while flying through the air at terrifying speed. One of them fought with a sword, while the other fought barehanded.","Every time the two collided, a massive shockwave erupted from their clash and spread in all directions, forcing the clouds apart and making the air tremble like the surface of a stormy sea.","The swordsman’s blade light was sharp enough to split mountain peaks from a distance, while the barehanded fighter’s fists seemed capable of smashing apart space itself. Neither of them was fighting casually. Each exchange carried the force of a true inheritance, and the more Max watched, the more his eyes narrowed with interest.","\"From their power level... could they be inheritors of Sword God and War God?\" Max wondered.","He looked around and then noticed a crowd gathered near a tall tower in the distance. The tower stood on a floating stone platform above a ruined plain, and its surface was covered in ancient formation marks that released a faint protective glow. Many people were standing there, watching the battle unfold from a safe distance, and judging by their relaxed postures, they were not here to interfere. They were spectators.","Max flew toward the tower.","Arriving on the tower, he saw that there were around fifty to sixty people gathered there, and all of them seemed unusually relaxed. Some sat on broken stone railings, some stood with their arms crossed, and some even had fruits, wine gourds, and snacks in their hands as if they had turned this battlefield into a viewing stage.","Their attention was fixed on the two figures fighting in the sky, and every time a powerful clash erupted, the crowd would burst into excited discussion.","\"Did you see that slash?\" one young man shouted, his eyes shining. \"That has to be the Sword God Palace’s strongest inheritor. No ordinary swordsman can release sword light that clean.\"","A woman beside him shook her head. \"Clean? That sword almost cut through the protective formation around the tower from this far away. If we were standing closer, half of us would already be dead.\"","Another participant laughed. \"That is why we are watching from here. I am not stupid enough to stand near two monsters fighting for entertainment.\"","A burly man with a scar across his cheek pointed toward the barehanded fighter in the sky and said loudly, \"Forget the swordsman for a moment. Look at that fist power. He is meeting every sword slash head-on with his bare hands. If that is not the War God Legacy’s inheritor, then I will swallow this tower stone by stone.\""]},{"number":1812,"title":"Chapter 1812: Damien Voss vs Rakan Throne","paragraphs":["Someone immediately replied, \"Then prepare your teeth, because I heard the War God Legacy has not fully chosen an inheritor yet.\"","\"That is nonsense,\" the scarred man retorted. \"Do you think someone can fight like that without receiving the War God’s inheritance? Look at his body. Every punch is like a battlefield collapsing.\"","The crowd erupted again as another clash exploded in the distance.","The swordsman descended from above, his sword leaving behind a long silver-white arc that looked like a river of sword light falling from the sky. The barehanded fighter did not dodge. He raised his right fist, and a golden-red war aura gathered around his arm before he punched upward. Sword and fist collided, and the entire sky shook violently.","A ring-shaped shockwave spread across the horizon, and even the tower’s protective formation rippled under the force.","\"Good!\"","\"That was insane!\"","\"These two are truly monsters.\"","\"I thought the first round would end quietly after so many people were eliminated, but who would have thought we would get to watch something like this before the end?\"","Max stood near the edge of the tower, quietly listening to them.","No one immediately recognized him, mostly because everyone was too focused on the battle. The few who glanced at him only saw another participant arriving to watch, and since many people had been gathering here for a while, his appearance did not draw too much attention at first. Max did not mind. He kept his aura restrained and looked toward the fight with calm interest.","A thin man in gray robes spoke to the group near him. \"I heard that the swordsman is Damian Voss from Sword God Palace. They say he was the one most favored by the Sword God Legacy from the beginning.\"","Another person quickly added, \"Damian Voss? No wonder his sword is so terrifying. Sword God Palace has been looking for the Sword of the Sword Sovereign too, right? If Damian gets both the legacy and that sword, he might become unstoppable among the younger generation.\"","Someone else snorted. \"That is assuming the sword ever reaches his hands. I heard the person carrying it is not easy to deal with.\"","\"Who? Max Morgan?\"","The moment that name was spoken, several people nearby turned their heads slightly.","Max’s expression did not change.","The gray-robed man nodded. \"Yes. That one. His name has been spreading everywhere recently. He killed many Sword God Palace disciples, offended the second faction elves, killed Selene Vaeloria, and even cut down Morgana Starveil from Stellar Templar.\"","A young woman’s eyes widened. \"Is that true? I thought those were exaggerated rumors.\"","\"Exaggerated?\" another man laughed. \"Maybe some parts are, but not all of them. Morgana’s name disappeared from the active ranking after she clashed with him. Selene’s side also lost badly. Even Seraphine and Fin were forced to kill themselves in front of him.\"","The scarred man clicked his tongue. \"That Max Morgan sounds like another madman. This conference is full of monsters.\"","Another spectator pointed toward the battle and said, \"If Damian Voss finds him, then things will become interesting. Sword God Palace will not ignore him carrying Dragonheart.\"","\"Interesting?\" someone replied with a laugh. \"It will be a disaster. Damian is already fighting someone who may be the War God Legacy’s inheritor. If Max Morgan also appears, this place might become the center of the first round’s final chaos.\"","The crowd became even more excited at that thought.","Someone looked toward the barehanded fighter again and said, \"Speaking of the other one, does anyone know his name?\"","\"I heard he is called Rakan Thorne,\" a woman in blue said. \"A body-refining monster from the War God Palace. Some people say he has been recognized by one of the War God’s battle marks, and others say he is one step away from becoming the true inheritor.\"","\"Rakan Thorne,\" the scarred man repeated with admiration. \"That name suits him. Look at him. He fights like every bone in his body was forged for war.\"","\"You guys aren’t updated on the news, I guess,\" just then another one added. \"There are five warlords in the War God Palace, and the names and figures of the four warlords are in public, and everyone knows them, but the fifth and the last warlord has never been revealed so far.\"","He added. \"If I have to guess, then this Rakan Thorne is the fifth and the final warlord of the War God Palace.\"","Hearing him, everyone was shocked. Warlords of the War God Palace were very famous figures in the Divine Realm, but the fifth warlord had always been a mysterious figure since nobody knew much about that person.","And now that they heard that the one battling Damien Voss was actually the fifth warlord, it shocked the crowd a bit too much.","Another clash erupted in the sky.","Damian Voss spun in midair, and thousands of sword shadows appeared around him. Each shadow carried a sharp sword intent, and for a moment, the entire sky looked like it had been filled with falling blades.","Rakan Thorne raised both fists and roared, his war aura turning into the faint image of a giant battlefield behind him. He punched forward again and again, smashing sword shadow after sword shadow until the entire sky exploded with shattered light.","The tower crowd shouted in excitement.","\"Damian is getting serious.\"","\"No, Rakan is still holding back. Did you not see how stable his stance is?\"","\"You are blind. Damian’s sword intent has not fully erupted yet.\"","\"And you are deaf if you cannot feel Rakan’s war aura shaking the air.\"","Their arguments grew louder, but there was no true hostility in them. Everyone was too thrilled by the battle to care about being polite. To them, this was a rare chance to watch two peak geniuses clash without risking their own lives, and with the first round only seven eliminations away from ending, scenes like this might soon become impossible to witness.","Max listened quietly.","Damian Voss of Sword God Palace.","Rakan Thorne of War God Palace.","One fought with a sword sharp enough to tear through the sky. The other fought barehanded with power worthy of the War God’s name. Both were strong enough to stand near the peak of the remaining participants, and from the way the crowd spoke, both seemed tied to the two great legacies Rosaline had mentioned earlier.","Max’s gaze moved toward Damian’s sword.","A faint interest appeared in his eyes.","\"If he is truly connected to the Sword God Legacy,\" Max muttered softly, \"then he may know something useful.\"","At that moment, another participant near him turned and casually said, \"Brother, you just arrived, right? You picked a good time. These two have been fighting for a while, and neither side has gained a true advantage yet.\"","Max looked at him.","The participant smiled excitedly and continued, \"Everyone is betting on who will win. Most are choosing Damian because Sword God Palace’s reputation is too strong, but I think Rakan might surprise us. That guy’s body is absurd. He has taken so many sword strikes and still looks completely fine.\"","Max glanced at the sky again. \"Are they fighting for a reason?\""]},{"number":1813,"title":"Chapter 1813: Meeting Rose again!","paragraphs":["The participant shrugged. \"From what I heard, they found a temporary legacy mark nearby. Damian wanted it because it was connected to sword intent, but Rakan said any mark appearing near a battlefield belongs to the one strong enough to take it. They argued, then they fought.\"","Max nodded slightly.","The reason was simple enough.","In the Cosmic Ascension Conference, many battles did not need deep hatred. Sometimes, one treasure, one opportunity, one mark, or even one sentence was enough.","The participant then lowered his voice and added, \"But honestly, I think everyone here is waiting for something else.\"","Max looked at him. \"What?\"","The participant smiled. \"For one of them to win and get weakened. If Damian or Rakan suffers serious injuries, some people here might not be able to control their greed.\"","Max glanced around the tower.","The spectators still looked relaxed, but after hearing that sentence, he noticed the hidden tension beneath their excitement. Several people were not merely watching. They were measuring.","Some watched Damian’s breathing. Some watched Rakan’s injuries. Some watched the battlefield below to see where the legacy mark might be hidden. The crowd looked casual, but many of them were waiting for an opportunity to strike.","Max smiled faintly.","So this tower was not only a viewing stage.","It was also a gathering place for vultures.","The battle in the sky continued to intensify.","Damian’s sword intent grew sharper.","Rakan’s war aura became heavier.","The crowd’s excitement rose with every clash.","And Max stood among them quietly, watching the two possible inheritors of the Sword God and War God legacies collide beneath the approaching end of the first round.","Just as Max was watching Damian Voss and Rakan Thorne clash in the distant sky, someone suddenly called out to him from behind.","\"Is that you, Max?\"","Max turned his head and looked behind him.","A woman was standing a short distance away, staring at him with surprise and uncertainty. She looked somewhat different from the last time he had seen her. Her aura was sharper, her clothes were slightly damaged, and there were faint signs of battle on her body, but Max recognized her almost immediately.","\"Rose?\" Max asked, clearly surprised.","It was Rose, Lucia’s friend from Orion, the same woman who had guided them when they first arrived there.","\"It is really you!\" Rose smiled and came closer, her eyes brightening with recognition. \"Your white hair and your back were too familiar to me, so I had to ask. I thought I might be mistaken at first, but it really is you.\"","Max looked at her for a moment, then smiled faintly.","\"I am surprised you survived this far into the first round,\" he said. \"If I am not wrong, Lucia and the other geniuses from the Black Dragon Clan should have all been eliminated by now.\"","Rose did not look offended. Instead, she smiled with a bit of helplessness.","\"That is true. Most of them were eliminated quite early, and Lucia lasted longer than some of them, but she still could not remain until this stage. As for me, I did not survive because I was stronger than them. I survived because I avoided most of the monsters and chose my fights carefully.\"","Max nodded slightly.","That made sense. In a place like the Cosmic Ascension Conference, raw strength was important, but survival instincts were just as necessary. Someone who knew when to fight, when to retreat, and when to hide could sometimes last longer than someone stronger but more arrogant.","Rose looked at Max deeply.","\"You are surprising as well,\" she said. \"When you told me last time that you would shine in the Cosmic Ascension Conference, I did not think much about it. I thought you were confident, maybe a little reckless, but I never expected this.\"","Max raised an eyebrow. \"This?\"","Rose smiled and pointed toward the crowd around them.","\"Your name is everywhere now. Max Morgan, the one carrying Dragonheart. Max Morgan, the one who killed Sword God Palace disciples. Max Morgan, the one who defeated Selene Vaeloria and cut down Morgana Starveil. Some people even say you are already standing on the same level as Damian Voss and Rakan Thorne.\"","Max glanced toward the distant battle again.","Damian’s sword light and Rakan’s war aura collided once more, and the tower shook faintly under the spreading shockwave.","Then Max smiled and shrugged.","\"I told you I would make a name for myself.\"","Rose looked at him for a moment, then shook her head with a faint laugh.","\"You really did.\"","Max’s gaze returned to her.","\"How about now?\" he asked. \"Are you willing to join my force?\"","Rose’s smile slowly faded, and her expression became much more solemn.","\"That will depend on whether you can help me with something.\"","Max was not surprised by the answer.","Rose had never seemed like someone without secrets. Even back on Orion, he had already felt that her situation was not simple. She carried herself like someone who had seen the Divine Realm, understood its forces, and yet chose to live on a dangerous planet where death could arrive any night. That was not normal.","\"Sure,\" Max said with a nod. \"After the tournament ends, I will find you.\"","Rose looked at him seriously. \"You are not even going to ask what it is?\"","Max smiled faintly. \"You would not mention it here if it was something simple.\"","Rose was silent for a moment before a small smile returned to her face.","\"That is true.\"","Max looked back at the battlefield, but his mind briefly moved to what he knew about Rose. From what he remembered, her family was as strong as the first-rate forces in the Divine Realm.","Someone with that kind of background should have been living in a sacred land, protected by powerful experts, surrounded by resources that ordinary geniuses could only dream of. Yet Rose had chosen to stay on Orion, a planet where one could not even guarantee if they would wake up alive after night fell.","That contradiction had always been strange.","Now that she had asked for help, Max was even more certain that there was a deeper reason behind it.","’Just what happened to make her live on Orion instead of staying with her own family?’ Max wondered.","Rose noticed his silence and seemed to understand part of what he was thinking.","\"My situation is complicated,\" she said softly.","Max nodded. \"Most worthwhile things are.\"","Rose looked at him, then smiled faintly. \"You really have changed, Max.\"","\"No,\" Max said calmly. \"I just stopped hiding how far I intend to go.\"","Rose was about to reply, but another deafening explosion erupted in the distance.","Everyone on the tower turned their attention back to the sky.","Damian Voss had finally released a much stronger sword intent. His sword light gathered into a massive silver-white sword image behind him, and the sky itself seemed to be split by its edge.","Opposite him, Rakan Thorne’s war aura surged like a burning battlefield, and a golden-red giant formed behind his body, raising both fists as if preparing to crush the heavens.","The crowd became even louder.","\"They are going all out now!\"","\"This might decide the battle.\"","\"Damian’s Sword God inheritance is showing itself.\"","\"Rakan’s war intent is not weaker. Look at that battle avatar.\""]},{"number":1814,"title":"Chapter 1814: A Challenge from Damien Voss","paragraphs":["Rose watched the scene with a serious expression.","\"These two are terrifying,\" she said.","Max looked at the battle calmly.","\"They are strong.\"","Rose glanced at him. \"Only strong?\"","Max smiled but did not answer.","Rose looked at his expression and immediately understood. To everyone else on the tower, Damian Voss and Rakan Thorne were monsters standing near the peak of the remaining participants.","But Max was not looking at them with fear or worship. He was measuring them, the same way they were measuring each other.","That realization made Rose’s gaze deepen.","The Max she had met on Orion had been confident.","The Max standing beside her now was different.","He had become someone who could stand among the strongest geniuses of the Divine Realm and still think about how to surpass them.","The battle in the sky reached another peak.","Damian’s sword descended.","Rakan’s fists rose.","The tower’s protective formation trembled violently.","The crowd held its breath.","Max stood beside Rose with calm eyes, watching the clash unfold while the first round of the Cosmic Ascension Conference drew closer and closer to its end.","The clash between Damian Voss and Rakan Thorne reached its peak.","Damian’s silver-white sword image descended from above, carrying a sharpness that seemed capable of cutting the sky itself into two clean halves. Rakan’s golden-red war avatar raised both fists and punched upward with a roar that shook the entire floating platform beneath the tower. Sword light and war aura collided in midair, and for a moment, the world seemed to lose all sound as the two forces pressed against each other, neither side willing to retreat.","Then the explosion came.","A terrifying shockwave spread across the sky in all directions, forcing the clouds apart and making the protective formation around the tower flare with dazzling light. Many of the spectators instinctively stepped back, while a few weaker ones almost lost their balance.","The tower groaned under the pressure, and countless cracks appeared on the nearby floating stones, but the formation barely managed to hold.","When the light finally faded, Damian and Rakan were standing several hundred meters apart in the sky.","Damian’s robe was slightly torn at the sleeve, and there was a faint bruise near his shoulder, but his sword remained steady in his hand. Rakan’s fists were covered in shallow sword marks, and a thin line of blood flowed down his arm, but his war aura had not weakened much either.","The two stared at each other in silence for a few breaths, and everyone on the tower held their breath, waiting to see who would attack first.","Rakan suddenly laughed.","\"Good sword.\"","Damian’s expression remained calm. \"Your fists are not bad either.\"","Rakan cracked his neck and lowered his hands slightly. \"If we continue, neither of us will be able to take the other down before the first round ends. Even if one of us wins, the people watching from that tower will become very courageous all of a sudden.\"","Several spectators on the tower stiffened when they heard that.","Damian glanced toward the tower faintly. \"True.\"","Rakan grinned. \"Then let us call it a draw for now. Next time, we fight without an audience waiting to pick up scraps.\"","Damian did not object.","The crowd on the tower immediately erupted.","\"A draw!\"","\"They actually stopped.\"","\"That makes sense. Both of them are too strong. If they fought to the end, even the winner would have to pay a heavy price.\"","\"Damian Voss really deserves to be the Sword God Palace’s strongest inheritor.\"","\"And Rakan Thorne is definitely the fifth warlord. There is no doubt about it now.\"","The spectators were still arguing excitedly when Damian suddenly turned his gaze away from Rakan.","His eyes moved toward the tower.","At first, many people thought he was looking at the crowd in general, and quite a few of them became nervous. Even though they had been hyping up the battle from a safe distance, none of them wanted Damian Voss to truly pay attention to them. But very soon, they realized that Damian was not looking at everyone.","He was looking at one person.","Max.","The noise around the tower slowly faded.","One by one, the spectators followed Damian’s gaze and turned toward the white-haired young man standing near Rose.","Rose’s expression changed slightly.","The participant who had spoken to Max earlier froze in place, then slowly widened his eyes as realization struck him.","\"Wait...\" he muttered. \"White hair...\"","Another person swallowed hard. \"That is Max Morgan?\"","The words spread through the tower like a spark falling into dry grass.","\"Max Morgan is here?\"","\"He was standing with us the whole time?\"","\"Damn it, I was talking about him earlier.\"","\"Then Damian Voss is looking at him because of Dragonheart.\"","Rose glanced at Max, but Max’s expression remained calm, as if being discovered by everyone did not matter to him at all.","High in the sky, Damian slowly raised his sword and pointed it toward Max.","\"Max Morgan.\"","His voice was not loud, but it carried clearly across the distance.","The entire tower became silent.","Damian looked at Max with sharp interest. \"I heard you have the Sword of the Sovereign.\"","The crowd immediately became even more tense.","Some looked at Damian. Some looked at Max. Some quietly stepped farther away from Max as if afraid that standing too close to him would drag them into whatever was about to happen.","Max looked at Damian from the tower and smiled faintly taking out the Dragonheart. \"I do.\"","Damian’s eyes moved toward Dragonheart.","For a moment, a trace of desire appeared in his gaze, but it was quickly suppressed by battle intent. He did not look like someone who wanted to snatch the sword through shameless means. Instead, he looked like a swordsman who had finally found something worthy of drawing his blade.","\"Since you have the Sword of the Sovereign,\" Damian said calmly, \"how about you exchange some moves with me?\"","The tower exploded with shocked voices.","\"He is challenging Max Morgan!\"","\"Damian just finished fighting Rakan, and now he wants to fight Max?\"","\"This is insane. The first round is almost over, and we are getting Damian Voss against Max Morgan?\"","\"Move back. Move back quickly. If they really fight near the tower, the formation might not survive.\"","Rose looked at Max with a serious expression. \"Are you going?\"","Max glanced at her and smiled.","\"Of course.\"","Rose frowned slightly. \"Damian Voss is not simple.\"","\"I know,\" Max said calmly.","Then he looked back at Damian.","His smile became a little sharper.","\"I was also curious about the Sword God Palace’s strongest genius.\"","The moment those words fell, Max stepped forward and rose from the tower.","He did not release an overwhelming aura immediately. He did not summon divine lightning or reveal dragon scales. He simply flew out calmly, white hair moving with the wind, Dragonheart resting at his side. Yet the moment he left the tower, every spectator unconsciously held their breath.","The atmosphere had changed.","Earlier, they had watched Damian and Rakan clash like two peak monsters fighting above the sky. But now, another monster had entered the battlefield.","Rakan Thorne, who had already moved aside, looked at Max with bright eyes and grinned.","\"So this is Max Morgan.\"","Damian’s gaze remained fixed on Max as he approached.","Max stopped in the air across from him, leaving a wide distance between them.","For a brief moment, neither of them spoke.","Then Damian slowly lifted his sword.","Max raised Dragonheart.","The crowd on the tower went completely silent.","The draw between the Sword God Palace’s strongest inheritor and the War God Palace’s fifth warlord had barely ended, and now another battle was about to begin.","Damian Voss against Max Morgan.","Sword God Palace’s genius against the wielder of the Sword of the Sovereign.","And everyone present understood that they might be about to witness something even more terrifying than the battle they had just seen."]},{"number":1815,"title":"Chapter 1815: Damian Vs Max","paragraphs":["\"Come,\" Max said, holding Dragonheart with both hands.","He was also curious about Damian Voss. Since Damian was the strongest genius of Sword God Palace and someone deeply connected to the Sword God Legacy, Max wanted to see what kind of sword path he was following.","However, Max did not release Emotion Severing Path. He did not summon Divine King Punishment, activate his dragon scales, or use any overwhelming bloodline pressure. He simply held Dragonheart like a swordsman and waited.","Damian noticed this and smiled faintly.","\"So you want to exchange pure sword moves first?\"","Max smiled back. \"Is that not what you asked for?\"","Damian’s eyes became sharper. \"Good.\"","The next instant, Damian moved.","His figure disappeared from where he stood, and a silver-white sword arc appeared in front of Max’s chest. The slash was fast, clean, and extremely precise. It carried no Pseudo Cosmic Path, no grand sword image, and no overwhelming force, but the technique itself was flawless enough to make many swordsmen on the tower feel their scalps go numb.","Max raised Dragonheart and blocked.","Clang!","The sound of metal rang across the sky.","Damian’s sword slid along Dragonheart’s edge, changed direction midway, and slashed toward Max’s wrist. Max turned his hand, lowered the tip of Dragonheart, and used the flat of his sword to redirect the attack. Damian stepped closer at once, his sword suddenly transforming into three afterimages that struck toward Max’s throat, chest, and waist from three different angles.","Max’s eyes remained calm.","He stepped back half a pace, turned his body sideways, and swept Dragonheart in a clean circular motion. The three sword afterimages shattered at the same time, and before Damian could press forward again, Max’s sword had already thrust toward his shoulder.","Damian’s eyes flickered.","He blocked the thrust, twisted his wrist, and forced Max’s blade aside before countering with a downward slash.","Clang! Clang! Clang!","In just a few breaths, the two exchanged more than thirty sword moves.","There were no massive explosions. There were no divine lights. There were no terrifying cosmic path manifestations. Yet every exchange made the spectators on the tower more shocked than the last.","The battle was not loud, but it was dangerous. Each sword move was aimed at a vital opening. Each defense was timed perfectly. Each counterattack appeared exactly where the opponent’s next move should have been weakest.","The crowd slowly fell silent.","Someone swallowed hard. \"He is actually keeping up with Damian Voss in pure sword moves?\"","Another person muttered, \"Damian is from Sword God Palace. Even without using his full power, his sword foundation should be terrifying. How is Max Morgan not losing?\"","\"He is not only not losing,\" a woman said with wide eyes. \"He is countering all of Damien’s moves.\"","That sentence made the crowd even more shocked.","In the distance, Rakan Thorne folded his arms and watched with a grin, but the careless smile on his face slowly became more serious. \"Interesting. I thought that sword was only strong because of its grade and his strange path, but his sword skill itself is not weak at all.\"","Near another floating ruin, Princess Rosaline stood with several people from the Lunarian Kingdom. Her golden-pink hair moved slightly in the wind as she watched Max and Damian exchange sword moves.","Her beautiful eyes revealed clear surprise. \"He can really exchange sword techniques with Damian Voss without falling behind. It seems I still underestimated him.\"","One of the Lunarian Kingdom geniuses beside her said in disbelief, \"Princess, Damian Voss is the strongest swordsman of Sword God Palace’s younger generation. Even if he is not using his true sword path, his basic swordsmanship should already be at the peak among us.\"","Rosaline nodded slightly. \"That is exactly why this is surprising.\"","Farther away, Orion Starfall stood above a broken stone pillar with his arms crossed. His nine star marks flickered faintly as he watched the battle. At first, he had only been observing casually, but after seeing Max block Damian’s seventh consecutive sword-chain without losing position, his eyes sharpened.","\"Interesting,\" Orion said softly. \"His sword foundation is also this stable.\"","Near the shadow of a cracked mountain, Kaiden Voidmere watched in silence, his silver-gray eyes calm and deep. He had already sensed the Void Genesis Art in Max before, but now he was seeing another side of him.","Max’s sword was not as refined as Damian’s in some areas, but his adaptability was frightening. Every time Damian changed rhythm, Max adjusted almost instantly.","Back in the sky, Damian’s sword suddenly became faster.","His blade moved like flowing silver water, sometimes soft, sometimes sharp, sometimes direct, and sometimes impossible to predict.","One moment, his sword seemed to be retreating. The next moment, it was already aimed at Max’s heart. He did not use any Pseudo Cosmic Path, but the rhythm of his sword alone carried an oppressive feeling, as though every movement had been polished through countless battles and teachings.","Max did not panic.","His Dimensional Sovereign Body helped him sense every change around him, but he did not rely on it completely. He forced himself to respond with swordsmanship.","Dragonheart moved in his hands, blocking, cutting, redirecting, and countering. Some of Damian’s moves were cleaner than his. Some of Damian’s angles were more refined. But Max’s sword carried something Damian had not expected.","Growth.","Each exchange made Max adapt faster.","At first, Damian’s sword forced Max to defend more than attack. After fifty moves, Max began countering once every few exchanges. After a hundred moves, he was able to interrupt Damian’s sword rhythm. After nearly two hundred moves, his sword had already adjusted to Damian’s style enough to create danger in return.","Clang!","Their swords locked in midair.","Damian looked at Max from across the crossed blades, and for the first time, his calm expression showed clear surprise.","\"You are learning my sword rhythm while fighting me.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"You noticed?\"","Damian’s eyes became even sharper. \"Of course I noticed.\"","Max pushed forward, and the two separated at the same time.","The crowd on the tower had already become completely quiet.","Even those who had been waiting to take advantage of a weakened genius no longer dared to think recklessly. This was not a battle they could interfere in. Damian Voss had just fought Rakan Thorne to a draw, and now Max Morgan was exchanging sword moves with him without losing. That alone was enough to place Max’s name at the same height as the top monsters of the first round.","Damian suddenly stepped forward again.","This time, his sword descended in a simple straight slash.","Max raised Dragonheart and met it directly.","Clang!","The two swords collided, and both fighters stopped in place.","No one moved for a breath.","Then Damian withdrew his sword first.","\"That is enough for pure sword moves,\" he said calmly.","Max lowered Dragonheart slightly. \"Done already?\"","Damian looked at him with a faint smile. \"If we continue like this, it will no longer remain an exchange. I will start wanting to use my real sword path.\"","Max smiled. \"I was waiting to see it.\"","The spectators immediately became tense again."]},{"number":1816,"title":"Chapter 1816: End of the First Round!","paragraphs":["Damian’s gaze deepened, but he did not attack immediately. Instead, he looked at Dragonheart in Max’s hand, then back at Max himself.","\"You are qualified to hold that sword,\" he said.","The words shocked many people even more than the battle itself.","For someone from Sword God Palace to say that Max was qualified to hold the Sword of the Sovereign meant that Damian had acknowledged his swordsmanship, at least to a certain extent. It did not mean the Sword God Palace would give up on Dragonheart, but it did mean Damian no longer saw Max as someone who had merely gotten lucky.","Max smiled faintly. \"That is good to hear.\"","Damian’s expression remained calm. \"But qualification and ownership are two different things.\"","Max’s smile became sharper. \"Then come and take it.\"","The sky became still.","Rakan laughed loudly in the distance. \"Good! Now this is getting interesting.\"","The pure sword exchange had ended.","But everyone could feel that the real battle had only just begun.","\"Remember, it was you who asked for it!\" Damian smiled coldly.","The moment his words fell, the sword in his hand began to release a terrifying sword intent in all directions. This was completely different from the pure sword exchange they had just finished.","The previous exchange had been sharp, clean, and restrained, but now Damian’s aura was rising without any intention of hiding itself. Silver-white sword light spread behind him like a rising tide, and the sky above the tower began to tremble as if countless invisible blades were being drawn at the same time.","The expressions of the spectators on the tower changed instantly.","\"He is really going to use his sword concept.\"","\"No, this is beyond ordinary sword concept. Damian Voss is about to reveal his Pseudo Cosmic Path.\"","\"Move back. If these two really clash with their true paths, the tower formation will not hold.\"","Rose’s expression became tense as she looked at Max, but Max only smiled faintly. Dragonheart rested in his hand, and the space around him slowly became quiet. He did not release Emotion Severing Path fully, but that silent and cold aura had already begun to gather around his blade, waiting for the moment Damian’s true sword path descended.","Damian’s eyes were sharp.","Max’s gaze was calm.","The crowd held their breath.","Rakan Thorne, who had been watching from a distance, grinned with interest, while Rosaline’s eyes brightened slightly. Orion Starfall, Ervin, and Kaiden Voidmere also focused their attention on the two swordsmen, because everyone could sense that the next clash would no longer be a simple exchange of sword moves.","Damian Voss was about to reveal the sword path that made him the strongest genius of Sword God Palace’s younger generation, and Max Morgan was clearly ready to answer with his own terrifying path.","Damian slowly raised his sword.","The silver-white sword intent around him gathered toward the blade, and a faint, ancient aura began to awaken from within it. It was as if a forgotten sword law was about to descend upon the battlefield, and even before it fully appeared, the surrounding space was already covered in countless thin sword marks.","Max tightened his grip on Dragonheart.","Then, just as Damian was about to fully reveal his Pseudo Cosmic Path, a system notification suddenly appeared in front of every remaining participant.","[Cosmic Ascension Conference: First Round Concluded.]","[Remaining Participants: 100]","[All Qualified Participants Will Now Be Transferred To The Second Round.]","For a moment, the entire world became silent.","Damian’s sword intent froze before it could fully erupt.","Max’s Emotion Severing aura also paused around Dragonheart.","The spectators on the tower stared at the notification in shock, and before anyone could react properly, brilliant beams of light descended from the sky one after another. Each beam locked onto one participant. The tower, the battlefield, the floating ruins, and the distant plains were all covered by the same light.","\"The first round ended?\"","\"It really reached one hundred participants.\"","\"Damn it, right before Damian and Max were about to fight.\"","\"This timing is too cruel.\"","Rakan Thorne burst into loud laughter as a beam of light descended on him. \"Looks like that fight has been saved for the real stage.\"","Rosaline looked toward Max from afar, her expression filled with interest. \"So the second round begins now.\"","Orion Starfall smiled faintly as starlight wrapped around him. \"Perfect timing. The main stage is finally here.\"","Damian Voss remained opposite him, his sword still raised. The Pseudo Cosmic Path he had been about to reveal was forcefully suppressed by the transfer light, and his expression carried a faint trace of dissatisfaction. He looked at Max with sharp eyes and slowly lowered his sword.","\"It seems our battle will have to wait.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"The second round should be a better place for it.\"","Damian’s gaze moved to Dragonheart, then back to Max.","\"In the second round, I will see whether you are truly worthy of holding the Sword of the Sovereign.\"","Max replied calmly, \"Then come and test it.\"","The transfer light grew brighter.","The entire battlefield began to blur.","The tower disappeared.","The sky disappeared.","The distant ruins, the floating platform, the watching crowd, and the battlefield where Damian and Rakan had fought all faded into white light. One by one, the remaining hundred participants vanished from the first-round world.","Max felt the space around him collapse and rebuild.","The last thing he saw before disappearing was Damian’s sharp gaze across the light.","Then everything turned white.","[Transfer Complete.]","[Second Round Initiation In Progress.]","The first round of the Cosmic Ascension Conference had officially ended.","****","The white light around Max did not disappear immediately.","For a brief moment, he felt as if his body was being carried through countless layers of space inside the Eternal Hourglass.","The transfer was smooth, far smoother than the sudden relocations of the first round, and it gave off a completely different feeling. The first round had scattered everyone across a vast and dangerous world where survival, hunting, ambushes, and opportunities were all mixed together in chaos.","But this time, the transfer felt orderly. Deliberate. As if the Cosmic Ascension Conference itself was now gathering the final hundred participants onto a true stage worthy of deciding who among them stood above the rest.","Then the light shattered.","Max opened his eyes and saw that he was no longer in the ruined battlefield near the tower."]},{"number":1817,"title":"Chapter 1817: The Second Round","paragraphs":["He had arrived in a colossal arena.","Even for someone who had already seen many shocking places inside the Eternal Hourglass, Max could not help but narrow his eyes slightly at the sight before him. This was not an ordinary fighting ground.","It was an enormous circular battle stage suspended in the middle of a vast dark space within the Eternal Hourglass. Above it, one could see countless rivers of time-light flowing like upside-down galaxies, crossing each other high in the black void.","Some were golden, some silver, some crimson, and some deep blue, and together they formed a breathtaking canopy that made the entire place feel ancient, mysterious, and absolute. It was as though the Eternal Hourglass had carved out a sacred dueling world for the final hundred.","At the center of that space was the main stage.","The stage itself was unbelievably huge, large enough to contain a city, yet its design was simple and imposing. It was a perfectly circular arena made of dark gold stone mixed with strange silver-white crystal veins.","Ancient runes were engraved across every inch of its surface, and those runes gave off a heavy aura of law, time, and battle. The entire stage was surrounded by a transparent barrier of light that rose like an invisible dome into the sky, clearly meant to contain the force of the one-on-one battles that would soon take place there.","Despite the sheer size of the stage, there was no unnecessary decoration upon it. It was clean, vast, and solemn, like a place built for the strongest geniuses to decide victory and defeat with no room for excuses.","But what truly made the scene shocking was what surrounded the stage.","Around the enormous circular battlefield stood one hundred giant pillars.","Each pillar was positioned in a wide ring around the stage, suspended in the air at equal distance from one another, forming a majestic circle that enclosed the entire arena. These pillars were towering and ancient, each one at least hundreds of meters high, with broad flat tops large enough for a person to stand on comfortably.","Their surfaces were covered with glowing symbols and strange flowing patterns that seemed to record the identities, rankings, and auras of the participants standing upon them. From a distance, the one hundred pillars looked like the seats of one hundred kings arranged around a sacred battlefield.","And on those pillars, one after another, figures began to appear.","Beams of light descended upon the tops of the pillars, and the final hundred participants of the first round were transferred there.","Max found himself standing atop one of those pillars.","He looked around calmly.","On the neighboring pillars, one could already see figures becoming clear within the fading transfer light. Some stood with their arms crossed, some looked around in surprise, some released their auras unconsciously before restraining them again, and some remained completely calm as if they had already expected such a scene.","Damian Voss was there. Rakan Thorne was there. Orion Starfall, Kaiden Voidmere, Ervin, Princess Rosaline, and many others were also among them. Even from a glance, Max could tell that everyone who had survived until now was extraordinary.","The weak had long since been filtered out in the first round. What remained here were the true monsters of the younger generation.","Soon all one hundred pillars were occupied.","The scene became extremely imposing.","One hundred peak geniuses stood on one hundred towering pillars, forming a complete circle around the central battle stage. The atmosphere was heavy, but not chaotic. Unlike the first round, there was no wilderness, no hidden attacks from beasts, no ambushes in ruins, and no endless territories to cross.","Everything had become straightforward now. The final round would no longer test survival in a chaotic world. It would test direct strength.","A low humming sound spread through the arena.","The runes on the main stage lit up one after another, and the one hundred pillars also began to shine. Then, in the empty air above the central battlefield, a massive projection of light appeared. It was a grand panel formed entirely from law and spiritual energy, and the names of all one hundred participants began to appear upon it in flowing golden text.","At the same time, a voice echoed throughout the arena.","It was ancient, emotionless, and majestic, as though it did not come from a person but from the Eternal Hourglass itself.","[Welcome To The Final Round Of The Cosmic Ascension Conference.]","The moment those words rang out, the expressions of all one hundred participants became more focused.","The voice continued.","[The First Round Tested Survival, Opportunity, Adaptability, And Fortune.]","[The Second Round Will Test True Strength.]","[This Round Will Be Conducted Through One-On-One Battles.]","The giant stage beneath them gave off an even heavier aura as the voice spoke.","[The Central Stage Is The Final Battle Arena.]","[The One Hundred Pillars Are The Seats Of The Final Hundred Participants.]","[Each Participant Will Remain Upon Their Assigned Pillar Until Called To Battle.]","The one hundred pillars continued to shine around the colossal central stage, and the atmosphere inside the arena grew heavier with every passing breath.","No one spoke loudly anymore.","Even the more arrogant participants had become quiet after hearing that the final round would be conducted through direct one-on-one battles. The first round had been chaotic and uncertain, but this place was different.","Here, there would be nowhere to hide, nowhere to run, and no endless wilderness to rely on. Once your name was called, you would step onto the central stage and prove your worth with your own strength.","Just then, the space above the arena rippled.","It was not a violent distortion, nor was it the kind of arrival that released overwhelming pressure from the very beginning. Instead, it was elegant, silent, and strangely noble. The air above the central battlefield folded open like a curtain of light, and from within that light, a woman slowly stepped out.","The moment she appeared, many participants instinctively looked up.","She was dressed in a long silver-white robe that seemed to be woven from moonlight itself, and faint golden patterns flowed across its edges like living symbols. Her hair was a pale golden color, soft and radiant, falling down her back like a stream of sacred light.","Her face was breathtakingly beautiful, but it was not a beauty that made people think of softness. It carried dignity, distance, and a quiet authority that made it difficult for others to look at her casually. Around her, the laws of the arena seemed to calm down on their own, as if even the Eternal Hourglass was acknowledging her presence.","Max narrowed his eyes slightly.","This woman was strong.","Not just strong in the ordinary sense, but the kind of strong that made the entire arena feel quieter the moment she arrived. Yet unlike the monstrous pressure of someone trying to suppress others, her presence felt controlled to an absurd degree. It was almost as if she stood there while perfectly containing an enormous world inside herself.","Many participants frowned.","They could feel that this woman was no ordinary host, but most of them did not recognize her at all.","However, a few people’s expressions changed at once.","Damian Voss’s eyes narrowed sharply.","Orion Starfall’s relaxed smile disappeared for the first time since entering the second round arena.","Kaiden Voidmere’s calm gaze grew much deeper.","Princess Rosaline straightened unconsciously.","They all recognized one thing at the same time.","This woman’s bearing, bloodline aura, and presence were not something a common first-rate force could nurture.","But even then, none of them spoke immediately."]},{"number":1818,"title":"Chapter 1818: Angelina Valerius","paragraphs":["The woman looked over the one hundred participants standing on the pillars. Her gaze was calm, and yet every participant felt as though they were being seen clearly.","Then she spoke.","Her voice was soft, elegant, and clear enough to spread across the entire arena without needing force.","\"Welcome to the final round of the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","The arena became completely silent.","The woman continued, \"My name is Angelina Valerius, and I will be the one conducting this final round.\"","For one brief moment, nothing happened.","Then, among the strongest geniuses with powerful backgrounds, expressions changed violently.","\"Valerius?\" Orion Starfall repeated under his breath, his eyes flashing with genuine shock.","Princess Rosaline’s pupils contracted. \"The Valerius Clan...\"","Damian Voss’s grip on his sword tightened slightly.","Kaiden’s silver-gray eyes grew colder and more focused.","Even a few other top geniuses who had remained quiet until now could no longer keep their expressions calm.","The surname alone was enough.","For the ordinary participants, the name Valerius meant nothing. At most, it sounded ancient and noble. But for those who came from forces with deep inheritance and ancient records, that name was a shock powerful enough to shake the heart.","Max noticed the reactions immediately.","He glanced toward Orion, Damian, Kaiden, and Rosaline, then back at Angelina. ’So they know who she is,’ he thought. ’Interesting.’","Around the arena, whispers began rising.","\"Why are Damian Voss and the others reacting like that?\"","\"Do they know her?\"","\"That surname... is it important?\"","Most participants were confused, but the few who understood stayed silent because the truth itself was too shocking to speak carelessly.","It was Rosaline who finally muttered in a low voice, \"One of the four hidden clans...\"","A nearby Lunarian genius heard her and went pale. \"The hidden clans? I thought they had disappeared long ago.\"","Rosaline did not answer.","Millions of years had passed since the four hidden clans had chosen to withdraw from the Divine Realm’s visible stage. Over time, even many first-rate forces had begun to believe that those clans had either perished, completely isolated themselves, or faded into nothing but legends.","Only the oldest records and the deepest inheritances still mentioned them from time to time, and even then, they were spoken of in uncertain terms.","Yet now, a direct descendant of one of those hidden clans was standing before them.","And not only had she appeared, she had appeared as the conductor of the final round.","The implications of that alone were enough to make people’s hearts tremble.","Angelina Valerius seemed to notice the subtle changes in expression among the crowd, but she did not comment on them. Her face remained calm as she continued.","\"You may now be wondering why I am here and why the final round is being conducted in this manner.\"","She turned slightly and gestured toward the massive central stage below.","\"The answer is simple. The first round was meant to remove the weak, the careless, the unlucky, and those who were not prepared to stand on the true stage of the Cosmic Ascension Conference. What remains here are the final hundred. This means all of you are qualified to compete for the true rankings of this conference.\"","Her gaze swept across the pillars.","\"But qualification is not enough.\"","The one hundred pillars gave off a low hum.","\"The final round exists to determine strength, consistency, adaptability, endurance, and the ability to stand above one’s peers in direct confrontation. Because of that, the final round will be divided into three main rounds.\"","The entire arena became even more attentive.","Angelina raised one hand, and a vast screen of light appeared in the sky above the arena. It displayed the number 100 first, then slowly separated into stages.","\"In the first main round,\" she said, \"the one hundred participants will be paired through the randomizer. Each battle will be a one-on-one fight on the central stage. The winner will advance. The loser will be eliminated.\"","The glowing number in the sky shifted.","\"After fifty battles, fifty participants will be eliminated, and fifty participants will remain.\"","A wave of pressure spread across the arena. The rules were simple, direct, and merciless.","Angelina continued, \"In the second main round, the remaining fifty participants will once again be paired through the randomizer. The same format will continue. One battle. One winner. One loser.\"","The glowing number changed again from 50 to 25.","\"After twenty-five battles, twenty-five participants will remain.\"","Many people’s expressions became heavier at those words.","The first two main rounds were straightforward elimination rounds. No matter how glorious or famous one might be, a single defeat would end everything. There would be no second life, no extra chance, and no excuse.","Then Angelina’s tone shifted slightly.","\"The third main round will be different.\"","The screen of light changed once more, and this time twenty-five names were represented by twenty-five points of light connected to one another in a complete web.","\"The remaining twenty-five participants will enter the final competitive stage. At that point, elimination through simple pairing will end. Instead, every remaining participant will fight all other remaining participants.\"","The arena stirred.","Max’s eyes sharpened.","Angelina said clearly, \"Each of the twenty-five remaining participants will fight twenty-four battles.\"","Now the crowd truly reacted.","\"Twenty-four battles each?\"","\"That means the final rankings will not be decided by one lucky pairing.\"","\"That is brutal.\"","Angelina nodded faintly, as if she had expected that reaction.","\"Yes. By that stage, random chance will no longer be allowed to decide too much. The strongest should prove it repeatedly. The most consistent should show it openly. And the champion should not be someone who won through a fortunate bracket.\"","Her voice remained calm, but each word carried great weight.","\"At the end of those twenty-four battles, the participant with the highest number of wins will become the champion of this generation’s Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","The entire arena became silent.","This structure was far harsher than many had expected.","The first two stages would mercilessly cut down the number of participants from one hundred to twenty-five. Then the final twenty-five would be forced into an exhausting, brutal sequence of twenty-four battles each, meaning that no one could become champion by relying on a single burst of strength alone. They would need endurance, adaptability, and a terrifyingly stable foundation.","Angelina looked at them calmly.","\"In case of equal wins, additional tiebreaker battles will be conducted between the tied participants until the rankings are resolved.\"","That sentence made the rules even more absolute.","There would be no uncertain champion.","No unclear first place.","Everything would be decided on the stage.","Angelina then added, \"You are allowed to surrender in a battle, but the moment surrender is accepted by the arena laws, the battle ends, and the result is final. Deliberately refusing to stop after the arena has judged a victor will be considered a violation of the conference rules.\"","She paused slightly.","\"Furthermore, the arena barriers will ensure that your battles do not spread beyond the central stage. The one hundred pillars will remain your observation seats whenever you are not actively fighting. While standing on your pillar, you may recover, observe, and prepare for the battles to come.\"","Max looked around at the one hundred pillars again.","So these pillars were not only for appearance. They were the resting and observation positions of the participants throughout the final round.","Angelina’s eyes moved across the crowd one last time.","\"Now, if there are no questions, the final round will begin shortly.\"","No one spoke.","Not because there were no questions, but because at that moment, most people were too focused on the reality of what lay ahead.","Damian Voss stood silently on his pillar, but his eyes carried a dangerous brightness. Orion Starfall’s smile had returned, but it was no longer casual. Rakan Thorne looked excited enough to fight immediately. Rosaline remained calm, though her expression had deepened. Kaiden stood as if nothing around him could disturb him, and Ervin’s gaze remained as unreadable as ever.","Max, meanwhile, looked at Angelina Valerius one more time.","He still did not know exactly what the Valerius name meant, but from the reactions of those around him, he could tell one thing clearly.","This woman’s appearance here was not ordinary.","And if even the conductor of the final round came from one of the four hidden clans, then the true depth of the Cosmic Ascension Conference was likely far greater than it had first seemed.","Then Angelina slowly raised her hand.","The giant randomizer above the arena began to spin.","And the true final round of the Cosmic Ascension Conference was about to begin."]},{"number":1819,"title":"Chapter 1819: First Round - 1","paragraphs":["The giant randomizer above the arena began to spin.","One hundred names appeared within the vast screen of light, each one glowing with a different intensity according to the participant’s aura, identity, and pillar mark. The names moved so quickly that most people could not follow them with their eyes. They circled, crossed, separated, and merged again like golden stars caught inside a heavenly wheel.","Angelina Valerius stood calmly above the central stage, her silver-white robe moving softly in the air. She raised one hand, and the randomizer slowed down slightly.","\"The first main round will now begin,\" she said clearly. \"There will be fifty battles in this round. Fifty participants will advance, and fifty participants will be eliminated.\"","The moment her voice fell, the atmosphere around the one hundred pillars changed.","Even the relaxed participants became serious.","This was no longer the chaotic first round where people could retreat, hide, ambush, or wait for better chances. Here, a name would be called, a person would appear on the stage, and the result would decide whether that person continued in the Cosmic Ascension Conference or left completely.","The randomizer stopped.","Two names shone brightly above the arena.","[Battle One]","[Calder Vayne vs Mirella Thorn]","Angelina glanced at the names and spoke calmly. \"Calder Vayne. Mirella Thorn. Enter the stage.\"","Two beams of light descended from separate pillars and wrapped around two participants.","One was a tall young man wearing black armor, holding a heavy axe covered in flame markings. The other was a green-haired woman holding a thin spear, her body surrounded by faint wind currents. Both appeared on opposite sides of the central stage, and the transparent barrier around the arena brightened at once.","[Battle One Begins.]","Calder Vayne acted first. He stomped forward, and flames rose from his axe as he swung it down with brute force. Mirella Thorn did not meet him head-on. She moved like a shadow carried by the wind, avoiding the axe by a narrow margin before thrusting her spear toward his shoulder.","Calder roared, turned his body, and let the spear scrape against his armor before countering with another heavy swing.","The battle was fierce but not shocking compared to the monsters everyone had seen before.","After nearly a hundred exchanges, Mirella finally found a gap in Calder’s defense. Her spear pierced through the joint of his armor and stopped at his throat before he could lift his axe again.","Angelina’s voice rang out.","[Winner: Mirella Thorn.]","[Calder Vayne Eliminated.]","A beam of light swallowed Calder before he could say anything, removing him from the stage. Mirella returned to her pillar, breathing heavily but smiling with relief. The first battle had ended, and the number of participants who could advance had already begun to shrink.","The randomizer spun again.","[Battle Two]","[Varun Eclipsar vs Thalia Mooncrest]","A young man covered in dark blue starlight appeared on the stage opposite a woman with moon-white hair and silver daggers. Their battle was much faster than the first. Varun used long-range eclipse spells, trying to force Thalia to keep her distance, but Thalia’s movement technique was strange. She stepped in and out of moonlight, closing the gap again and again until her dagger touched the center of Varun’s chest.","[Winner: Thalia Mooncrest.]","[Varun Eclipsar Eliminated.]","The second battle ended cleanly.","The randomizer spun again.","[Battle Three]","[Gorath Ironhide vs Elian Vale]","This time, the fight drew more attention.","Gorath was a massive beastman with bronze skin and a body like a mountain, while Elian Vale was a slender young man dressed in scholar-like white robes. At first glance, many people assumed Gorath would crush him quickly, but once the battle began, Elian revealed terrifying control over runic chains. Each time Gorath tried to charge, golden chains rose from the stage and slowed his movements.","Gorath endured three rounds of binding and finally tore through the runes with raw strength, but Elian had already prepared his final technique. A formation circle opened beneath Gorath’s feet, and countless chains wrapped around his limbs, neck, and waist at the same time.","Gorath struggled violently, but he could not break free before Elian’s palm stopped in front of his forehead.","[Winner: Elian Vale.]","[Gorath Ironhide Eliminated.]","On the pillars, many participants began whispering.","\"These battles are not weak.\"","\"Of course they are not weak. Everyone here survived until the final hundred.\"","\"But the randomizer is clearly avoiding the top monsters for now.\"","\"That is normal. If Damian Voss, Orion Starfall, Rakan Thorne, Kaiden Voidmere, Ervin, or Max Morgan meet each other in the first elimination stage, the final ranking will become strange. The real monsters should collide later.\"","Max stood on his pillar and listened quietly.","He had also noticed the pattern.","The randomizer did not seem completely ordinary. It called itself random, but there was likely some hidden rule preventing the most famous top-tier geniuses from encountering each other too early. That made sense. The Cosmic Ascension Conference wanted a proper final ranking, not a situation where several peak monsters eliminated each other before the final twenty-five even formed.","Angelina Valerius showed no reaction to the whispers.","The randomizer spun again.","The sixth battle came next.","[Battle Six]","[Toren Ashguard vs Bellara Sain]","This was a battle between a shield user and a healer-type combatant who used light-based restraints. Many people expected it to last a long time, and it did. Toren’s defense was extremely strong, and Bellara could not break it easily, but Bellara was clever. Instead of trying to destroy his shield, she used her light restraints to bind his feet, then his arms, then slowly forced him into a position where he could no longer move properly.","In the end, Toren surrendered with a helpless expression.","[Winner: Bellara Sain.]","[Toren Ashguard Eliminated.]","Rakan Thorne yawned from his pillar. \"These fights are not bad, but when are they going to call someone interesting?\"","Orion Starfall smiled from a nearby pillar. \"Be patient. The stage is warming up.\"","Damian Voss stood silently, eyes half-closed as if none of these battles interested him. Kaiden Voidmere watched calmly, while Ervin seemed to be studying every participant’s habits without showing much emotion. Princess Rosaline observed the flow of battles with a thoughtful expression, perhaps memorizing who might become troublesome in later rounds.","Rose stood on her own pillar in the distance. She had not been called yet, but her expression was serious. She knew she had survived the first round mostly through careful movement and good judgment. In a direct battle, luck would not help her as much."]},{"number":1820,"title":"Chapter 1820: First Round - 2","paragraphs":["The randomizer spun again.","[Battle Seven]","[Hector Marrow vs Yulina Starbloom]","Hector was a bone-armored warrior with a cruel fighting style, while Yulina used star-thread techniques that looked delicate but were extremely dangerous. Hector tried to overwhelm her with brutal attacks, but Yulina’s star threads gradually wrapped around his weapon, then his arms, then his body. The more he struggled, the tighter the threads became.","After a short but intense fight, Yulina’s star threads forced Hector’s knees to bend, and a shining thread stopped at his neck.","[Winner: Yulina Starbloom.]","[Hector Marrow Eliminated.]","The eighth battle was even faster.","[Battle Eight]","[Draven Hollow vs Mirael Sunveil]","Draven attempted to use illusion techniques, but Mirael’s sunfire burned through his false images almost immediately. Within twenty exchanges, he was forced off balance and defeated by a palm of golden flame.","[Winner: Mirael Sunveil.]","[Draven Hollow Eliminated.]","As battle after battle passed, the tension in the arena continued to build.","The top geniuses had not moved yet.","Damian Voss remained on his pillar.","Rakan Thorne remained on his pillar.","Orion Starfall, Kaiden Voidmere, Ervin, Rosaline, and several other frightening figures were still waiting. Even Max had not been called. That made many people even more nervous because each spin of the randomizer could drag any one of them onto the stage.","Then the randomizer spun for the ninth time.","The golden names moved faster than before.","Finally, two names stopped and enlarged above the stage.","[Battle Nine]","[Max Morgan vs Arvian Dreadspire]","The entire arena fell silent for a breath.","Then the whispers erupted.","\"Max Morgan.\"","\"It is his turn already.\"","\"Who is Arvian Dreadspire?\"","\"I have heard of him. He is from the Dreadspire Clan, a powerful demon-blooded family. He survived the first round by hunting smaller groups alone.\"","\"That is unlucky for him.\"","\"Do not say that too quickly. Anyone who reached the final hundred is not weak.\"","On his pillar, Max looked at the name calmly.","Arvian Dreadspire stood on another pillar across the arena. He was a tall young man with ash-gray skin, black horns, and dark red markings crawling across his neck. His aura was gloomy and heavy, and when he saw that his opponent was Max, his expression became extremely ugly for a moment before he forced himself to calm down.","Angelina Valerius looked toward both of them.","\"Max Morgan. Arvian Dreadspire. Enter the stage.\"","Two beams of light descended.","Max did not resist the transfer.","The next moment, he appeared on one side of the central arena, Dragonheart resting quietly at his waist. Opposite him, Arvian appeared with a long black spear in his hand. The barrier around the central stage lit up again, and the names above the arena glowed brightly.","[Battle Nine Begins.]","Arvian stared at Max with a solemn expression.","He knew Max’s reputation. Everyone here knew Max’s reputation by now. But surrendering without fighting was not something he could accept. He had survived the first round, reached the final hundred, and carried the pride of his clan. Even if he lost, he had to at least make a move.","Max looked at him calmly.","\"Are you going to surrender?\" he asked.","Arvian’s face twitched slightly.","\"Do not look down on me too much, Max Morgan.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"Then come.\"","On the pillars, everyone focused their attention on the stage.","Arvian Dreadspire tightened his grip around his long black spear.","He had already heard too many rumors about Max Morgan, and none of them were comforting. Some said Max had killed Selene Vaeloria. Some said he had forced Seraphine and Fin to end themselves. Some said he had cut down Morgana Starveil from Stellar Templar with one sword.","Some said he had exchanged sword moves with Damian Voss without losing. Arvian did not know which rumors were exaggerated and which were true, but standing opposite Max on the central stage, he understood one thing clearly. The white-haired young man before him did not look nervous at all.","That calmness made Arvian even more uneasy.","\"Do not think I will go down easily,\" Arvian said in a deep voice.","Max looked at him calmly. \"Then show me.\"","Arvian roared.","Dark red energy erupted from his body, and the markings on his neck spread across his face like burning cracks. He stomped forward, and the entire central stage trembled under his charge. His spear stabbed out like a black dragon, carrying a heavy demonic pressure that would have forced most opponents to retreat instantly.","Max did not move.","The spear arrived before him in an instant.","Only then did Max raise his hand.","He did not draw Dragonheart.","He simply stretched out two fingers and caught the spearhead between them.","The arena fell silent.","Arvian’s expression changed wildly. He pushed forward with both hands, but the spear did not move at all. It was as if the weapon had been nailed into the void by Max’s fingers. The dark red energy around the spear surged violently, but Max’s hand remained steady, and his expression did not change in the slightest.","\"What?\" Arvian muttered in disbelief.","Max looked at him. \"Too weak.\"","Before Arvian could react, Max twisted his fingers.","Crack!","The spearhead shattered.","Arvian’s eyes widened, but Max had already stepped forward. His movement was not flashy. It was not even particularly exaggerated. He simply crossed the distance between them in one step and struck Arvian’s chest with his palm.","Boom!","Arvian’s body flew backward like a broken meteor.","He crashed into the barrier at the edge of the arena, and the impact made the entire protective dome ripple violently. Blood sprayed from his mouth, and the dark red markings across his body dimmed at once. He tried to stand, but his knees buckled before he could stabilize himself.","Max remained where he was.","From beginning to end, he had not drawn Dragonheart.","The sight made many participants on the pillars fall completely silent.","Angelina Valerius glanced at Arvian for a moment, then announced calmly, \"Arvian Dreadspire is unable to continue.\"","[Winner: Max Morgan.]","[Arvian Dreadspire Eliminated.]","A beam of light descended and removed Arvian from the stage.","Max was transferred back to his pillar a moment later, his expression calm as if the battle had not even warmed him up. The participants who had been wondering whether his reputation was exaggerated could no longer say anything.","Even if Arvian was not one of the peak monsters, he had still survived until the final hundred. Yet against Max, he had not even been able to force Dragonheart out of its sheath."]},{"number":1821,"title":"Chapter 1821: First Round - 3","paragraphs":["Rakan Thorne laughed from his pillar. \"That was too fast. At least let the man show one more move.\"","Orion Starfall smiled faintly. \"He did show one move. It was just not enough.\"","Princess Rosaline’s eyes remained on Max. \"His physical strength is also terrifying. He defeated a demon-blooded spear user without using his sword, bloodline, or any visible path.\"","Kaiden Voidmere watched Max quietly and said nothing, but his gaze became deeper.","Ervin smiled faintly. \"He is hiding far more than the others realize.\"","Damian Voss opened his eyes from his pillar and looked at Max for a moment. His expression did not change much, but the sharpness in his gaze increased. He had already acknowledged Max’s swordsmanship earlier, but now he had seen that Max’s combat foundation was not limited to the sword. That made him even more difficult to measure.","Angelina raised her hand again.","The randomizer spun.","Several more battles passed after Max’s victory.","Some were fierce, some were brief, and some ended with surrender the moment the weaker participant realized the gap. The arena continued eliminating names one after another, and the number of qualified participants slowly moved toward fifty.","Then the randomizer stopped again.","[Battle Fourteen]","[Damian Voss vs Soren Blackwater]","The entire arena became alert at once.","Damian Voss finally stood from his pillar.","His opponent, Soren Blackwater, was a black-robed man with water-like shadows surrounding his body. He had survived the first round through assassination techniques and strange movement, and his aura was slippery and difficult to lock onto. However, the moment he saw that his opponent was Damian, his face became extremely solemn.","Two beams of light descended.","Damian appeared on the stage with his sword resting at his side.","Soren appeared opposite him and immediately spread his shadow-water aura across the ground. A dark mist covered his body, and in the next instant, he split into several afterimages, each one rushing toward Damian from a different direction.","Damian did not move.","His sword left its sheath by an inch.","A clean sword light flashed.","All the afterimages were cut apart at the same time.","Soren’s real body appeared behind Damian with a dagger aimed at his back, but before the dagger could land, Damian’s sword was already touching Soren’s throat.","No one saw when he had turned.","No one saw when the blade had fully left its sheath.","Soren froze.","Damian said calmly, \"You lose.\"","Angelina’s voice followed immediately.","[Winner: Damian Voss.]","[Soren Blackwater Eliminated.]","The crowd on the pillars became silent again.","Max watched calmly from his pillar. Damian had not used any Pseudo Cosmic Path. He had not even shown his real sword concept. Just one clean sword movement had ended the battle. His sword was simple, direct, and terrifyingly precise.","Compared to the flashy sword light many swordsmen preferred, Damian’s sword felt far more dangerous because every movement existed only to end the fight.","’His sword is extremely refined,’ Max thought while watching Damian return to his pillar. ’He does not waste a single movement.’","The randomizer continued.","[Battle Seventeen]","[Rakan Thorne vs Yelric Flamehorn]","Rakan’s opponent was a horned fire-attribute warrior with a massive flaming halberd. Yelric Flamehorn clearly knew he could not hold back against someone like Rakan, so the moment the battle began, he released all his flame power and charged forward with a roar.","Rakan grinned and walked toward him barehanded.","The flaming halberd descended.","Rakan punched it.","The weapon bent.","Yelric’s face changed, but Rakan’s second punch had already landed on his stomach. The fire around Yelric’s body exploded outward, then scattered completely as his body folded around Rakan’s fist. He flew backward, crashed into the arena floor, and rolled several dozen times before stopping.","Rakan shook his hand as if disappointed.","\"That is it?\"","Angelina’s voice rang out.","[Winner: Rakan Thorne.]","[Yelric Flamehorn Eliminated.]","Max observed Rakan quietly.","Rakan’s strength was straightforward but horrifying. He did not rely on tricks, but his raw body, war aura, and combat instincts were so overwhelming that ordinary geniuses could not even force him to defend. If Damian’s sword was refined to the extreme, then Rakan’s fists were the opposite. They were blunt, brutal, and absolute.","The next top genius to be called was Princess Rosaline.","[Battle Twenty-One]","[Rosaline Lunara vs Cressa Thornveil]","Rosaline appeared on the central stage with graceful calm, her white and rose-gold gown moving softly around her. Cressa Thornveil was a poison vine user who immediately tried to fill the arena with thorny roots and dark green mist. However, Rosaline only lifted one hand, and gentle golden-pink light spread outward like dawn touching the earth.","The poison mist dissolved.","The thorny vines withered.","Cressa tried to summon more, but Rosaline’s light had already formed a radiant cage around her.","The battle ended without Rosaline taking a single step.","[Winner: Rosaline Lunara.]","[Cressa Thornveil Eliminated.]","Several participants looked uneasy.","Max watched with interest. Rosaline’s power did not feel aggressive at first, but its suppression was extremely clean. It purified, restrained, and sealed at the same time. Against many opponents, she would not need to overpower them directly. She only needed to remove the foundation of their techniques and trap them afterward.","’Not bad,’ Max thought.","Soon after, Orion Starfall’s name appeared.","[Battle Twenty-Five]","[Orion Starfall vs Marek Ironstorm]","Orion entered the stage with the same warm smile on his face. His opponent, Marek Ironstorm, wielded a pair of heavy gauntlets and controlled storm-metal energy. Marek clearly did not want to lose without trying, so he attacked with full force as soon as Angelina announced the start.","Thunder roared.","Metallic storm clouds gathered above the stage.","Orion looked up and smiled. \"Nice weather.\"","Then one of the nine star marks on his body lit up.","A single star beam descended.","It pierced through the storm clouds, shattered Marek’s gauntlet aura, and stopped just in front of his forehead. The beam did not touch him, but the pressure alone forced Marek’s entire body to stiffen.","Marek stared at the light in front of his face and slowly raised his hands.","\"I surrender.\"","Angelina nodded.","[Winner: Orion Starfall.]","[Marek Ironstorm Eliminated.]","Rakan laughed from his pillar. \"You are still pretending to be harmless.\"","Orion returned to his pillar and smiled. \"I am harmless when people surrender quickly.\""]},{"number":1822,"title":"Chapter 1822: First Round - 4","paragraphs":["Max looked at him for a few breaths.","Orion had used only one star mark, and even that had not revealed much. But the precision, speed, and pressure of that single beam were enough to show why he was considered one of the strongest geniuses of the Nine Star Court. His strength was not only destructive. It was controlled.","Then came Kaiden Voidmere.","[Battle Twenty-Nine]","[Kaiden Voidmere vs Liora Sunshard]","Kaiden’s opponent was a woman with radiant sunfire wings. She did not underestimate him. The moment the battle began, she rose into the air and released dozens of golden fire feathers, each one carrying enough heat to burn through divine metal.","Kaiden stood still.","The fire feathers reached him.","Then they vanished.","There was no explosion. No impact. No clash.","They simply disappeared into faint ripples of void.","Liora’s expression changed, and she immediately tried to retreat, but the space behind her quietly folded. Kaiden appeared there as if he had never moved, one finger already touching the back of her neck.","\"You lose,\" he said calmly.","Liora’s face turned pale.","[Winner: Kaiden Voidmere.]","[Liora Sunshard Eliminated.]","Max narrowed his eyes slightly.","Kaiden’s use of void power was extremely clean. It was different from ordinary space manipulation. It felt deeper, quieter, and more absolute. Since Kaiden had already sensed the Void Genesis Art in him and called him junior brother in a roundabout way, Max had been paying closer attention to him.","Now, after seeing this battle, Max was even more certain that Kaiden was not simple.","’His void path is far ahead of mine,’ Max thought.","Not long after, Ervin’s name appeared.","[Battle Thirty-Two]","[Ervin vs Darius Stoneveil]","Darius Stoneveil was a defensive cultivator with an earthstone body. The moment he entered the stage, stone armor covered him from head to toe, and layers of heavy barriers rose around him. It was clear that he wanted to survive long enough to find an opening.","Ervin walked forward with his black spear in hand.","There was no violent aura at first.","Only a faint darkness gathered around the spear tip.","Darius roared and strengthened his barriers.","Ervin thrust once.","The black spear pierced through the first barrier, then the second, then the third, then the stone armor, stopping just before Darius’s chest. Every layer had been penetrated in a straight line, as if the spear had ignored the distance between them and gone directly to its target.","Darius froze.","Ervin withdrew his spear calmly.","[Winner: Ervin.]","[Darius Stoneveil Eliminated.]","Max’s expression became a little more focused.","He had fought Ervin in the Genesis Trial, so he already knew Ervin was dangerous. But outside the trial, Ervin’s abyssal spear still carried that same strange depth. It did not look overwhelming, but once it moved, it seemed to sink through all defenses until it reached the core.","’Still hiding most of his strength,’ Max thought.","Battle after battle continued.","More names were called. More participants were eliminated. Some battles lasted long enough to draw attention, while others ended in a few moves when the difference in strength was too large.","As the first main round progressed, it became clear that the strongest geniuses were being preserved for later clashes. Damian, Rakan, Rosaline, Orion, Kaiden, Ervin, and Max had all won without revealing their true trump cards.","On the pillars, the participants who had advanced watched the remaining battles with heavier expressions.","The weaker half of the final hundred was being removed.","The arena was becoming more dangerous with every victory.","Max stood quietly on his pillar, observing everything.","He had seen Damian’s refined sword, Rakan’s brutal fists, Rosaline’s radiant suppression, Orion’s star power, Kaiden’s void control, and Ervin’s abyssal spear. None of them had revealed their Pseudo Cosmic Paths or deepest foundations yet, but even the small glimpse they had shown was enough to prove one thing.","The final round would not be boring.","Max’s gaze swept across the pillars of the top geniuses, and a faint smile appeared on his face.","The first elimination stage was only the beginning.","The real battles were still waiting ahead.","The randomizer continued spinning after Ervin’s battle.","Several more names flashed across the light screen before finally slowing down again. This time, when the two names appeared, many participants instinctively turned their attention toward one particular pillar.","[Battle Thirty-Five]","[Revona vs Caelum Brightforge]","The moment Revona’s name appeared, Max’s eyes shifted toward her.","Revona stood silently on her pillar, her long hair moving slightly in the faint wind of the arena. Her expression was calm, almost indifferent, and her eyes were still closed. She had not shown much presence since the final round began, but Max had never underestimated her. He had fought her before, and he knew better than most people here how strange and dangerous her Void Origin Eyes could be.","Caelum Brightforge, on the other hand, was a tall young man wearing golden armor. A blazing hammer rested on his shoulder, and his aura carried the heat and weight of divine flame mixed with forging power.","From the whispers around the pillars, Max quickly learned that Caelum was a famous genius from an ancient blacksmith clan, someone who combined weapon refinement, fire control, and body tempering into one combat style.","Angelina Valerius looked at both of them calmly.","\"Revona. Caelum Brightforge. Enter the stage.\"","Two beams of light descended.","Revona appeared on one side of the central arena, her eyes still closed, while Caelum appeared opposite her with his golden hammer in hand. The barrier around the arena brightened again, and the runes across the stage lit up beneath their feet.","Caelum looked at Revona seriously.","\"I have heard of your eyes,\" he said. \"I know they are dangerous.\"","Revona’s voice was calm. \"Then you should attack with everything from the beginning.\"","Caelum’s expression became sharper. \"That was my plan.\"","[Battle Thirty-Five Begins.]","Caelum moved first.","Flames erupted from his golden armor, and the hammer in his hand expanded in size as if it had awakened from a dormant state. He stomped on the ground and rushed forward, each step leaving behind a burning footprint on the arena floor. The temperature inside the barrier rose sharply, and a wave of golden fire surged behind him like a furnace being opened.","\"Divine Forge Hammer, First Strike!\"","His hammer descended with terrifying force.","The attack was powerful enough to make many participants narrow their eyes. It carried both brute strength and flame pressure, and as the hammer fell, the air itself seemed to be compressed into a burning wave."]},{"number":1823,"title":"Chapter 1823: First Round - 5","paragraphs":["Revona finally opened her eyes.","A strange void-colored light appeared in her pupils.","The hammer reached her.","Then it vanished.","It simply became nothing.","The golden flames disappeared first, as if a hole had been carved into their existence. Then the hammer force collapsed, and the pressure following behind it also scattered into empty ripples. Caelum’s body still moved forward because of momentum, but the attack he had released was gone before it could touch Revona.","The entire arena fell silent for a brief moment.","Then the whispers exploded.","\"What just happened?\"","\"His attack disappeared?\"","\"No, it did not disappear normally. It was nullified.\"","\"That is the Void Origin Eyes?\"","Caelum’s expression changed greatly, but he reacted quickly. He pulled back his hammer and spun in place, releasing a ring of golden fire around his body. Several flame-forged weapons appeared in the air, including spears, swords, axes, and chains, all burning with the same divine forging flame.","\"Let me see how many attacks you can erase at once!\"","He roared and swung his hammer forward.","The flame-forged weapons shot toward Revona from every direction.","Revona stood still.","Her Void Origin Eyes glowed deeper.","One spear vanished.","Then one sword.","Then three axes disappeared at the same time.","A chain reached her ankle, but the moment it entered the range of her gaze, the burning links broke apart into faint void ripples. The remaining weapons circled around her, trying to attack from angles outside her direct line of sight, but Revona only turned her head slightly. Wherever her eyes passed, the attacks were erased.","Max’s gaze sharpened.","This was different.","When he had fought Revona before, her Void Origin Eyes had already been powerful, but they had not been this smooth.","Back then, there had been limits. Her eyes could make attacks turn into nothingness, but the timing, range, and control had not reached this level. If someone attacked fast enough, with enough physical power, or from a close enough distance, she could still be forced into a difficult situation.","But now, her eyes had clearly awakened further.","Caelum also realized this.","His expression became ugly as he backed away and raised his hammer with both hands. The golden armor on his body opened slightly, releasing streams of blazing light, and a massive furnace image appeared behind him. The furnace roared with fire, and countless divine runes appeared across the hammer’s surface.","The participants on the pillars became serious.","\"He is using his strongest technique.\"","\"That furnace image is not ordinary. It should be the core inheritance of the Brightforge Clan.\"","\"If even this gets erased, then her eyes are too unreasonable.\"","Caelum roared, \"Divine Forge Hammer, Heaven-Melting Descent!\"","The massive furnace image poured all its flames into the hammer.","Then Caelum leapt into the air and smashed downward.","This strike was far stronger than all his previous attacks combined. The hammer carried enough heat to distort the stage itself, and the golden flames condensed into a giant burning hammer that descended like a falling sun. Even through the barrier, many participants felt a wave of heat brush against them.","Revona looked up.","Her eyes remained calm.","The void-colored light in her pupils expanded.","The falling sun touched her gaze.","Then a hole appeared in it.","The golden hammer image lost its center first. Then the surrounding flames collapsed inward. The heat vanished. The pressure vanished. The divine runes vanished. The entire technique, which had been powerful enough to threaten most participants in the final hundred, disappeared before it could touch her.","Caelum fell from the air, his face pale.","His real hammer was still in his hand, but the strongest force behind the strike had been nullified completely. Before he could stabilize himself, Revona appeared in front of him with one finger raised toward his forehead.","She had not even used a weapon.","Caelum froze.","Angelina Valerius announced the result calmly.","[Winner: Revona.]","[Caelum Brightforge Eliminated.]","A beam of light descended and removed Caelum from the stage.","Revona closed her eyes again and returned to her pillar.","For a few seconds, no one spoke.","Then the arena erupted into discussion.","\"That is ridiculous.\"","\"How are you supposed to fight her if your attacks disappear before reaching her?\"","\"Caelum Brightforge was not weak at all. His strongest strike was erased like smoke.\"","\"She did not even look tired.\"","\"Those eyes are terrifying.\"","Max stood on his pillar and watched Revona silently.","His expression did not show fear, but his eyes had become more serious. He remembered his earlier battle with her very clearly. At that time, he had defeated her because of his overwhelming physical strength and because her Void Origin Eyes had not fully awakened. He had closed the distance, pressured her body, and forced her into a situation where her eyes could not completely erase his raw power before he overwhelmed her.","But now things would not be so simple.","Her eyes had grown stronger.","Their range had improved. Their stability had improved. Their ability to nullify attacks from multiple directions had improved. Most importantly, she seemed much calmer while using them, which meant the burden on her body might have decreased as well.","’If I fight her again, relying only on brute force will not be enough,’ Max thought.","He looked at Revona’s closed eyes.","’Last time, I defeated her before those eyes could truly control the battle. Now, if she opens them properly, every attack I use might be erased before it reaches her.’","For a moment, Max imagined how his different powers would fare against her.","Ordinary sword light would likely be nullified.","Divine King Punishment might be erased if it entered her gaze directly.","Even space-based movements could become risky if her eyes could target the origin of the movement rather than the movement itself.","As for Emotion Severing Path, Max was not sure.","That uncertainty made his interest grow.","On another pillar, Damian Voss also looked toward Revona with a rare serious expression.","\"Void Origin Eyes,\" he murmured. \"So they have awakened to that level.\"","Orion Starfall’s smile became thoughtful. \"This conference really has too many troublesome people.\"","Rakan Thorne grinned, but even he looked more focused than before. \"So if I punch her, will the punch disappear, or will her eyes fail before my fist reaches her?\"","Ervin glanced at him and said calmly, \"That depends on whether your fist reaches her before she sees enough of it.\"","Rakan laughed. \"Then I just need to punch faster.\"","Kaiden Voidmere watched Revona quietly, his silver-gray eyes reflecting a faint void light of their own. Unlike the others, his reaction was harder to read, but Max could tell that he was paying attention. As someone connected to the void path himself, Kaiden likely understood more about Revona’s eyes than most people here.","Princess Rosaline’s expression also became solemn.","\"Her eyes are almost unfair in direct combat,\" one of the Lunarian geniuses beside her said.","Rosaline nodded slightly. \"Almost. But no power is truly without weakness. The problem is whether anyone here can find it before losing.\"","Revona returned to her pillar and remained silent, as if the battle had not mattered much to her.","Max watched her for a moment longer before looking back at the central stage.","The final round was becoming more interesting.","Damian’s sword was terrifying.","Rakan’s body was overwhelming.","Orion’s star power was precise and controlled.","Kaiden’s void was deep and quiet.","Ervin’s abyssal spear was strange and dangerous.","Rosaline’s radiant suppression was extremely clean.","And Revona’s Void Origin Eyes could nullify attacks as if they had never existed.","Max smiled faintly.","The first main round had not even ended yet, but the true threats were already revealing themselves one by one.","And that made the coming battles worth waiting for."]},{"number":1824,"title":"Chapter 1824: First Round - 6","paragraphs":["After Revona returned to her pillar, the atmosphere around the arena remained strange for quite some time.","Her battle had not been long, but its impact was far greater than many of the longer battles before it. Caelum Brightforge had not been weak. His forging flame, hammer technique, and defensive foundation were all strong enough to place him above most ordinary geniuses, yet every attack he used had simply disappeared before Revona’s Void Origin Eyes.","That kind of power made many participants feel uncomfortable because it was difficult to understand and even harder to counter.","Max watched her for a while before shifting his gaze back to the central stage.","The randomizer continued spinning.","Battle after battle unfolded before him, and Max observed each one with calm attention. Most fights were between geniuses he did not recognize, but none of them were truly weak. A silver-armored knight defeated a beast-blooded archer by closing the distance in three breaths.","A shadow cultivator lost to a woman who controlled sound waves because his stealth became useless the moment her spiritual perception spread through vibration. A flame user fought a water user for nearly half an hour before finally winning by exhausting his opponent’s reserves. Each battle showed a different path, different foundation, and different weakness.","Max did not watch casually.","His Dimensional Sovereign Body allowed him to perceive details others missed. He noticed how some people hid injuries behind stable breathing, how some used feints to draw out trump cards, how some carried strength far above what their surface aura suggested, and how some were already thinking about later rounds even while fighting their current opponent. This final round was not merely a place to win battles. It was also a place to study future enemies.","Then the randomizer stopped again.","[Battle Thirty-Eight]","[Aurelian Lareth vs Kovan Ashrune]","The name made Max’s eyes turn cold.","Aurelian Lareth.","The Divine Son of the second elven faction.","The one who had received Max’s stolen Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline.","The moment that name appeared, many participants turned toward one of the pillars. A young man stood there in white-gold robes, his long golden hair falling behind him, his face handsome and almost too perfect. His eyes carried a sacred radiance, and a faint divine light flowed around his body even though he had not released any power.","Compared to Selene’s pure and noble aura, Aurelian’s presence felt deeper, heavier, and more complete, as if something precious and powerful had been forcefully rooted inside him and cultivated for years.","Max stared at him silently.","Aurelian seemed to sense his gaze and turned his head.","Their eyes met across the arena.","For a brief moment, the air between their pillars seemed to freeze.","Aurelian smiled faintly.","It was not a friendly smile. It was calm, distant, and filled with an arrogance that came from knowing exactly what he possessed. His gaze briefly moved across Max’s body, as if he was studying the true owner of the bloodline inside him, and then he turned away as though Max could wait.","Max’s fingers moved slightly.","Angelina Valerius spoke calmly. \"Aurelian Lareth. Kovan Ashrune. Enter the stage.\"","Two beams of light descended.","Aurelian appeared on the central stage with both hands behind his back. Kovan Ashrune, his opponent, was a gray-robed man wielding a staff covered in ash-colored runes. The moment he saw Aurelian standing opposite him, his expression became extremely heavy. He knew very well that he had drawn one of the worst possible opponents.","[Battle Thirty-Eight Begins.]","Kovan acted immediately.","Ash-gray runes spread under his feet, and a storm of burning ash rose around him. The ash condensed into chains, spears, and shields, forming a battlefield that tried to suppress Aurelian from every direction. The technique was not weak. It carried both fire and decay, and if an ordinary opponent was trapped inside, their energy would be slowly burned away.","Aurelian did not move.","The moment the ash storm approached him, golden-white divine light spread from his body.","The ash chains dissolved.","The ash spears melted.","The entire burning field was purified in a single breath.","Kovan’s face changed, and he quickly raised his staff to form another rune array, but Aurelian simply lifted one finger. A beam of Heavenly Luminance light shot forward and pierced through the center of the rune array, shattering it before stopping an inch from Kovan’s forehead.","Kovan froze.","Aurelian’s voice was calm. \"Surrender.\"","Kovan’s face turned pale. After a long breath, he lowered his staff.","\"I surrender.\"","[Winner: Aurelian Lareth.]","[Kovan Ashrune Eliminated.]","Aurelian returned to his pillar without even looking at his defeated opponent again.","Max’s eyes remained fixed on him.","The bloodline aura Aurelian had displayed was unmistakable. It was not exactly the same as Max’s current Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline, but it was deeply connected to it. The second faction had stolen something from his body, and now they had raised Aurelian as the vessel for it. Seeing that divine light being used so calmly by someone else made Max’s gaze colder than before.","’So that is the Divine Son,’ Max thought. ’Good. I was wondering when I would meet him.’","Not long after Aurelian’s battle, another familiar name appeared.","[Battle Forty]","[Selene Vaeloria vs Dorian Frostmarch]","The atmosphere changed again.","The Divine Daughter of the second faction stepped onto the stage.","Selene Vaeloria looked almost unchanged from when Max had defeated her near the Witch God Tree. Her white-gold hair shone faintly, her eyes carried cold pride, and her aura was once again stable. The life-restoration rules of the Cosmic Ascension Conference had clearly allowed her to continue, and despite her previous defeat, she had still survived to enter the final hundred.","The moment she appeared, her gaze turned toward Max.","There was hatred in her eyes.","Not fear.","Hatred.","Max looked back at her calmly.","Selene did not speak, but her expression said enough. She had not forgotten the humiliation of being defeated by Max, nor the fact that he had shattered her superiority in front of so many people.","Her opponent, Dorian Frostmarch, was an ice-attribute swordsman. He released frost sword intent the moment the battle began, sending dozens of ice blades across the stage. The air turned cold, and crystalline snow spread across the arena floor.","Selene raised her hand.","Heavenly Luminance light unfolded behind her like a pair of radiant wings.","The frost sword intent was suppressed.","Dorian tried to force through with a stronger technique, forming a giant ice sword above his head, but Selene’s expression did not change. A golden-white wheel appeared behind her, spinning slowly with majestic pressure.","\"Luminance Judgment.\"","The radiant wheel released a pillar of light.","Dorian’s ice sword shattered instantly.","The light stopped in front of his chest, burning through his defensive aura without touching his flesh. Dorian stared at the light, then slowly lowered his sword.","\"I surrender.\"","[Winner: Selene Vaeloria.]","[Dorian Frostmarch Eliminated.]","Selene returned to her pillar, but before the transfer light faded completely, she looked at Max again.","Max only smiled faintly.","That smile made Selene’s expression turn even colder."]},{"number":1825,"title":"Chapter 1825: First Round - 7","paragraphs":["The randomizer continued.","A few more battles passed.","Some participants were eliminated quickly, while others managed to advance after hard-fought clashes. A spearwoman with thunder wings defeated a poison cultivator by overwhelming him before his toxins could spread.","A demon youth with black flames lost to a calm monk-like participant who reflected his flame back through a strange palm art. A silver-haired beastkin girl surrendered after realizing that her opponent’s soul attacks had already trapped her in an illusion field.","Then another familiar name appeared.","[Battle Forty-Three]","[Morgana Starveil vs Elara Mistwood]","Max’s eyes shifted.","Morgana Starveil appeared on the stage with her midnight-blue hair, black-violet dress, and purple eyes. Her witch hat tilted slightly over her head, and her lips carried a faint smile, but that smile did not reach her eyes. She looked toward Max almost immediately after appearing.","Their gazes met.","Morgana’s smile widened.","Unlike Selene, there was no open hatred in her expression. Instead, there was resentment hidden beneath playful calm, along with a dangerous curiosity. Max had killed her before with one Emotion Severing Path slash, splitting her apart despite all her curse defenses. Yet here she was again, revived by the rules of the conference and standing among the final hundred.","Elara Mistwood, her opponent, was a graceful woman with green hair and forest-like energy around her body. She used wood spirit techniques, summoning vines, petals, and misty roots to surround Morgana from all sides.","Morgana laughed softly.","\"Wood against a witch? How nostalgic.\"","Elara frowned and attacked first.","The vines moved like serpents, each one carrying spiritual poison. Mist spread across the stage, hiding dozens of thorned branches that shot toward Morgana’s body from blind spots. But Morgana merely raised one finger, and black-violet symbols appeared in the air around her.","\"Stellar Witchcraft, Curse of the Wandering Root.\"","The vines stopped.","Then they turned around.","Elara’s expression changed as her own wood techniques twisted under Morgana’s curse and attacked her instead. She quickly tried to regain control, but Morgana’s second curse had already descended. Seven purple-black stars appeared above the stage, each one releasing thin curse threads that wrapped around Elara’s limbs and spirit energy.","Elara struggled, but the more she resisted, the tighter the curse became.","Morgana walked forward slowly and stopped in front of her.","\"You should surrender before the curse reaches your soul.\"","Elara’s face turned pale. After a few breaths, she lowered her head.","\"I surrender.\"","[Winner: Morgana Starveil.]","[Elara Mistwood Eliminated.]","Morgana returned to her pillar and looked at Max again.","This time, she placed one finger near her lips and smiled, as if telling him that their unfinished business would continue later.","Max’s expression remained calm.","Morgana was still dangerous. Her direct combat strength might not be as overwhelming as Damian or Rakan, but her curse methods were troublesome and unpredictable. If she was allowed time to prepare, she could turn a simple battle into a trap. Max had killed her once because he had given her three moves and then crushed her with Emotion Severing Path, but that did not mean she was weak. It only meant his path had been a terrible match for her.","The battles continued.","Max also saw Seraphine Lareth and Fin Arclight among the remaining hundred.","Seraphine fought a halberd user who relied on violent close combat. She did not look as arrogant as before, but her Radiant Judgment Path was still fierce. Golden judgment light descended again and again, forcing her opponent to retreat until he finally failed to block a radiant spear and was judged unable to continue.","[Winner: Seraphine Lareth.]","Fin’s battle came shortly after. His Pale Eclipse Path spread across the arena like a gray-white moon shadow, dulling his opponent’s senses and weakening the rhythm of their attacks. He did not win as explosively as Seraphine, but he won cleanly, trapping his opponent in an eclipse field before ending the battle with a blade of pale light.","[Winner: Fin Arclight.]","Max looked at both of them without much emotion.","He had already killed them before. He had even forced them to end themselves once. But because of the rules of the first round, they had survived and returned to the final hundred. That did not bother him. If anything, it made things simpler. The more second faction people remained in the final round, the more chances he had to crush them on a stage everyone could see.","Rose’s battle also appeared later.","[Battle Forty-Six]","[Rose Valen vs Iskar Duskfang]","Rose’s opponent was a wolf-blooded fighter with sharp claws and terrifying speed. From the beginning, it was clear that Rose was not stronger than him in raw power. Iskar moved faster, attacked harder, and forced her to defend almost immediately. Several people assumed Rose would lose quickly, but Max watched with interest.","Rose did not panic.","She used small movements, defensive talismans, and precise footwork to keep herself alive. She never tried to overpower Iskar. Instead, she slowly guided him toward certain positions on the stage. After dozens of exchanges, Iskar finally stepped into a hidden formation mark she had placed through earlier movements.","Light chains erupted from beneath him.","Iskar roared and tore through two of them, but that small delay was enough.","Rose appeared behind him and placed a short blade against his neck.","Angelina declared the result.","[Winner: Rose Valen.]","[Iskar Duskfang Eliminated.]","Max smiled faintly.","Rose had not survived this far by luck alone. Her strength was not the most overwhelming, but her judgment, patience, and preparation were excellent. She knew how to make stronger opponents fall into her rhythm, and in a tournament setting, that could be just as valuable as raw power.","More battles followed.","Max saw battles battles of Tamara, and other few geniuses he could recognize but for some reason he didn’t find the prince from the first faction who had warned him about Caroline.","’With his strength he should have survive to top 100.’ Max thought deeply. ’But why isn’t he here?’","Finally, after the fiftieth battle ended, the massive screen of light above the arena changed.","[First Main Round Completed.]","[Total Participants: 100]","[Eliminated Participants: 50]","[Remaining Participants: 50]","The arena became silent.","Half of the final hundred had been removed.","The pillars belonging to eliminated participants dimmed and sank into the darkness below, while the remaining fifty pillars glowed brighter. The circle around the central stage became wider and emptier, making the remaining figures stand out even more clearly.","Angelina Valerius looked over the survivors calmly.","\"Congratulations. The first main round of the final round has concluded. The remaining fifty participants will advance to the second main round.\"","Max looked around at the remaining pillars. There were many he recognized among them.","Along with them, many hidden experts whose names Max had only learned through watching their battles had also advanced. The arena had become smaller in number but far more dangerous in quality.","Max’s gaze moved from one familiar enemy to another.","A faint smile appeared on his face.","The people he had defeated once were still here.","The people he had not yet fought were waiting too.","And from the second main round onward, the chance of avoiding dangerous opponents would become smaller and smaller.","Angelina raised her hand again, and the randomizer above the arena began to awaken for the next stage.","\"The second main round will begin shortly,\" she announced. \"Fifty participants will fight. Twenty-five will remain.\"","The pillars hummed.","The remaining participants became silent.","Max watched the randomizer begin to spin again.","The true pressure of the final round was finally beginning to descend."]},{"number":1826,"title":"Chapter 1826: Second Round - 1","paragraphs":["The second main round continued with growing pressure.","After several top geniuses had already secured their victories, the remaining participants became even more tense.","Every battle now carried the weight of elimination. Winning meant entering the final competitive stage with the remaining twenty-five, while losing meant leaving the Cosmic Ascension Conference before the true ranking battles even began.","The randomizer spun again.","[Second Main Round, Battle Twelve]","[Max Morgan vs Veyron Soulbinder]","The moment Max’s name appeared, many eyes turned toward his pillar.","Max opened his eyes calmly.","His opponent, Veyron Soulbinder, stood on a distant pillar wearing dark purple robes. His face was pale, his body was thin, and several small black bells floated around him without any visible strings. Unlike brute-force fighters or elemental geniuses, his aura was quiet and eerie. It did not press against the body. It pressed against the mind.","Several participants immediately became serious.","\"Veyron Soulbinder. He is the soul-bell user who forced his previous opponent to surrender without even touching him.\"","\"His soul attacks are extremely troublesome. Physical defense is useless against him.\"","\"This might not be easy for Max Morgan. Even if Max’s body is monstrous, soul attacks are different.\"","Max heard the whispers but remained calm.","Angelina Valerius looked at both of them.","\"Max Morgan. Veyron Soulbinder. Enter the stage.\"","Two beams of light descended.","Max appeared on one side of the central arena, while Veyron appeared opposite him. The floating black bells around Veyron began to spin slowly, releasing a faint ringing sound that made some spectators on the pillars frown even though the arena barrier blocked most of the power.","Veyron looked at Max and smiled faintly.","\"Max Morgan, I know you are strong. Your body is strong. Your sword is strong. Your bloodline is strong. But strength of the body does not always protect the soul.\"","Max looked at him calmly. \"Are you done?\"","Veyron’s smile stiffened slightly.","Then the battle began.","[Battle Begins.]","Veyron attacked immediately.","The black bells around him rang at the same time.","Ding.","The sound was soft, but the moment it rang out, an invisible soul wave rushed toward Max. It did not travel through the air like ordinary sound. It pierced directly toward the soul, trying to bypass the body, bloodline, sword, and physical defenses entirely.","Several participants watched closely.","Damian Voss narrowed his eyes slightly.","Rakan Thorne frowned. \"Soul attacks. Annoying.\"","Orion Starfall smiled faintly but focused more than before. \"Let us see how Max deals with this.\"","Veyron’s soul wave reached Max. Then nothing happened.","Max stood in place without moving. His expression did not change at all.","Veyron’s eyes narrowed.","He rang the bells again.","This time, the sound became layered. Several soul waves overlapped, forming a strange illusionary field around Max. Within that field, ordinary opponents would hear countless whispers from their own memories, regrets, fears, and weaknesses. Their minds would become unstable, their movements would slow, and their souls would gradually be bound by the ringing bells.","But Max only looked at him.","The soul waves entered his body and vanished as if they had fallen into a boundless domain.","Veyron’s expression changed for the first time.","\"What?\"","Max’s eyes remained calm.","He had the Dimension of Soul.","Against ordinary soul attacks, his soul was not an exposed weakness. It was a dimension. A vast inner space. The moment Veyron’s attacks tried to invade, they were swallowed by that dimension before they could affect him. It was not that Max was simply resisting the soul attacks. The attacks could not even properly touch the core of his soul.","Veyron gritted his teeth and raised both hands.","The black bells multiplied.","Three became nine.","Nine became thirty-six.","All thirty-six bells rang at once, and the sound turned sharp enough to make the barrier around the stage ripple faintly.","\"Soul-Burial Bell Formation!\"","A dark purple formation opened beneath Max’s feet. Countless soul chains rose from it, attempting to bind his soul directly. At the same time, ghostly faces appeared in the air, whispering curses meant to shake his consciousness and drag him into a soul illusion.","Max finally moved. He took one step forward.","The soul chains touched him.","Then they broke apart.","The ghostly faces screamed without sound before being pulled into an invisible depth around Max’s body. The Soul-Burial Bell Formation trembled violently, then collapsed from the center outward.","Veyron staggered backward, blood flowing from the corner of his mouth.","The backlash had struck him.","The arena became silent.","\"How is that possible?\"","\"Veyron’s soul attack failed completely.\"","\"Not failed. It was swallowed.\"","\"What kind of soul defense does Max Morgan have?\"","On her pillar, Revona opened her eyes slightly.","Kaiden Voidmere’s gaze deepened.","Ervin smiled faintly. \"So his soul is also not ordinary.\"","Rosaline looked at Max with visible surprise. \"He really has too many foundations.\"","Aurelian Lareth’s eyes narrowed, and Selene Vaeloria’s expression became colder.","Veyron stared at Max with disbelief. \"What are you?\"","Max walked toward him.","Veyron quickly rang all the bells again, but the result did not change. Soul needles, soul chains, soul illusions, soul curses, and soul-burial sound waves all entered the invisible depth around Max and disappeared. Nothing reached him. Nothing slowed him. Nothing shook his consciousness.","For Veyron, it was like attacking an ocean with drops of rain.","Max appeared in front of him.","Veyron’s face turned pale.","Max lifted one hand and stopped his fingers an inch from Veyron’s forehead.","\"Your attacks are useless against me.\"","Veyron clenched his fists, but after a few breaths, he lowered his head.","\"I surrender.\"","Angelina announced the result calmly.","[Winner: Max Morgan.]","[Veyron Soulbinder Eliminated.]","Max returned to his pillar.","The entire arena looked at him differently now.","Until this point, most people had known that Max was physically terrifying, possessed Dragonheart, had a dangerous sword path, and carried mysterious bloodline power. But now, they had seen that even soul attacks were almost useless against him. A participant who had specialized in attacking the soul had been completely restrained without Max even drawing his sword."]},{"number":1827,"title":"Chapter 1827: Second Round - 2","paragraphs":["Max stood calmly on his pillar, as if the battle had not mattered much.","But many others were no longer calm.","Rakan Thorne clicked his tongue. \"Body is monstrous. Sword is monstrous. Soul defense is monstrous. Does this guy have a normal weakness?\"","Orion Starfall smiled. \"If he does, he is hiding it well.\"","Damian Voss looked at Max in silence, his gaze sharper than before.","Kaiden Voidmere murmured softly, \"Dimension of Soul?\"","Ervin heard those words and glanced toward Kaiden, but Kaiden did not explain further.","Max ignored the reactions and looked back at the central stage.","The randomizer continued.","Aurelian Lareth was called soon after.","[Second Main Round, Battle Thirteen]","[Aurelian Lareth vs Corvin Nightsteel]","Corvin Nightsteel was not weak. He used dark metal armor and a heavy sword, and his first attack released a black storm of blade fragments that covered half the stage. Against most opponents, the storm would have been difficult to defend against.","Aurelian simply raised his hand.","Heavenly Luminance divine light spread outward.","The black blade fragments melted like snow beneath the sun.","Corvin tried to charge through the light with his armor glowing, but Aurelian’s expression remained calm. A golden-white spear of light appeared above him and descended. It broke Corvin’s armor, forced him to one knee, and stopped just above his head.","[Winner: Aurelian Lareth.]","[Corvin Nightsteel Eliminated.]","Max’s gaze became cold.","Aurelian still had not shown the full depth of the bloodline he had received, but every time he used that light, Max could feel the connection more clearly. It was like watching someone use a stolen part of his own existence.","Selene Vaeloria’s battle came later.","[Second Main Round, Battle Fifteen]","[Selene Vaeloria vs Aurelia Flamecrest]","This pairing became one of the first battles in the second main round where a famous genius was given a truly troublesome opponent. Aurelia Flamecrest had advanced through a hard-fought match in the first main round and possessed extremely powerful sunfire. The moment the battle began, she released a golden sun wheel that pushed even Selene’s luminance aura back slightly.","Selene’s expression turned cold.","She raised both hands, and the Heavenly Luminance Queen Avatar appeared faintly behind her. She did not use her Pseudo Cosmic Path, but the avatar alone increased the pressure of her light sharply. Aurelia’s sunfire clashed with Selene’s radiance again and again, and for the first time in this round, Selene was forced to take several steps back.","The crowd stirred.","\"She is being pushed?\"","\"No, not pushed. She is measuring the attack.\"","Max watched calmly.","He could tell that Selene was not in real danger. Aurelia’s sunfire was strong, but Selene’s foundation was still higher.","As expected, after a few more exchanges, Selene’s gaze sharpened.","\"Twelve Luminance Edicts.\"","Twelve golden runes appeared around Aurelia.","Her sunfire trembled.","The edicts suppressed the flames from twelve directions, and Selene’s palm descended immediately afterward. Aurelia tried to resist, but the radiant palm broke through her sunfire and stopped before her chest.","Aurelia clenched her teeth, then lowered her hands.","\"I surrender.\"","[Winner: Selene Vaeloria.]","[Aurelia Flamecrest Eliminated.]","Selene returned to her pillar and looked at Max again, but Max’s expression remained indifferent.","Her hatred was obvious.","Her strength was real.","But Max had already defeated her once when she used far more than this.","The battles continued one after another. Some of the hidden experts who had looked promising in the first main round fell quickly when matched against more famous figures. Some managed to struggle, forcing their opponents to reveal a little more of their foundation before losing. The second main round was doing exactly what it was meant to do. It was separating the strong from the truly dangerous.","Revona’s second battle appeared near the later half.","[Second Main Round, Battle Eighteen]","[Revona vs Seraphine Lareth]","The moment the names appeared together, the arena became extremely quiet.","Seraphine’s face turned ugly.","She had survived the first main round, but now she had drawn Revona. Her Radiant Judgment Path was powerful, but after everyone had seen Revona’s Void Origin Eyes, no one knew whether Seraphine’s judgment light could even reach her.","Seraphine entered the stage with a cold expression.","Revona appeared opposite her with her eyes closed.","[Battle Begins.]","Seraphine attacked immediately.","Golden judgment spears descended from above, filling the stage with radiant killing light. Revona opened her eyes, and the void-colored glow appeared again.","The first spear vanished.","Then the second.","Then all the spears within her gaze disappeared one after another.","Seraphine’s expression became stiff. She clenched her teeth and released a stronger radiant wheel, trying to suppress Revona from above. But Revona looked up, and the center of the wheel was erased.","The entire technique collapsed.","Revona appeared before Seraphine and raised one finger toward her forehead.","Seraphine trembled with anger, but she could not deny the result.","\"I surrender.\"","[Winner: Revona.]","[Seraphine Lareth Eliminated.]","Max smiled faintly.","Watching Seraphine lose so quickly was not unpleasant.","Fin Arclight’s battle came soon after, and unlike Seraphine, he managed to draw an opponent who was not a top monster. His Pale Eclipse Path dimmed the battlefield, weakened his opponent’s senses, and trapped them in a gray-white domain of distorted perception. After a short struggle, his opponent surrendered.","[Winner: Fin Arclight.]","Max watched Fin quietly.","Fin was not at the level of Damian, Rakan, or the others, but he remained troublesome. His Pale Eclipse Path was suited for weakening and trapping opponents, and if someone underestimated him, they could be dragged into a bad rhythm.","Morgana’s next battle also drew attention.","[Second Main Round, Battle Twenty-Two]","[Morgana Starveil vs Rose Valen]","Rose’s expression changed the moment her name appeared opposite Morgana’s.","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly.","This was a bad match for Rose.","Rose was clever, careful, and skilled at creating traps, but Morgana was a witch whose curse methods specialized in turning other people’s preparations against them. If Rose tried to play a long tactical battle, she might end up giving Morgana more mediums to curse."]},{"number":1828,"title":"Chapter 1828: Final Round Starts!","paragraphs":["Rose entered the stage with a serious face.","Morgana smiled sweetly. \"How unlucky. You seem like someone who likes planning.\"","Rose did not answer.","The battle began, and Rose immediately spread several rune marks across the stage through subtle movements. She tried to keep distance and use defensive formations to block Morgana’s curse threads. For a short time, it worked. Her runes lit up one after another, forming protective layers around her body.","Morgana looked amused.","\"Not bad.\"","Then she raised one hand.","\"Stellar Witchcraft, Curse of the Borrowed Mark.\"","Rose’s runes trembled.","Her expression changed.","The protective layers she had placed began twisting, and several rune marks turned purple-black. Rose immediately cut off her connection to them, but Morgana had already closed the distance with curse threads spreading around her fingers.","A purple star appeared behind Rose.","Rose stopped moving.","Morgana’s voice was gentle. \"If this were a real fight outside the arena, your soul would already be marked.\"","Rose’s expression was bitter, but she still lowered her blade.","\"I surrender.\"","[Winner: Morgana Starveil.]","[Rose Valen Eliminated.]","Max watched Rose disappear from the stage.","She had lost, but she had not performed badly. Against most opponents, her formations and careful thinking could have won. Against Morgana, however, her own preparation had become a weakness. The matchup had been too unfavorable.","Morgana returned to her pillar and glanced toward Max again.","This time, Max finally looked back at her directly.","Morgana’s smile paused slightly.","There was no killing intent in Max’s gaze, but the calmness in his eyes made her remember the sword that had split her in half near the Witch God Tree. Her smile returned quickly, but it was a little less relaxed than before.","The final few battles of the second main round passed quickly.","A silent swordsman from an unknown force defeated a beast prince in three sword moves, revealing enough skill to draw even Damian’s attention. A bloodfire woman from the Blood Sun Temple won after a brutal clash that left half the stage covered in crimson flames. A soul-bell user had already fallen to Max, making the remaining mind-path participants much more cautious whenever they looked at him. Several other participants advanced with difficulty, while others disappeared under beams of elimination light.","At last, the twenty-fifth battle ended.","The giant screen above the arena changed again.","[Second Main Round Completed.]","[Total Participants At Start Of Round: 50]","[Eliminated Participants: 25]","[Remaining Participants: 25]","The dimmed pillars of the eliminated participants sank into the darkness below.","Only twenty-five pillars remained around the central arena.","The space suddenly felt much emptier.","And much more oppressive.","Angelina Valerius looked across the remaining participants with a calm expression.","\"Congratulations,\" she said. \"You have entered the final competitive stage of the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","Max looked around and saw the top experts were looking at each other with caution in their eyes.","Along with them, several hidden experts with strange and dangerous methods had also survived. Rose had been eliminated, Seraphine had been eliminated, and many others who had seemed strong were gone.","From this point onward, there would be no more random elimination bracket.","Each of the remaining twenty-five would fight twenty-four battles.","Everyone would face everyone.","Max’s gaze swept across the final competitors, and his smile became faint.","Now, there was no need to wonder when he would meet Damian, Rakan, Orion, Kaiden, Ervin, Revona, Rosaline, Aurelian, Selene, Morgana, or anyone else.","He would fight them all.","Angelina raised her hand, and the arena lights became brighter.","\"The final competitive stage will begin after a short preparation period.\"","The twenty-five remaining pillars hummed.","The true battle for the championship was finally about to begin.","The twenty-five remaining pillars shone brighter than before.","After the second main round ended, the arena inside the Eternal Hourglass had become much emptier, yet the pressure in the air had increased many times over. Only twenty-five participants remained, and every one of them had already proven that they were strong enough to survive two direct elimination rounds. The weak were gone. The lucky were gone.","The ones who remained were either monsters standing openly at the peak or hidden blades that had not yet fully revealed themselves.","After the little rest, Angelina Valerius appeared again and stood above the central stage, her silver-white robe fluttering gently as she looked at the twenty-five participants surrounding the arena.","\"The final competitive stage will now begin,\" she said calmly.","The massive screen of light above the arena changed, and the names of all twenty-five remaining participants appeared in a large circle.","[Final Competitive Stage Initiated.]","[Remaining Participants: 25]","[Battle Format: Complete Round-Robin Combat.]","[Each Participant Will Fight Every Other Remaining Participant Once.]","[Total Battles Per Participant: 24.]","[Ranking Method: Total Number Of Wins.]","Angelina’s voice continued, clear and dignified.","\"In this stage, there will be no random elimination. No participant will be removed after a single loss. Each of you will fight every other participant once, which means each of you will fight twenty-four battles in total.\"","The expressions of many participants became serious.","A single loss would no longer end everything immediately, but that did not make the round easier. In fact, it made it much harsher. No one could rely on lucky pairings anymore. If someone wanted to become champion, they would have to defeat almost everyone.","Angelina raised one finger.","\"After each battle, the battle record of the participant will be updated. Your name, total battles fought, and total wins will be displayed for all to see.\"","The giant screen above the arena changed again.","[Battle Record Format:]","[Participant Name]","[Total Battles Fought:]","[Total Wins:]","Angelina continued, \"If two or more participants have the same number of wins after all scheduled battles are completed, tiebreaker battles will be conducted between them. If a participant surrenders, the surrender will count as a loss. If a participant is judged unable to continue, the battle will end immediately. If a participant refuses to stop after the arena has declared the result, that participant will be punished by the laws of the Eternal Hourglass.\"","The central stage hummed as if confirming her words.","\"No outside interference will be allowed. No one may leave their pillar unless called to battle. Recovery time will be granted according to the order of battles, but in the final competitive stage, endurance is also part of strength.\"","Her gaze swept across Damian Voss, Rakan Thorne, Orion Starfall, Kaiden Voidmere, Ervin, Revona, Rosaline, Aurelian Lareth, Selene Vaeloria, Morgana Starveil, Max, and the other remaining participants.","\"Now, the first battle of the final competitive stage will begin.\"","The screen of light above the arena flickered.","Two names appeared.","[Final Competitive Stage, Battle One]","[Max Morgan vs Rosaline Lunara]"]},{"number":1829,"title":"Chapter 1829: Max vs Rosaline","paragraphs":["The moment those two names appeared, the arena became lively.","Many participants turned toward Max’s pillar, then toward Rosaline’s pillar. Some were surprised. Some were excited. Some were already focusing with great attention, because this battle was not between an obvious top monster and an ordinary survivor. Rosaline was not weak. She had advanced through both elimination rounds without suffering any real damage, and her radiant suppression had already proven to be extremely clean and dangerous.","Max also looked toward Rosaline.","Rosaline met his gaze from her pillar, and a faint helpless smile appeared on her face.","\"I did not expect my first battle to start with you,\" she said.","Max smiled faintly. \"Neither did I.\"","Angelina raised her hand.","Two beams of light descended.","Max appeared on one side of the central stage. Opposite him, Rosaline appeared with her golden-pink hair moving gently behind her, her white and rose-gold gown shining faintly beneath the arena light. She looked elegant, calm, and noble, but the aura around her was already becoming sharper.","Rosaline looked at Max seriously.","\"I have watched enough of your battles to understand one thing,\" she said. \"Against you, holding back is meaningless.\"","Max raised an eyebrow. \"Is that so?\"","Rosaline nodded. \"Yes. Your body is monstrous, your sword foundation is terrifying, your soul defense is abnormal, and you still have several powers you have not shown properly. If I try to test you slowly, I will lose before showing anything worthwhile.\"","Max smiled nodding his head. \"That is a good judgment.\"","Rosaline’s expression became solemn.","\"So I will use my full strength from the beginning.\"","The moment her words fell, the atmosphere around the stage changed.","Golden-pink light rose from Rosaline’s body, soft at first, then brighter and brighter until it became like the first dawn spreading over an endless kingdom. The air filled with a sacred fragrance, and petals of radiant light began to fall from the sky.","Each petal looked gentle, but Max could clearly sense that every one of them carried sealing power, purification power, and a strange suppressive authority that tried to calm, bind, and weaken everything it touched.","The participants on the pillars became serious.","Damian Voss narrowed his eyes slightly. \"She is revealing it from the start.\"","Orion Starfall smiled with interest. \"So that is her Pseudo Cosmic Path. It’s very strong.\"","Kaiden Voidmere watched quietly. \"A path combining radiance, sovereignty, and binding law.\"","Ervin’s abyss-like gaze focused on Rosaline. \"Not bad.\"","Rakan Thorne grinned. \"Good. This is what the final stage should look like.\"","Rosaline raised both hands, and behind her, a vast illusory kingdom appeared. It was made of golden-pink light, filled with towering palaces, radiant walls, floating crowns, and countless blooming flowers.","Above that luminous kingdom hovered a great rose-gold throne, and from that throne descended a gentle yet absolute pressure.","Rosaline’s voice rang across the stage.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path, Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary.\"","The moment the name was spoken, the entire battlefield transformed.","The central stage was covered by golden-pink light. Radiant petals fell in endless layers, and wherever they landed, the laws of the arena seemed to soften under Rosaline’s will.","Max immediately felt a suppressive force surrounding him. It was not violent. It did not try to crush him directly. Instead, it tried to seal his movements, purify his energy, suppress his killing intent, and weaken the sharpness of Dragonheart before he even drew it.","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly.","This Pseudo Cosmic Path was strong.","It was not the kind of path that destroyed everything with raw power. It was a sanctuary-type path that turned the battlefield itself into Rosaline’s domain.","Inside this Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary, her light strengthened herself, weakened enemies, purified hostile energy, sealed movements, and restrained violent intent. Against most opponents, this path would make them feel as if they were fighting an entire sacred kingdom by themselves.","Rosaline lifted one hand.","\"Dawn Edict, First Seal.\"","A rose-gold seal appeared above Max.","It descended instantly.","Max stepped aside, but the petals beneath his feet lit up and tried to bind his movement. The seal followed him, adjusting its position as if it had already locked onto his presence. At the same time, several radiant chains rose from the ground and wrapped toward his arms and legs.","Max raised his hand and shattered the first chain with physical strength.","However, the broken chain turned into petals and reformed again.","Rosaline’s voice remained calm. \"Inside my sanctuary, brute force alone will not end the binding.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"I noticed.\"","The seal descended again.","This time, Max drew Dragonheart.","A sharp sword light cut upward and split the seal in half, but the split halves dissolved into more radiant petals. Those petals surrounded Max from all directions, each one releasing soft light that tried to suppress his aura and dull his sword intent.","The crowd watched with widened eyes.","\"Rosaline’s Pseudo Cosmic Path is this strong?\"","\"She is actually forcing Max to defend.\"","\"It is not ordinary defense. Her path is suppressing him from every direction.\"","\"Against most people, this would already be enough to decide the battle.\"","Rosaline did not stop.","\"Dawn Edict, Second Seal.\"","\"Dawn Edict, Third Seal.\"","\"Dawn Edict, Fourth Seal.\"","Three more seals appeared around Max. One targeted his body, one targeted his energy, and one targeted his weapon. The three seals descended together, while the sanctuary behind Rosaline became brighter. The rose-gold throne released a majestic pressure, and for a moment, it looked as if Max had been surrounded by the laws of an entire sacred kingdom.","Max’s expression finally became more serious.","He could break the seals one by one with sword moves and raw strength, but that would drag the battle into Rosaline’s rhythm. Her path was designed to slow, seal, and suppress. The longer he stayed inside it without answering with an equal level of power, the more troublesome it would become.","\"So this is your full strength,\" Max said.","Rosaline’s gaze remained steady. \"Not everything. But enough to make you take me seriously.\"","Max smiled.","\"You have.\"","The moment his words fell, the air around him changed."]},{"number":1830,"title":"Chapter 1830: First Win!","paragraphs":["The lively golden-pink light surrounding him suddenly began to quiet down. The falling petals slowed. The radiant chains trembled. The seals descending toward him paused for a fraction of a breath as if something unseen had passed through the battlefield and cut away the emotions supporting their authority.","Dragonheart released a silent, cold aura.","Rosaline’s eyes sharpened.","Max did not use Divine King Punishment.","He did not use his dragon scales.","He did not use his Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline.","Instead, he raised Dragonheart and released the path he had just refined inside the reward chamber.","\"Emotion Severing Path.\"","The moment the words left his mouth, the golden-pink sanctuary trembled.","A dark-gray sword aura spread outward from Dragonheart. It was not flashy. It was not grand. It was not loud. But wherever it passed, the radiant petals stopped glowing. The chains lost their binding intent. The seals lost their sense of authority. Even the majestic pressure of the Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary seemed to grow still for a moment.","Rosaline’s expression changed.","Max stepped forward.","One slash.","The first seal was severed.","Not destroyed.","Severed.","Its connection to Rosaline’s sanctuary was cut, and the seal dissolved into powerless light.","Second slash.","The radiant chains surrounding Max lost the will to bind and collapsed.","Third slash.","The petals in front of him split apart, and a clear path opened through the Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary.","Rosaline immediately raised both hands.","\"Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary, Royal Mandate of Purifying Light.\"","The rose-gold throne behind her shone brilliantly, and an enormous pillar of golden-pink light descended toward Max. This was not a simple attack. It carried purification, sealing, and sovereign suppression together. It tried to purify the hostility in Max’s sword, seal the movement of Dragonheart, and suppress the Emotion Severing Path itself beneath Rosaline’s mandate.","Max looked up calmly.","Dragonheart moved.","The chamber training with the first owner of the Emotion Severing Path flashed through his mind for a brief instant. He remembered the warning that this path was volatile. He remembered that uncontrolled severing could devour the user. He remembered that the blade had to remain in his hand, not his heart. He remembered every word of the first user of Emotion Severing Path.","His eyes became colder, but not empty.","Then he slashed.","The silent sword light rose.","The Royal Mandate of Purifying Light split apart from the center.","The purification was severed from its target.","The sealing power was severed from its authority.","The sovereign suppression was severed from the throne behind Rosaline.","The massive pillar collapsed into scattered golden-pink fragments.","The entire arena went silent.","Rosaline’s face turned slightly pale, but she did not give up. The Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary behind her shook as she gathered its remaining power into one final attack. The radiant kingdom compressed into a single rose-gold crown above her head, and countless petals fused into a long spear of dawn light.","\"Final Dawn Edict, Sovereign Rose Spear.\"","The spear shot toward Max. It carried all the remaining pressure of the sanctuary.","Max stepped forward and raised Dragonheart with both hands.","\"Good attack.\"","Then he cut down.","Emotion Severing Path descended in a single silent line.","The Sovereign Rose Spear split apart.","The crown above Rosaline shattered.","The illusory kingdom behind her dimmed and vanished like a dream at sunrise.","Before Rosaline could gather another defense, Max’s figure appeared in front of her. Dragonheart stopped a finger’s width away from her throat. The cold severing aura did not touch her, but she could feel that if Max moved even slightly, the battle would end completely.","Rosaline looked at the blade near her throat, then slowly lowered her hands.","\"I surrender.\"","Angelina Valerius announced the result calmly.","[Winner: Max Morgan.]","[Rosaline Lunara Defeated.]","The screen above the arena immediately changed.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Max Morgan]","[Total Battles Fought: 1]","[Total Wins: 1]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Rosaline Lunara]","[Total Battles Fought: 1]","[Total Wins: 0]","The arena remained silent for several breaths before whispers began spreading from pillar to pillar.","\"She used her Pseudo Cosmic Path from the beginning and still lost.\"","\"Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary was terrifying. It suppressed the whole battlefield.\"","\"But Max’s sword cut through it.\"","\"That Emotion Severing Path is too strange. It did not just destroy her power. It cut the connection behind it.\"","Damian Voss looked at Max with sharp eyes, his grip tightening around his sword.","Orion Starfall’s smile deepened. \"So he finally showed it properly.\"","Rakan Thorne laughed softly. \"That sword path is nasty. I like it.\"","Kaiden Voidmere’s silver-gray eyes became thoughtful. \"It severed the authority behind the sanctuary. Very strange, how did Max do it?\"","Revona opened her eyes for a moment, and the void-colored light in her pupils flickered faintly.","Aurelian Lareth’s expression became cold when he saw Max defeat Rosaline’s light-based Pseudo Cosmic Path so cleanly. Selene Vaeloria also stared at him with a darker gaze, remembering very clearly how Max had used another path to crush her own strength before.","Morgana Starveil smiled faintly from her pillar, but this time, the smile carried more caution than amusement.","On the central stage, Rosaline looked at Max and sighed softly.","\"I knew anything less than my full strength would be useless, but I still did not expect you to break my sanctuary that cleanly.\"","Max lowered Dragonheart.","\"Your path is strong,\" he said calmly. \"Against most people here, it would be very troublesome.\"","Rosaline smiled faintly. \"But not against you.\"","Max did not deny it. If he had fought against her before the reward chamber then perhaps, her attacks might have pushed Max to use his other Pseudo Cosmic Paths but after he came out of the reward chamber, his Pseudo Cosmic Path of Emotion Severing Path was nearing perfection state.","Rosaline shook her head lightly, then the transfer light descended and returned her to her pillar.","Max also returned to his pillar a moment later.","The first battle of the final competitive stage had ended.","Max Morgan had started with one battle and one win."]},{"number":1831,"title":"Chapter 1831: Fin vs Serena","paragraphs":["Angelina Valerius looked across the twenty-five pillars after Max and Rosaline returned to their places.","The first battle of the final competitive stage had already set a heavy tone. Rosaline had used her Pseudo Cosmic Path from the very beginning, yet Max had still broken through it with Emotion Severing Path and taken the first win.","Because of that, the remaining participants no longer looked at this round as a simple sequence of battles. If even the first match had reached the level of Pseudo Cosmic Paths, then the battles that followed would only become more intense.","Angelina raised her hand.","\"The second battle of the final competitive stage will now begin.\"","The massive screen of light above the arena flickered, and two names appeared in bright golden text.","[Final Competitive Stage, Battle Two]","[Fin Arclight vs Seren Frostveil]","The moment the names appeared, the arena grew quiet again.","Fin Arclight was not considered one of the absolute peak monsters like Damian, Rakan, Orion, Kaiden, or Max, but everyone knew he was dangerous. His Pale Eclipse Path had already shown its ability to weaken perception, dull energy flow, and trap opponents inside a strange gray-white field where their senses could no longer be trusted.","Seren Frostveil was also not simple. She had reached the final twenty-five with her refined ice control and calm battle judgment. Her frost techniques were not the most explosive, but they were precise, layered, and extremely difficult to break once she gained control of the battlefield. Against a direct attacker, she could slowly freeze the rhythm of the fight until the opponent had nowhere left to move.","Angelina looked toward the two pillars.","\"Fin Arclight. Seren Frostveil. Enter the stage.\"","Two beams of light descended.","Fin appeared on one side of the central stage, dressed in pale robes with gray-white moonlight gathering around him. His expression was cold and faintly arrogant, but after everything that had happened with Max, his arrogance had become more restrained than before.","Seren appeared opposite him in a robe of pale-blue and white, her ice spear resting lightly in her hand. Frost mist gathered beneath her feet the moment she arrived, but it did not spread too far yet. She looked at Fin calmly, clearly understanding that this would not be an easy battle.","Fin smiled faintly. \"You are unlucky.\"","Seren’s expression did not change. \"People who say that usually want to hide their own uneasiness.\"","Fin’s smile faded slightly.","Angelina’s voice rang out.","[Battle Begins.]","Fin moved first.","Gray-white light spread from beneath his feet, forming a pale crescent moon behind him. The light did not rush toward Seren in a straight line. Instead, it spread through the arena like a quiet eclipse, dimming the brilliance of the stage and making the air feel colder and heavier.","\"Pale Eclipse Field.\"","The moment the field expanded, Seren’s frost mist trembled.","Her eyes narrowed slightly.","Within the Pale Eclipse Field, her perception became distorted. The distance between her and Fin seemed to stretch and shrink at the same time. His figure flickered in and out of sight, sometimes appearing near, sometimes far, and sometimes as several overlapping shadows. Even the flow of her energy became slightly sluggish, as if her body had been placed under moonlight that weakened movement, senses, and reaction.","Fin raised one hand.","Several pale crescent blades appeared in the air and shot toward Seren from different directions.","Seren stepped back and spun her ice spear.","Frost walls rose around her, blocking the first wave of crescent blades, but the moment those blades touched the ice, they did not explode. They slipped through the surface like pale moonlight passing through thin clouds, cutting toward her body from behind the wall.","Seren’s eyes sharpened.","She tapped the ground with her spear.","\"Ice Mirror Formation.\"","Several ice mirrors appeared around her and reflected her body in different positions. The crescent blades passed through one reflection after another, but they failed to strike her real body. Seren appeared on the left side of the stage and thrust her spear forward. A dragon of frost rushed toward Fin, freezing everything in its path.","Fin smiled coldly and stepped into the eclipse light.","His body blurred.","The frost dragon passed through him and struck only an afterimage.","From the pillars, several participants watched with serious eyes.","\"This matchup is troublesome.\"","\"Fin’s Pale Eclipse Field distorts perception, but Seren’s ice mirrors can create false positions too.\"","\"They are both trying to make the other lose track of the real body.\"","Max stood on his pillar and watched calmly.","Fin’s path was indeed annoying. It was not overwhelming like Selene’s light or sharp like Damian’s sword, but it created uncertainty. In a fight, uncertainty was dangerous because even one wrong judgment could decide the result.","On the stage, Seren suddenly raised her spear high.","Frost energy erupted from beneath her feet and spread outward in circles, freezing the ground, the air, and even parts of the gray-white eclipse light. Fin’s expression changed slightly as his Pale Eclipse Field slowed down for the first time.","Seren spoke calmly.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path, Frozen World Stillness.\"","The entire arena seemed to drop into a frozen silence.","A vast icy world appeared behind Seren. There were endless frozen mountains, rivers locked beneath transparent ice, snowstorms suspended in midair, and a pale-blue moon hanging over a silent winter kingdom. This was not ordinary frost. It was a path that tried to freeze movement, energy, sound, and even the rhythm of thought.","The Pale Eclipse Field trembled under the pressure.","Fin’s eyes narrowed. \"So you had hidden this much.\"","Seren did not answer.","She thrust her spear forward.","The frozen world behind her responded.","Cold silence spread across the stage, and Fin’s eclipse light slowed visibly. His afterimages became fewer, his crescent blades became duller, and the distorted space around him began to freeze into clear lines. For the first time, his real body was forced to reveal itself.","A wave of surprise moved through the pillars.","\"She forced Fin out of hiding.\"","\"Frozen World Stillness can freeze even the distortion inside his field.\"","\"Seren is stronger than I thought.\"","Fin’s expression became ugly.","Then he smiled coldly.","\"Fine. Since you are using yours, I will use mine properly too.\"","The pale crescent moon behind Fin darkened.","Gray-white light turned deeper, and the entire stage seemed to enter an eclipse where the moon devoured the sun. His aura spread outward sharply, and a strange pressure fell upon the frozen world behind Seren.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path, Pale Eclipse Burial.\""]},{"number":1832,"title":"Chapter 1832: A Hard Fought Win","paragraphs":["The moment the name rang out, the field changed completely.","An enormous pale moon appeared above the arena, half-covered by a black shadow. Beneath that moon, everything seemed to lose color. The frozen mountains behind Seren dimmed. The suspended snowstorms turned gray. Even the pale-blue moon in her frozen world began to look as if it was being swallowed by an eclipse.","Fin raised his hand.","\"Eclipse Burial Blade.\"","A long crescent blade descended from the darkened moon.","Seren’s expression became serious.","She lifted her spear and released a storm of frozen light. The frozen world behind her pushed back against the eclipse, and countless ice spears rose into the sky to meet the descending blade.","The two Pseudo Cosmic Paths collided.","This time, the central stage shook violently.","The arena barrier lit up, and the runes beneath the stage blazed brightly to contain the impact. Pale eclipse light and frozen stillness devoured each other in waves. Fin’s path tried to bury Seren’s frozen world in a lightless eclipse, while Seren’s path tried to freeze the eclipse itself and stop its descent.","For a while, neither side gained a clear advantage.","Then Fin suddenly vanished.","Seren’s eyes narrowed.","A pale eclipse mark appeared beneath her feet.","Her Frozen World Stillness instantly reacted, freezing the mark before it could fully activate, but Fin appeared behind her at that same moment. His hand held a thin crescent blade of pale light aimed at the back of her neck.","Seren turned quickly and raised her spear.","Clang!","The crescent blade struck the spear.","Fin pressed forward.","Seren retreated half a step, then released a burst of frozen silence from her body. Fin’s arm stiffened slightly, and Seren used that opening to counter with a thrust toward his chest. Fin avoided it narrowly, but frost still spread across his shoulder.","Both separated at the same time.","For the first time, both of them looked slightly exhausted.","Max watched the battle with interest.","Seren’s Pseudo Cosmic Path was stronger than he had expected. If she fought someone who relied heavily on speed, sound, or energy flow, Frozen World Stillness would be extremely troublesome. However, Fin’s Pale Eclipse Burial was also dangerous because it could distort, bury, and weaken a battlefield from the outside in.","On the stage, Fin’s expression became colder.","He lifted both hands.","The pale eclipse moon above him darkened further, and several burial blades formed around it.","Seren’s face turned pale, but she also raised her spear with both hands. The frozen world behind her compressed into a single massive ice spear, its surface covered in pale-blue runes of stillness.","Fin spoke first.","\"Pale Eclipse Burial, Moonless Descent.\"","Seren answered at the same time.","\"Frozen World Stillness, Eternal Ice Spear.\"","The two strongest attacks descended and rose at once.","The moonless eclipse light fell from above, while the eternal ice spear shot upward from below. When the two collided, the center of the arena was swallowed by gray-white and pale-blue light. The impact was not as destructive as Max and Rosaline’s clash, but it was more suffocating. One power tried to bury the world in a pale eclipse, while the other tried to freeze that burial forever.","The collision lasted several breaths.","Then a crack appeared in the Eternal Ice Spear.","Seren’s expression changed.","Fin gritted his teeth and poured more power into his attack.","The Moonless Descent pushed downward inch by inch, finally breaking the ice spear apart. However, the Frozen World Stillness did not disappear without effect. The broken ice released one final burst of stillness, freezing most of the eclipse light and weakening its force before it could fully descend.","Even so, enough of the attack remained.","The weakened Moonless Descent struck Seren’s defense and forced her to one knee.","Her ice spear cracked.","Fin landed several meters away, breathing heavily but still standing.","Angelina Valerius looked at Seren.","Seren tried to stand, but the pale eclipse mark on her body flickered, suppressing her energy flow. After a few breaths, she lowered her head and sighed softly.","\"I surrender.\"","Angelina announced the result.","[Winner: Fin Arclight.]","[Seren Frostveil Defeated.]","The giant screen above the arena changed immediately.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Fin Arclight]","[Total Battles Fought: 1]","[Total Wins: 1]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Seren Frostveil]","[Total Battles Fought: 1]","[Total Wins: 0]","The arena remained quiet for a moment before discussions began.","\"That was close.\"","\"Seren actually forced Fin to use his Pseudo Cosmic Path properly.\"","\"She almost froze his eclipse.\"","\"But Fin’s path still won in the end.\"","\"Both of them are strong enough to threaten many people here.\"","Max watched Fin return to his pillar.","Fin looked tired, but his gaze still carried pride. Seren returned to her own pillar with a pale expression, clearly affected by the loss, but she had forced out Fin’s true path and shown that she belonged among the final twenty-five.","Max’s eyes remained thoughtful.","’Pale Eclipse Burial,’ he thought. ’It is stronger than the version he used before, but not impossible to break.’","His gaze shifted to Seren.","’Frozen World Stillness is also troublesome. If she gains momentum, even movement and energy flow can be slowed.’","The second battle had made one thing clear.","The final competitive stage would not only be about the absolute monsters at the top.","Even the participants who seemed slightly below them had Pseudo Cosmic Paths capable of forcing serious battles.","Angelina Valerius looked at the result of the second battle for a moment before raising her hand again.","The massive screen above the arena flickered, and the names of the remaining twenty-five participants began to rotate once more. After Max defeated Rosaline and Fin defeated Seren, the atmosphere had become even heavier.","Everyone had already understood that in this final competitive stage, even the early battles could force out Pseudo Cosmic Paths, and no one could assume that a famous name would win without paying any price.","Angelina’s calm voice spread across the arena.","\"The third battle of the final competitive stage will now begin.\"","The rotating names slowed down.","Two names enlarged at the center of the screen.","[Final Competitive Stage, Battle Three]","[Aurelian Lareth vs Morgana Starveil]"]},{"number":1833,"title":"Chapter 1833: Divine Son vs Witch","paragraphs":["The moment those names appeared, the entire arena reacted.","Aurelian Lareth was the Divine Son of the second elven faction, the vessel who had received Max’s stolen Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline.","Morgana Starveil was the witch genius from Stellar Templar, a dangerous woman whose curses had already defeated multiple opponents in extremely strange ways. Both of them were important figures, and both had already been marked by Max in different ways.","Max’s gaze immediately turned cold when he saw Aurelian’s name.","Morgana’s smile, on the other hand, became faintly playful.","\"How troublesome,\" she said softly from her pillar. \"I thought I would get to play with someone easier first.\"","Aurelian looked at her from across the arena with calm golden eyes.","\"You are not qualified to call this troublesome yet.\"","Morgana’s smile deepened, but there was a trace of danger in her eyes. \"Divine Son of the second faction, you sound even more unpleasant than the rumors.\"","Angelina raised her hand.","\"Aurelian Lareth. Morgana Starveil. Enter the stage.\"","Two beams of light descended.","Aurelian appeared on one side of the central stage, his white-gold robes spotless, his long golden hair falling behind him, and a sacred radiance flowing faintly around his body. He did not immediately release overwhelming pressure, yet his presence was heavy enough to make many participants narrow their eyes.","Morgana appeared opposite him, wearing her black-violet dress and witch hat, her midnight-blue hair moving gently as purple-black starlight gathered around her fingers. Her expression still carried a smile, but her eyes had already become serious.","She knew very well that Aurelian was not an opponent she could play with casually.","Angelina’s voice rang out.","[Battle Begins.]","Morgana moved first.","She raised her hand, and seven purple-black stars appeared behind her. Threads of curse energy shot outward from those stars, spreading across the battlefield like a spiderweb woven from night.","At the same time, tiny witch symbols began appearing beneath Aurelian’s feet, each one trying to connect to his shadow, his breath, his spiritual energy, and even the rhythm of his heartbeat.","\"Stellar Witchcraft, Sevenfold Curse Thread.\"","Aurelian did not move.","Golden-white light spread from his body.","The curse threads closest to him began to burn.","Morgana’s eyes narrowed slightly. \"As expected, ordinary curses are useless against that light.\"","Aurelian raised his hand.","A beam of Heavenly Luminance light shot forward.","Morgana’s figure shattered like a reflection, and the real her appeared several dozen meters away. The shattered reflection turned into a curse mirror that absorbed part of the luminance beam and reflected it back in a twisted purple-black form.","\"Stellar Witchcraft, Mirror Curse Reversal.\"","The cursed light flew back toward Aurelian.","Aurelian’s expression remained indifferent.","He lifted one finger, and the cursed light dissolved before reaching him.","\"Small tricks.\"","Morgana laughed softly. \"Small tricks can still kill arrogant men.\"","Her hands moved quickly.","More curse mirrors appeared in the air. Some reflected light. Some distorted distance. Some showed false versions of Aurelian standing in different positions. Purple-black star marks spread across the stage, and within a few breaths, the battlefield seemed to have become Morgana’s witchcraft field.","Aurelian finally took one step forward.","The divine light around him brightened.","Wherever he stepped, the curse symbols on the ground burned away.","Morgana’s smile faded slightly.","The spectators on the pillars watched closely.","\"Morgana’s curses are being purified.\"","\"That is not ordinary light. Aurelian’s Heavenly Luminance power directly counters many curse techniques.\"","\"But Morgana is not weak. She has not used her Pseudo Cosmic Path yet.\"","Max watched silently.","His gaze was fixed mostly on Aurelian.","Every time Aurelian used that golden-white light, Max could feel a faint reaction from his own Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline. It was disgust. Rejection. A deep instinctive hatred toward something that should never have belonged to Aurelian in the first place.","Aurelian lifted his palm.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Sacred Spear Rain.\"","Dozens of golden-white spears appeared above the stage and descended toward Morgana.","Morgana raised both hands.","\"Stellar Witchcraft, Thousand Night Veil.\"","A curtain of black-violet stars unfolded around her. The luminance spears struck the veil, and each impact caused a burst of golden and purple light. For a few breaths, the veil held. Then cracks began appearing across it.","Morgana clicked her tongue.","\"Fine. Since gentle methods will not work, let us be a little rude.\"","The air around her changed.","The purple-black stars behind her expanded into a vast starry sky. Countless witch symbols floated within that sky, forming a circle of curses around a dark moon. A cold and ancient aura spread from Morgana’s body, and several participants immediately felt uncomfortable, as if invisible fingers had brushed against their souls.","Morgana’s voice became soft and dangerous.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path, Star-Curse Labyrinth.\"","The moment the path appeared, the battlefield changed.","Aurelian was no longer standing on the central stage alone. Around him, countless starry corridors appeared, each one filled with curse mirrors, witch symbols, and dark moonlight. The space within the arena did not truly expand, but perception, direction, and causality inside the field became twisted. Every step could lead into a curse.","Every attack could be reflected. Every attempt to break through could become a medium for another spell.","Several participants became solemn.","Orion Starfall’s smile turned thoughtful. \"That path is nasty.\"","Kaiden Voidmere said calmly, \"It distorts direction through curse connection, not space alone.\"","Ervin’s eyes narrowed slightly. \"If one loses the first rhythm, it becomes difficult to escape.\"","Rakan Thorne grinned. \"So I just smash everything.\"","Damian Voss glanced at him. \"If you smash the wrong mirror, you may curse yourself.\"","Rakan laughed. \"Then I smash the curse too.\"","Inside the Star-Curse Labyrinth, Morgana’s voice echoed from every direction.","\"Divine Son, let me see if your light can purify a path made of curses.\"","Hundreds of curse mirrors lit up.","From each mirror, a different attack shot toward Aurelian. Some were shadow blades. Some were curse needles. Some were reflected versions of his own luminance spears. Some were invisible threads aimed at his soul. Some tried to mark his bloodline directly."]},{"number":1834,"title":"Chapter 1834: Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion","paragraphs":["Aurelian’s eyes became colder.","For the first time, his calm expression changed.","A golden-white crown slowly appeared above his head.","The moment the crown appeared, Max’s expression turned colder.","His bloodline reacted more strongly.","Aurelian raised his hand, and behind him, an enormous figure of divine radiance began to appear. It was not the same as Selene’s Heavenly Luminance Queen Avatar. This one was more masculine, more domineering, and filled with a sacred authority that seemed to stand above all lesser light.","Aurelian spoke calmly.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path, Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion.\"","Golden-white light exploded outward.","The Star-Curse Labyrinth trembled violently.","A divine kingdom of light spread behind Aurelian, filled with radiant pillars, sacred halls, and a golden throne beneath an endless sun.","The power of this path was different from Rosaline’s Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary. Rosaline’s path was gentle, sealing, purifying, and suppressive. Aurelian’s path was far more domineering. It did not only purify. It judged, claimed, and overruled.","The curse mirrors closest to Aurelian cracked.","Morgana’s expression became serious.","\"Dominion-type Pseudo Cosmic Path.\"","Aurelian looked at her through the collapsing labyrinth.","\"Your curses have no authority before my light.\"","He raised his hand.","\"Divine Dominion, Luminance Decree.\"","A golden decree appeared above the stage.","The moment it opened, countless words of light descended like law.","The curse mirrors shattered one after another.","The starry corridors burned.","The dark moon in Morgana’s path dimmed slightly.","Morgana’s face turned pale, but she gritted her teeth and pressed both hands together.","\"Star-Curse Labyrinth, Nameless Witch Burial.\"","All the remaining curse mirrors broke at once, and from their fragments emerged a giant black-violet witch coffin covered in star symbols. The coffin opened toward Aurelian, releasing a terrifying curse meant to bury his light, seal his body, and drag his soul into the labyrinth’s deepest layer.","Aurelian’s eyes flashed.","The golden crown above his head shone brighter.","\"Divine Dominion, Sacred Sun Judgment.\"","The endless sun behind him released a pillar of light.","The pillar struck the witch coffin directly.","For several breaths, the coffin resisted. Curse symbols crawled across the light, trying to contaminate it, while sacred radiance burned them away layer by layer. The clash shook the central stage, forcing the arena barrier to flare brightly.","Then the coffin cracked.","Morgana’s eyes narrowed.","The Sacred Sun Judgment pierced through the coffin and stopped just before her chest. The remaining light did not touch her body, but its pressure alone forced her to stumble back, blood flowing from the corner of her lips.","Aurelian lowered his hand.","The Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion still shone behind him.","\"Surrender.\"","Morgana stared at him for a few breaths.","Her smile returned slowly, though it looked colder than before.","\"How boring. Light-type opponents really are the worst.\"","Aurelian’s expression remained calm. \"You lost.\"","Morgana wiped the blood from her lips and lowered her hand.","\"I surrender.\"","Angelina Valerius announced the result.","[Winner: Aurelian Lareth.]","[Morgana Starveil Defeated.]","The screen above the arena changed immediately.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Aurelian Lareth]","[Total Battles Fought: 1]","[Total Wins: 1]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Morgana Starveil]","[Total Battles Fought: 1]","[Total Wins: 0]","The arena remained quiet for a moment.","This battle had not been one-sided. Morgana’s Star-Curse Labyrinth had clearly forced Aurelian to reveal his own Pseudo Cosmic Path, and that alone proved her strength. However, Aurelian’s Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion had suppressed her curse path with frightening authority.","On his pillar, Max watched Aurelian silently.","His gaze was colder than before.","’Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion,’ Max thought. ’So that is the Pseudo Cosmic Path he built using what was stolen from me.’","The feeling was different from Selene’s Heavenly Luminance Genesis. Selene’s path felt pure, noble, and deeply rooted in her own bloodline.","Aurelian’s path was powerful, but to Max, it felt wrong. It was as if a stolen seed had been forcefully grown into a divine tree, beautiful on the outside but carrying a scent that made his bloodline reject it instinctively.","Aurelian returned to his pillar.","Before the light around him faded, he looked at Max.","Their gazes met.","Aurelian smiled faintly.","Max did not smile back.","Morgana also returned to her pillar, her face slightly pale but her eyes still sharp. She looked annoyed rather than broken. Losing one battle in this round did not eliminate her, but it had forced her to expose far more than she wanted.","Orion Starfall glanced between Aurelian and Max, then smiled with interest.","\"This final stage is getting better.\"","Damian Voss remained silent, but his eyes had become sharper.","Rakan Thorne laughed softly. \"Good. That guy is worth punching.\"","Kaiden Voidmere looked at Aurelian’s fading divine kingdom and said calmly, \"That path is strong, but not flawless.\"","Revona’s eyes opened slightly, and the void-colored light in them flickered once before vanishing again.","After Aurelian Lareth and Morgana Starveil returned to their pillars, the weight of the final competitive stage became even clearer.","Three battles had already passed, and each of them had revealed something important. Max had defeated Rosaline’s Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary with Emotion Severing Path, Fin had barely overcome Seren’s Frozen World Stillness with his Pale Eclipse Burial, and Aurelian had suppressed Morgana’s Star-Curse Labyrinth with his Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion.","No one could call this stage ordinary anymore. Every participant among the final twenty-five carried enough strength to shock the outside world, but even among them, the distance between top geniuses and the rest was gradually becoming visible.","Angelina Valerius raised her hand again.","\"The fourth battle of the final competitive stage will now begin.\"","The screen of light above the arena spun briefly before stopping.","[Final Competitive Stage, Battle Four]","[Damian Voss vs Corvin Nightsteel]","Corvin Nightsteel’s expression became extremely heavy the moment his name appeared opposite Damian’s.","When the battle began, Corvin immediately used his strongest defensive technique, causing countless black metal plates to overlap around him like a fortress.","Damian drew his sword once. A single sword light passed through the stage, and the black metal fortress split cleanly from top to bottom. Corvin froze in place, his heavy sword cut in half, while Damian’s blade stopped at his throat before he could launch his next attack.","Angelina announced the result without hesitation.","[Winner: Damian Voss.]","[Corvin Nightsteel Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Damian Voss]","[Total Battles Fought: 1]","[Total Wins: 1]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Corvin Nightsteel]","[Total Battles Fought: 1]","[Total Wins: 0]"]},{"number":1835,"title":"Chapter 1835: Ervin vs Selene","paragraphs":["Damian returned to his pillar without showing even a trace of excitement, and the entire arena understood that he still had not revealed anything important. His sword was already enough to suppress most people here.","Angelina raised her hand again.","[Final Competitive Stage, Battle Five]","[Rakan Thorne vs Vaela Sunspire]","Vaela Sunspire was a talented flame cultivator whose sunfire had burned through several difficult opponents in earlier rounds. She knew Rakan’s strength, so the moment the battle began, she spread a blazing sun domain across the stage and sent waves of golden flame toward him from all directions. Rakan did not dodge. He walked forward through the fire, his body glowing with a brutal war aura, and every step shattered the flames pressing against him.","Vaela gritted her teeth and condensed her sunfire into a blazing spear, but before she could throw it, Rakan had already reached her. His fist stopped inches from her face, and the wind pressure alone tore apart the sunfire spear in her hand.","Vaela’s face turned pale.","\"I surrender.\"","[Winner: Rakan Thorne.]","[Vaela Sunspire Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Rakan Thorne]","[Total Battles Fought: 1]","[Total Wins: 1]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Vaela Sunspire]","[Total Battles Fought: 1]","[Total Wins: 0]","Rakan returned to his pillar with a grin, looking disappointed that the battle had ended so quickly. Max watched him quietly, once again noting how terrifying Rakan’s pure body strength was. Against someone like him, ordinary elemental power became almost meaningless if it could not stop his advance.","Angelina did not delay.","[Final Competitive Stage, Battle Six]","[Orion Starfall vs Hadeon Granite]","Hadeon Granite had a defensive foundation strong enough to survive many attacks, but when he stood opposite Orion Starfall, his expression showed no confidence. He covered his body in layers of stone armor and raised several walls of earth around himself, clearly intending to stall the battle and observe Orion’s strength.","Orion smiled faintly and lifted one hand.","Two star marks on his body lit up.","The first star beam descended and shattered the outer earth walls. The second star beam pierced through the remaining stone armor and stopped in front of Hadeon’s chest. Hadeon stared down at the light hovering before him, then looked up at Orion with a bitter expression.","\"I surrender.\"","[Winner: Orion Starfall.]","[Hadeon Granite Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Orion Starfall]","[Total Battles Fought: 1]","[Total Wins: 1]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Hadeon Granite]","[Total Battles Fought: 1]","[Total Wins: 0]","Orion returned to his pillar, still wearing that relaxed smile, but no one felt relaxed while looking at him. He had only used two star marks this time, and yet the result had been decided instantly.","The seventh battle followed soon after.","[Final Competitive Stage, Battle Seven]","[Kaiden Voidmere vs Aurelia Flamecrest]","Aurelia Flamecrest’s expression became grim when she saw Kaiden’s name. She had already shown powerful sunfire before, but Kaiden’s void power was an entirely different problem. When the battle began, Aurelia immediately released a wide storm of golden flame, trying to fill the stage so Kaiden would have no room to appear behind her.","Kaiden simply raised his hand.","The space before him folded inward.","A large portion of the sunfire vanished into the void.","Aurelia tried to retreat, but the road behind her suddenly disappeared. Her movement technique failed halfway, and Kaiden appeared at her side with one finger pointed at her neck. The battle ended before her strongest flame could even gather.","[Winner: Kaiden Voidmere.]","[Aurelia Flamecrest Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Kaiden Voidmere]","[Total Battles Fought: 1]","[Total Wins: 1]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Aurelia Flamecrest]","[Total Battles Fought: 1]","[Total Wins: 0]","Max’s gaze lingered on Kaiden for a moment. Kaiden’s void power was too clean. He did not just dodge attacks or move through space. He removed the path of movement itself, making ordinary techniques collapse before they could finish.","The eighth battle came quickly.","[Final Competitive Stage, Battle Eight]","[Revona vs Yelric Flamehorn]","Yelric Flamehorn was a horned warrior with a violent fire-attribute body. The moment the battle began, he transformed into a blazing demon-like figure and charged forward with a flaming halberd. His attack was strong enough to make the stage tremble, but Revona only opened her Void Origin Eyes.","The flames vanished first.","Then the halberd force vanished.","Then the blazing armor around Yelric’s body dimmed as if its power had been erased layer by layer. Yelric stopped in shock, and before he could gather another attack, Revona had already appeared in front of him with one finger raised toward his forehead.","Yelric clenched his teeth, but there was nothing he could do.","\"I surrender.\"","[Winner: Revona.]","[Yelric Flamehorn Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Revona]","[Total Battles Fought: 1]","[Total Wins: 1]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Yelric Flamehorn]","[Total Battles Fought: 1]","[Total Wins: 0]","The arena once again fell into a heavy silence.","Revona’s victory was clean, quiet, and deeply unsettling. Every time her Void Origin Eyes erased an attack, the other participants felt as if they were watching combat itself become meaningless. Max watched her with calm seriousness. He had already understood that her eyes had awakened far beyond what they had shown in their earlier battle.","Angelina continued without changing her expression.","[Final Competitive Stage, Battle Nine]","[Morgana Starveil vs Darius Stoneveil]","Morgana had just lost to Aurelian, but that loss clearly had not broken her confidence. Darius Stoneveil relied on thick stone defenses and layered barriers, but against Morgana, those defenses became a burden. She used one curse to mark the cracks in his stone armor, another curse to make those cracks widen, and a third curse to turn his own defensive energy against him.","Darius tried to endure, but the more power he poured into his defenses, the faster the curse spread.","In the end, Morgana stood before him with a purple-black star hovering above his head.","\"Surrender before your armor crushes you from the inside,\" she said sweetly.","Darius’s face turned pale.","\"I surrender.\"","[Winner: Morgana Starveil.]","[Darius Stoneveil Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Morgana Starveil]","[Total Battles Fought: 2]","[Total Wins: 1]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Darius Stoneveil]","[Total Battles Fought: 1]","[Total Wins: 0]","Morgana returned to her pillar with her smile restored, though her eyes still glanced toward Aurelian once before shifting toward Max. Her first loss had not eliminated her, and now she had begun recovering her record.","More battles passed in quick succession.","Rosaline fought a hidden spear genius from a minor divine force and won cleanly with her radiant seals, never needing to release Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary again. Fin Arclight fought a sound-attribute participant and trapped him inside Pale Eclipse light until his senses collapsed.","Seren Frostveil recovered from her loss and defeated a beast-blooded warrior by freezing his movement step by step. Several lesser-known participants also collected their first wins against others of similar strength, but whenever they looked toward the true monsters standing on the brightest pillars, their expressions remained heavy.","The records above the arena continued updating after every result, making the pressure even more visible.","Some names already had clean victories.","Some had one loss.","Some had begun to fall behind.","And this was only the beginning.","Moreover Max noticed that the randomizer this time was completely random. Some had fought two battles and some hadn’t even done their first battle.","’It seems like in this final round one can match with anyone here.’ Max thought silently.","Angelina Valerius raised her hand once more, and the lights above the arena gathered into the next pairing.","The names slowed.","Then two of them enlarged.","[Final Competitive Stage, Battle Fourteen]","[Ervin vs Selene Vaeloria]","The moment those names appeared, the arena became quiet again.","Selene Vaeloria opened her eyes from her pillar, her white-gold hair shining faintly as cold pride returned to her face. Ervin stood on another pillar, black spear in hand, his abyss-like aura still calm and unreadable.","Max’s gaze sharpened slightly.","This battle would not be simple.","Angelina looked toward both of them and spoke calmly.","\"Ervin. Selene Vaeloria. Enter the stage.\""]},{"number":1836,"title":"Chapter 1836: A Good Battle","paragraphs":["Two beams of light descended at the same time.","Ervin appeared on one side of the central stage with his black spear resting lightly in his hand, his posture relaxed and his expression calm. He did not look excited, nervous, or arrogant. He simply stood there like a shadow beneath deep water, quiet enough to seem harmless at first glance, yet deep enough to make anyone with true perception feel uneasy.","Selene Vaeloria appeared opposite him.","Her white-gold hair fell behind her like a river of light, and her eyes carried the cold pride of the Divine Daughter of the second elven faction. Even after losing to Max near the Witch God Tree, she had not lost her confidence completely.","She was still Selene Vaeloria. She was still one of the most carefully raised geniuses of the second faction. Her Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline was pure, her foundation was terrifying, and her Pseudo Cosmic Path had already proven strong enough to force countless participants to lower their heads.","The moment she stepped onto the stage, the aura around her brightened.","Ervin looked at her quietly.","Selene also studied him for a few breaths.","\"I know you are strong,\" she said coldly. \"But I am not Morgana, and I am not one of those people you can defeat with one hidden spear thrust.\"","Ervin smiled faintly. \"Good. Then this battle might be worth fighting.\"","Selene’s eyes narrowed.","Angelina Valerius raised her hand.","[Battle Begins.]","Selene attacked first.","Golden-white light burst from her body, forming dozens of radiant swords in the air. Each sword carried a trace of Heavenly Luminance power, sharp, pure, and oppressive. With a slight movement of her fingers, all the swords shot toward Ervin from different angles.","Ervin stepped forward.","His spear moved.","It was only a simple thrust, yet the spear tip seemed to pass through the gaps between the incoming radiant swords with impossible precision. One thrust broke three swords. A turn of the shaft deflected five more. A sweep of the spear scattered a dozen beams of light before they could reach him.","Selene’s expression did not change.","She raised her hand again.","\"Luminance Sword Rain.\"","Hundreds of radiant swords appeared above the stage, far denser and more powerful than the first wave. They fell like a divine storm, covering every possible path of movement around Ervin. The attack was fast enough to make several participants narrow their eyes.","Ervin did not retreat.","He rotated his spear once, and dark energy spread from the spearhead in a thin circle.","The first wave of swords struck the circle and bent away slightly. The second wave pressed harder, forcing Ervin to finally move his feet. His body flickered through the sword rain, not with speed like Max’s Vein of Speed, nor with spatial distortion like Kaiden’s void movement, but with a strange sense of depth, as if he was stepping into shadows between moments.","He passed through the sword rain and arrived ten meters closer to Selene.","Selene’s eyes sharpened.","\"Solar Luminance Palm.\"","A giant golden palm condensed in front of her and struck forward with majestic force. The palm carried heat, light, and suppressive pressure together, making the air tremble as it descended toward Ervin.","Ervin raised his spear with one hand.","A dark point appeared at the tip.","Then he thrust.","The spear tip pierced into the center of the golden palm. For a moment, the palm and spear stood in a deadlock. Then the darkness at the spear tip began spreading through the palm like ink dissolving inside clear water. The golden light dimmed from the center outward, and the entire palm collapsed before reaching him.","A murmur spread across the pillars.","\"What kind of spear force is that?\"","\"It is not simple darkness.\"","\"It devoured part of Selene’s luminance power.\"","Selene finally took one step forward.","The light behind her rose higher.","\"Heavenly Wheel of Radiant Execution.\"","A massive golden wheel appeared above her, its edges covered in countless sharp rays of light. The wheel began rotating, and the sound of its movement filled the arena like divine law grinding against the world. Radiant pressure descended upon Ervin, trying to lock his body in place.","Ervin’s expression became slightly more serious.","The Heavenly Wheel shot forward.","He raised his spear horizontally and blocked.","Boom!","The impact forced him backward for the first time.","His feet slid across the stage, leaving two long marks on the dark-gold stone. The heavenly wheel pressed against his spear, spinning violently as sparks of golden light and dark energy exploded between them.","Selene’s eyes brightened.","She clenched her hand.","The heavenly wheel split into six smaller wheels, each one attacking Ervin from a different direction. This time, Ervin could no longer block them all with simple spear movement. His body blurred, his spear flickered, and several dark spear shadows appeared around him. The six wheels clashed with those spear shadows again and again, forcing him to retreat step by step.","On the pillars, Aurelian Lareth watched with a calm expression.","\"She has improved her control,\" he said softly.","Max also watched carefully.","Selene was indeed strong. She had not used her Pseudo Cosmic Path yet, but her ordinary techniques were already enough to suppress most geniuses among the final twenty-five. If Ervin were an ordinary spear user, he would have already been cut apart by the heavenly wheels.","However, Ervin was not ordinary.","His spear suddenly changed.","The dark spear shadows around him stopped defending and turned into one straight line.","Ervin stepped forward instead of retreating.","His spear pierced through the gap between two wheels, then curved strangely and struck the inner edge of the third. The balance between the six heavenly wheels broke at once. The six wheels collided with each other in midair and exploded into golden fragments.","Selene’s gaze became colder.","\"So you were waiting for the rhythm.\"","Ervin smiled faintly. \"Your attacks are strong, but they still have structure.\"","Selene’s expression sank.","Behind her, a majestic female figure of divine radiance began to appear.","The pressure around the stage increased.","\"Heavenly Luminance Queen Avatar.\"","The radiant avatar rose behind Selene, noble and overwhelming, with a crown of light above its head and a spear of pure luminance in its hand. The moment it appeared, Selene’s aura rose sharply. The golden-white light around her became far more solid, and the pressure of her bloodline spread across the stage like a divine decree."]},{"number":1837,"title":"Chapter 1837: Abyssal Origin Descent!","paragraphs":["Several participants became serious.","\"She is using the Queen Avatar already.\"","\"Against Max, she used this before going into her Pseudo Cosmic Path.\"","\"This Ervin is forcing her faster than expected.\"","Selene lifted her hand.","The avatar behind her lifted its spear.","\"Queen’s Divine Spear.\"","A spear of Heavenly Luminance shot toward Ervin.","This attack was different from the previous ones. It carried a noble, commanding force that tried to pierce through defense, energy, and will at the same time. Ervin’s eyes finally sharpened.","He held his black spear with both hands.","Darkness gathered around him.","Then he thrust forward.","The two spears collided.","The impact shook the arena barrier.","Ervin’s body trembled slightly, and the ground beneath his feet cracked. Selene’s light pressed forward fiercely, trying to overwhelm him with the purity of the Queen Avatar. The black spear in Ervin’s hand bent slightly under the pressure, but Ervin’s gaze remained calm.","A faint abyssal aura rose behind him.","It was not large.","It was not showy.","But the moment it appeared, Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body sensed something strange.","Depth.","An almost impossible depth.","It felt as if there was something behind Ervin that did not belong to the surface of the world. Something deep beneath law, beneath space, beneath ordinary darkness. The abyssal aura did not roar or explode. It simply existed, and because it existed, the light of the Queen’s Divine Spear began to sink.","Selene’s expression changed.","Ervin took one step forward.","His spear pushed back the Queen’s Divine Spear.","Then he twisted his wrist, and the dark spear force spiraled into Selene’s attack, tearing open a narrow path through the luminance. He stepped through that path and appeared closer to Selene than before.","Selene immediately retreated.","At the same time, the Queen Avatar behind her raised its other hand.","\"Twelve Luminance Edicts.\"","Twelve golden runes appeared around Ervin.","One sealed movement.","One suppressed energy.","One restrained weapon force.","One attacked spiritual will.","One weakened darkness.","One strengthened heavenly light.","The remaining six reinforced the first six, forming a complete suppression array around him.","For the first time, Ervin stopped.","The twelve edicts descended.","Selene did not wait. She joined both hands together, and the Queen Avatar behind her pointed its spear at Ervin once more. The pressure rising from her body made the entire stage glow with radiant lines.","Max watched without blinking.","’This is stronger than what she used earlier,’ he thought. ’She is not holding back.’","Ervin lowered his gaze slightly.","The twelve edicts pressed closer.","His black spear trembled.","Then he smiled.","\"Not bad.\"","Selene’s expression became colder. \"You still have time to surrender.\"","Ervin raised his head.","His eyes had changed.","They looked darker than before, not because of anger, but because something behind them had opened. The abyssal aura around him deepened rapidly, and the twelve luminance edicts surrounding him began to shake.","\"I have not even truly started yet,\" he said.","The stage grew silent.","The darkness behind Ervin suddenly expanded.","It did not rush outward like a normal domain. It descended.","The air sank.","The light sank.","The sound sank.","Even the golden-white glow of Selene’s edicts seemed to become heavier, as if the entire battlefield had been placed above a bottomless sea and was slowly being pulled downward.","Ervin’s voice was calm.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path, Abyssal Origin Descent.\"","The moment those words appeared in the arena, almost every top genius reacted.","Damian Voss narrowed his eyes sharply.","Rakan Thorne stopped smiling.","Orion Starfall’s expression became truly serious for the first time.","Kaiden Voidmere’s silver-gray eyes flickered with a strange light.","Revona opened her Void Origin Eyes halfway.","Aurelian Lareth’s calm expression changed slightly.","Even Max’s gaze sharpened.","The Pseudo Cosmic Path behind Ervin was not an ordinary abyss path.","A vast black sea appeared behind him, but it was not made of water. It was made of depth, gravity, darkness, and some mysterious ancient origin that seemed to swallow the meaning of distance itself. Above that black sea stood a single broken gate, half-submerged, half-visible, covered in ancient symbols no one could clearly read. Behind the gate, there seemed to be something even deeper, but the arena laws prevented the vision from fully opening.","The twelve luminance edicts around Ervin sank at the same time.","Their light dimmed.","Their authority weakened.","It was not that they had been destroyed.","They had been dragged downward, buried beneath the pressure of the abyssal origin.","Selene’s face changed.","\"Heavenly Luminance Genesis.\"","She did not hesitate anymore.","Her own Pseudo Cosmic Path erupted.","Golden-white light exploded from her body, and a pure world of first light appeared behind her. It was a world at the moment of creation, where dawn had just been born and all darkness was meant to be driven away. The Queen Avatar vanished, replaced by a higher and more ancient radiance. Her aura rose sharply, and the sinking feeling caused by Ervin’s Abyssal Origin Descent slowed for a moment.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path, Heavenly Luminance Genesis.\"","The stage became divided in two.","One side was an abyssal black sea with a broken ancient gate sinking into unknown depth.","The other was a world of first light, radiant and pure, as if heaven itself had opened at the beginning of creation.","The clash between them made the entire Eternal Hourglass arena tremble.","Selene raised her hand, her face pale but determined.","\"Heavenly Luminance Genesis, Spear of First Dawn.\"","A spear of pure creation light condensed above her.","Max recognized it immediately.","This was the same kind of attack she had used before near the Witch God Tree, the attack that had forced him to take it with his dragon scales because Morgana’s roots had interfered. But now, Selene had poured even more hatred and pressure into it, and the spear seemed even more concentrated than before.","Ervin looked up at the spear.","For the first time, his smile disappeared.","He held his black spear tightly.","The broken gate behind him opened slightly.","A soundless pressure spread from inside the gate.","Max’s eyes narrowed.","’What is behind that gate?’","He could not see clearly.","Even his Dimensional Sovereign Body could only sense depth, danger, and something old enough to make ordinary perception feel useless. The Abyssal Origin Descent was not merely a path of darkness. It seemed connected to some origin beneath the world, a place where light, law, and matter all had to sink eventually."]},{"number":1838,"title":"Chapter 1838: Battle Continues one after another!","paragraphs":["Ervin spoke softly.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, Gate of the First Depth.\"","The broken gate behind him opened a little wider.","The black sea rose.","Selene’s Spear of First Dawn descended.","The spear and the abyssal gate collided.","There was no immediate explosion.","Instead, the golden-white spear pushed into the dark gate inch by inch, while the gate tried to swallow it into its depth. Radiance and abyssal pressure fought silently at first, then the entire collision erupted into a terrifying shockwave that struck the arena barrier from within.","Golden-white light tried to purify the abyss.","The abyss tried to drag the light downward.","Selene gritted her teeth, blood slowly flowing from the corner of her mouth. Her Heavenly Luminance Genesis burned brighter, but her energy was clearly being consumed at a terrifying speed. Ervin also did not look relaxed. His face was slightly paler, and the hand gripping his spear had tightened until his knuckles whitened.","For several breaths, the two seemed evenly matched.","Then Ervin took one step forward.","The black sea behind him rose again.","The gate opened another fraction.","The Spear of First Dawn trembled.","Selene’s pupils contracted.","The golden-white spear began to sink.","It was not breaking but sinking slowly by slowly.","The light was dragged into the gate, swallowed layer by layer by the Abyssal Origin Descent.","Selene forced out more power, and the Heavenly Luminance Genesis behind her blazed with desperate brilliance. For a moment, the spear shone brighter than ever before, piercing deeper into the gate and causing cracks to appear on its surface.","Ervin’s eyes darkened further.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, Return To Depth.\"","The black sea surged.","A terrifying pull erupted from the opened gate.","The cracked Spear of First Dawn lost its direction.","Its light curved.","Its radiance distorted.","Then, under the shocked gazes of the participants, Selene’s strongest attack was dragged into the gate and vanished.","The Heavenly Luminance Genesis behind her flickered violently.","Selene staggered.","Ervin did not give her time to recover.","He moved.","His figure crossed the stage in silence, not with speed but with depth, as if the distance between them had sunk beneath his feet. Selene tried to raise another luminance barrier, but the abyssal pressure around Ervin’s spear dragged the barrier downward before it could fully form.","His spear stopped in front of her chest.","The black spear tip did not touch her, but the abyssal aura around it made her entire body stiffen. Selene’s face was pale, and her Heavenly Luminance Genesis had already become unstable behind her.","Angelina Valerius looked at the stage calmly.","\"Selene Vaeloria is unable to continue.\"","Selene clenched her teeth, humiliation and disbelief flashing in her eyes.","But she could not deny it.","She had lost.","[Winner: Ervin.]","[Selene Vaeloria Defeated.]","The screen above the arena changed.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Ervin]","[Total Battles Fought: 3]","[Total Wins: 3]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Selene Vaeloria]","[Total Battles Fought: 3]","[Total Wins: 2]","The arena remained silent.","This silence was different from before.","When Max defeated Rosaline, everyone had been shocked by the strangeness of Emotion Severing Path. When Aurelian defeated Morgana, they had been shocked by the domineering authority of Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion. But Ervin’s Pseudo Cosmic Path had created a different kind of shock.","It was mysterious.","Heavy.","Deep.","It did not feel like an attack that simply destroyed its enemy. It felt like a path that returned everything to some unknown depth where all things eventually sank.","Rakan Thorne stared at Ervin with rare seriousness. \"That guy is not simple.\"","Orion Starfall’s smile had disappeared. \"Abyssal Origin Descent. I have never heard of such a Pseudo Cosmic Path.\"","Kaiden Voidmere’s eyes narrowed. \"That gate is the problem. The sea is only the surface.\"","Revona looked at Ervin with her Void Origin Eyes open, and even she did not look completely relaxed.","Damian Voss’s grip tightened slightly around his sword hilt.","Aurelian Lareth’s expression became colder as he watched Selene lose. As the Divine Daughter of the second faction, Selene’s defeat was not merely personal. It also meant that the second faction’s prestige had been struck in front of everyone.","Max stood on his pillar, his gaze fixed on Ervin.","He had fought Ervin in the Genesis Trial. He knew Ervin was strong. He knew Ervin had hidden much of his power. But even Max had not expected his Pseudo Cosmic Path to be this strange.","’Abyssal Origin Descent,’ Max thought. ’That gate swallowed Selene’s Spear of First Dawn instead of breaking it. If I fight him, I cannot treat it like ordinary darkness or ordinary abyssal power.’","On the stage, Ervin withdrew his spear.","The black sea behind him faded slowly, and the broken gate disappeared last. Even as it vanished, Max felt as if something behind that gate had looked at the arena for a brief moment.","Selene was returned to her pillar by a beam of light, her face still pale and her eyes filled with unwillingness.","Ervin returned to his own pillar quietly, as if nothing special had happened.","But everyone now looked at him differently.","After Ervin returned to his pillar, the atmosphere inside the Eternal Hourglass remained heavy for a long time.","Selene Vaeloria had lost.","That fact alone was enough to silence many people. She was the Divine Daughter of the second elven faction, a wielder of the Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline, and someone who had revealed the terrifying Pseudo Cosmic Path, Heavenly Luminance Genesis.","Yet even after using the Spear of First Dawn, she had still been defeated by Ervin’s mysterious Abyssal Origin Descent. The black sea and broken gate behind Ervin had left a deep impression on every remaining participant, and even the top geniuses who had been relaxed earlier were now looking at him with more caution.","However, the final competitive stage did not stop because of anyone’s shock.","Angelina Valerius stood calmly above the arena and continued announcing battles.","The next few matches ended far more quickly.","A hidden swordsman from a minor divine force stepped onto the stage against a beast-blooded warrior and won in only four sword strikes, his blade moving so quietly that even some participants failed to catch the exact rhythm of his attack.","A bloodfire woman from the Blood Sun Temple defeated a soul-bell user by burning the sound waves before they could reach her mind, forcing him to surrender once his bells began cracking under her crimson flames.","Rosaline Lunara fought again and recovered from her earlier loss by suppressing her opponent with radiant seals, never needing to reveal Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary a second time. Fin Arclight defeated another mid-tier participant with Pale Eclipse Burial, though he only opened the edge of his Pseudo Cosmic Path for a breath before forcing his opponent to lose all sense of direction.","Morgana Starveil fought a silent spear genius and won by placing a curse on his shadow, causing every thrust he made to bend away from her at the last moment until he finally surrendered with an ugly expression."]},{"number":1839,"title":"Chapter 1839: Max vs Rakan","paragraphs":["Records continued to update above the arena.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Rosaline Lunara]","[Total Battles Fought: 2]","[Total Wins: 1]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Fin Arclight]","[Total Battles Fought: 2]","[Total Wins: 2]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Morgana Starveil]","[Total Battles Fought: 3]","[Total Wins: 2]","More names appeared, more beams descended, and more battles ended before they could truly become fierce. Orion Starfall used three star marks to defeat a thunder-winged spearwoman who had advanced with great momentum, never allowing her to cross half the stage.","Damian Voss met a powerful axe user whose battle intent was strong enough to make the arena floor crack, but Damian’s sword still cut through the axe, the armor, and the man’s fighting rhythm in one clean sequence.","Kaiden Voidmere faced a participant who used shadow movement, and the battle ended almost embarrassingly fast when Kaiden folded the path of the shadow itself and appeared beside him before the first assassination strike could land.","Revona fought again, and this time her opponent surrendered after watching his strongest attack vanish under her Void Origin Eyes without leaving even a trace.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Orion Starfall]","[Total Battles Fought: 2]","[Total Wins: 2]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Damian Voss]","[Total Battles Fought: 2]","[Total Wins: 2]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Kaiden Voidmere]","[Total Battles Fought: 2]","[Total Wins: 2]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Revona]","[Total Battles Fought: 2]","[Total Wins: 2]","The battles continued, but for a while, the strongest names did not collide with one another.","It was not that the matches were boring. Every participant remaining in the top twenty-five was strong enough to dominate an ordinary generation. Even the ones who lost quickly still had methods that could make weaker geniuses despair.","But after Max against Rosaline, Aurelian against Morgana, and Ervin against Selene, everyone had already tasted the difference between a strong battle and a true clash of monsters.","Then Angelina raised her hand once more.","The screen above the arena began to rotate.","For some reason, the spinning names seemed slower this time.","The remaining participants looked upward.","Max stood calmly on his pillar, one hand resting near Dragonheart. Rakan Thorne stood on his own pillar, arms crossed over his chest, his wild grin already spreading as if he had sensed something before the names stopped.","The screen flashed.","Two names appeared.","[Final Competitive Stage, Battle Twenty-Three]","[Max Morgan vs Rakan Thorne]","For a breath, the entire Eternal Hourglass arena became silent.","Then the atmosphere exploded.","Rakan Thorne laughed loudly from his pillar, his voice rolling across the arena like thunder. \"Finally!\"","Max looked toward him with a faint smile.","The other top geniuses immediately focused.","This was different.","This was not a top genius fighting someone below the peak.","This was the first major collision between two true monsters of the final competitive stage.","And outside the Eternal Hourglass, the Divine Realm erupted.","Across countless cities, ancient forces, divine clans, floating palaces, hidden academies, merchant heavens, and starry viewing platforms, enormous light screens reflected the names of Max Morgan and Rakan Thorne.","The Cosmic Ascension Conference had already drawn the attention of the entire Divine Realm, but the moment this pairing appeared, countless spectators stood up at the same time.","\"Max Morgan against Rakan Thorne!\"","\"The black dragon genius against the first Warlord of War God Palace!\"","\"This is the first real monster-level battle!\"","\"Max defeated Rosaline’s Pseudo Cosmic Path, but Rakan’s body is like a divine weapon. Can that sword path even cut him?\"","\"Rakan has not used his full strength once. He might be the strongest body-refining genius in the conference!\"","At the Black Dragon Clan, the massive viewing plaza was completely packed.","Countless disciples stood beneath a gigantic screen suspended above the central square. On that screen, Max and Rakan’s names shone in golden light, and the moment the pairing appeared, the excitement that had filled the plaza turned into nervous silence.","Many young disciples clenched their fists. Some had been cheering loudly every time Max won, but now that his opponent was Rakan Thorne, their confidence was mixed with fear.","\"That is Rakan Thorne...\"","\"The first Warlord of War God Palace.\"","\"I heard he once crushed a divine mountain beast with his bare hands.\"","\"He has not even been pushed properly until now.\"","\"Max is strong, but Rakan is different. He is not someone you can defeat with ordinary methods.\"","\"Stop saying unlucky things. Max already defeated Rosaline, and he has not shown everything either.\"","The disciples argued, but no one could hide the tension in their voices.","Rakan Thorne’s reputation was too heavy.","The War God Palace was one of the strongest first-rate forces in the Divine Realm, and its Warlords were not ordinary geniuses. Each Warlord represented battle, body, will, and war path taken to a frightening level. Rakan, as the first Warlord, carried a name that even other peak geniuses respected.","High above the plaza, Lady Virelia stood before the viewing screen, her elegant face calm but her eyes serious. Around her, the seven family heads of the Black Dragon Clan were also watching. None of them spoke for a while.","Then Lady Virelia softly said, \"Max, do well.\"","Her voice was not loud, but the family heads beside her heard it clearly.","The Grimes family head Matthew nodded slowly. \"This battle will show the Divine Realm whether his previous victories were only due to strange methods or whether he can truly stand against the strongest geniuses.\"","Lady Virelia did not turn away from the screen.","Her gaze remained fixed on Max’s figure.","\"All the best, Max,\" she whispered.","At the same time, inside the War God Palace, the reaction was completely different.","The War God Palace disciples were roaring.","An enormous battlefield-like plaza shook beneath their voices. Thousands of disciples raised their fists, weapons, and war banners toward the huge screen above them. The moment Rakan Thorne’s name appeared opposite Max’s, the entire palace seemed to awaken with battle intent.","\"Rakan!\"","\"First Warlord!\"","\"Crush him!\"","\"Show the Divine Realm the strength of the War God Palace!\"","\"Max Morgan is strong, but no one beats our first Warlord in close combat!\"","\"Rakan Thorne has not even used his War God Body yet!\"","\"Let that black dragon genius learn what true war power is!\"","The disciples shouted until the sky above the War God Palace trembled.","Several elders watched from higher platforms, their expressions filled with pride and expectation. To them, Rakan Thorne was not merely a participant. He was one of the sharpest blades of their younger generation, a genius raised through blood, battle, pain, and endless war trials.","He was someone who could carry the War God Palace name into the next era.","In a shadowed corner above the battlefield plaza, a silent figure watched the screen.","Saint Reiner stood there without drawing attention.","His eyes were fixed not on Rakan, but on Max.","He had seen many geniuses. He had seen arrogant heirs, monstrous bloodlines, hidden physiques, and terrifying paths. But Max Morgan had become increasingly difficult to measure. Every time people believed they had seen his strength, he revealed another layer.","Saint Reiner’s gaze narrowed slightly.","\"Boy,\" he muttered softly, \"let me see your true strength now. Let me see my legacy shine once again.\"","Back inside the Eternal Hourglass, Rakan Thorne cracked his neck and stepped forward on his pillar.","\"Max Morgan,\" he called out, his grin wild and excited. \"I have been waiting for this.\"","Max looked at him calmly. \"I know.\"","Rakan laughed. \"You defeated Rosaline’s Pseudo Cosmic Path with that strange sword path. You crushed soul attacks like they were nothing. You have a strong body, a strong sword, and more secrets than anyone here. But against me, tricks will not be enough.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"Good. I do not like wasting tricks.\"","Rakan’s grin widened.","Angelina Valerius looked toward both of them.","\"Max Morgan. Rakan Thorne. Enter the stage.\"","Two beams of light descended.","The Divine Realm held its breath.","The first major battle between the peak geniuses was about to begin."]},{"number":1840,"title":"Chapter 1840: To Not Use Dragonheart","paragraphs":["Max materialized on one side of the arena, his white hair stirring gently in the breeze produced by the transfer. He stood in complete composure, his black clothing undisturbed and his expression at ease, while Dragonheart rested in his dimensional space without any hint that he intended to draw it.","Compared to the swelling clamor rising from the Divine Realm outside and the strained attention of every participant within the Eternal Hourglass, Max appeared almost unnaturally calm, as though this were not the first great collision between peak geniuses but simply another fight he had chosen to walk into on his own terms.","Rakan Thorne landed on the opposite side with far greater force.","The instant his feet met the ground, the dark gold stone beneath him shuddered. His tall and battle-worn frame seemed to carry the weight of an entire mountain shaped by war, and his bare arms bore faint bronze markings that resembled old scars earned through countless trials of tempering.","He carried no weapon, and he needed none. His fists served as his weapons, his body served as his armor, and the aura of war wrapped around him like an unseen beast waiting for permission to wake.","For several breaths, neither of them moved, and the entire arena seemed to hold its breath along with them.","Beyond the Eternal Hourglass, countless gazes across the Divine Realm were fixed on that same stage.","At the Black Dragon Clan, the disciples had stopped shouting altogether. They stared at the enormous screen with clenched fists, and many of them could barely remember to breathe.","At the War God Palace, the reaction was the exact opposite. The disciples roared louder with every passing moment until their voices shook the sky above the battlefield plaza.","\"Rakan!\"","\"First Warlord!\"","\"Show him what true body strength means!\"","\"Crush the black dragon genius!\"","At the center of the stage, Rakan studied Max for a long moment, and then his grin slowly widened.","\"You are not drawing your sword?\"","Max glanced down at Dragonheart and then looked back at Rakan. \"Not for now.\"","Rakan raised an eyebrow. The excitement in his eyes deepened, though it now carried a trace of genuine surprise. \"You used that strange sword path to defeat Rosaline. You carry the Sword of the Sword Sovereign. You traded pure sword techniques with Damian Voss and never once fell behind. And yet against me, the first Warlord of the War God Palace, you choose to not use your sword?\"","Max smiled faintly. \"That is right.\"","Rakan laughed, and the sound held no mockery yet. It was deep and rough and saturated with the desire for battle. \"Do you understand what that means?\"","Max regarded him calmly. \"I do.\"","Rakan’s grin turned wilder. \"Then tell me why.\"","Max lifted his hand and slowly closed it into a fist. A subtle ripple of physical force spread outward from his body. It was not energy, nor sword intent, nor the Pseudo Cosmic Path, but purely the strength of flesh contained beneath his skin, his bones, his blood, and a vitality that resembled that of a dragon.","The stage beneath his feet gave a low hum, as though the arena itself had recognized that the body standing upon it was far from ordinary.","\"I have fought swordsmen, bloodline users, curse wielders, soul attackers, and cultivators of strange and unusual paths,\" Max said evenly. \"But I have never properly measured my body against the strongest body cultivators in the Divine Realm.\"","His gaze settled on Rakan.","\"And when people speak of body cultivation in the Divine Realm, they speak of the War God Palace.\"","The words carried clearly through the arena, and for a moment even the disciples of the War God Palace outside fell silent. Then the entire palace erupted with noise even greater than before.","\"He wants to test his body against the War God Palace?\"","\"Against Rakan Thorne himself?\"","\"He is out of his mind!\"","\"Does he believe dragon blood alone can rival the first Warlord?\"","At the Black Dragon Clan, many disciples looked stunned.","\"He is really not using Dragonheart?\"","\"He intends to fight Rakan with his bare body?\"","\"That is far too dangerous. Rakan is no ordinary body cultivator.\"","Lady Virelia’s eyes narrowed slightly, and even the seven family heads grew solemn. They knew Max’s body was formidable, for they had witnessed enough to understand that much.","Even so, choosing to challenge Rakan Thorne in the very domain where Rakan was most terrifying remained an extraordinarily bold decision.","Matthew Grimes released a slow breath. \"That boy truly refuses to walk any ordinary road.\"","Inside the arena, Rakan stared at Max for several long breaths before he smiled again. This time his smile carried more than excitement. It was nearly predatory.","\"You have made an enormous mistake,\" Rakan said.","Max’s expression did not shift. \"Have I?\"","Rakan rolled his neck, and a series of loud cracks sounded from his bones. \"If you had used your sword, your strange Cosmic Path, or any of your other hidden tricks, this battle might have grown complicated from the very first exchange. But if you wish to contend with me through the body alone, then you have walked straight into my kingdom.\"","A bronze aura rose slowly from Rakan’s skin, and the air around him grew heavy. His muscles did not swell in any exaggerated fashion, yet every line of his body seemed to become more solid, more ancient, and more oppressive.","The war markings along his arms brightened one after another, and thin cracks began spreading through the stage beneath his feet.","Rakan raised his fist.","\"This body has been broken inside war furnaces, crushed beneath divine mountains, burned within battlefield suns, drowned in seas of blood, and rebuilt more times than I can count. Every bone in me has been tempered for combat. Every drop of blood in my veins carries the intent of war. Every breath I draw exists for the sake of battle.\"","His eyes locked onto Max.","\"So allow me to teach you something, Max Morgan.\"","The bronze aura surrounding him grew suddenly denser.","\"When you challenge the War God Palace in a contest of the body, you do not begin by testing us.\"","He took a single step forward, and the arena shook.","\"You begin by surviving us.\""]},{"number":1841,"title":"Chapter 1841: Going Head-to-Head with RAKAN!","paragraphs":["Max looked at the cracks radiating outward from Rakan’s step, and the faint smile on his face never wavered. If anything, his eyes grew brighter with interest.","\"Good,\" he said. \"That is exactly what I wanted to hear.\"","Rakan’s grin froze for an instant before stretching even wider. \"You truly are insane.\"","Max slowly raised both hands and loosened his shoulders. Dragonheart remained in its sheath. The Emotion Severing Path did not appear, nor did the Divine King Punishment, nor the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline. Not a single dragon scale covered his skin.","Only his body stood there, calm and prepared, and the sight alone made the blood of countless spectators run hot.","On the participant pillars, Damian Voss narrowed his eyes. \"He genuinely intends to fight with his bare hands.\"","Orion Starfall smiled. \"This is either arrogance or confidence.\"","Kaiden Voidmere replied evenly, \"With Max, it may well be both.\"","Ervin kept his eyes fixed on the stage. \"He wants to learn exactly where his body stands.\"","Revona glanced toward Rakan and then back toward Max. \"That knowledge may cost him dearly.\"","Aurelian Lareth sneered faintly from his pillar. \"Foolish.\"","Selene Vaeloria’s gaze turned cold. \"He will suffer for that arrogance.\"","Morgana Starveil smiled with amusement, though her eyes were entirely serious. \"Perhaps. But the people who dismiss him as merely arrogant usually live to regret it.\"","Angelina Valerius observed both fighters from her position above the stage. Her face remained composed, yet her eyes lingered on Max for a brief moment.","She had overseen countless battles, watched countless geniuses rise and fall, and judged countless varieties of pride. Some pride was hollow, and some pride was born of ignorance, but the pride Max carried resembled neither.","It felt like the pride of a man deliberately walking toward danger because he wanted to measure the height of the mountain with his own two hands.","Angelina raised her hand, and the arena barrier brightened.","[Battle Begins.]","Rakan’s grin vanished, and pure battle intent took its place. The first Warlord of the War God Palace sank slightly into his stance, drawing his fist back as the bronze aura around him condensed into a single terrifying point.","Max simply stood where he was with his body relaxed and his eyes calm.","Then Rakan moved.","The stage detonated beneath his feet, and his body shot forward like a bronze meteor, crossing the distance between them in a single instant. There was no elaborate movement technique behind it, no illusion, no distortion of any path, and no concealed trick.","It was raw physical speed born from a body refined to an abnormal degree. The air ahead of him compressed violently, and his fist ripped through it with a horrifying howl as it hurtled toward Max’s chest.","Max did not dodge. He stepped forward and threw a punch of his own.","Boom!","The two fists met head-on. A shockwave burst from the point of contact and swept across the central stage like an invisible storm. The dark gold stone beneath their feet fractured into circular patterns, and the transparent barrier enclosing the arena flared brightly as it absorbed the force rushing outward.","Something shifted in Rakan’s eyes. Max’s body had not been thrown backward, and his arm had not so much as trembled. He had taken Rakan’s punch directly and remained standing exactly where he was.","For a brief moment, the entire War God Palace grew quieter.","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, Rakan’s grin slowly returned. \"Interesting.\"","Max shook out his wrist once and smiled faintly. \"Is that all you have?\"","Rakan laughed, and in the next instant his body blurred again. This time he threw three punches in rapid succession. The first was aimed at Max’s shoulder, the second at his ribs, and the third at his jaw.","Each strike carried enough power to shatter a divine mountain, yet Max answered with movements just as direct. He blocked the first punch with his forearm, met the second with his elbow, and tilted his head past the third by the narrowest of margins before driving his knee toward Rakan’s abdomen.","Rakan dropped his arm and caught the knee.","Boom!","Another impact rocked the arena, and Rakan slid back half a step. It was only half a step, but it was enough. The eyes of every participant sharpened at once, because Rakan Thorne, the first Warlord of the War God Palace, had just been pushed backward in a purely physical exchange.","Rakan glanced down at the faint mark his foot had carved into the stage, then looked back up at Max. His smile stretched far wider than before, and the battle intent in his eyes sank to a deeper level.","\"You really do have the body to back up those words.\"","Max lowered his leg without hurry. \"I told you. I wanted to test it.\"","Rakan’s shoulders shook with laughter. \"Good. Very good. Most people who claim they want to test their bodies against mine are already sprawled on the ground after the first punch.\"","He charged forward again, and the two of them collided at the center of the stage.","This time they did not trade only one or two blows. Their fists, elbows, knees, shoulders, and palms crashed together in relentless succession, and every collision produced a dull peal of thunder that made the stage tremble.","Rakan’s attacks were savage and wild, yet never careless. Every punch carried years of battlefield refinement, every step cut off one of Max’s possible retreats, and every roll of his shoulders concealed the seed of another strike.","Max answered with nothing but physical skill. His punches were direct, his footwork was stable, and his reactions were frighteningly sharp. Rakan’s blows fell like war hammers, but Max either met them head-on or shifted just enough to let their force slide harmlessly past before striking back.","His body lacked the visible oppressiveness of Rakan’s, yet the strength packed inside it was compact and dense and absurdly steady.","Boom!","Rakan’s fist hammered into Max’s forearm. Max rotated his wrist and drove a punch into Rakan’s chest. Rakan blocked it with his palm, but the force still bent his upper body slightly backward. Rakan surged forward and slammed his shoulder toward Max, and Max met him shoulder against shoulder.","The air between them burst apart, and both fighters took a single step back.","For the first time since the battle had begun, the grin on Rakan’s face dimmed, and he stared at Max with complete seriousness.","On the participant pillars, the reactions grew far more intense. Rakan was no longer playing around, and yet Max was still standing his ground."]},{"number":1842,"title":"Chapter 1842: War God Body!","paragraphs":["Damian Voss narrowed his eyes. \"His body is far stronger than I expected.\"","Orion Starfall’s smile grew brighter. \"He really is fighting Rakan with nothing but his body.\"","Kaiden Voidmere watched with deep and thoughtful eyes. \"There is no visible bloodline armor, no sword path, and no external force at work. What we are seeing is his base body.\"","Ervin kept his gaze fixed on Max. \"That is no ordinary dragon physique. There is something else beneath it.\"","Revona’s eyes opened a fraction wider, and even she appeared somewhat surprised.","Aurelian Lareth’s expression turned colder, while Selene Vaeloria stared at Max with her hands clenched tight. Her earlier defeat at his hands suddenly felt even more humiliating than before. If Max’s body alone was enough to trade blows with Rakan like this, then how much had he truly held back during their battle near the Witch God Tree?","Outside the Eternal Hourglass, the viewing plaza of the Black Dragon Clan erupted.","\"He took Rakan’s punch!\"","\"He did more than take it. He pushed Rakan back!\"","\"Max never even drew Dragonheart!\"","\"He is genuinely fighting the first Warlord with his body alone!\"","Lady Virelia’s eyes gleamed faintly, and the seven family heads standing beside her looked far more animated than before. Matthew Grimes slowly curled his hand into a fist, unable to conceal the shock in his eyes.","\"This boy,\" he muttered. \"Just how many foundations is he hiding?\"","At the War God Palace, the disciples no longer shouted so carelessly. They still believed in Rakan, but the easy confidence they had carried into the match had been shaken. Their first Warlord had failed to crush Max instantly, and that fact alone was enough to plant disbelief in many of their hearts.","On the central stage, Rakan drew a slow breath, looked at Max, and laughed once more. This laugh was different from the ones before it. It was not casual in the slightest, for it overflowed with genuine excitement.","\"Max Morgan,\" Rakan said, his voice deep and resonant, \"you are the first person in this entire conference who has made me happy in a contest of body against body.\"","Max smiled. \"Then continue.\"","Rakan shook his head. \"No. Not like this.\"","Max raised an eyebrow.","Rakan slowly lifted both arms and clenched his fists. The bronze markings running across his arms began to glow with growing intensity. At first they resembled old scars, but soon they took on the appearance of ancient runes seared directly into his flesh.","A crushing pressure radiated outward from his body, and the faint rhythm of a war drum seemed to echo from somewhere deep within his bones.","Outside the Eternal Hourglass, the disciples of the War God Palace shot to their feet.","\"He is using it!\"","\"The War God Body!\"","\"The first limit! He is opening the first limit!\"","\"Rakan is finally taking him seriously!\"","Across the Divine Realm, countless spectators snapped to attention. The War God Body stood among the greatest body cultivation inheritances of the War God Palace. It was said to contain seven limits, and each limit represented a shackle bound around the physical body.","For an ordinary body cultivator, breaking even the first limit was enough to transform them into a terrifying genius. Breaking the second could allow a cultivator to dominate an entire generation within the same realm, and breaking the third was a feat reserved for the true monsters of the War God Palace alone.","Rakan Thorne, the strongest inheritor of the War God Body in the current generation, had already broken three of those limits. Now he was opening the first.","A deep rumbling rose from Rakan’s body. It was not the sound of flowing energy. It was the sound of flesh, bones, blood, muscles, tendons, and organs awakening in unison.","\"War God Body,\" Rakan said slowly.","The bronze light surrounding him erupted.","\"First Limit. War Blood Awakening.\"","Boom!","The stage sank beneath him, and a terrifying wave of physical pressure swept outward like a storm. Rakan’s blood seemed to roar within his veins, and his skin gleamed with a bronze luster that made him resemble a living statue of war.","His muscles did not swell grotesquely, yet the density of his body had visibly changed, as though a single layer of the power sealed within every inch of his flesh had just been unlocked.","Max’s eyes sharpened. He could feel it with absolute clarity. Rakan’s strength had increased, and not by some slight or trivial margin. The instant the first limit opened, Rakan’s physical power had climbed to an entirely different level.","Rakan sank into his stance, and his grin returned.","\"Now, Max Morgan, let us see how long that body of yours can keep up.\"","He vanished.","Max’s pupils contracted. Rakan reappeared directly in front of him and struck, and Max crossed both arms to block.","Boom!","The impact crashed into him like a divine mountain falling out of the sky. For the first time in the battle, Max was driven backward. His feet dragged across the dark gold stage and carved two deep trenches into it before he finally steadied himself.","The Divine Realm erupted once again. At the War God Palace, the disciples roared until the battlefield plaza itself seemed to shake.","\"That is it!\"","\"The First Limit!\"","\"War Blood Awakening!\"","\"Crush him, Rakan!\"","At the Black Dragon Clan, the disciples grew anxious once more, and their earlier excitement hardened into tense, clenched-jaw silence.","\"He was pushed back.\"","\"The first limit raised Rakan’s strength by too much.\"","\"Can Max really keep this up without drawing Dragonheart?\"","Lady Virelia watched in silence, but her eyes never strayed from Max for even a moment.","On the stage, Max lowered his arms. A faint red mark lingered on his forearms, and then it vanished almost as quickly as it had appeared. Rakan noticed, and his eyes lit up.","\"Even that failed to injure you properly?\"","Max rolled his shoulders and regarded Rakan with unmistakable interest. \"That was better.\"","Rakan stared at him for a moment, and then he laughed louder than before. \"Good. Then do not disappoint me too quickly.\"","Max smiled faintly and closed both fists. \"I was about to say the same to you.\"","In the next instant, both of them moved, and the true battle of bodies finally began."]},{"number":1843,"title":"Chapter 1843: Releasing the First Vein","paragraphs":["The moment they closed the distance, the central stage transformed into a battlefield of pure physical violence. Rakan’s body, empowered by the First Limit of the War God Body, no longer felt like mere flesh and blood. Every punch he threw carried the weight of a collapsing mountain, and every step he planted sent tremors through the stage.","The bronze light wrapped around him was not ordinary energy but the awakened force of his blood, his bones, his muscles, and his organs, all releasing the power that had been stored behind the first shackle of the War God Body.","He appeared before Max once more and drove a punch toward his chest. Max raised his arm and blocked it.","Boom!","The impact forced Max’s body to sink slightly. The dark gold stone fractured beneath his feet, and a ring of force rippled outward across the stage.","Before Max could answer with a counter, Rakan’s second punch had already arrived, followed by a knee strike, an elbow, and a crushing slam of his shoulder. His attacks chained together like the beating of war drums, and each one landed faster and heavier than the last.","Max blocked, deflected, and countered, yet the difference created by the first limit was impossible to ignore. War Blood Awakening had lifted Rakan’s physical power onto another plane entirely. His body had grown stronger, his blood burned fiercer, and every movement carried a violent rhythm of battle that sought to overwhelm Max completely.","Boom!","Rakan’s fist hammered into Max’s crossed arms again, and this time Max slid back several steps.","Outside the Eternal Hourglass, the War God Palace disciples roared with delight.","\"Rakan is suppressing him!\"","\"Even Max Morgan cannot match the War God Body forever!\"","\"Crush him!\"","At the Black Dragon Clan, many disciples ground their teeth. Max had not drawn Dragonheart, had not invoked the Emotion Severing Path, and had not even revealed his dragon scales. To them, the sight was equal parts thrilling and terrifying.","If Max could truly match Rakan through his body alone, his reputation would soar to new heights. But if he insisted on fighting this way for too long, he might suffer a crushing defeat before ever bringing out his real advantages.","On the stage, Rakan pressed the attack once more. His fist tore through the air and fell toward Max like a bronze war hammer.","Max raised his hand and caught it.","Boom!","The stage shuddered yet again. This time Max’s feet sank into the ground, but his body did not retreat a single inch.","Rakan’s eyes narrowed.","Max slowly lifted his head. There was no anger in his eyes, no panic, and no frustration. In their place shone a clear brightness, as though the pressure of Rakan’s War God Body had finally handed him the answer he had been searching for.","\"You are strong,\" Max said.","Rakan grinned. \"You are only realizing that now?\"","Max shook his head lightly. \"No. I confirmed it.\"","Rakan’s smile froze for the briefest moment.","Max released Rakan’s fist and stepped back once. His body grew utterly still. For an instant the sounds of battle seemed to fade around him, and even the violent bronze aura bearing down on him appeared to pause.","Then something deep inside Max’s body began to rumble. It started low, and it was deep and ancient, as though a sealed gate somewhere within him had begun to swing open.","The participants on the pillars sensed the change immediately.","Damian Voss’s gaze sharpened. Orion Starfall’s smile slowly dissolved into genuine focus. Kaiden Voidmere’s eyes narrowed as he murmured, \"Something inside his body is awakening.\"","Ervin watched Max in silence, his abyssal gaze sinking even deeper. \"Is one of his hidden foundations?\"","Revona opened her eyes a little wider, and the void-colored light within them flickered as though straining to see through to the source of the change.","Aurelian Lareth frowned, and Selene Vaeloria’s face grew colder still.","Morgana Starveil tilted her head slightly, and for the first time in a long while her smile disappeared. \"Now what is he opening?\"","On the central stage, Max drew a slow breath as the rumbling within him grew louder. It was nothing like Rakan’s War God Body, in which blood and bones and muscles roared with the intent of war.","The change taking place in Max felt far more foundational and far more primal, as though the very root of his existence was being reinforced from within, and every part of his body was being reminded of its true origin.","A faint and profound glow surfaced beneath his skin. It did not resemble ordinary light in any way. It felt like the first pulse of life stirring inside an ancient body.","Max’s voice rang out with perfect calm.","\"Seven Divine Veins.\"","Rakan’s eyes widened slightly as heard those words.","Max’s body rumbled once more, and this time the sound reached so deep that the stage itself seemed to answer it.","\"First Vein.\"","The air around him sank.","\"Vein of Origin.\"","Boom!","A terrifying pulse erupted from Max’s body. It lacked the wildness of Rakan’s War Blood Awakening, yet it ran far deeper. The instant the Vein of Origin opened, Max’s physical body seemed to grow heavier, denser, and more complete.","His bones, his blood, his muscles, his skin, his organs, and even the hidden foundation of his body were all strengthened at the root. This was no simple increase in raw strength. It was a reinforcement at the level of origin itself, as though his body had returned to a purer and mightier state of existence.","Cracks spread outward from beneath Max’s feet, but this time they were not the result of him being driven back. They came from the sheer pressure his body released while he simply stood in place.","The viewing plaza of the Black Dragon Clan fell utterly silent, and then someone shouted.","\"What is that?\"","\"His body just changed!\"","\"He opened something inside himself!\"","\"Seven Divine Veins? Did he just say Seven Divine Veins?\"","Lady Virelia’s eyes widened a fraction, and even the seven family heads looked shaken. Only a handful of people had ever known that Max cultivated the Seven Divine Veins, and since Lady Virelia was among them, her surprise was far milder than everyone else’s.","At the War God Palace, the shouting grew unsteady. The disciples who had been roaring for Rakan only a moment earlier now stared at Max in open disbelief. They could not comprehend what had just happened.","Max’s body had not swelled, he had not transformed into a dragon, and he wore no armor of any kind. Yet the pressure rolling off him made even some of the War God Palace’s own disciples feel their blood constrict."]},{"number":1844,"title":"Chapter 1844: Max Dominating The Battle!","paragraphs":["On the stage, Rakan stared at Max, and then his grin returned fiercer than it had ever been.","\"Seven Divine Veins.... Just how many secrets are you carrying?\"","Max slowly closed his fist, and the air around his fingers compressed.","\"I told you,\" Max said evenly. \"I wanted to test my body. I never said I had shown all of it.\"","Rakan laughed loudly. \"Good!\"","He stepped forward. The War Blood Awakening within him roared back to life, and bronze light surged around his frame. He drew his fist back, gathered the full power of the First Limit, and punched with far greater force than anything he had thrown before.","Max punched as well, and their fists collided.","Boom!","This time, the outcome changed. Rakan’s arm trembled, and his bronze aura convulsed violently. The force of Max’s fist tore through Rakan’s arm, surged into his shoulder, and swept across his entire body. Rakan’s feet dragged backward over the stage, gouging two long trenches into the dark gold stone.","The entire arena froze. Rakan had been forced back, and it had been done with a fist. A pure and unadorned fist.","Max lowered his hand without a word. Rakan looked down at his own trembling arm, and for the first time in the battle, genuine surprise showed on his face.","Then Max moved.","He crossed the distance in a single step and drove a punch toward Rakan’s chest. Rakan crossed both arms to block.","Boom!","Rakan was shoved backward again, and Max pursued him instantly. One punch crashed against Rakan’s guard, another knocked his elbow aside, and a third landed squarely on his shoulder and tilted his entire body.","Rakan gritted his teeth and answered with a knee strike, but Max caught it with his palm. The impact unleashed another shockwave, yet Max’s arm did not so much as waver. He twisted at the waist and buried his own knee in Rakan’s abdomen.","Boom!","Rakan’s body folded slightly.","The disciples of the War God Palace stared at the screen in stunned silence.","\"Impossible.\"","\"Rakan is being pushed back?\"","\"That is the First Limit!\"","\"Who in the world can dominate the First Limit of the War God Body with pure physical strength?\"","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, the participants were no less shocked.","Damian Voss watched with narrowed eyes. \"His physical foundation rose by far too much.\"","Orion Starfall spoke softly. \"But how? Is the War God Body not the strongest body cultivation method in the world? How could Max surpass a War God Body?\"","Kaiden Voidmere’s gaze remained deep and unreadable. \"There is a legend about a technique called the Seven Divine Veins. It is said that by opening the seven divine veins hidden within one’s body, a cultivator could lay the foundation for the strongest physical body in the world. With the power it grants, one could supposedly shatter stars with nothing more than a flick of the fingers.\"","\"What? How could a technique that powerful even exist?\" Orion turned to stare at Kaiden in shock.","Even Damian was left speechless. Destroying stars with a mere flick of the fingers was godlike power even by the standards of the Divine Realm, and he simply could not understand how any single technique could grant a person that much strength.","Kaiden continued. \"I heard from my master that no human has ever succeeded in opening all Seven Divine Veins. The difficulty of the technique is so extreme that even the Primordials only managed to reach the fourth vein. Because of that terrifying difficulty, the Seven Divine Veins technique was lost in ancient times, and I doubt even the Primordials ever possessed the complete version.\"","He looked toward Max and added, \"As for how Max managed to open the first of the Seven Divine Veins, I have no idea at all.\"","Both Orion and Damian fell silent at his words. Neither of them had expected such a body cultivation method to exist, let alone one with a history like that behind it.","Aurelian Lareth’s expression darkened even further.","On the stage, Rakan finally steadied himself. A thin line of blood appeared at the corner of his mouth. He wiped it away with his thumb and studied the red stain for a moment. Then he smiled. It was not a casual smile, and it was not an arrogant one. It was a smile blazing with pure excitement.","\"Max Morgan,\" Rakan said slowly, \"you truly are worth fighting.\"","Max stood before him with the power of the Vein of Origin rumbling steadily through his body.","\"Then fight properly.\"","Rakan laughed and charged forward again, but this time Max met him even more directly.","Their fists collided again and again, and every collision rang out like divine drums being struck above the world. Rakan’s War Blood Awakening granted him terrifying strength, but Max’s Vein of Origin had made his physical foundation absurdly stable.","No matter how ferocious Rakan’s attacks became, Max did not crumble, did not lose his balance, and did not give ground. Instead, he slowly began to seize control of the battle’s rhythm.","Rakan punched, and Max blocked before answering with a counter. Rakan kicked, and Max stepped inside the arc to strike his ribs. Rakan attempted a shoulder slam, and Max met the charge shoulder against shoulder and forced him back half a step.","The longer they fought, the clearer the truth became. With the First Vein open, Max was no longer merely matching Rakan’s First Limit. He was beginning to dominate it.","The Divine Realm was shaken to its core.","At the Black Dragon Clan, the disciples exploded into wild cheering.","\"Max!\"","\"He is pushing Rakan back!\"","\"He is beating the First Limit of the War God Body!\"","\"Brother Max is insane!\"","Lady Virelia finally allowed a faint smile to touch her face. The seven family heads exchanged glances, and the astonishment in their eyes was impossible to conceal.","Matthew Grimes exhaled slowly. \"The Divine Realm will remember this battle.\"","At the War God Palace, the disciples grew tense, yet their fighting spirit refused to collapse. Instead, many of them began roaring once more, and this time their voices carried real urgency.","\"Rakan!\"","\"Open the second limit!\"","\"Show him the true War God Body!\"","\"First Warlord, you cannot lose in a contest of body strength!\"","In a shadowed corner, Saint Reiner watched the screen with narrowed eyes, and his entire attention rested on Max rather than Rakan.","Back inside the Eternal Hourglass, Max’s fist smashed through Rakan’s guard and struck him square in the chest.","Boom!","Rakan was hurled backward more than ten steps, and every step cracked the arena floor beneath him. He finally came to a stop, lowered his head, and released a long, deep breath.","The bronze light of the First Limit still burned around him, but the confidence in his eyes had transformed into something sharper. There was respect in his gaze now, along with excitement and an even fiercer hunger for battle.","Max stood across from him with the Vein of Origin still rumbling within his body, his expression calm and unshakable.","Rakan slowly raised his head.","\"The First Limit is not enough,\" he said.","Max smiled faintly. \"I noticed.\"","Rakan’s grin returned.","\"Then let us go higher.\""]},{"number":1845,"title":"Chapter 1845: Second Limit","paragraphs":["Rakan’s words fell, and the entire central stage seemed to grow heavier under them.","The bronze light of the First Limit still burned across his body, but it was no longer enough, and everyone present could see that plainly.","The War Blood Awakening had allowed him to suppress Max for a brief stretch, but once Max opened the Vein of Origin, the rhythm of the battle changed completely. Rakan, the first Warlord of the War God Palace, had been forced back again and again in the very domain where he was supposed to reign supreme.","For the War God Palace, this was no small matter, and for the Divine Realm as a whole, it was even more shocking. Rakan Thorne was not merely a body cultivator. He was one of the most terrifying body cultivators of the entire younger generation, the first Warlord of the War God Palace, and a monster who had already broken three limits of the War God Body.","Yet Max, who belonged to no part of the War God Palace and had not even touched his dragon transformation, had dominated Rakan’s First Limit using nothing but the first vein of the Seven Divine Veins.","On the stage, Rakan lowered his head for a moment, and his shoulders began to shake. Then he started to laugh. The laughter began low, then swelled louder and louder until it rolled across the arena like thunder, saturated with excitement, madness, and burning war intent.","He slowly raised his head, and the casual confidence that had lived in his eyes was gone. In its place remained only the pure joy of finding an opponent capable of forcing him beyond his comfort.","\"Max Morgan,\" Rakan said, his voice deep and rough, \"you are dangerous.\"","Max regarded him calmly. \"Is that a compliment?\"","\"It is the highest compliment I can offer you right now.\" Rakan clenched both fists, and the bronze markings across his body flared brighter. \"The First Limit alone is enough to crush nearly anyone in this conference foolish enough to fight me body against body, yet you broke through it so easily.\"","Max said nothing, and Rakan’s grin stretched wider still.","\"Good. Then I will not insult you by taking this slowly.\"","The moment those words rang out, the War God Palace disciples outside the Eternal Hourglass fell completely silent, for many of them knew exactly what was coming. At the Black Dragon Clan, the disciples felt their throats tighten as well.","The enormous screen above the viewing plaza showed Rakan standing at the center of the stage with bronze light blazing around him like a war furnace, and every disciple could sense that the first Warlord was about to unleash a far more terrifying tier of physical power.","On the central stage, Rakan slowly spread both arms. The runes that had been glowing along his arms and shoulders began crawling across his chest, his back, his neck, and his legs. His skin took on a deeper bronze luster, and the sound rising from within his body changed in character. During the First Limit, his blood had roared like war drums. Now his bones began to answer.","Crack. Crack. Crack.","The sound was nothing like ordinary bones popping. It resembled divine metal being reforged inside a living body.","Rakan’s voice rang out.","\"War God Body.\"","The pressure surrounding him climbed sharply.","\"Second Limit.\"","The air around his frame twisted.","\"War Bone Reforging.\"","Boom!","A terrifying wave of physical pressure detonated outward. The stage beneath Rakan’s feet sank several inches, and the cracks already webbing the dark gold stone tore wider. His body did not grow in size, yet his entire frame seemed to become indestructible.","The aura radiating from his bones grew so dense that even the geniuses watching from the pillars felt as though they were staring at a divine weapon shaped like a man.","The War God Palace erupted.","\"The Second Limit!\"","\"War Bone Reforging!\"","\"Rakan has opened the Second Limit!\"","\"Now let us see how Max keeps up!\"","At the Black Dragon Clan, the disciples clenched their fists once more.","\"He went straight to the Second Limit.\"","\"His body feels completely different now.\"","\"Can Max’s Vein of Origin still dominate him?\"","Lady Virelia watched without so much as blinking. The seven family heads beside her no longer spoke in casual tones, for all of them could tell that Rakan’s physical body had undergone a qualitative transformation.","The First Limit awakened the blood, and the Second Limit reforged the bones. With this limit open, Rakan’s body was not merely stronger. It had become harder to injure, harder to shake, and far more stable under any impact.","On the participant pillars, Damian Voss’s gaze turned grave.","Orion Starfall exhaled slowly. \"This must be the true bodily foundation of the War God Palace.\"","Kaiden Voidmere gave a faint nod. \"The First Limit released the power of his blood, and the Second Limit reinforces the body’s frame. If Max intends to overpower him now, pure strength will not be enough unless his own foundation runs even deeper.\"","Ervin watched in silence. \"Rakan is not finished.\"","Just as Ervin spoke, Rakan raised his head once more, and the bronze light around him continued to climb. Max’s eyes sharpened slightly. Rakan had no intention of attacking with the Second Limit alone. He was still going.","The War God Palace disciples stared at the screen with widening eyes.","\"He is not stopping?\"","\"Is he going to open the Third Limit as well?\"","\"Against Max, he is opening two limits back to back?\"","Saint Reiner, standing in the shadows of the War God Palace, narrowed his eyes, and for the first time a faint trace of approval surfaced in his gaze as he watched Rakan.","\"Good,\" he muttered. \"Do not test him half-heartedly.\"","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, Rakan’s body rumbled yet again. This time the sound came neither from his blood nor from his bones, but from his flesh itself. His muscles tightened, his tendons gleamed, and every line of his body seemed to swell with explosive war power.","The bronze markings across his skin joined into a single unbroken pattern, forming an ancient design of war that covered him like living divine armor carved directly into his flesh. The pressure around him grew so heavy that the very space near his body appeared to tremble."]},{"number":1846,"title":"Chapter 1846: Third Limit","paragraphs":["Rakan’s voice dropped deeper.","\"Third Limit.\"","His eyes blazed with ferocious battle intent.","\"War Flesh Unbound.\"","Boom!","The entire central stage convulsed. A pillar of bronze physical force surged up from Rakan’s body and slammed into the barrier above the arena, and the transparent dome flashed over and over as though battered by a storm of invisible fists.","Rakan’s flesh, bones, blood, tendons, organs, and muscles now resonated as one, producing a complete state of war embodiment that stood far beyond the First Limit.","The difference was immediate. If the First Limit had made Rakan feel like an awakened battlefield beast, and the Second Limit had made him feel like a divine weapon, then the Third Limit made him feel like a walking calamity of war.","Every breath he drew carried pressure, every heartbeat rang out like a war drum, and every twitch of his fingers forced the surrounding air to compress.","Across the Divine Realm, countless spectators rose to their feet.","\"He opened the Third Limit!\"","\"The strongest disciple of the War God Body has revealed the Third Limit!\"","\"This is Rakan Thorne’s true physical strength!\"","\"Max pushed him this far!\"","At the Black Dragon Clan, the earlier cheers died away once more. The disciples stared at the screen in a mixture of shock and worry, for the pressure pouring off Rakan was so terrifying that some of them felt their blood tremble even through the projection.","One disciple swallowed hard. \"This is still just body strength?\"","Another muttered, \"How can a physical body alone release that much pressure?\"","A third clenched his fists and said, \"Max has to bring out more now. He cannot keep fighting with only one vein, can he?\"","Lady Virelia’s eyes never left Max, and the seven family heads exchanged grave looks.","The first family head spoke slowly. \"The Third Limit of the War God Body. This is no longer a simple enhancement.\"","The second family head nodded. \"His blood, his bones, and his flesh have all been released. His body has entered a complete state of war.\"","The third family head looked at Max on the screen. \"Now we will see whether Max can still suppress him.\"","On the stage, Max stood opposite Rakan with the Vein of Origin rumbling steadily inside him. The pressure of the Third Limit crashed toward him like a storm. His clothes whipped violently around him, his white hair streamed backward, and the ground beneath his feet cracked, yet his body did not bend.","Rakan slowly lowered his arms. His grin had vanished, and pure seriousness had taken its place.","\"Max,\" he said, \"from this point onward, if you insist on relying on only one Divine Vein, you might genuinely get hurt.\"","Max studied Rakan’s transformed state with calm eyes. He could feel the difference clearly. Rakan’s body had truly ascended to another level.","The First Limit had strengthened his blood, the Second Limit had reforged his bones, and the Third Limit had unbound his flesh. With all three combined, his physical body had become several times more terrifying than before, and this was no longer anything the First Limit alone could compare to.","Max smiled faintly. \"Good.\"","Rakan’s eyes narrowed. \"Still that same answer?\"","Max clenched his fists, and the Vein of Origin within him rumbled at a deeper pitch. \"Yes.\"","For a moment, the two of them stared at each other across the fractured battlefield. Then Rakan moved.","No one saw the first step clearly. The stage shattered beneath his foot, and his body materialized before Max like a bronze thunderbolt. His fist came down carrying no flashy display of energy but rather a bodily force so horrifying that the air ahead of it compressed into a visible wall.","Max crossed both arms, and Rakan’s fist landed.","Boom!","The impact was nothing like anything that had come before. Max’s body was blasted backward, and his feet tore across the stage, ripping open two deep trenches that stretched for dozens of meters.","The barrier behind him blazed with light, and only when he stomped down with tremendous force did his body finally come to a halt. The shock of that single stomp cracked the stage beneath him into a spiderweb pattern.","The War God Palace disciples exploded into cheers.","\"The Third Limit!\"","\"That is the Third Limit!\"","\"Rakan is back!\"","\"Even Max cannot stand his ground against that!\"","At the Black Dragon Clan, the disciples grew tense all over again.","But on the stage, Max slowly lowered his arms. His sleeves hung in tatters, and red marks streaked his forearms, yet his bones remained unbroken and his body had suffered no serious injury.","Rakan saw all of it clearly, and his eyes shone even brighter.","\"You blocked that?\"","Max flexed his fingers once, and the red marks along his arms began to fade. \"That one was heavy.\"","Rakan laughed sharply. \"Then take more!\"","He appeared again. With the Third Limit open, his speed far exceeded anything he had shown before. The stage cracked with his every movement, and each punch carried a layered force born from his blood, his bones, and his flesh releasing their power in unison.","Max met him head-on, but this time every collision forced him to adjust his stance. The Vein of Origin kept his foundation remarkably stable, yet Rakan’s Third Limit now commanded enough raw force to shake even that stability.","Boom!","Fist met fist, and Max’s arm trembled slightly. Rakan followed with an elbow, and though Max blocked it, the impact drove his shoulder downward. Rakan spun into a kick, and Max caught the leg, but the sheer force shoved him sideways across the stage.","The rhythm of the battle had shifted once again. Rakan was no longer the one being dominated. With the Second and Third Limits open, he had dragged the fight back into balance, and in terms of pure explosive physical force, he had even begun to suppress Max once more.","The participants watched with burning focus.","Damian Voss spoke quietly. \"Rakan’s body has become terrifying.\"","Orion Starfall nodded. \"All three limits at once. No wonder the War God Palace is known as the strongest force in body cultivation.\"","Kaiden Voidmere looked toward Max. \"And yet Max is still relying on only the first vein.\"","Ervin’s eyes remained calm. \"This is still not his full physical strength.\"","Revona watched in silence while her Void Origin Eyes reflected both figures as they crashed together again and again."]},{"number":1847,"title":"Chapter 1847: Draconic Essences shock the world!","paragraphs":["On the stage, Rakan’s fist hurtled toward Max’s head. Max ducked beneath it and drove a punch toward Rakan’s ribs, and Rakan took the blow directly.","Boom!","The force slammed into his body, but this time Rakan slid back only half a step. The Third Limit allowed his flesh to absorb and disperse the impact, while the Second Limit kept his frame perfectly stable.","Rakan grinned. \"Your punch is still strong, but it is no longer enough.\"","Max regarded him calmly.","Rakan stepped forward again with his battle intent blazing even higher. \"So, Max Morgan, will you open the second vein?\"","Max did not answer right away. The Vein of Origin continued to rumble within him, steady and profound, but the pressure of Rakan’s Third Limit was now unmistakably pressing against its edge. Max looked at Rakan’s bronze war body and smiled faintly.","\"You really are worthy of testing my body.\"","Rakan’s grin turned wild once more. \"Then stop holding back.\"","The two of them rushed forward again. Their fists collided at the center of the stage, and the shockwave surged upward like a pillar of invisible force, rattling the barrier and making the entire Eternal Hourglass arena tremble. The battle had climbed to a new level.","For several breaths, Max and Rakan remained locked together at the center of the stage, fist against fist, body against body, and strength against strength. The whole arena shuddered beneath them.","The cracks running through the dark gold stage tore wider, and the ancient runes embedded in the arena floor glowed brighter, as though the Eternal Hourglass itself had been forced to reinforce the battlefield just to withstand their clash.","Rakan’s Third Limit burned at full power. War Blood Awakening roared through his veins, War Bone Reforging held his frame as steady as divine metal, and War Flesh Unbound released terrifying explosive power from every inch of his body.","In that moment, Rakan no longer resembled an ordinary young genius. He looked like a living weapon that the War God Palace had forged for the single purpose of crushing enemies with his bare hands.","Yet Max still stood before him. The Vein of Origin rumbled steadily inside his body, deep and ancient, strengthening his physical foundation at its very root. Even though Rakan’s Third Limit had dragged the battle back into balance and had even begun to suppress him in raw explosive force, Max’s eyes remained perfectly calm.","Rakan grinned fiercely. \"Open the second vein.\"","Max looked at him, and the entire arena went quiet.","Countless spectators across the Divine Realm leaned forward without realizing they had moved. The disciples of the Black Dragon Clan sat rigid with tension, while the disciples of the War God Palace watched with burning eyes.","The top geniuses inside the Eternal Hourglass fixed their full attention on Max as well, because all of them understood what the second vein might mean. If the first vein alone had allowed Max to dominate Rakan’s First Limit, then the second vein would almost certainly lift his body to a far more terrifying height.","But Max only smiled faintly.","\"I will not need the second vein against you.\"","The words fell like thunder, and for a moment even Rakan’s grin froze in place.","The War God Palace disciples erupted in fury.","\"What did he just say?\"","\"He does not need the second vein against Rakan?\"","\"Arrogant!\"","\"That is the Third Limit of the War God Body!\"","\"Rakan, crush him!\"","At the Black Dragon Clan, many disciples were stunned at first, and then their blood began to heat. They could not tell whether Max was being recklessly arrogant or whether he genuinely held another method in reserve, but they had already watched him produce miracles time and time again.","Lady Virelia’s eyes narrowed slightly, and the seven family heads stared at the screen without blinking.","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, Rakan slowly withdrew his fist and took a single step back. His bronze war body still radiated terrifying pressure, but his expression had grown deeper and far more serious.","\"You will not need the second vein?\" Rakan asked.","Max nodded calmly. \"That is right.\"","Rakan stared at him for a moment and then laughed, and this time his laughter carried anger, excitement, and disbelief all at once.","\"Good. Very good. Then show me what gives you the confidence to say that.\"","Max did not answer with words. Instead, something inside his body awakened. It was not another vein, nor a Pseudo Cosmic Path, nor Dragonheart, nor the Emotion Severing Path. Deep within his body, two thousand Draconic Essences stirred at the same instant.","The change was immediate. A low dragon’s roar seemed to echo from within Max’s flesh and bones. It did not leave his mouth, and it did not come from the outside world. It rose from inside his body itself, from the countless essences of dragon power that had been refined, accumulated, and stored within him over time.","The moment those two thousand Draconic Essences began to circulate, the Vein of Origin responded as though it had finally found the perfect foundation to strengthen.","The rumbling inside Max’s body grew heavier. His blood flowed like a hidden river of dragons, and his bones released a faint resonance of gold and black. His muscles tightened, though never in any exaggerated way. Instead, his entire body grew more compact, more refined, and more terrifyingly dense.","The profound glow of the Vein of Origin deepened, and within that glow, traces of dragon force flickered like ancient scales concealed just beneath the surface of his skin.","The aura around Max rose once, then twice, and then rose yet again.","The central stage began to sink beneath his feet. The air around his body compressed until faint ripples spread visibly outward. His white hair lifted slightly, and his eyes grew brighter, colder, and far more oppressive than before. He still had not transformed.","No dragon scales covered his skin, and no enormous dragon shadow loomed behind him. Yet everyone present could feel that his physical strength had entered an entirely new tier.","The participants on the pillars reacted at once.","Damian Voss’s eyes sharpened. \"His body just rose again.\"","Orion Starfall’s smile disappeared completely. \"That feels like dragon aura.\"","Kaiden Voidmere’s gaze grew immeasurably deep. \"This must be the black dragon bloodline of the Black Dragon Clan.\"","Ervin watched in silence, though his expression grew more focused than before. \"The Vein of Origin strengthens the root, and the dragon bloodline supplies overwhelming physical force. That combination is dangerous.\"","Aurelian Lareth’s face turned dark, while Selene Vaeloria stared at Max with clenched fists, her pride battered again and again by every new layer he revealed."]},{"number":1848,"title":"Chapter 1848: A Cheap Copy","paragraphs":["On the stage, Rakan felt the change more keenly than anyone else. Max’s aura had risen, but Rakan was not convinced. Not yet. After all, an aura was only an aura, and body strength had to be proven through collision. The War God Body was not something that could be intimidated by pressure alone.","Rakan’s eyes blazed with war intent. \"Then take this!\"","He drew his fist back. The bronze markings across his entire body flared to life as the First Limit, the Second Limit, and the Third Limit resonated together. His blood roared, his bones hummed like divine metal, and his flesh poured out boundless war force.","The power of all three limits gathered into his right fist and twisted the air around it into a distorted vortex.","The War God Palace disciples roared along with him.","\"Rakan!\"","\"First Warlord!\"","\"The Three-Limit War Fist!\"","\"Crush him!\"","Rakan stepped forward and punched with everything he had. The stage shattered beneath him, and his fist tore through the air toward Max like a falling star of war.","Max raised his hand. He did not raise a fist, and he did not raise a palm. He extended a single index finger, calmly, and touched it to Rakan’s incoming fist.","Boom!","The impact detonated outward. The barrier around the central stage flashed violently, the arena floor beneath both fighters cracked in every direction, and a storm of compressed air swept across the stage with enough force that even the watching participants had to narrow their eyes.","But Max did not move. His finger remained pressed against Rakan’s fist, and Rakan’s full-strength punch had stopped dead.","The entire Eternal Hourglass arena plunged into absolute silence.","Rakan’s pupils contracted, and his body froze in place. The War God Palace disciples, who had been roaring only a moment earlier, suddenly lost their voices. Thousands of people stared at the giant screen as though their souls had drifted out of their bodies.","They had expected Max to block, or perhaps to retreat, and some had even expected him to reveal another vein. But not one of them had imagined he would stop Rakan’s full-strength Three-Limit War Fist with a single finger.","At the Black Dragon Clan, the disciples fell silent as well, and then the plaza exploded.","\"One finger!\"","\"He blocked Rakan with one finger!\"","\"That was Rakan’s full-strength punch!\"","\"Max did not even move!\"","\"Brother Max is a monster!\"","Lady Virelia’s lips parted slightly, and for one brief moment even she could not hide the shock in her eyes. The seven family heads stared at the screen while their expressions shifted again and again.","They had always known Max was special, and they had known he possessed hidden depths, but the scene before them had gone far beyond anything they had anticipated.","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, the top geniuses were shaken just as badly. Damian Voss’s hand tightened around the hilt of his sword. Orion Starfall stared at the stage and said nothing at all.","Kaiden Voidmere’s eyes reflected faint ripples of void, as though he were trying to perceive exactly how the Vein of Origin and the Draconic Essences had fused within Max’s body.","Ervin’s expression turned deadly serious, and Revona’s Void Origin Eyes stayed locked on Max’s finger. Aurelian Lareth’s face twisted into something ugly, and Selene Vaeloria went pale with disbelief.","Morgana Starveil whispered, \"That is simply unreasonable.\"","On the stage, Max looked at Rakan with unshaken calm. Rakan’s fist trembled against his finger, and it was not because Max was pushing him back. It was because Rakan was still pouring his strength forward and could not move that one finger by even the smallest fraction.","Max spoke quietly. \"Is this your full power?\"","Rakan’s eyes went wide, and then he roared. He wrenched his fist back and punched again, and Max raised the same finger.","Boom!","The second punch stopped. Rakan attacked again with a third punch, then a fourth, and then a fifth. Each blow carried the terrifying strength of the Third Limit, each one shook the stage, and each one made the barrier flare, yet every single strike was halted by Max’s finger.","It happened again, and again, and again.","Rakan’s fists grew faster and heavier. His body blurred as he attacked from every conceivable angle, striking from the front, from the sides, from above, and from below. He threw straight punches, hook punches, elbow strikes, shoulder slams, and even a crushing knee strike that could have snapped an ordinary divine body in half.","Max never moved from his spot. Sometimes he used only the tip of his finger, sometimes he shifted it half an inch, and sometimes he turned his wrist by the slightest degree. But no matter how Rakan attacked, everything ended at that single finger.","Boom! Rakan’s fist slammed into Max’s finger and stopped.","Boom! His elbow crashed down and stopped.","Boom! His shoulder charge thundered forward and stopped.","Boom! His knee rose with enough force to split the stage in two, but Max’s finger pressed down lightly and pinned it in place.","The more Rakan attacked, the quieter the arena became. This was no longer a fierce exchange between equals. This had become a gap, and it was a visible and undeniable one.","Rakan, the man who had forced Max to reveal the Vein of Origin and then pressed him hard enough to call upon two thousand Draconic Essences, was now incapable of moving Max at all with his full power.","The shock in Rakan’s eyes deepened with every blocked strike. At first there had been excitement, and then disbelief, and then anger, and then raw unwillingness. But as punch after punch failed to budge Max’s finger, even that unwillingness slowly began to change into something else.","It became acceptance.","Rakan finally stopped attacking. He stood before Max, breathing hard, with bronze light still burning around him and his fists trembling from the repeated impacts. His body was not broken, and his will had not collapsed, but his eyes had changed completely.","He looked at Max’s finger, and then he looked at Max, and for a long time he said nothing at all.","The War God Palace disciples watched in silence. No one was shouting anymore.","Even Saint Reiner, standing in the shadows, remained quiet for several breaths. His eyes were fixed on Max, and the faint smile he had worn earlier had dissolved into deep contemplation.","\"I expected this result,\" he sighed softly. \"After all, the War God Body was never anything more than a cheap imitation of the Seven Divine Veins.\"","He alone understood the truth of it. In ancient times, no human had ever been able to use the Seven Divine Veins, and so a number of them had gathered together to create a crude imitation of the technique, which later came to be known as the War God Body.","From that point onward, the War God Body reigned as the strongest body cultivation art in existence, for the simple reason that no one alive could open even a single vein of the true Seven Divine Veins.","But Saint Reiner had always known that a cheap copy would forever remain a cheap copy. He had devoted himself to researching the Seven Divine Veins and had eventually managed to piece together the complete technique, along with the method for opening all seven veins.","Even so, not a single genius, nor anyone else from the War God Palace, had ever succeeded in opening the Seven Divine Veins, and it was this failure that had driven Saint Reiner to build the two combat towers in search of a successor worthy of inheriting his life’s work."]},{"number":1849,"title":"Chapter 1849: Rakan Admits Defeat!","paragraphs":["Back inside the arena, Rakan slowly lowered his fists, and his bronze aura began to settle. Max watched him calmly and made no move to attack.","Rakan drew a deep breath, and then he laughed once. The laugh was not loud, and it was not arrogant. It was a rough sound woven from helplessness, admiration, and a warrior’s honest acceptance.","\"I lose.\"","The words carried across the stage, and the entire Divine Realm fell silent once more. Rakan Thorne, the first Warlord of the War God Palace, had just admitted defeat in a battle of pure body strength.","Max lowered his hand. \"You are strong,\" he said calmly.","Rakan looked at him and shook his head. \"Not strong enough.\"","Max did not mock him.","Rakan stared down at his trembling fists and smiled bitterly. \"I opened three limits of the War God Body, and I still could not move a single finger. If this had been a fight to the death, you would have crushed me the moment you brought out that dragon power.\"","Max remained silent. Rakan lifted his head again, and though his eyes still burned, the battle inside him had already ended.","\"I accept defeat.\"","Angelina Valerius looked at the two of them and made the announcement in a calm voice.","[Winner: Max Morgan.]","[Rakan Thorne Defeated.]","The screen above the arena changed immediately.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Max Morgan]","[Total Battles Fought: 2]","[Total Wins: 2]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Rakan Thorne]","[Total Battles Fought: 3]","[Total Wins: 2]","The result appeared before everyone, and for a moment no one reacted at all. Then the Divine Realm erupted.","At the Black Dragon Clan, countless disciples screamed Max’s name with everything their lungs could give, and some grew so excited that their voices cracked. Lady Virelia gazed at the screen with a faint smile, though her eyes held an emotion that ran far deeper than simple pride.","The seven family heads stood in silence for a few breaths until one of them finally burst out laughing, and soon the rest of them followed.","At the War God Palace, the disciples stayed quiet. No one blamed Rakan, and no one would have dared to. They had watched the entire battle unfold. Rakan had opened three limits and had fought with every ounce of power his body could release at this stage of his cultivation, yet Max had surpassed him in the very field that was the War God Palace’s greatest pride.","A defeat of that kind could not be waved away with excuses. It could only be swallowed.","On the central stage, Rakan looked at Max one final time as the transfer light began to descend.","\"Next time,\" he said, \"I will have broken the fourth limit.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"We will see.\"","Rakan stared at him for a moment, and then he laughed loudly as the transfer light carried him back to his pillar.","Max returned to his own pillar a moment later, the Vein of Origin gradually quieting within his body while the power of the two thousand Draconic Essences settled back into his flesh.","The other participants looked at him differently now. Before this battle, they had known Max was dangerous. After this battle, they understood something far more unsettling.","Even when he set aside Dragonheart, the Emotion Severing Path, the Divine King Punishment, the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline, his dragon scales, and every other hidden power he carried, his body alone was enough to crush one of the strongest body cultivators of the entire younger generation.","The final competitive stage had only just begun, but Max Morgan had already shaken the Divine Realm.","After Max and Rakan returned to their pillars, the entire Eternal Hourglass arena remained restless for a long while.","Rakan Thorne had lost, and he had not lost through swordsmanship, nor through a Pseudo Cosmic Path, nor through soul power, lightning, space, or bloodline suppression. He had lost in a battle of pure body strength, and that fact made the result far more shocking than any ordinary defeat.","The first Warlord of the War God Palace had opened the first three limits of the War God Body, yet Max had stopped his full-strength attacks with a single finger after combining the Vein of Origin with the power of two thousand Draconic Essences.","That one scene had swept across the Divine Realm like a thunderclap, and countless forces watching the conference quietly began recalculating Max Morgan’s position in their plans.","Inside the arena, the remaining participants also looked at Max with new eyes. Damian Voss’s gaze toward him had grown sharper, and Orion Starfall’s smile now carried a deeper layer of interest. Kaiden Voidmere watched him as though attempting to decipher a complicated secret, while Ervin remained silent, though his eyes no longer drifted away from Max casually.","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes opened and closed from time to time, as if even she was weighing how her nullification would fare against a body foundation of that kind.","Angelina Valerius did not allow the arena to linger in its shock for long, because the final competitive stage had to continue.","\"The next battle will now begin,\" she said calmly.","The screen above the arena spun once more.","[Final Competitive Stage, Battle Twenty-Four]","[Selene Vaeloria vs Hadeon Granite]","Selene stepped onto the stage wearing a cold expression. She had already lost to Ervin, and that defeat plainly weighed on her pride. Hadeon Granite, by contrast, was a defensive fighter who had already endured several punishing matchups. The moment the battle began, he wrapped himself in layers of gray stone armor and tried to hold out while waiting for an opening.","Selene refused to give him one. Heavenly Luminance light flooded across the stage, and the Heavenly Luminance Queen Avatar materialized behind her in a flash. She raised one hand, and twelve radiant edicts descended at once. Hadeon’s stone armor cracked beneath the pressure and his barriers dimmed, and before he could reinforce them, a spear of golden white light came to a halt before his forehead.","\"I surrender,\" Hadeon said bitterly.","[Winner: Selene Vaeloria.]","[Hadeon Granite Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Selene Vaeloria]","[Total Battles Fought: 3]","[Total Wins: 2]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Hadeon Granite]","[Total Battles Fought: 2]","[Total Wins: 0]","Selene returned to her pillar, but her expression did not soften. A victory over Hadeon could not erase her loss to Ervin, nor could it wash away the humiliation of having been defeated by Max before the final stage had even begun.","The next battle arrived quickly.","[Final Competitive Stage, Battle Twenty-Five]","[Damian Voss vs Yelric Flamehorn]","Yelric Flamehorn’s face went stiff the instant he saw Damian’s name. He had already lost to Revona, and now he faced the strongest genius of the Sword God Palace. Even so, he did not surrender on the spot, for his pride would not permit it. Flames erupted across his body, and he charged forward with a blazing halberd in hand.","Damian drew his sword. His first slash cut the flames apart, his second slash severed the halberd’s head from its shaft, and his third stroke of sword light came to rest at Yelric’s throat. The battle ended so cleanly that many spectators had barely begun to cheer before Angelina announced the result.","[Winner: Damian Voss.]","[Yelric Flamehorn Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Damian Voss]","[Total Battles Fought: 4]","[Total Wins: 4]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Yelric Flamehorn]","[Total Battles Fought: 2]","[Total Wins: 0]","Damian returned to his pillar with the same composed expression, still keeping his Pseudo Cosmic Path hidden. Max watched him quietly. Damian’s swordsmanship remained simple, direct, and terrifyingly refined, and every time he fought, he revealed only enough to win and not a fraction more.","The battles pressed onward."]},{"number":1850,"title":"Chapter 1850: Orion vs Revona","paragraphs":["[Final Competitive Stage, Battle Twenty-Six]","[Aurelian Lareth vs Vaela Sunspire]","Vaela Sunspire had already suffered one loss, yet she still unleashed the full measure of her sunfire the moment the battle began. Golden flames rolled across the stage and transformed half the arena into a burning solar field.","Against ordinary light cultivators, her sunfire might have posed a real problem, but Aurelian’s Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion was simply too domineering. This time he did not even need to manifest it in full.","A golden decree appeared above the stage, and the sunfire was pressed down from on high as though a greater authority had descended upon it. Vaela struggled to resist, but Aurelian’s divine light pierced through her flames and stopped just before her chest.","She gritted her teeth and surrendered.","[Winner: Aurelian Lareth.]","[Vaela Sunspire Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Aurelian Lareth]","[Total Battles Fought: 3]","[Total Wins: 3]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Vaela Sunspire]","[Total Battles Fought: 2]","[Total Wins: 0]","Max’s gaze turned cold once more as Aurelian returned to his pillar. Every time Aurelian wielded that divine light, the rejection stirring within Max’s bloodline grew clearer. The Divine Son’s strength was undeniably real, but to Max it still felt like a beautiful palace erected on stolen foundations.","The next several battles passed even faster. Kaiden Voidmere defeated a beast-blooded warrior by folding the space beneath his feet so that his charge collapsed halfway through. Morgana Starveil overcame a thunder-winged spearwoman by cursing the lightning around her wings until every burst of speed dragged the woman deeper into Morgana’s trap.","Rosaline Lunara faced a soul-path participant and calmly sealed his soul bells inside radiant petals, forcing his surrender before he could activate his strongest technique. Fin Arclight fought a bloodfire cultivator and scraped out a narrow victory after using Pale Eclipse Burial to dull the burning rhythm of the bloodfire, though the battle left him breathing harder than before.","The records kept shifting.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Kaiden Voidmere]","[Total Battles Fought: 3]","[Total Wins: 3]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Morgana Starveil]","[Total Battles Fought: 4]","[Total Wins: 3]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Rosaline Lunara]","[Total Battles Fought: 3]","[Total Wins: 2]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Fin Arclight]","[Total Battles Fought: 3]","[Total Wins: 3]","With every passing battle, the gap between the strongest participants and everyone else grew more obvious. The top geniuses kept on winning. Some claimed victory with casual ease, some prevailed only after drawing on a small portion of their deeper strength, and some concealed their trump cards so carefully that even their victories felt incomplete, as though everyone watching understood they had shown nothing but the surface.","Max fought again as well. His next opponent was a silver-haired beastkin genius named Kael Thornclaw, whose speed and claws had shredded several opponents earlier in the stage.","The moment the battle began, Kael underwent a partial transformation, silver fur sweeping down his arms while his claws gleamed like divine blades. He shot toward Max with enough speed to scatter afterimages across the stage.","Max did not call upon the Vein of Origin this time, because he did not need it. When Kael appeared behind him and slashed toward his neck, Max turned slightly, caught the incoming wrist, and hurled him across the stage. Kael twisted in midair, landed on his feet, and attacked again, but Max stepped forward and struck him once in the chest with his palm.","Boom!","Kael crashed into the barrier and slid down its surface, coughing blood. He tried to rise, and then he slowly lowered his head.","\"I surrender.\"","[Winner: Max Morgan.]","[Kael Thornclaw Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Max Morgan]","[Total Battles Fought: 3]","[Total Wins: 3]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Kael Thornclaw]","[Total Battles Fought: 2]","[Total Wins: 0]","The result surprised no one anymore, yet it still thickened the pressure gathering around Max. After his victory over Rakan, even his effortless wins felt terrifying, because everyone understood that he was not using even a fraction of what he had revealed in that body battle.","Another battle followed.","[Final Competitive Stage, Battle Thirty-Two]","[Ervin vs Darius Stoneveil]","Darius Stoneveil entered the stage with several defensive layers already raised, but against Ervin, defense alone counted for very little.","Ervin’s black spear pierced through the barriers in a single unbroken line, not by shattering them with violence, but by sinking through them as though the distance between the spear and its target had simply been swallowed.","The spearpoint came to rest before Darius’s chest. Darius stared at Ervin with a pale face and surrendered without attempting to drag out the battle.","[Winner: Ervin.]","[Darius Stoneveil Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Ervin]","[Total Battles Fought: 3]","[Total Wins: 3]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Darius Stoneveil]","[Total Battles Fought: 3]","[Total Wins: 0]","Ervin returned to his pillar in silence. After his battle with Selene, no one regarded him as an unknown dark horse any longer, for his Abyssal Origin Descent had already placed him firmly among the most dangerous figures in the final stage.","Battle followed battle. Rakan also fought again after recovering from his loss to Max. His opponent was a sound-attribute participant who tried to attack his inner organs through vibration, but Rakan opened only the First Limit of the War God Body, crushed the sound waves beneath a roar of pure battle intent, and ended the fight with a single punch.","His victory restored a measure of morale to the War God Palace disciples, though the shadow of his defeat to Max still lingered over them.","[Winner: Rakan Thorne.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Rakan Thorne]","[Total Battles Fought: 4]","[Total Wins: 3]","The final competitive stage surged forward like a storm. Some participants began sinking under repeated losses, and others fought simply to keep their records even, but the top monsters continued their climb.","Max, Damian, Orion, Kaiden, Ervin, Revona, Aurelian, and a handful of others held their places near the front. Whenever one of their names appeared opposite a weaker opponent, the result felt almost predetermined, and the only real question was whether the weaker participant could force them to reveal anything useful before falling.","For a while, the strongest were never matched against one another, and that fact only wound the arena tighter. Every spin of the screen carried the same silent question. When would the next monster collide with another monster?","The answer arrived sooner than many had expected.","Angelina Valerius raised her hand once more, and the giant screen above the arena began to rotate.","Names flashed past one after another, including Max Morgan, Damian Voss, Aurelian Lareth, Kaiden Voidmere, Ervin, Rakan Thorne, Morgana Starveil, Selene Vaeloria, Rosaline Lunara, Revona, and Orion Starfall.","The light slowed, and the entire arena went quiet. Then two names expanded at the center of the screen.","[Final Competitive Stage, Battle Thirty-Nine]","[Orion Starfall vs Revona]","A wave of excitement rippled through the arena at once. Orion Starfall, the strongest genius of the Nine Star Court, had finally been matched against Revona, the woman whose Void Origin Eyes could nullify attacks and reduce even powerful techniques to nothingness.","Max’s eyes sharpened immediately, for this was a battle worth watching.","Orion looked toward Revona’s pillar and smiled faintly. \"This will be troublesome.\"","Revona opened her eyes slowly, and the void-colored light within them flickered like some ancient emptiness given form.","\"You think so?\" she asked with a smile.","The arena fell completely silent.","Angelina Valerius looked toward the two of them and spoke calmly.","\"Orion Starfall. Revona. Enter the stage.\""]},{"number":1851,"title":"Chapter 1851: Power of Stars!","paragraphs":["Two beams of light descended from above.","Orion Starfall appeared on one side of the central stage, his dark gold armor reflecting the flowing rivers of time-light that streamed above the Eternal Hourglass.","The nine star marks on his body glowed faintly, not yet fully awakened, but bright enough to make him look as though he carried a small night sky within his own flesh. His expression remained composed, and his familiar smile still rested on his face, though the easy playfulness in his eyes had noticeably thinned.","Revona appeared opposite him. She stood quietly with a relaxed posture, her eyes half open while a faint void-colored light flickered within her pupils. Compared to Orion’s radiant aura of stars, she felt almost silent, yet that very silence was what made her so dangerous. Her Void Origin Eyes had already nullified far too many attacks for anyone present to take her lightly.","For a moment, neither of them attacked.","Orion studied her with interest and asked, \"Before we begin, may I ask you something?\"","Revona’s expression did not shift. \"Ask.\"","\"Is there truly a way to bypass the ability of your Void Origin Eyes?\"","The question made several participants lean in with sharper focus. Revona’s eyes flickered slightly, and then she nodded. \"Yes.\"","The answer sent a ripple of surprise across the pillars.","Orion’s eyebrows rose. \"There is?\"","Revona turned her gaze toward one particular pillar, where Max stood in silence. Orion followed her line of sight.","Revona said calmly, \"One individual managed to do so in the past.\"","Orion paused before asking, \"Who?\"","Her answer was simple. \"Max.\"","The arena went quiet for the space of a breath, and then many gazes swung toward Max all at once. His expression remained calm, as though the matter had nothing to do with him at all.","He had defeated Revona once before, but he understood perfectly well that the Revona standing on the stage now was no longer the same woman he had fought back then. Her Void Origin Eyes had awakened further since that day, and her power to nullify attacks had grown far smoother and far more complete.","Orion stared at Max for a moment, then shook his head with a wry smile. \"Of course it would be him.\"","A few of the participants wore complicated expressions after hearing it.","Rakan Thorne chuckled softly from his pillar. \"That guy really is everywhere.\"","Morgana Starveil smiled faintly. \"At this point, I would be more surprised if Max had not done it.\"","Kaiden Voidmere looked toward Max with thoughtful eyes, while Damian Voss said nothing at all.","Orion turned his attention back to Revona and exhaled lightly. \"Then I suppose I will have to find my own way.\"","Revona opened her eyes fully, and void-colored light spread through her pupils. \"You can try.\"","Angelina Valerius raised her hand.","[Battle Begins.]","Orion moved first, though he did not rush forward. In truth, he showed no intention of entering close combat at all. As the strongest genius of the Nine Star Court, Orion Starfall rarely fought with fists, blades, or techniques of short range.","His strength lived among the stars. His attacks descended from above, crossed vast distances as beams of light, and overwhelmed opponents through precision, sheer numbers, and celestial pressure. He was a long-range fighter by his very nature, and nearly all of his methods were built around commanding the battlefield from afar.","One star mark on his body lit up, and a single beam of starlight dropped from above the stage. It was thin, bright, and fast enough to arrive before most people could even react. The beam shot toward Revona’s shoulder, and it was clearly intended as a probe rather than a genuine killing blow.","Revona looked at it, and the beam vanished. There was no explosion, no resistance, and no sound of any kind. It simply ceased to exist the instant it entered the range of her gaze.","Orion showed no surprise. A second star mark lit up, and this time two beams of starlight descended from different angles, one aimed at Revona’s left side while the other curved around toward her back. Their paths were clean and precise, designed to force her to either turn or defend in two directions at once.","Revona’s eyes shifted. The first beam vanished, and then the second followed it into nothing.","Orion smiled faintly. \"So two is not enough.\"","Three star marks lit up, and then five, and then ten. The sky above the central stage darkened as ten points of starlight bloomed in the air. Each point released a beam, and the ten beams descended together like divine arrows loosed from the night sky.","Nor did they travel in straight lines alone. Some curved, some split apart, some accelerated at the halfway mark, and some delayed themselves by a fraction of a breath so they might strike after the first wave had been erased.","Revona stood without moving as her Void Origin Eyes shone brighter. Wherever her gaze swept, the star beams winked out one after another. Some vanished long before reaching her, some disappeared mere inches from her body, and some were erased in the middle of their curving flight, leaving behind nothing but faint ripples of empty space.","The ten-star attack failed.","Orion raised his hand, and a hundred stars appeared. The entire arena brightened. Many participants narrowed their eyes as one hundred points of starlight took shape above the stage and surrounded Revona from every direction.","The pressure of this attack belonged to an entirely different order than what had come before. Each star carried a compressed beam, and together they wove a vast celestial net that left almost no gap through which to escape.","\"Nine Star Court. Hundred Star Descent.\"","The one hundred beams fell, and for a moment the stage looked as though an entire starry sky were collapsing upon it. Spectators across the Divine Realm held their breath. The attack was grand, beautiful, and terrifying all at once.","Every beam carried enough force to punch through a formidable defense, and with one hundred descending in unison, the pressure was enough to make even some of the top geniuses treat it with respect.","Revona finally moved, though she went neither backward nor forward. She simply turned slowly in place while her Void Origin Eyes glowed like two entrances into nothingness. The first twenty beams vanished, then forty, then seventy, and then all one hundred.","The entire Hundred Star Descent was erased before a single beam could touch her."]},{"number":1852,"title":"Chapter 1852: A Bad Match Up?","paragraphs":["The arena fell silent, and Orion’s smile grew more serious.","He lifted both hands. The nine star marks across his body brightened in unison, and the space above the arena transformed into a vast night sky teeming with countless small stars.","At first there were hundreds, then a thousand, and then several thousand more. The starlight gathered so densely that it looked as though an inverted galaxy had formed above the central stage.","Even Max’s eyes sharpened slightly, for this attack was anything but weak. A thousand star beams did not simply mean greater numbers. Every beam carried Orion’s personal control, and every star possessed its own angle, speed, delay, and trajectory.","Against any ordinary opponent, an attack of this kind would be impossible to defend, because even if they somehow blocked hundreds of beams, the remainder would pierce through whatever opening appeared.","Orion’s voice rang out with calm authority.","\"Nine Star Court. Thousand Star Rain.\"","The galaxy descended. Thousands of star beams plunged toward Revona, and the entire arena was swallowed in starlight. The barrier around the central stage flashed as the pressure of the attack rolled outward, and audiences throughout the Divine Realm erupted in shock.","The disciples of the Nine Star Court, watching from their own divine viewing platform, rose to their feet with shining eyes and faces full of pride. This was exactly the kind of grand and overwhelming assault their force was famous for. Their stars never needed to draw close, for their stars passed judgment from above.","But Revona stood beneath that falling galaxy and simply raised her head. Her Void Origin Eyes released a deeper glow. The first layer of starlight vanished, then the second, and then the third. The beams poured down without end, yet wherever her eyes traveled, they dissolved into nothingness.","The sight was almost impossible to believe. A thousand beams of starlight descended with magnificent force, and they were erased layer after layer, as though the sky itself were being emptied by nothing more than her gaze.","Some beams attempted to strike from behind her, but Revona’s eyes flickered, a faint ripple of void spread around her body, and those beams disappeared as well.","Other beams delayed their descent and dove in from blind angles, yet she turned only slightly and they vanished before arrival. Still others split into smaller beams at the final moment, and even those fragments were wiped away.","By the time the Thousand Star Rain ended, Revona remained standing exactly where she had begun, untouched and unshaken. The stage around her had not suffered so much as a scratch, because not one of the attacks had ever been permitted to land.","The silence that followed weighed heavier than any before it.","Orion regarded her for a long moment, then lowered his hands, and his smile turned wry. \"You might be the worst possible matchup for me.\"","Revona watched him quietly.","Orion shook his head and went on. \"Nearly all of my attacks are long-ranged. I fight with star beams, star rain, star spears, falling star arrays, and celestial suppression. I control the battlefield from a distance and overwhelm my opponents before they can ever approach me. But your Void Origin Eyes can nullify ranged attacks before they reach you, and against someone like me, that ability is almost unfair.\"","Revona’s expression stayed calm. \"Almost.\"","Orion laughed softly. \"You are right. Almost.\"","On the pillars, the top geniuses watched with grave expressions, and Max’s gaze remained fixed on the stage. He had expected Revona to be troublesome, but watching her erase Orion’s attacks one after another confirmed just how much stronger her eyes had grown.","A single beam, ten beams, a hundred beams, and finally a thousand beams had all dissolved beneath her gaze. Unless Orion revealed something deeper, this battle would lead nowhere.","Revona looked at Orion and spoke with quiet certainty. \"Use your Pseudo Cosmic Path.\"","Orion’s smile slowly faded. The nine star marks on his body began to glow once more, but this time the light was different. It ran deeper, felt older, and carried a majesty far beyond anything he had shown. Revona’s Void Origin Eyes brightened as she watched him.","Orion lifted his gaze to the vast space above the arena and said softly, \"I was hoping to save this for later.\" Then his eyes returned to Revona. \"But against you, ordinary stars truly are useless.\"","The stage began to tremble faintly, and high above the central arena, the rivers of time-light reflected the birth of a new starry sky.","Orion raised one hand. \"Then let us see whether your Void Origin Eyes can erase my path itself.\"","The moment Orion raised his hand, the entire atmosphere of the central stage transformed. The thousands of stars that Revona had erased did not return, yet their disappearance seemed to have roused something far deeper within him.","The nine star marks on his body no longer resembled simple symbols. They had become nine ancient star gates carved into his flesh, and each one released a different rhythm of celestial power.","One gate carried burning heat like a young sun, another carried cold silver light like a frozen moon, and another carried sharpness like a falling meteor. One bore crushing weight like a dead star, one held speed like a shooting comet, and one radiated endless pressure like a collapsing sky. The remaining three were more mysterious still, glowing with colors that shifted between gold, blue, violet, and pure white.","Revona’s expression finally changed by a fraction. She could tell that what stood before her was no longer a mere star technique. This was no longer a simple attack that fell from the sky and flew toward her body.","This was a path. It was a majestic, complete, and terrifying Pseudo Cosmic Path that had gathered the inheritance, the pride, and the very foundation of the Nine Star Court into a single body.","Orion slowly lowered his hand to his chest, and the star marks across his body blazed brighter and brighter until the space above him fell into darkness. It was not dark in the way of the abyss that surrounded Ervin, and it was not the darkness of empty nothingness.","This was the darkness of the universe in the moments before dawn, wide and silent and endless, filled with countless stars waiting for the signal to awaken.","Then the starry sky descended, and it did not fall upon Revona. It converged into Orion."]},{"number":1853,"title":"Chapter 1853: Nine Star Sovereign Body","paragraphs":["The first star entered his left hand, and the second entered his right. The third star sank into his spine, the fourth entered his eyes, and the fifth merged with his heart. The sixth star wrapped itself around his bones, the seventh burned its way into his blood, and the eighth spread across his flesh.","Finally, the ninth star formed a brilliant crown of starlight above his head before sinking into his body like a divine seal.","Orion’s aura changed completely.","Until this moment, he had been a long-range star cultivator whose attacks descended from above and overwhelmed his enemies through their numbers, their angles, their speed, and their celestial pressure.","But now, with his Pseudo Cosmic Path fully open, the power of the stars no longer hung far away from him. It gathered into his body and transformed him from a distant commander of stars into a supreme genius of close combat.","His fingers glowed with lines of starlight, his bones released faint celestial hums, and his very steps fell into rhythm with a starry sky. The entire arena could feel the difference.","Orion Starfall was no longer using stars. He had become the vessel of his stars.","His voice rang across the stage, calm and clear.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path. Nine Star Sovereign Body.\"","Boom!","A wave of majestic star pressure erupted from him, and the central stage trembled. Above his head, an enormous illusory star palace took shape. It stood among galaxies, encircled by nine vast stars, and at its center rose a throne forged from condensed starlight.","The throne did not look tyrannical the way Aurelian’s Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion did, and it did not feel suppressive like Rosaline’s Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary. Instead, it felt grand, noble, and nearly immeasurable, as though Orion had borrowed the ancient authority of the starry heavens and set that authority directly into his own flesh.","Across the Divine Realm, countless spectators rose from their seats, and at the Nine Star Court, the disciples and elders erupted into roaring cheers.","\"The Nine Star Sovereign Body!\"","\"Senior Brother Orion has revealed it!\"","\"That is one of the strongest Pseudo Cosmic Paths in the Divine Realm!\"","\"It is no ordinary star technique. Once he enters that state, every star he controls becomes part of his body!\"","\"Long range, close combat, movement, defense, and suppression all become star power!\"","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, every one of the top geniuses grew serious.","Damian Voss’s gaze sharpened. \"So that is his path.\"","Kaiden Voidmere narrowed his eyes. \"The stars are no longer traveling toward Revona. They have already converged into him, and that changes the very nature of the attack.\"","Ervin studied Orion with a deeper gaze. \"It turns a long-range star cultivator into a close combat monster.\"","Rakan Thorne grinned as his battle intent visibly climbed again. \"Good. That guy was hiding something fun.\"","Morgana Starveil’s eyes flickered. \"The Nine Star Court truly raised a terrifying genius.\"","Max watched in silence. He had always known Orion was strong, yet this Pseudo Cosmic Path still managed to surprise him. The Nine Star Sovereign Body was not flashy in any shallow sense. Its majesty came from the fact that it solved the greatest weakness of a star-based long-range fighter.","Orion’s ordinary methods could be erased by Revona’s Void Origin Eyes before they ever arrived, but once the stars entered his body, every punch, step, elbow, palm, and knee became a star attack delivered through direct physical contact.","Revona could nullify attacks that traveled toward her. But could she erase a star that had already become part of Orion’s body? That was the real question.","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes shone brighter. \"You chose a good path,\" she said calmly.","Orion smiled faintly. \"I had no choice. A person of the Nine Star Court is supposed to command the stars from above, but I never liked having only one way to fight.\"","Revona raised one hand. \"Then come.\"","Orion vanished. He did not move the way a normal body cultivator moved. His movement resembled a shooting star crossing a stretch of night sky. One moment he stood at a distance, and the next he appeared directly in front of Revona with his fist wrapped in condensed starlight.","Revona’s eyes locked onto that fist, and the starlight around it dimmed, yet it did not vanish completely. Orion’s fist still arrived. Revona slid sideways, and the blow brushed past her shoulder. The star force packed inside it struck the air behind her and detonated into a brilliant ring of light that set the barrier trembling.","Orion’s eyes brightened. \"So direct star force can be weakened, but it cannot be erased instantly.\"","Revona gave no answer. Her eyes flickered, and a ripple of void spread toward Orion’s chest. Had that ripple touched him, it would have tried to nullify the star power converged within his body, but Orion had already stepped clear.","The third star in his spine flashed, and his body cut away along a sharp diagonal, trailing a brief streak of blue and white light behind him.","He attacked again. His palm, his elbow, his knee, and his finger strike each carried a different star. The palm bore the crushing pressure of a dead star, the elbow carried the sharpness of a meteor, the knee burned with solar force, and the finger strike moved with the compressed speed of a comet.","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes worked without pause. Wherever her gaze fell, the star force weakened, distorted, or dimmed. Yet the attacks no longer disappeared as easily as they once had. Orion’s stars were not beams crossing open air anymore.","They had already fused into his body, and by the time Revona’s gaze reached them, they had become part of his movement, his flesh, and his martial rhythm.","The battle accelerated. Orion circled Revona like a living constellation, while Revona stayed composed, stepping back, turning, and raising her hands only when it became necessary.","Her Void Origin Eyes still erased a great deal of his force, but she could no longer stand motionless the way she had beneath the Thousand Star Rain. Now she had to move, she had to predict, and she had to decide which part of each attack to nullify first."]},{"number":1854,"title":"Chapter 1854: Bypassing Her Ability!","paragraphs":["The shift stunned many of the spectators.","\"She moved!\"","\"Revona actually stepped back!\"","\"Orion’s Pseudo Cosmic Path is working!\"","\"His attacks are not being fully erased!\"","At the Nine Star Court, the cheering swelled even louder, and at the Black Dragon Clan, the disciples watched with widening eyes. Even at the War God Palace, many body cultivators regarded Orion with newfound respect.","They rarely admired long-range fighters, but the Nine Star Sovereign Body had turned Orion into a genius of close combat without ever abandoning his star foundation, and that alone was enough to earn their attention.","On the stage, Orion’s attacks grew heavier.","\"Nine Star Sovereign Body. First Star Fist.\"","His fist descended wrapped in blazing star heat. Revona’s eyes flashed, and half the heat vanished, but the remaining half still forced her to raise her arm.","Boom!","Revona slid back half a step, and for one breath the entire arena went silent.","Orion did not stop.","\"Second Star Step.\"","His body shifted behind Revona like a star changing its orbit. She turned instantly with her Void Origin Eyes already seeking him, but Orion’s third star flashed before her gaze could fully settle.","\"Third Star Elbow.\"","The elbow strike arrived from an impossible angle. Revona nullified most of it, but a small remnant of star force slipped through and struck the defensive ripple of void surrounding her body.","Bang!","A faint crack appeared in the void ripple, and Revona’s expression grew colder.","Orion smiled. \"It seems there is a delay.\"","Revona’s eyes narrowed slightly.","Orion pressed on. \"Your Void Origin Eyes are terrifying against anything that travels toward you, but when the attack is already bound to my body, you have to identify the exact star force inside each movement before you can erase it. If I change stars quickly enough, even you cannot erase everything in the same instant.\"","Revona did not deny it. Instead, she stepped forward for the first time as void light gathered around her fingers.","\"Then I will erase you before you finish changing.\"","She attacked. Her movement was quiet, yet the danger inside it was terrifying. Her fingers carried the nullification of the void origin, no longer as a ranged phenomenon but as a direct close combat technique.","Orion’s eyes sharpened, the fourth star sank into his right leg, and he pivoted just clear of her fingers while sweeping his leg toward her waist.","Revona’s eyes flickered, and the star force inside his leg dimmed. But Orion changed again. The fifth star entered his left shoulder, he abandoned the kick midway, stepped inside her guard, and struck with his shoulder.","Revona’s pupils contracted slightly. The change had come too fast. Her gaze had already locked onto the leg, and by the time it shifted to the shoulder, Orion was already upon her.","Boom!","The shoulder strike landed, and Revona was driven backward. She did not lose half a step this time. She lost three full steps.","The entire arena exploded with shock.","\"He hit her!\"","\"Orion bypassed the Void Origin Eyes!\"","\"That was a clean, direct strike!\"","\"Did Revona’s ability fail?\"","\"No, it did not fail. Orion changed his star force faster than she could erase it!\"","Revona came to a stop after the third step, her long hair drifting around her face. Her body carried no serious injury, but the fact that Orion had landed a clean strike mattered far more than any damage.","It proved something important. Her Void Origin Eyes could be bypassed. It could not be done easily, and it could not be done with ordinary power, but with sufficient speed, transformation, timing, and a Pseudo Cosmic Path strong enough to change the very nature of its attacks, it could be done.","On the pillars, even the top geniuses reacted.","Damian Voss’s eyes turned razor sharp. \"He found an opening.\"","Kaiden Voidmere spoke softly. \"It is not an opening in the eyes themselves, but an opening in the reaction process behind them.\"","Ervin nodded faintly. \"The eyes can erase what they recognize, and Orion keeps changing what they need to recognize.\"","Rakan Thorne laughed. \"Now that is more like it.\"","Morgana Starveil looked at Orion with fresh caution. \"So the smiling star prince is also a monster in close combat.\"","Aurelian Lareth’s expression stayed cold, though even he could not dismiss what he had just witnessed, and Selene Vaeloria stared at the stage with a complicated look in her eyes.","Max watched in silence, his gaze calm but intent. Orion had not simply overwhelmed Revona with strength. He had found a way to pressure the very mechanism behind her ability, and that made him far more dangerous than anyone who relied only on grand displays of star power.","On the stage, Orion lowered his shoulder and smiled faintly, though his breathing had grown a touch heavier. Sustaining the Nine Star Sovereign Body while constantly cycling star forces through his own flesh was clearly no effortless feat.","Revona slowly raised her hand and touched the spot where his shoulder had struck her. Then she looked at him, and for the first time a faint smile crossed her face.","\"Good.\"","Orion shook his head lightly. \"You are saying that after being hit?\"","\"Yes,\" Revona said calmly. \"Because now this battle has become meaningful.\"","The void-colored light in her eyes deepened, and the air around her began to disappear in small, silent fragments.","As her words settled, the void surrounding her grew deeper still. The place where Orion’s shoulder had struck her still bore a faint trace of starlight, but that trace was already dissolving beneath the glow of her Void Origin Eyes.","She did not look angry, and she did not look humiliated. Instead, her expression carried a calm seriousness that dimmed Orion’s own smile a little further, because he understood what it meant. The battle had finally reached the point where Revona would stop treating him as someone whose attacks could simply be erased from a distance.","Orion rolled his shoulder once, and the Nine Star Sovereign Body within him burned brighter. Star lines spread from his chest into his arms and from his spine down into his legs, until his entire body looked as though a miniature galaxy had been carved beneath his skin.","The nine ancient stars revolving inside him began to spin faster, and every rotation lifted his close combat power to a higher level. His breathing grew heavier, yet his aura became more majestic, as if each breath drew power down from some faraway starry heaven and condensed it into his flesh.","Revona raised her hand slowly, and the air around her fingertips vanished. It was not shattered, and it was not cut apart. It simply vanished. A circle of emptiness spread out beneath her feet, silent and smooth, and wherever it passed, the light of the arena dimmed as though it had been swallowed before it could exist.","The stage did not break, the cracks did not widen, and even the dust near her feet disappeared without a sound, leaving behind a clean and hollow space that looked disturbingly calm."]},{"number":1855,"title":"Chapter 1855: Revona’s Pseudo Cosmic Path!","paragraphs":["Orion’s eyes narrowed. \"That looks dangerous.\"","Revona regarded him evenly. \"It is.\"","Then she stepped forward.","For the first time in the battle, Revona attacked with clear initiative. Her figure crossed the stage in strange silence. She was not fast in the explosive way Rakan moved, she was not elegant like Kaiden with his void steps, and she was not grand like Orion in his star movement.\\","She moved as though distance had simply forgotten to resist her. Her right hand reached for Orion’s chest, and the void gathered around her fingers carried the power to erase the star force inside his body before it could finish circulating.","Orion reacted instantly.","\"Second Star Step.\"","A blue and white star flashed within his spine, and his body slid away along a diagonal like a comet changing orbit. Revona’s fingers passed through the space where his chest had been, and the starlight afterimage he left behind winked out of existence at once.","Orion reappeared at her side as the fifth star entered his shoulder again, and he drove it toward her ribs.","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes turned toward him, and the fifth star dimmed. But Orion changed midway. The seventh star surged into his blood, his shoulder strike flowed into a palm thrust, and burning red star force gathered in his hand. Revona’s eyes tracked the shift, yet Orion changed once more before her nullification could finish its work.","\"Ninth Star Crown Pressure.\"","A crown-shaped star mark flashed above his head, and his entire body descended with heavy celestial pressure, transforming the palm thrust into a suppressive downward strike. Revona finally raised her left arm to block.","Boom!","The collision drove both of them backward. A thin line of blood appeared on Revona’s wrist, but Orion’s palm trembled as well, for the void-origin power crawling up from her arm was trying to erase the star force inside his hand.","He withdrew at once and circulated the third star through his bones, forcing the invading ripple of void out of his body before it could sink any deeper.","The entire arena went quiet. This was no longer the one-sided nullification from earlier in the battle. Orion had forced Revona to block, Revona had forced Orion to retreat, and both of them had drawn blood from the other, even if only slightly.","Orion smiled faintly despite the pressure. \"You really are troublesome.\"","Revona’s gaze stayed calm. \"You are changing your star force faster.\"","\"I have to,\" Orion replied. \"If I slow down even a little, you will erase it.\"","\"Then keep changing.\"","The void-colored light in her eyes brightened, and Revona moved again. Orion met her head-on.","The two figures collided at the center of the stage, and in an instant the entire battlefield became a storm of stars and emptiness. Orion’s fists carried blazing stellar heat, his elbows carried the sharpness of meteors, his knees bore collapsing star pressure, and his steps alternated between the speed of a comet and the weight of a dead star.","Revona’s eyes erased whatever they managed to catch, while her hands wielded void-origin nullification capable of dissolving any star power that touched her body.","Every time Orion changed stars, Revona’s pupils shifted, and every time her gaze locked onto him, Orion altered the star circulating through his flesh. It had become a battle of speed, reaction, transformation, and understanding.","Orion drove Revona back once with a First Star Fist. She erased most of it and answered by striking his shoulder with two fingers. A patch of starlight vanished from his shoulder and blood sprayed from beneath his armor, but Orion immediately twisted at the waist and countered with a Fourth Star Knee.","The knee crashed into Revona’s guard and sent her sliding backward across the stage, and before she could steady herself, his Sixth Star Pressure descended from above, making the air around her body feel as heavy as a dead star.","Revona’s eyes shone. The pressure vanished around her head and chest, but it lingered around her feet, and for a fraction of a breath her movement slowed.","Orion seized that instant.","\"Eight Star Convergence Strike.\"","Eight of the stars within his body ignited at once and converged into his right fist. The attack was no longer some distant beam. It was a compact stellar explosion carried by living flesh. He punched toward Revona’s abdomen, and the terrifying power packed inside that fist cracked the stage beneath him before the blow had even landed.","Revona’s eyes narrowed and her Void Origin Eyes blazed. Most of the converged star force vanished, but not all of it.","Boom!","Orion’s fist struck her abdomen, and for the first time in the battle, Revona’s body was sent flying backward.","The entire Divine Realm erupted.","\"She was hit again!\"","\"Orion struck her directly!\"","\"That was an Eight Star Convergence Strike!\"","\"He is truly forcing the Void Origin Eyes to their limit!\"","At the Nine Star Court, the disciples screamed until their starry viewing platform shook. Elders who had watched calmly earlier now rose to their feet with pride burning in their eyes as Orion pushed Revona past the point where stillness and nullification alone could carry her.","Their strongest genius had transformed from a long-range star cultivator into a close combat star sovereign, and he was proving before the entire Divine Realm why the Nine Star Court deserved its place among the strongest first-rate forces.","On the stage, Revona landed lightly, though blood trickled from the corner of her mouth. She lowered her gaze to the wound, then looked back at Orion, and for the first time the air around her truly changed.","The void beneath her feet expanded. Her pupils deepened, and what dwelled within those eyes was no longer merely the power to erase attacks.","A vast hollow world began to unfold behind her. It was not a world of darkness like Ervin’s abyss, and it was not a world of space like Kaiden’s void. It was a realm of origin-level emptiness, a place with no sky, no ground, no stars, no wind, no sound, and no color. Everything that entered that realm seemed to lose its very reason to keep existing.","Orion’s smile vanished completely, and every participant on the pillars grew solemn.","Max’s eyes sharpened.","’So this is her Pseudo Cosmic Path.’","Revona’s voice drifted quietly across the stage.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path.\"","The hollow world behind her yawned wider.","\"Void Origin Realm.\"","Boom!","There was no deafening explosion. There was only silence, and that silence was terrifying. The central stage seemed to lose all sound for an instant. The star glow surrounding Orion dimmed, and the cracks spreading across the arena floor simply stopped, not because they had healed, but because even the force that should have extended them had been erased.","The air inside the stage turned hollow, and the sense of Revona’s existence became faint and absolute at the same time.","Her Void Origin Eyes had already been terrifying, but once the Void Origin Realm unfurled behind her, her nullification was no longer bound to what her eyes could directly observe.","The entire region around her had become a field of origin emptiness, and any power entering it would be weakened, erased, or returned to nothingness unless it carried enough authority, enough density, or enough transformation speed to withstand the realm itself.","Orion drew a slow breath. \"So that is your path.\"","Revona looked at him. \"Now use everything.\"","Orion stared at her for a moment, and then he laughed softly. \"Fine.\""]},{"number":1856,"title":"Chapter 1856: Orion giving his all!","paragraphs":["The nine stars inside his body blazed as one, and his aura surged violently upward. The illusory star palace behind him shone brighter, and the nine massive stars encircling the throne poured streams of light down into Orion’s body. His skin split in several places under the pressure, yet he did not stop.","Blood ran down his arms, and even that blood glimmered with faint starlight. His eyes became twin stars, and the crown of starlight reappeared above his head, far clearer than it had been before.","\"Nine Star Sovereign Body.\"","His voice dropped deeper.","\"Full Star Convergence.\"","Boom!","The entire stage shuddered beneath the clash of two Pseudo Cosmic Paths. On one side, the Void Origin Realm spread outward as a hollow world that erased existence itself. On the other, the Nine Star Sovereign Body had transformed Orion into a vessel carrying all nine stars at once.","Orion moved, and this time his speed was terrifying. He crossed the field like a star plunging through empty space. The Void Origin Realm began erasing the star force around him the instant he entered it, but the nine stars within his body kept replenishing what was lost.","Every step burned through his stamina, every punch consumed the power circulating through his organs and bones, and every shift of star force tore at his meridians, yet Orion pressed forward without a moment’s hesitation.","Revona raised both hands, and ripples of void origin spread outward like invisible waves. Orion punched through the first wave and lost half the star power in his fist, so he changed stars. He stepped through the second wave and his left leg went numb as the void devoured the force inside it, so he changed again. He pushed into the third wave and struck.","Boom!","Revona blocked with both arms, but the impact shoved her backward, and a crack split the hollow space behind her.","The spectators were stunned.","\"He is fighting inside her Pseudo Cosmic Path!\"","\"His star power keeps being erased, but he keeps replacing it!\"","\"This is insane!\"","\"Both of them are burning through their power far too fast!\"","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, the top geniuses watched without blinking.","Damian Voss’s eyes were cold and sharp. \"Orion is forcing his way through by overloading the gap between her erasure and his replenishment.\"","Kaiden Voidmere gave a slight nod. \"But that method costs him too much. The Void Origin Realm is multiplying the price of every single attack.\"","Ervin’s gaze ran deep. \"If he cannot break through soon, he will be the one to collapse first.\"","Rakan Thorne clenched his fists, his grin wild yet serious. \"Even so, that star bastard is amazing.\"","Max said nothing. He could see everything the others saw, and more besides. Orion’s Pseudo Cosmic Path was among the strongest paths he had witnessed in the entire conference. It had turned a long-range star genius into a supreme close combat monster, and even inside Revona’s Void Origin Realm, Orion was still forcing her back one step at a time.","But Revona’s path was perfectly suited to bleeding him dry. Every strike Orion threw was partially erased before it could land, every movement demanded more power than it normally would, and every attempt to change stars grew harder beneath the pressure of that origin emptiness.","Yet Orion kept going. He struck Revona’s shoulder and broke through her void guard. Her palm landed on his chest and erased a great slab of his star armor, tearing open the flesh beneath it. He answered with a Third Star Elbow that cut across her side and scattered blood through the air.","She turned the Void Origin Realm on his right leg, swallowed the force within it, and very nearly brought him down. He shifted to the Sixth Star and slammed both fists downward, forcing her onto one knee for the length of a breath. She lifted her eyes, and the void around him surged upward, stripping three layers of star force from his body at once.","Orion coughed blood. Then he smiled.","\"Not enough.\"","He stepped in again.","The battle climbed to a terrifying intensity. The stage became a place where stars were born and erased with every passing second. Star fists detonated and vanished, and waves of void spread and cracked. Orion’s body was soon covered in wounds, with his armor broken, his hair in disarray, and blood running down his forehead into one eye.","Revona had not escaped unharmed either. Blood stained her sleeves, her breathing had grown heavy, and the hollow world behind her shuddered several times under Orion’s relentless assault.","Neither of them stopped, and neither surrendered. Orion drove Revona to the brink by endlessly changing the star circulating through his body, forcing her Void Origin Eyes to chase one force after another.","Revona drove Orion to the brink by expanding the Void Origin Realm until every step he took cost him more strength than an ordinary full-power attack. Their Pseudo Cosmic Paths collided in a way that made countless spectators forget how to breathe.","Then, at last, Orion found one more opening. Revona’s gaze had locked onto the Seventh Star burning in his blood, and the Void Origin Realm had begun erasing the star force in his veins. In that moment, Orion abruptly shifted everything into the Ninth Star Crown above his head, and for a fraction of a breath, Revona’s nullification lagged behind.","Orion appeared in front of her.","\"Nine Star Sovereign Body. Celestial Crown Breaker.\"","His fist descended with all nine stars compressed into a single crown-shaped strike. Revona’s eyes widened slightly, and for the first time, she could not fully erase it in time.","Boom!","The strike landed square against her chest. Revona was hurled backward with blood spilling from her lips, and her body slammed into the far side of the barrier. The entire arena shook, and the hollow world behind her flickered violently.","The Nine Star Court went mad with cheering, but Orion did not celebrate. He dropped to one knee, coughing blood onto the fractured stage while his right arm trembled beyond his control. That single strike had very nearly emptied him.","Across from him, Revona slowly pushed herself away from the barrier. Her face was pale, and the front of her clothes was soaked with blood. The Void Origin Realm behind her had dimmed, but it had not collapsed.","Orion lifted his head, saw it still standing, and a bitter smile crossed his face. \"You endured even that?\"","Revona wiped the blood from her lips. \"Barely.\"","Orion laughed once, though the laugh quickly broke apart into another cough. He forced himself back to his feet as the nine stars within his body flickered. One of them dimmed, then another, and then a third.","Revona regarded him calmly, though her own breathing had grown unsteady. \"You are exhausted.\"","Orion smiled, and strangely enough, that smile was brighter than it had been all battle. Blood still ran from the corner of his mouth, several wounds across his arms and chest gaped deep enough to expose the flesh beneath his broken armor, and the star lines tracing his body had dimmed to an unstable flicker, yet he looked as though none of it mattered to him in the slightest.","\"Almost,\" he said lightly.","\"Not almost,\" Revona replied. \"You are at your limit.\""]},{"number":1857,"title":"Chapter 1857: Starfall Extinction!","paragraphs":["Orion did not deny it. He only laughed softly, wiped the blood from his chin with the back of his hand, and took one more step forward. In that moment, everyone watching could feel that he genuinely had nothing left to spare.","The Nine Star Sovereign Body had already pushed him past the natural endurance of his flesh, and Full Star Convergence had burned through his meridians, his flesh, and his blood at a terrifying rate. Any ordinary genius would have collapsed long before now.","Even so, Orion remained on his feet, and the light in his eyes had not dimmed at all. If anything, it had grown sharper, as though he had finally arrived at the exact moment he had been waiting for since the battle began.","\"The Nine Star Court taught me many star arts,\" Orion said as the starlight around him trembled weakly. \"It taught me how to call down stars, how to command them, and how to wear their power as my own body. But this final move...\" His smile widened. \"This one is mine.\"","The instant those words fell, the expressions of the Nine Star Court elders and disciples watching from afar changed all at once, and even the participants on the pillars felt their attention sharpen further.","A technique created by Orion himself was no trivial matter. For a genius of his caliber to speak this way at the very end of a battle meant that whatever he was about to unleash was not simply another inherited attack. It was a move born from his own understanding, his own martial will, and his own path as the strongest genius of the Nine Star Court.","Orion slowly closed his right hand into a fist.","The nine dimming stars within his body abruptly stopped flickering and went still. For one brief instant, it seemed as though all of them were about to go out. Then, in the very next moment, all nine stars blazed at once with a brightness so intense that even the barrier around the central stage shook violently.","The broken star palace reappeared behind him, though not in its earlier majestic and stable form. It returned in a wilder and more desperate shape, as if the entire palace had been forcibly reignited by nothing but Orion’s will.","Cracks raced across the illusory structure, and the nine stars surrounding it began breaking apart into countless streams of star essence. Rather than scattering into the sky, every one of those streams rushed straight back into Orion’s body.","His injuries worsened instantly. Blood burst from several splits along his arms and shoulders, his knees shook, and the faint groan of bones straining under the pressure could actually be heard. Yet Orion did not stop.","He accepted all of that star essence into himself, compressing it, forcing it, and refining it within the span of a single breath. The pressure released by that compression was so immense that the stage caved in beneath his feet, and even Revona’s Void Origin Realm rippled heavily in answer.","Revona’s calm eyes finally shifted in a way anyone could see. She could feel it clearly. This attack was different from everything that had come before. It was not merely a stronger star punch, and it was not another variation of his close combat star arts.","This was Orion taking the Nine Star Sovereign Body, shattering the stars within himself down to their rawest essence, and gathering all of it into one final eruption. This was a move built to end battles, a move that no longer cared about preservation, or recoil, or what would become of his body once the strike was released.","Orion opened his eyes fully, and they shone like two collapsing stars.","\"This technique,\" he said, his voice lower and heavier than before, \"is called Starfall Extinction.\"","The moment he spoke the name, the entire arena seemed to lose all lesser light, as though every fragment of brightness in the stage, the barrier, and the surrounding pillars had been dragged toward Orion’s fist. What remained around him was a terrifyingly dense sphere of rotating star essence.","It looked small next to the grand phenomena of his earlier attacks, yet the power compressed inside it was enough to make even the top geniuses feel their hearts tighten. It stood as the exact opposite of his sprawling celestial assaults. It was all of his stars, all of his remaining strength, all of his will, and all of his understanding condensed into a single point of destruction.","Revona inhaled slowly, and the Void Origin Realm behind her began to shrink. It no longer spread outward as a hollow world. Instead, it withdrew toward her body, condensing layer upon layer until it formed a deep, translucent ring of pure origin emptiness hovering before her.","The ring was not large, standing only slightly wider than her own frame, but the moment it appeared, everyone understood that this was no ordinary defense. It was the very core of her Pseudo Cosmic Path, the deepest defensive response she could summon under pressure.","Orion smiled brightly. Even now, with blood streaking his face and his body shaking beneath the weight of his own technique, he looked genuinely happy. It was the smile of someone who had finally found an opponent worth everything he could give.","Then he disappeared.","He did not move like a meteor or a comet this time. He moved like a star collapsing at the end of its life, shrinking into nothing for one impossible instant before exploding back into existence directly in front of Revona.","The compressed star sphere around his fist roared in utter silence, and when he punched forward, it was as though an entire constellation had been buried inside that single strike.","\"Starfall Extinction!\"","The punch landed against the hollow ring.","For one breath, nothing happened at all. Then the world shook.","The hollow ring before Revona trembled so violently that visible cracks began spidering across its surface. The sound that emerged was not the sound of an explosion but a low and terrifying grinding, as though two concepts that should never have met were tearing directly at each other.","Orion’s fist kept pushing forward. The compressed star essence unraveled in layers, and each layer released enough force to destroy ordinary divine techniques several times over. Revona’s condensed Void Origin Realm erased one layer, then another, and then another, but the attack never stopped coming, because Orion had constructed it so that every erased layer immediately triggered the collapse of the next one waiting inside his fist.","The first layer of emptiness shattered, the second layer cracked, and the third layer bent inward. Revona’s expression became the most serious it had been in the entire battle. Blood began to seep once more from the corner of her lips, and the light of her Void Origin Eyes deepened to a frightening degree.","Even so, Orion’s fist kept advancing. It gained a palm’s width, then another inch, and then another after that. The hollow ring was being forced back toward her chest, and the star essence within his punch had grown so concentrated that even her direct nullification could no longer erase it quickly enough.","The arena erupted.","\"He is breaking through!\"","\"That is his own technique!\"","\"Revona is being pushed back!\"","\"Her Void Origin Realm cannot stop it!\""]},{"number":1858,"title":"Chapter 1858: Last One Standing!","paragraphs":["Max’s eyes narrowed sharply, Damian’s grip tightened around his sword, Kaiden’s expression turned deeply solemn, and Ervin stared without blinking. Even Angelina Valerius, who had remained perfectly composed through every battle so far, watched the collision with a slightly keener gaze.","Revona finally understood that if she tried to withstand this attack through ordinary nullification alone, she would lose. The force of Starfall Extinction was too compressed, too layered, and too desperate.","Orion had not built a move meant to overwhelm from range. He had built a move meant to burn everything in a single instant and force a path straight through whatever stood in front of him.","At that critical moment, Revona’s eyes blazed with terrifying intensity.","\"Void Origin Realm,\" she said softly, though the words seemed to echo from somewhere far deeper than her own voice. \"Return to Nothing.\"","The cracked hollow ring before her collapsed inward. It did not break apart. It folded into itself. Every layer of emptiness, every trace of nullification, and every fragment of erased existence within the Void Origin Realm converged upon one single point in front of Revona’s body.","It was a point so utterly empty that even the space around it seemed to flinch away. The shattered force of Orion’s fist, the overflowing star essence, and the compressed destruction of Starfall Extinction were all drawn into that point of absolute void.","Then it vanished, though it did not vanish all at once, and it did not vanish cleanly. The star essence fought back like a dying supernova. It tore at the point of emptiness, forcing blood to spill from Revona’s lips and draining the color from the skin around her eyes.","But in the end, Return to Nothing prevailed. The point of origin emptiness swallowed the last portion of Starfall Extinction and returned it to nothing.","When the blinding light finally faded, Orion’s fist had stopped just short of Revona’s chest. The star sphere around his hand was gone. The stars inside his body darkened one after another, the crown above his head shattered, and the reignited star palace behind him broke into dim fragments that dissolved into the air.","For a moment, Orion remained standing. He looked at Revona, then at his own fist, and then he laughed softly. It was a tired laugh, yet it carried not even a trace of bitterness. He had pushed her that far. He had forced the woman with the Void Origin Eyes to reveal the true core of her defensive ability just to survive him.","\"Good,\" he said weakly, still smiling brightly. \"That really was the limit.\"","The moment the words left him, all the strength drained from his body at once. His knees buckled, his shoulders sagged, and his eyes slid shut as his consciousness finally gave out. He fell forward like a star that had burned through the very last of its light.","Revona caught him by the shoulder before he could strike the ground. She was breathing hard as well, her face pale, her chest rising and falling faster than before, and a faint streak of blood still marking her lips.","Return to Nothing had allowed her to survive, but it had not come without a price. Even so, she remained on her feet, while Orion had finally spent everything he had.","The entire arena fell silent.","Then Angelina Valerius raised her hand and announced the result.","\"Orion Starfall is unable to continue. Winner, Revona.\"","The great screen above the arena changed at once. Yet even after the result appeared, the silence lingered for several more breaths, because everyone understood that what they had just witnessed was no ordinary exchange of victory and defeat. It had been two peak geniuses driving each other to the absolute edge.","Orion had forced Revona to reveal the deepest ability of her Void Origin Realm, while Revona had withstood the strongest self-created technique Orion could release at the very end of his strength.","One of them remained standing and the other had fallen unconscious, but together they had raised the standard of the final round to an even more terrifying height.","Watching the unconscious Orion in Revona’s grasp, many of the Nine Star Court disciples felt their blood boil with pride rather than shame. Their strongest genius had lost, but he had lost while displaying a brilliance that carved his name into the memory of the entire Divine Realm more deeply than ever before.","Revona gazed quietly at the fainted Orion for a moment before the transfer light descended to carry him away. Then she too returned to her pillar, and for the first time since the battles had begun, even the top geniuses exchanged looks weighted with something far heavier than before.","After watching Orion and Revona push each other so far, all of them understood one thing with perfect clarity.","The final round had only grown more dangerous from this point onward.","[Winner: Revona.]","[Orion Starfall Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Revona]","[Total Battles Fought: 4]","[Total Wins: 4]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Orion Starfall]","[Total Battles Fought: 4]","[Total Wins: 3]","The result appeared clearly on the screen, yet no one spoke for several breaths.","Orion had lost, but no one could bring themselves to look down on him. He had forced Revona to move, he had forced her to fight with real initiative, and he had forced her to reveal the Void Origin Realm itself.","He had wounded her again and again, and at the very end he had come within a hair of breaking through her Pseudo Cosmic Path entirely. Had his strength lasted even a few breaths longer, the result might well have been different.","Revona remained on the stage for a moment, still holding Orion upright. Her face was pale, her aura wavered unsteadily, and blood still stained her lips. She looked down at Orion, who had fainted with a faint smile lingering on his face, and then she spoke softly enough that only those closest could hear.","\"You were strong.\"","A transfer light descended and carried Orion back to his pillar, where the laws of the Eternal Hourglass began stabilizing his injuries. Revona returned to her own pillar as well, but she sat down the moment she arrived.","The Void Origin Realm had vanished, and the light in her Void Origin Eyes had dimmed noticeably. This victory had not come easily. She had won, but the battle had driven her to the very edge of exhaustion.","Across the Divine Realm, the disciples of the Nine Star Court were silent at first. Then, one by one, they began to cheer. They cheered not because Orion had won, but because he had fought a battle worthy of their strongest genius.","He had displayed the majesty of the Nine Star Sovereign Body before the entire Divine Realm, and even in defeat he had made countless forces understand exactly why the Nine Star Court stood among the greatest first-rate powers.","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, Max watched Revona quietly.","’Her Void Origin Realm is dangerous,’ he thought. ’Even Orion’s Pseudo Cosmic Path could not break through before his strength ran out.’","Damian Voss’s gaze was sharp, and Kaiden Voidmere looked deep in thought. Ervin’s eyes remained calm, though his grip on his spear tightened by a fraction.","Rakan Thorne laughed softly from his pillar. \"That was a good fight.\"","Morgana Starveil nodded faintly. \"Too good. Now everyone has more problems to worry about.\"","Aurelian Lareth’s expression stayed cold, though even he could not deny the level of the battle that had just unfolded.","Angelina Valerius waited until Orion’s injuries had stabilized and Revona’s aura had settled enough for her to remain conscious. Then she turned back toward the screen of light above the arena.","\"The next battle will now begin.\""]},{"number":1859,"title":"Chapter 1859: Damian vs Divine Son!","paragraphs":["The silence that followed Orion’s defeat did not fade quickly.","Even after the transfer light carried him back to his pillar and the healing laws of the Eternal Hourglass began stabilizing his body, many spectators across the Divine Realm continued staring at the screen without a word.","Orion Starfall had lost, yet his loss carried more weight than many victories. He had forced Revona to reveal the Void Origin Realm, pushed her into using Return to Nothing, and burned through every last trace of his strength with his self-created technique, Starfall Extinction.","In the end he had fainted before he could break through that final layer of nothingness, but no one could claim that the strongest genius of the Nine Star Court had been weak.","Revona sat quietly on her pillar after returning, her face still pale and her breathing still uneven. The void-colored glow in her eyes had dimmed considerably, and for the first time since the final competitive stage began, she no longer looked untouchable.","Her victory was real, but so was the price she had paid for it. The Void Origin Realm had defended her and Return to Nothing had saved her, yet Orion’s final attack had pushed her to the very edge of what she could endure.","On the surrounding pillars, the top geniuses kept their silence.","Max looked toward Orion’s pillar for a moment before shifting his gaze to Revona. His expression barely changed, but his eyes had grown deeper, because the battle had handed him valuable information.","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes could erase incoming attacks, yet sufficient transformation speed could carve out openings. Her Void Origin Realm could expand that ability into an entire field, but even that field could be pressured by an attack carrying enough density and layered power.","The true problem was Return to Nothing. It was no simple defense. It gathered everything that had been erased and folded it back into a single point of origin emptiness, and it had caused even Orion’s strongest self-created technique to fail within the final stretch of distance.","Damian Voss watched quietly as well. His hand rested near his sword hilt, and the sharpness in his eyes had not faded since the moment Orion unleashed Starfall Extinction.","Others may have seen only the brilliance of that final attack, but Damian had seen the will behind it, and for a swordsman, will mattered every bit as much as technique. A person capable of creating a move like that at the brink of collapse deserved respect.","Aurelian Lareth stood on his own pillar with a cold and dignified expression. Unlike many of the others, he displayed no open admiration. His golden-white light flowed faintly around him while his eyes swept occasionally across Max, Revona, Damian, and the remaining peak geniuses.","The Divine Son of the second elven faction still carried his proud composure, but after the battles that had already taken place, even he could no longer pretend that the road ahead would be easy.","Angelina Valerius gave Revona a few moments to steady herself, and then she raised her hand.","\"The previous battle has concluded,\" she said calmly, her voice carrying across the Eternal Hourglass arena. \"The final competitive stage will continue.\"","The giant screen of light above the arena brightened once more, and names began to rotate. The randomizer spun faster and faster while every remaining participant looked upward.","After the battle between Orion and Revona, no one dared to relax, for the final competitive stage had already proven that the randomizer cared nothing for timing, reputation, recovery, or fear. It could match monster against monster at any moment it pleased.","The names flashed rapidly past, among them Max Morgan, Rakan Thorne, Kaiden Voidmere, Ervin, Rosaline Lunara, Morgana Starveil, Selene Vaeloria, Fin Arclight, Revona, Damian Voss, and Aurelian Lareth.","The light slowed, and a strange pressure spread through the arena. Many spectators leaned forward without meaning to.","The first name stopped.","[Damian Voss]","The moment Damian’s name appeared, the atmosphere of the arena sharpened. The strongest genius of the Sword God Palace had finally been called into another major battle.","Until now, Damian had won every match cleanly and calmly, never revealing more than the bare minimum. His sword had looked simple, yet every victory had displayed terrifying control. He had never been pushed, he had never used his Pseudo Cosmic Path, and he had never shown the full depth of the Sword God Palace inheritance.","The second name continued spinning while the participants watched closely. Max’s gaze sharpened slightly, and Aurelian’s golden eyes narrowed.","The light stopped.","[Aurelian Lareth]","For one brief moment, the entire Eternal Hourglass arena went silent. Then the screen enlarged both names at once.","[Final Competitive Stage, Battle Forty]","[Damian Voss vs Aurelian Lareth]","The silence shattered, and a wave of shock swept through the arena and across the Divine Realm. Damian Voss was the strongest genius of the Sword God Palace, and Aurelian Lareth was the Divine Son of the second elven faction.","One was the blade raised by one of the greatest sword forces in the Divine Realm, a genius whose swordsmanship had remained calm, precise, and unfathomable from the very start of the conference.","The other was the Divine Son of a royal elven faction, the vessel of the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline stolen from Max, and the wielder of the domineering Pseudo Cosmic Path known as Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion.","This was no ordinary matchup. This was another true collision between peak geniuses.","The Divine Realm erupted once again. In the Sword God Palace, countless disciples gathered before massive screens with their eyes burning. Damian Voss had been too calm for too long, and many of them had waited eagerly for an opponent strong enough to force out his true sword.","\"Senior Brother Damian!\"","\"Show the Divine Son the sword of our Sword God Palace!\"","\"Aurelian’s Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion is strong, but no dominion can suppress the true sword!\"","\"Senior Brother Damian has not even used his real strength yet!\"","At the same time, within the territories controlled by the second elven faction, countless elves watched with cold pride. To them, Aurelian Lareth was far more than a mere participant. He was their Divine Son, their symbol, and their living proof that their faction still stood above countless forces in both talent and bloodline.","His battle against Morgana had already put the Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion on display, but now he faced Damian Voss, and many elders understood that this fight would determine how the Divine Realm judged his true standing among the peak."]},{"number":1860,"title":"Chapter 1860: A Quick Battle!","paragraphs":["Inside the Eternal Hourglass, Max stood on his pillar and stared at the screen. His expression did not shift, but the air around him grew slightly colder. Aurelian, the Divine Son of the second faction, was the one who carried the stolen Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline.","Max had already witnessed the Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion during Aurelian’s battle against Morgana, but he knew perfectly well that Aurelian had not shown everything.","Someone raised as the Divine Son of the second faction could not possibly possess only that much, and this battle against Damian might finally drag more of it into the open.","Aurelian turned his head slightly and looked toward Max. For one brief moment their gazes met, and a faint smile touched Aurelian’s face. It was calm, arrogant, and cold.","Max did not smile back.","Then Damian Voss opened his eyes fully. He looked at Aurelian, and the sword intent around him grew faintly sharper. He did not raise his voice, and he showed neither anger nor excitement.","He simply stood there like a sword still resting in its sheath, quiet enough for fools to overlook and sharp enough to make true experts sense danger before the blade was ever drawn.","Aurelian looked away from Max and turned his gaze toward Damian. \"So my opponent is you,\" he said calmly.","Damian’s expression did not change. \"Yes.\"","Aurelian smiled faintly. \"The Sword God Palace has been very quiet in this final stage.\"","Damian replied, \"A sword does not need to make noise before cutting.\"","The words were spoken calmly, yet the arena tensed in an instant.","Rakan Thorne grinned from his pillar. \"Good. This one should be fun too.\"","Orion Starfall, still recovering under the laws of the Eternal Hourglass, forced his eyes partway open and smiled weakly when he saw the pairing. \"Of course. I faint for one moment, and another good battle starts.\"","Morgana Starveil looked between Damian and Aurelian with shining eyes. \"This will be dangerous.\"","Kaiden Voidmere said softly, \"Sword authority against divine light authority.\"","Ervin’s gaze deepened. \"No, it is more than that. Damian has not revealed his path yet.\"","Revona, still pale from her fight with Orion, opened her eyes and regarded the stage with rare seriousness. Even after her exhausting battle, this match was important enough to hold her attention.","Angelina Valerius looked down at the two named participants.","\"Damian Voss.\"","Her gaze shifted.","\"Aurelian Lareth.\"","The transfer lights began gathering above their pillars.","\"Enter the stage.\"","Two beams of light descended, one carrying a silent sword sharpness and the other carrying a golden-white divine radiance. The next great battle of the final competitive stage was about to begin.","The two beams faded from the central stage. Damian Voss stood on one side with his sword still sheathed, his posture calm and his eyes deep. He released no violent aura and made no attempt to smother the stage with sword intent the moment he landed, yet the space around him felt unnaturally keen, as though the air itself were being quietly divided into invisible lines.","Aurelian Lareth stood opposite him with golden-white radiance flowing around his body like a sacred cloak. Compared to Damian’s silence, Aurelian’s presence was far more majestic.","His pale golden hair drifted behind him, his eyes shone with divine light, and every breath he drew carried the oppressive dignity of the second elven faction’s Divine Son. The Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline within him had already begun to stir, and to Max, that light still felt unpleasantly familiar.","Angelina Valerius looked down at the two of them.","[Battle Begins.]","The moment those words appeared, Damian moved. He announced no technique and made no show of raising his sword slowly. His hand simply brushed the hilt, and a thin sword light flashed into being between him and Aurelian.","Aurelian’s eyes narrowed.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Sacred Mirror Guard.\"","A golden-white mirror of light formed before his body, and the sword light struck it.","Crack!","The mirror split apart instantly, but before its broken fragments could scatter, Aurelian had already raised his hand. Thousands of golden spears materialized above him and shot toward Damian like divine punishment descending from the heavens.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Sacred Spear Rain.\"","Damian stepped forward, and his sword left its sheath.","\"Silent Sword Art, First Cut, Parting Wind.\"","A single horizontal slash swept across the stage. It did not look grand at first glance, but the moment it met the descending spears, all the golden-white light in front of Damian was cleaved into two clean halves. The sword light passed through the spear rain without slowing, splitting hundreds of radiant spears before fading near Aurelian’s position.","Aurelian raised one finger.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Sunwheel Descent.\"","A golden sunwheel appeared above his head and descended with burning divine pressure. Its edges spun like a sacred blade, and the light pouring from it carried a purifying heat intense enough to set the arena barrier glowing.","Damian’s expression did not waver. He stepped sideways with a movement so small that many spectators barely registered it, and then his sword rose.","\"Sword God Palace, Falling Peak Sword.\"","The slash descended from above like a mountain forged from sword intent, and the Falling Peak Sword collided with the Sunwheel Descent.","Boom!","The central stage shook violently as golden light and sword force detonated together. Aurelian was the first to move through the explosion, his body wrapped in a layer of radiant armor.","\"Heavenly Luminance Battle Form, Divine Step.\"","His speed spiked sharply. In an instant he appeared before Damian and struck with a palm brimming with golden-white power.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Sacred Palm Seal.\"","Damian turned his sword and blocked with the flat of the blade. The palm struck the steel, and a dull explosion rolled outward. Damian slid back half a step while Aurelian’s radiant palm seared a burning mark into the air, and before Damian could fully counter, Aurelian’s other hand had already shaped a spear of light and thrust it toward his chest.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Piercing Dawn Spear.\"","Damian shifted his body and let the spear slide past his ribs by a hair’s width, and in the same motion his sword swept upward toward Aurelian’s wrist.","\"Silent Sword Art, Second Cut, Returning Thread.\"","Aurelian snatched his hand back instantly, but the sword light still grazed his sleeve and sliced through the golden-white defensive layer covering his arm.","The spectators burst into excitement at once.","\"So fast!\"","\"They are opening directly with high-level moves!\"","\"Damian’s sword is too precise!\"","\"Aurelian is keeping up in close combat too!\""]},{"number":1861,"title":"Chapter 1861: Damian’s Pseudo Cosmic Path!","paragraphs":["Aurelian’s expression cooled further. He stepped back, and the radiance around him erupted outward.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Twelve Sacred Wings.\"","Twelve wings woven from golden-white light unfurled behind him. Each wing shed countless feathers of light, and every feather carried sharpness, purification, and explosive force all at once. The twelve wings beat a single time, and the entire stage filled with golden feathers streaking toward Damian from every direction.","Damian finally raised his sword with both hands, and his sword intent expanded.","\"Sword God Palace, Ten Thousand Line Sword Formation.\"","Thin lines of sword light bloomed around Damian, numbering dozens at first, then hundreds, and then thousands. They crisscrossed the air like invisible threads made visible for a single breath. The golden feathers struck those lines and were sliced apart one after another, until the stage became a storm of broken light and fragmented sword intent with neither side giving ground.","Aurelian moved again. He passed through the collapsing golden feathers and appeared above Damian with one hand raised high.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Crowned Sun Judgment.\"","A vast crown of light materialized above his palm, and from within that crown descended a pillar of golden-white power. The attack was not as complete as his full Pseudo Cosmic Path, yet it already carried a trace of divine judgment authority. The pillar plunged straight toward Damian, seeking to crush his sword intent from above.","Damian looked up, and for the first time his eyes grew colder.","\"Sword God Palace, Heaven-Cutting Ascension.\"","His sword rose, and a straight lance of sword light shot upward. It bit into the descending pillar and split it from the center, forcing the golden-white radiance to part around him like a river divided by a cliff. The sword light continued its climb and struck the crown above Aurelian’s hand.","Crack!","The crown shattered. Aurelian’s eyes sharpened, and he descended immediately with both hands aglow.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Twin Divine Seals.\"","Two golden-white seals formed in his palms and pressed in toward Damian from the left and the right. Damian turned his body as his sword traced a narrow arc.","\"Silent Sword Art, Third Cut, Moonless Return.\"","The blade vanished for an instant, and then two sword lights appeared at the same moment. One struck the left seal while the other struck the right, and both seals shattered together, though the impact drove Damian and Aurelian apart in opposite directions.","For a breath, the two stood at a distance once more, and neither had claimed a clear advantage. The opening exchange had been brief, yet it had already shaken the arena. They had flowed from close combat to long-range suppression, from sword formations to divine seals, and from palm strikes to crown judgment, and every single collision had carried enough power to crush an ordinary participant of the final stage. Yet between Damian and Aurelian, those attacks had been nothing more than probes.","Aurelian glanced at the cut on his sleeve and then at Damian’s sword. \"You are worthy of the Sword God Palace,\" he said calmly.","Damian lowered his blade slightly. \"And you are worthy of being called Divine Son.\"","Aurelian smiled faintly. \"Then ordinary moves are meaningless.\"","Damian did not deny it, and the air around the stage changed yet again.","On the pillars, the top geniuses sharpened their focus.","Rakan Thorne grinned. \"Now they are finally starting.\"","Orion Starfall, still pale with exhaustion, forced himself to keep watching with bright eyes. \"Good. Do not disappoint me after making me miss the beginning.\"","Revona sat in silence, but her gaze never strayed from the stage.","Kaiden Voidmere said softly, \"Aurelian has already shown his path once. Damian has not.\"","Ervin’s eyes deepened. \"This will be Damian’s first reveal.\"","Max watched Damian carefully. He had always known the man was dangerous. The Sword God Palace would never raise an ordinary genius as its strongest participant, and Damian’s sword had never once felt shallow. Yet until this moment, Damian had never truly opened the depths of his path.","Aurelian raised his hand first. Golden-white light erupted behind him, taking the shape of sacred halls, radiant pillars, and a divine throne resting beneath an endless sun. The same domineering kingdom of light from his battle against Morgana began to manifest again, but this time it felt more complete.","The Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion descended with far greater pressure than before, and the golden-white crown above Aurelian’s head shone with new clarity.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path,\" Aurelian said calmly.","The divine kingdom spread wide behind him.","\"Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion.\"","Boom!","The entire stage was swallowed in golden-white authority. Aurelian’s aura surged, and within the dominion his light was no longer a mere weapon. It was command, it was judgment, and it was purification. It was the authority of a divine king forcing the battlefield itself to bow before his will.","But Damian did not retreat. He stood beneath the crushing pressure of the Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion with his sword lowered at his side, and for a moment his figure looked almost small against the vast divine kingdom looming behind Aurelian.","Then Damian closed his eyes. The sword in his hand released a soft sound, and it was not the ring of metal. It was like the first note of a blade being born at the very beginning of heaven and earth.","The stage grew quiet. The golden-white light pressing toward Damian suddenly slowed, and Aurelian’s eyes narrowed.","Damian opened his eyes, and the sharpness within them was no longer ordinary sword intent. It was older, purer, and far more terrifying.","Behind Damian, an illusory sword world began to take form. At first there was only a single sword standing upright in a boundless void, ancient, simple, and silent.","Then the emptiness around it opened outward, revealing mountains built from sword edges, rivers flowing with sword light, skies etched with sword marks, and countless broken weapons buried beneath an endless sword altar. Above that altar floated a vast palace, formed neither of stone nor of light but woven entirely from condensed sword law.","At the highest point of the palace stood a throne, and that throne was empty. Before the empty throne, a single sword hung point-downward, as though waiting for someone worthy to claim it.","Damian’s voice rang across the stage.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path.\"","The sword world expanded.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven.\""]},{"number":1862,"title":"Chapter 1862: Sword Sovereign Heaven!","paragraphs":["The moment the name was spoken, every sword in the arena trembled. Damian’s own blade trembled, the swords of the participants trembled, and even the weapons carried by spectators far beyond the Eternal Hourglass shivered in their sheaths.","Even Dragonheart at Max’s waist released a faint vibration, not out of fear, but in acknowledgment that a mighty sword path had arrived.","Across the Divine Realm, countless swordsmen shot to their feet in shock. Inside the Sword God Palace, the disciples fell silent for the space of one breath, and then the entire palace erupted.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven!\"","\"Senior Brother Damian revealed it!\"","\"That is his Pseudo Cosmic Path!\"","\"It is one of the supreme sword paths of the younger generation!\"","\"No wonder the elders said he was born to inherit the Sword God’s battlefield!\"","Damian’s Sword Sovereign Heaven felt nothing like a normal sword technique, nor did it resemble a simple domain. It was a world in which the sword stood above all other weapons, a place where every mountain, river, cloud, and shadow existed as an extension of sword authority. Within it, Damian’s sword intent did not merely grow sharper.","It became sovereign. It judged other powers through the purity of the blade, and it could cut force, cut light, cut laws, cut rhythm, and even cut the command hidden behind an enemy’s technique, provided Damian’s understanding ran deep enough.","Max’s eyes sharpened slightly.","’Sword Sovereign Heaven,’ he thought. ’So this is Damian’s path.’","Dragonheart grew still again at his waist, but Max could feel that the sword had responded. Damian’s path was not as forbidden as the Emotion Severing Path, not as primal as the Divine King Punishment, and not as mysterious as the Abyssal Origin Descent, yet in terms of pure sword authority it stood among the strongest Pseudo Cosmic Paths Max had witnessed anywhere in the Divine Realm.","For the first time, Aurelian’s expression turned truly serious. His Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion blazed brighter, pressing its golden-white authority against Damian’s sword world. Damian raised his blade, and the Sword Sovereign Heaven behind him answered.","Countless sword lights rose from the mountains, the rivers, the altar, and the palace. Aurelian’s divine throne glowed beneath its endless sun, and golden-white light collided with pure sword authority at the center of the stage before either man had even moved.","Boom!","The barrier shook, and spectators across the Divine Realm held their breath. Two majestic Pseudo Cosmic Paths had finally met. Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion stood against Sword Sovereign Heaven, and the true battle between Damian Voss and Aurelian Lareth had begun.","The collision between the two paths set the entire central stage trembling. Golden-white divine authority pressed forward from Aurelian’s side like an endless sacred kingdom descending from the sun. Radiant halls, divine pillars, sacred crowns, and a golden throne beneath an eternally blazing sky poured out waves of judgment, purification, and domination.","Every ray of light seemed to carry an edict, and every edict sought to force Damian’s sword world to lower itself before the authority of the Divine Son.","Opposite him, Damian’s Sword Sovereign Heaven refused to retreat. The ancient sword world expanded in silence. The mountains of sword edges climbed higher, the rivers of sword light flowed faster, and the endless sword altar gleamed with cold brilliance while the countless broken weapons buried beneath it trembled, as though acknowledging the arrival of a true sovereign of the blade.","Above the sword palace, the empty throne kept its silence, but the single sword hanging before it slowly turned until its tip pointed toward Aurelian’s divine kingdom.","The pressure between the two Pseudo Cosmic Paths grew terrifying. One side demanded that all things be judged beneath divine light, and the other demanded that all things be cut beneath the sword.","Aurelian raised his hand first.","\"Divine Dominion, Luminance Decree.\"","A golden-white decree unfurled above the stage like a sacred scroll written in light, and the moment it opened, countless words of radiance rained down toward Damian’s Sword Sovereign Heaven.","Each word carried the power to suppress sword intent, purify hostile energy, and bind the movement of the blade. The decree did not merely target Damian himself. It attempted to command the sword world behind him to dim.","Damian’s eyes stayed calm as he lifted his sword slightly.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, First Edict, All Blades Refuse Submission.\"","The sword altar behind him released a piercing hum, and countless sword lights rose from the ground to meet the descending words of radiance. Every sword light was thin, yet every one of them carried a pure and absolute refusal to submit. When they collided with the golden-white decree, the sound resembled thousands of blades striking against divine chains.","Crack!","The Luminance Decree shuddered. Aurelian narrowed his eyes and pressed his palm downward, and the decree flared brighter while the sacred halls behind him poured out still more light. The pressure of the Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion multiplied several times over, bearing down on Damian’s sword world until the rivers of sword light began to churn violently.","Damian stepped forward, and his sword moved.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, Second Edict, One Sword Divides Heaven.\"","A single sword light rose from his blade. It looked nowhere near as grand as Aurelian’s divine kingdom, nor as vast as the golden decree overhead, yet the instant it appeared, a chill ran through the heart of everyone watching.","The sword light traveled upward in a perfectly straight line and cut through the middle of the Luminance Decree. The decree split apart, and its sacred words of light shattered into countless fragments.","Aurelian’s expression grew colder, though he did not panic. His golden-white crown blazed, the divine throne behind him radiated majestic pressure, and twelve radiant pillars rose around the stage, each one covered in divine runes and all of them locking onto Damian at once.","\"Divine Dominion, Twelve Pillars of Sacred Judgment.\"","The twelve pillars fired beams of golden-white light in the same instant.","Damian turned his sword.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, Sword River Encircles The Throne.\"","The river of sword light behind him surged forward and coiled around Damian like a flowing silver dragon forged from blades. The twelve beams crashed down into the sword river and birthed a storm of shattered light and broken sword sparks. The stage cracked beneath Damian under the strain, but he did not yield a single step.","Then Aurelian vanished from where he stood.","\"Heavenly Luminance Divine Step.\"","He reappeared above Damian with a spear of divine light in his hand.","\"Divine Dominion, Sacred Sun Spear.\"","The spear plunged toward Damian’s head with terrifying speed. This was no long-range beam. It was a close combat strike empowered by the Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion, carrying the full weight of Aurelian’s bloodline and his Pseudo Cosmic Path together, and it burned so brightly that it looked capable of piercing a star."]},{"number":1863,"title":"Chapter 1863: Even The Sword Bleeds!","paragraphs":["Damian looked up, and his sword rose to meet it.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, Third Edict, Blade Meets The Sun.\"","Sword and spear collided.","Boom!","The impact rocked the entire arena. Golden-white light exploded downward while pure sword force erupted upward. Damian’s feet sank into the stage, and Aurelian’s arm shook faintly from the force traveling back through his spear. The two remained locked together for a breath, their eyes meeting through the blaze of light.","Aurelian’s voice was cold. \"Your sword is sharp.\"","Damian replied calmly, \"Your light is heavy.\"","Then both of them attacked at once. Aurelian’s spear fell like a descending sun while Damian’s sword moved like a silent line drawn through the world, and they clashed at the center of the stage again and again. Divine light scorched the air, and sword light carved through that radiance in turn.","Aurelian’s attacks were majestic, forceful, and domineering, while Damian’s sword remained clean, precise, and terrifyingly decisive. Every time Aurelian sought to suppress him with divine authority, Damian’s sword severed the command hidden within the light, and every time Damian tried to pierce Aurelian’s defense, the Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion wove another layer of sacred protection around its master.","The participants watched with grave faces.","Rakan Thorne’s grin had disappeared. \"That Divine Son is stronger than I thought.\"","Orion Starfall, still pale and recovering, smiled weakly. \"And Damian has still not lost his rhythm.\"","Kaiden Voidmere’s eyes narrowed. \"Damian’s sword is not merely cutting attacks. He is cutting the structure inside Aurelian’s authority.\"","Ervin nodded faintly. \"But Aurelian’s divine light keeps rebuilding it.\"","Revona watched in silence, her eyes dim yet focused.","Max’s gaze stayed locked on Aurelian. He could feel it more distinctly now. The light within Aurelian’s dominion carried the echo of the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline, but that echo rang impure.","It held power, it held majesty, and it held oppressive divine authority, yet beneath all of it, Max could still sense the unnatural mismatch between Aurelian and the bloodline dwelling inside him. That bloodline had not been born with him. It had been taken.","On the stage, Aurelian’s eyes grew colder as he realized Damian was not being overwhelmed. He raised one hand toward the divine throne behind him.","\"Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion, Royal Mandate of the Endless Sun.\"","The endless sun above the divine kingdom released a vast pillar of golden-white power, and that pillar did not fall toward Damian. It descended upon Aurelian himself, sending his aura surging upward. His crown grew more solid, his spear burned brighter, and his entire body seemed to take on the judgment of a divine ruler.","Aurelian stepped forward, and the stage beneath him melted into radiant lines.","\"Divine Dominion, Sun King’s Execution.\"","The spear in his hand swelled into a massive blade of golden-white light, and he swung it toward Damian with the full authority of the endless sun at his back. The attack blanketed half the stage and left almost nowhere to evade.","Damian finally drew a deeper breath, and the Sword Sovereign Heaven behind him changed. The empty throne within the sword palace released a faint glow, and the single sword hanging before that throne descended by a fraction.","Damian raised his sword with both hands.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, Fourth Edict, Palace Sword Descends.\"","The sword before the throne cast out a projection, and that projection sank into Damian’s blade. In an instant, his aura turned terrifyingly sharp. His entire body seemed to merge with the sword world at his back, and the blade in his grip no longer looked like a weapon held by a man. It looked like the judgment of the Sword Sovereign Heaven made manifest.","He slashed. The sword met the Sun King’s Execution, and for one moment the entire stage split into halves, one of golden-white light and one of pure silver sword radiance.","Then the golden-white blade broke apart.","Aurelian’s pupils contracted. The sword light did not stop after cleaving through the Sun King’s Execution. It swept onward, struck Aurelian’s sacred armor, and drove him backward for the first time since both Pseudo Cosmic Paths had fully opened. A thin line opened across his chest, and golden-white blood seeped from the wound.","The arena erupted.","\"Aurelian was injured!\"","\"Damian cut through the Sun King’s Execution!\"","\"That Sword Sovereign Heaven is too strong!\"","\"The Divine Son is being pushed!\"","Inside the viewing halls of the second elven faction, the atmosphere turned frigid. Many elders stared at the screen with dark faces. Aurelian’s injury was not severe, but the meaning behind it could not be ignored. His Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion had been cut open by Damian’s sword.","At the Sword God Palace, countless disciples roared.","\"Senior Brother Damian!\"","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven!\"","\"Cut down the divine light!\"","Aurelian looked down at the wound across his chest, and his face emptied of expression. Then the golden-white light around him began to change. It grew purer, hotter, and far more dangerous.","Max’s eyes narrowed.","’He is drawing deeper from the stolen bloodline.’","Aurelian slowly raised his head. \"You are strong enough to make me use this,\" he said.","Damian’s expression remained calm. \"Then use it.\"","Aurelian’s crown flared, and the golden-white throne behind him shattered. The divine kingdom did not collapse. Instead, the fragments of the throne streamed into Aurelian’s body, fusing with his bloodline and driving his aura up to a level that was less stable but far more terrifying. Sacred runes surfaced across his skin, and the Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion condensed around him into a smaller and denser form.","\"Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion, Crownless Divine King.\"","Boom!","The pressure of Aurelian’s path transformed completely. If his earlier dominion had been the authority of a ruler seated upon a divine throne, then this state was the ruler abandoning that throne and turning himself into the instrument of judgment.","The sacred halls vanished, the radiant pillars vanished, and even the endless sun dimmed, for all the authority of the dominion had gathered into Aurelian’s body and spear. His speed increased, his strength increased, and his divine light condensed to a far greater density.","Aurelian moved and appeared in front of Damian in an instant.","\"Crownless Divine King, Light That Judges All Blades.\"","His spear thrust forward, and the golden-white light around it wove countless judgment runes aimed directly at Damian’s sword. The attack did not target Damian’s body first. It targeted his blade, his sword intent, and the very connection between him and the Sword Sovereign Heaven.","Damian’s eyes sharpened.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, Fifth Edict, Sword Heart Cannot Be Judged.\"","His sword met the spear. The judgment runes coiled around the blade and strained to suppress it, but Damian’s sword heart released a single pure vibration, and the runes cracked apart one by one. Aurelian, however, had already flowed into his next attack.","\"Crownless Divine King, Radiant Execution Step.\"","Aurelian’s body flickered around Damian, trailing several golden-white afterimages, and each afterimage stabbed out with a spear of light carrying divine judgment authority. Damian’s sword answered with terrifying precision, blocking, cutting, and redirecting each strike in turn, but this time Aurelian’s speed and pressure clearly outstripped everything that had come before.","Damian was forced back one step, then a second, and then a third. At last Aurelian’s spear broke through Damian’s net of sword light and pierced his shoulder. Blood splashed across the stage, and for one breath the disciples of the Sword God Palace fell silent.","Aurelian’s eyes were cold. \"Even the sword bleeds.\""]},{"number":1864,"title":"Chapter 1864: Damian Wins!","paragraphs":["Damian looked at the spear buried in his shoulder, and then he looked at Aurelian.","\"Yes,\" he said calmly. \"But it does not stop cutting.\"","His left hand closed around the spear’s shaft. Aurelian’s eyes narrowed, and Damian stepped forward instead of retreating, allowing the spear to sink a little deeper as his sword rose from below.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, Sixth Edict, Bleeding Sword Severance.\"","Aurelian tried at once to withdraw, but Damian’s hand pinned the spear in place for that single fraction of a breath, and that fraction was enough. The sword light flashed, Aurelian’s radiant spear was sheared in half, and in the same instant a deep sword wound opened across Aurelian’s right arm.","Aurelian retreated sharply, and his expression finally broke. Damian pulled the severed spear tip from his shoulder and let it clatter onto the stage. Blood ran freely down his arm, yet his sword remained perfectly steady.","The arena went silent once more.","Rakan Thorne laughed under his breath. \"That guy is ruthless.\"","Orion’s eyes shone weakly. \"That is a swordsman.\"","Kaiden Voidmere said softly, \"He accepted the wound to create a cutting chance.\"","Ervin’s gaze stayed deep. \"Damian’s calmness is more dangerous.\"","On the stage, Aurelian’s face grew colder and colder. His golden-white blood dripped from his arm, but the Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion still burned around him. The Crownless Divine King state had granted him greater power, and Damian had cut through it at close range regardless.","Aurelian raised both hands, and the broken spear of light dissolved. Behind him, the dimmed endless sun suddenly compressed into a single golden-white point, and the pressure radiating from that point was terrifying. Damian looked up, and the Sword Sovereign Heaven behind him grew quieter in answer.","Aurelian’s voice rang out like a divine decree.","\"Crownless Divine King, Final Luminance Judgment.\"","The golden-white point expanded into a colossal divine sword of light. It was no longer a spear at all. It was a blade of judgment forged from Aurelian’s dominion, his bloodline, and his crownless state combined, and it carried enough power to burn straight through the sword world standing before Damian.","The Divine Realm held its breath. Aurelian swung his hand down, and the massive divine sword descended.","Damian stood beneath it with his shoulder bleeding, his clothes torn, and his aura drained far beyond anything the battle had cost him before. Yet his eyes remained calm, and he raised his sword one final time.","The Sword Sovereign Heaven behind him changed once more. The empty throne within the sword palace began to shine, the countless swords buried in the altar rose as one, the sword mountains bowed their peaks, and the sword rivers ceased to flow. Everything in the sword world turned toward Damian’s blade.","Damian spoke quietly.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven.\"","His voice was not loud, yet every swordsman across the Divine Realm heard it echo in their hearts.","\"Final Edict.\"","The sword hanging before the empty throne dissolved into light and poured completely into his blade.","\"Throne Of The Only Sword.\"","Boom!","For one instant, every other sword light in existence vanished, and only Damian’s sword remained. There was no river, no mountain, no palace, no altar, and no host of countless blades. There was only one sword, and because only one sword remained, that sword became absolute.","Damian slashed upward, and the single sword light met Aurelian’s Final Luminance Judgment.","The collision was silent at first. Then the colossal divine sword of light cracked.","Aurelian’s expression changed drastically. \"No.\"","The crack spread from the tip into the body, and from the body into the core, and then the entire Final Luminance Judgment split apart. Damian’s sword light passed through it, crossed the stage, cut through the remaining authority of the Crownless Divine King, and sliced through Aurelian’s sacred armor before stopping just short of his throat.","A thin line of blood appeared on Aurelian’s neck. The divine light around him shattered, and the Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion collapsed behind him, its sacred halls breaking apart, its radiant pillars toppling, and its endless sun dimming into scattered motes of gold.","Aurelian stood frozen in place. Damian stood opposite him with his sword still raised and blood flowing from his wounded shoulder. For several breaths, no one spoke at all.","Then Angelina Valerius’s voice rang across the arena.","\"Aurelian Lareth is unable to continue.\"","The screen above the stage changed.","[Winner: Damian Voss.]","[Aurelian Lareth Defeated.]","The entire Divine Realm plunged into shocked silence, and then the Sword God Palace erupted. Their disciples screamed Damian’s name until the skies above their palace shook. Elders who had watched with perfect composure until now finally allowed themselves to smile, and countless swords rose from their sheaths as though saluting the Sword Sovereign Heaven.","Damian had defeated the Divine Son of the second elven faction and had revealed one of the strongest Pseudo Cosmic Paths in the Divine Realm before the eyes of everyone.","At that same moment, the territories of the second elven faction fell deathly quiet. Aurelian Lareth had lost. Their Divine Son, the bearer of the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline and the one expected to display absolute dominance over his generation, had been cut down by Damian Voss in front of the entire Divine Realm.","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, Max watched the defeated Aurelian without blinking. There was no joy on his face. There was only cold clarity. Aurelian was strong, and in truth he was very strong, for both his Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion and his Crownless Divine King state were terrifying.","But he was not invincible. His stolen light could bleed, his dominion could be cut, and his pride could be broken.","Damian slowly lowered his sword. Aurelian’s face had gone pale, and his golden eyes churned with disbelief, humiliation, and cold fury. His body trembled as though he wished to keep fighting, but the sword light that had rested before his throat made the result impossible to deny.","Damian regarded him calmly. \"You are strong,\" Damian said.","Aurelian’s jaw tightened.","Damian continued, \"I always felt your light attacks were strong but not stable. Either way, the result wouldn’t have changed.\"","The words struck Aurelian harder than the sword wound had. Max’s eyes sharpened. Aurelian stared at Damian with a cold and dangerous gaze, but before he could speak, the transfer light descended and returned him to his pillar.","Damian returned to his own pillar a moment later. The laws of the Eternal Hourglass began mending his shoulder, yet the sword aura around him remained sharp and steady.","The screen above the arena updated.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Damian Voss]","[Total Battles Fought: 5]","[Total Wins: 5]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Aurelian Lareth]","[Total Battles Fought: 4]","[Total Wins: 3]","The result shone above everyone. Damian Voss had won, and Aurelian Lareth had lost, and with that victory, the final competitive stage became even more unpredictable than before."]},{"number":1865,"title":"Chapter 1865: Max vs Selene!","paragraphs":["After Damian Voss defeated Aurelian Lareth, the final competitive stage entered a long and relentless rhythm.","The shock of the Divine Son’s defeat had not fully faded, but Angelina Valerius did not allow the arena to remain frozen in that moment. The laws of the Eternal Hourglass continued rotating the names above the central stage, and battles fell one after another like rain.","Some were fierce enough to make the spectators focus, while others ended so quickly that the result appeared before the crowd could even finish discussing the previous match.","Damian Voss continued to advance with terrifying steadiness.","After defeating Aurelian, he met several participants below the top monster level and won without revealing Sword Sovereign Heaven again.","Against a flame halberd genius, he used \"Silent Sword Art, Fourth Cut, Withered Flame\" and severed the heart of the flame technique before the halberd could descend.","Against a storm-winged woman, he used \"Falling Peak Sword\" to cut through her speed route and stopped his blade at her throat.","Against a defensive earth cultivator, he used only one vertical slash and split all nine layers of stone armor apart. His battle count climbed quickly, and his win count remained perfect.","Aurelian also continued fighting, but after losing to Damian, the air around him had changed. His victories were still clean. His Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion still suppressed most opponents before they could resist properly.","He defeated Hadeon Granite with \"Luminance Decree,\" defeated Yelric Flamehorn with \"Sacred Sun Judgment,\" and defeated a hidden spear genius with \"Crownless Divine King, Radiant Execution Step.\"","Yet every time he returned to his pillar, his face remained cold and unpleasant. No matter how many weaker opponents he defeated, the wound Damian left behind could not be erased from his pride.","Orion Starfall recovered slowly under the laws of the Eternal Hourglass and returned to battle with a smile on his face, though his aura was clearly not as full as before. Even so, anyone below the true peak could not withstand him.","He defeated a thunder-winged woman with \"Hundred Star Descent,\" defeated a beast-blooded warrior with \"Second Star Step\" and \"Fourth Star Knee,\" and forced a soul-path participant to surrender with \"Nine Star Court, Celestial Pressure Field.\"","Every victory reminded the Divine Realm that although Orion had lost to Revona, he had only lost after pushing her to the edge.","Revona, on the other hand, fought less aggressively after her exhausting battle with Orion, but that did not make her any easier to face. Her Void Origin Eyes remained terrifying. She defeated two opponents without using Void Origin Realm, simply erasing their strongest attacks until they understood the gap and surrendered.","Against a poison mist cultivator, she only opened her eyes once, and the entire poison field vanished as if it had never existed. Her battle count climbed steadily, and her record remained spotless.","Rakan Thorne also recovered his momentum. After his loss to Max, the War God Palace disciples had been quiet for a while, but Rakan quickly reminded everyone why he was the first Warlord.","He crushed one opponent with the First Limit of the War God Body, defeated another with the Second Limit, and did not need the Third Limit again unless the opponent truly had enough strength to withstand a few exchanges.","His loss to Max remained shocking, but no one dared to use that loss to underestimate him, because every participant who faced him afterward was beaten down with overwhelming physical force.","Kaiden Voidmere continued to win with quiet efficiency. He folded space, erased movement paths, and made techniques collapse before their full power could erupt.","Morgana Starveil also gathered several wins with her curse arts, though she sometimes took longer because her opponents had begun defending against her curses more carefully.","Fin Arclight remained dangerous with Pale Eclipse Burial, while Seren Frostveil recovered from her early loss and won several battles using Frozen World Stillness.","The records above the arena changed constantly.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Damian Voss]","[Total Battles Fought: 12]","[Total Wins: 12]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Revona]","[Total Battles Fought: 11]","[Total Wins: 11]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Max Morgan]","[Total Battles Fought: 10]","[Total Wins: 10]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Rakan Thorne]","[Total Battles Fought: 13]","[Total Wins: 12]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Aurelian Lareth]","[Total Battles Fought: 12]","[Total Wins: 11]","The battles kept moving.","Max also received several easier opponents during this stretch.","One of them was a blood-armor cultivator who tried to trap Max with a crimson prison. Max walked through it and shattered the prison with one punch. Another was a wind-attribute swordsman who relied on speed, but Max caught the blade between two fingers and forced him to surrender before the second exchange.","A third was a soul-path participant who tried to attack Max’s consciousness, only for the attack to vanish into the Dimension of Soul without causing even the slightest ripple.","Against those opponents, Max did not use Dragonheart, did not reveal Emotion Severing Path, did not open the Seven Divine Veins, and did not use Draconic Essences. His base strength alone was already enough.","Slowly, everyone’s battle count passed ten.","Then twelve.","Then fourteen.","Finally, the records of almost every remaining participant crossed fifteen battles.","At this point, the final competitive stage became even heavier. The weak had already collected many losses. The mid-level geniuses were struggling to preserve decent records.","The top monsters were beginning to look toward one another more often, because most of the easier matches had already passed. Every remaining major pairing would affect the final rankings.","Then Angelina Valerius raised her hand once again.","The giant screen spun.","The names rotated through the air in bright lines.","Max Morgan.","Selene Vaeloria.","Aurelian Lareth.","Kaiden Voidmere.","Ervin.","Rosaline Lunara.","Morgana Starveil.","Rakan Thorne.","Damian Voss.","Revona.","The light slowed.","The first name appeared.","[Max Morgan]","The arena immediately became alert.","Then the second name stopped.","[Selene Vaeloria]","The screen enlarged both names.","[Max Morgan vs Selene Vaeloria]","A strange silence fell over the arena.","This pairing carried a different meaning.","Max and Selene had already fought near the Witch God Tree. Everyone who had watched the earlier events remembered that battle. Selene had used her Heavenly Luminance Genesis and Spear of First Dawn, yet Max had still defeated her.","Since then, Max had revealed even more terrifying strength. He had defeated Rosaline’s Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary, crushed Rakan in a pure body battle, and continued winning without exposing his full power."]},{"number":1866,"title":"Chapter 1866: Ervin vs Rosaline!","paragraphs":["Selene stood on her pillar with a cold expression.","For a few breaths, she did not move.","Angelina looked toward them calmly.","\"Max Morgan. Selene Vaeloria. Enter the stage.\"","Two beams of light descended.","Max appeared on one side of the central stage.","Selene appeared opposite him, her white-gold hair moving gently behind her, her face pale but composed. She looked at Max silently. The Heavenly Luminance power inside her body stirred faintly, but it did not rise. No avatar appeared behind her. No Genesis light opened. No spear formed above the stage.","Max looked at her.","Selene clenched her hands for a moment.","Then she spoke coldly.","\"I surrender.\"","The entire arena froze.","Even Max raised an eyebrow slightly.","Angelina Valerius looked at Selene for a breath, then announced calmly, \"Selene Vaeloria has surrendered.\"","[Winner: Max Morgan.]","[Selene Vaeloria Defeated.]","The screen updated immediately.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Max Morgan]","[Total Battles Fought: 16]","[Total Wins: 16]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Selene Vaeloria]","[Total Battles Fought: 16]","[Total Wins: 11]","The silence lasted for several breaths before whispers spread across the arena.","\"She surrendered?\"","\"She did not even fight?\"","\"She already lost to Max before.\"","\"After seeing what Max did to Rakan, perhaps she knew fighting was meaningless.\"","\"But she is the Divine Daughter of the second faction.\"","On his pillar, Aurelian Lareth’s expression became ugly.","Disgust flashed in his eyes for a brief instant.","Selene had surrendered without fighting. To others, it might be a practical choice. To Aurelian, it was humiliation. The second faction’s Divine Daughter had stepped onto the stage before Max Morgan and given up without even raising her spear. It was not only her personal surrender. It felt like another stain on the prestige of their faction.","But Aurelian did not speak.","He only looked away coldly.","Selene noticed his expression, but she did not respond. Her hands remained clenched at her sides, yet her face stayed calm. She had fought Max before. She knew better than most what kind of pressure he carried.","After watching him defeat Rakan with one finger while using only one Divine Vein and a portion of his Draconic Essences, she understood that forcing a battle here would only result in a deeper humiliation.","Max watched her quietly.","He did not mock her.","The transfer light returned Selene to her pillar, and Max returned to his own.","The battles continued again.","Some matchups were quickly resolved.","[Kaiden Voidmere vs Hadeon Granite]","Kaiden Voidmere won after folding the ground beneath Hadeon’s defenses and making all his stone barriers collapse inward.","[Winner: Kaiden Voidmere.]","[Hadeon Granite Defeated.]","[Morgana Starveil vs Yelric Flamehorn]","Morgana Starveil won by placing a curse on Yelric’s flame core, making each burst of fire burn backward into his own armor until he surrendered.","[Winner: Morgana Starveil.]","[Yelric Flamehorn Defeated.]","[Rakan Thorne vs Corvin Nightsteel]","Rakan Thorne won with one punch after opening the First Limit of the War God Body.","[Winner: Rakan Thorne.]","[Corvin Nightsteel Defeated.]","[Damian Voss vs Seren Frostveil]","Seren Frostveil tried to freeze his sword rhythm with Frozen World Stillness, but Damian cut through the stillness with \"Sword Sovereign Heaven, First Edict, All Blades Refuse Submission\" and forced her to surrender after three exchanges.","[Winner: Damian Voss.]","[Seren Frostveil Defeated.]","[Aurelian Lareth vs Fin Arclight]","Fin tried to trap Aurelian inside Pale Eclipse Burial, but Aurelian’s Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion purified the eclipse field and shattered the Moonless Descent before it could fully form. Fin surrendered with an unwilling expression.","[Winner: Aurelian Lareth.]","[Fin Arclight Defeated.]","[Orion Starfall vs Vaela Sunspire]","Orion won with \"Nine Star Court, Hundred Star Descent,\" never needing to use Nine Star Sovereign Body.","[Winner: Orion Starfall.]","[Vaela Sunspire Defeated.]","[Revona vs Darius Stoneveil]","Darius Stoneveil surrendered after Revona erased three layers of his strongest defensive formation with one look.","[Winner: Revona.]","[Darius Stoneveil Defeated.]","The final competitive stage kept tightening.","Names appeared.","Battles ended.","Records updated.","Some participants had already lost any chance of reaching the top rankings, while others fought desperately to preserve their pride. The truly important names continued meeting one another, and every time two strong participants were called, the Divine Realm leaned closer to the screens.","Then the randomizer spun again.","The light slowed.","Two names appeared.","[Ervin vs Rosaline Lunara]","The arena grew quieter.","This was not a battle between the absolute highest-ranked monsters, but it was still important. Ervin had revealed the terrifying Abyssal Origin Descent against Selene and won, while Rosaline’s Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary had already shown itself to be a powerful sealing and suppression Pseudo Cosmic Path.","Both of them had strong records. Both had already lost or struggled against the peak monsters. This battle would decide who could remain closer to the upper ranks.","Angelina raised her hand.","\"Ervin. Rosaline Lunara. Enter the stage.\"","Two beams descended.","Ervin appeared with his black spear in hand, his aura still quiet and deep.","Rosaline appeared opposite him, golden-pink light already gathering around her body. She did not smile casually this time. After losing to Max, she had fought carefully and rebuilt her record, but Ervin was not someone she could treat lightly.","\"I suppose holding back would be foolish,\" Rosaline said.","Ervin nodded. \"Against you, yes.\"","Rosaline raised both hands.","Golden-pink light rose like dawn.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path, Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary.\"","The luminous kingdom appeared behind her, filled with rose-gold palaces, radiant walls, falling petals, and the great throne of dawn. The sanctuary spread across the stage, releasing sealing, purification, and sovereign binding power. Rosaline did not test slowly. She used her strongest battlefield control immediately.","\"Dawn Edict, First Seal.\"","\"Dawn Edict, Second Seal.\"","\"Dawn Edict, Third Seal.\"","Three rose-gold seals descended toward Ervin, one targeting his body, one targeting his spear, and one targeting the dark energy flowing around him. At the same time, radiant chains rose from the floor, trying to bind his movement before he could open his abyssal path.","Ervin stepped forward.","His black spear moved once.","A dark spear line pierced through the first seal.","Then he twisted his wrist, and the spear line sank into the second seal like a shadow falling into deep water. The second seal dimmed but did not fully break. Rosaline’s sanctuary reinforced it immediately, and the third seal descended faster."]},{"number":1867,"title":"Chapter 1867: Five Undefeated Geniuses!","paragraphs":["Ervin’s eyes sharpened slightly.","\"Good control.\"","Rosaline’s expression remained serious. \"I learned from my fight with Max that if I give someone like you space, I lose.\"","She raised her hand again.","\"Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary, Royal Mandate of Purifying Light.\"","A massive golden-pink pillar descended toward Ervin, carrying purification and sealing authority together. The light tried to purify his abyssal aura before it fully awakened, but Ervin’s spear struck upward, and a dark spiral formed around the tip.","\"Abyss Spear Art, Hollow Descent Thrust.\"","The spear pierced into the golden-pink pillar.","The collision shook the stage.","Rosaline’s sanctuary brightened, and the rose-gold throne behind her released greater pressure. Ervin was forced back two steps, which immediately made the spectators realize that Rosaline’s control was working. She could not overpower him directly, but her sanctuary was restricting his rhythm and forcing him to spend more power to move.","Rosaline pressed the advantage.","\"Dawn Edict, Fourth Seal.\"","A crown-shaped seal appeared above Ervin’s head.","At the same time, countless petals gathered around him, each one carrying a soft but dangerous binding light. Ervin’s spear swept out, tearing through hundreds of petals, but more appeared immediately. The Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary was not a simple attack. As long as it remained active, Rosaline could rebuild, reinforce, and suppress again and again.","Ervin finally stopped.","The air around him sank.","The smile on Rosaline’s face faded.","Ervin spoke calmly.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path, Abyssal Origin Descent.\"","The black sea appeared behind him.","The broken ancient gate rose from the depths.","The entire battlefield became heavier.","Rosaline’s golden-pink sanctuary trembled as the abyssal pressure spread through it. The petals slowed. The chains sank. The seals dimmed slightly, as if their authority was being dragged downward toward an unknown depth.","Rosaline gritted her teeth and raised both hands.","\"Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary, Final Dawn Edict, Sovereign Rose Spear.\"","The entire sanctuary compressed.","The rose-gold throne, the falling petals, the luminous palaces, and the sovereign binding power gathered into a single spear of dawn light. It shot toward Ervin with far more force than before, carrying the full majesty of Rosaline’s Pseudo Cosmic Path.","Ervin’s Abyssal Origin Descent opened wider.","The broken gate behind him released a deep, soundless pressure.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, Gate of the First Depth.\"","The gate opened slightly.","The Sovereign Rose Spear struck it.","For several breaths, the golden-pink spear resisted the pull of the abyssal gate. Rosaline poured everything into it, and the dawn spear pierced deeper than many expected, forcing cracks to appear across the shadow surrounding the gate. Ervin’s expression became slightly more serious, and his hand tightened around his spear.","Rosaline was strong.","Her sanctuary was not enough to defeat him, but it was enough to force him to take her seriously.","Then Ervin stepped forward.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, Return To Depth.\"","The black sea rose.","The gate pulled.","The Sovereign Rose Spear trembled.","Rosaline’s face turned pale as the golden-pink light began sinking into the broken gate. She tried to maintain the spear, but the abyssal origin pressure dragged its authority downward layer by layer until the spear finally collapsed into scattered dawn fragments.","Ervin moved through those fragments.","His spear stopped before Rosaline’s throat.","Rosaline looked at the spear tip, then slowly lowered her hands.","\"I surrender.\"","Angelina Valerius announced the result.","[Winner: Ervin.]","[Rosaline Lunara Defeated.]","The screen updated.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Ervin]","[Total Battles Fought: 17]","[Total Wins: 17]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Rosaline Lunara]","[Total Battles Fought: 17]","[Total Wins: 15]","Rosaline let out a soft breath as the transfer light descended.","\"You are difficult to fight,\" she said.","Ervin withdrew his spear. \"So are you.\"","Rosaline smiled faintly. \"That is kind of you to say after swallowing my strongest attack.\"","Ervin’s expression remained calm. \"It was strong enough to make the gate crack.\"","The transfer light carried both of them back to their pillars.","The arena remained thoughtful after that battle. Ervin had won, but Rosaline had proven again that Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary was not weak.","Against almost anyone below the peak monsters, her sealing and sovereign suppression would have been enough to control the entire fight. Unfortunately for her, Ervin’s Abyssal Origin Descent was one of the few paths capable of dragging that authority into a deeper darkness.","Max watched Ervin quietly.","That broken gate remained troublesome.","Even now, after seeing it twice, Max still felt that the black sea was only the surface.","The true danger lay behind the gate.","After Ervin defeated Rosaline Lunara, the final competitive stage continued moving forward with an even heavier momentum.","By now, almost every important participant had already crossed seventeen battles, and the records above the arena were beginning to look brutal. The ones at the top had separated themselves from the rest.","Max Morgan, Damian Voss, Revona, Kaiden Voidmere, Ervin, Rakan Thorne, Orion Starfall, Aurelian Lareth, Morgana Starveil, Rosaline Lunara, Selene Vaeloria, Fin Arclight, and Seren Frostveil had all carved their names into the upper half of the ranking field, but the gap between them was no longer equal.","A few losses could now decide whether someone remained close to the championship path or fell into the lower ranks of the top twenty-five.","Angelina Valerius continued calling battles one after another.","Some matches were fierce but brief.","Damian Voss defeated Morgana Starveil after cutting through her Star-Curse Labyrinth with Sword Sovereign Heaven, though Morgana forced him to reveal several sword edicts before admitting defeat.","Rakan Thorne defeated Fin Arclight after opening the Second Limit of the War God Body and shattering the Pale Eclipse Field through sheer physical force.","Orion Starfall fought Seren Frostveil and won after using Nine Star Sovereign Body to break through Frozen World Stillness, though his injuries from the Revona battle made the victory much harder than it should have been.","Aurelian Lareth defeated Rosaline Lunara by suppressing her Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary with Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion, but his expression remained cold and unpleasant afterward, as though each victory that was not against Max or Damian felt meaningless to him.","The mid-tier participants continued falling behind.","[Winner: Damian Voss.]","[Morgana Starveil Defeated.]","[Winner: Rakan Thorne.]","[Fin Arclight Defeated.]","[Winner: Orion Starfall.]","[Seren Frostveil Defeated.]","[Winner: Aurelian Lareth.]","[Rosaline Lunara Defeated.]","The screen kept updating.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Damian Voss]","[Total Battles Fought: 18]","[Total Wins: 18]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Max Morgan]","[Total Battles Fought: 17]","[Total Wins: 17]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Revona]","[Total Battles Fought: 18]","[Total Wins: 18]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Kaiden Voidmere]","[Total Battles Fought: 17]","[Total Wins: 17]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Ervin]","[Total Battles Fought: 18]","[Total Wins: 18]","At this stage, every battle involving the top few names became important.","Max remained undefeated.","Damian remained undefeated.","Revona remained undefeated.","Kaiden remained undefeated.","Ervin remained undefeated.","The Divine Realm could feel the pressure building. Everyone knew that these unbeaten names could not avoid one another forever. The round-robin format guaranteed that each of them would eventually collide, and every collision would reshape the upper rankings."]},{"number":1868,"title":"Chapter 1868: Max vs Kaiden!","paragraphs":["Then the randomizer began spinning again.","The giant screen above the arena flashed with countless names.","Rakan Thorne.","Aurelian Lareth.","Orion Starfall.","Ervin.","Revona.","Damian Voss.","Kaiden Voidmere.","Max Morgan.","Selene Vaeloria.","Rosaline Lunara.","Morgana Starveil.","The light slowed.","The first name stopped.","[Max Morgan]","The entire arena became alert.","Even before the second name appeared, the atmosphere had already changed. Whenever Max’s name appeared now, the Divine Realm paid attention. He had defeated Rosaline, crushed Rakan in body strength, forced Selene to surrender without fighting, and continued gathering wins without revealing everything.","Every battle involving him carried the possibility of another hidden card being shown.","Then the second name slowed.","It passed over Damian Voss.","It passed over Revona.","It passed over Ervin.","Finally, it stopped.","[Kaiden Voidmere]","The screen enlarged both names at once.","[Final Competitive Stage]","[Max Morgan vs Kaiden Voidmere]","For a moment, the arena went completely silent.","Then the shock spread like a wave.","Max Morgan against Kaiden Voidmere.","This was not merely another battle between undefeated participants. This was a collision between two people connected by something far deeper than the tournament rankings. Kaiden Voidmere was the supreme genius of the Grand Void Sanctum, a force whose understanding of space and void stood among the highest in the Divine Realm.","He had moved through the final stage with terrifying ease, folding space, collapsing movement paths, and making opponents lose the very road beneath their feet before their attacks could land.","Max, however, was different.","Max had also walked the path of space.","Max had cultivated the Void Genesis Art.","And the more he had watched Kaiden fight, the more certain he had become of one thing.","The master who had given him the Void Genesis Art was the same master Kaiden had.","They had the same teacher.","They had walked the same path in the Space Concept.","Perhaps their branches had developed differently. Perhaps Kaiden had learned openly under the Grand Void Sanctum, while Max had inherited the Void Genesis Art through a much stranger path. But the source, the rhythm, and the foundation carried the same invisible mark.","Every time Kaiden folded space, every time he collapsed distance, and every time he stepped through a void gap without disturbing the surface of the world, Max could feel the echo of the same inheritance inside his own Space Concept.","Kaiden Voidmere slowly opened his eyes.","On his pillar, a faint silver-gray ripple spread around him.","He looked toward Max.","For the first time in a long while, a small smile appeared on Kaiden’s face.","\"So our battle finally came.\"","Max looked back at him calmly.","\"Yes.\"","The surrounding participants immediately noticed the difference.","Rakan Thorne crossed his arms and grinned. \"These two know something we do not.\"","Orion Starfall, still pale but recovering, smiled with interest. \"That expression from Kaiden is rare.\"","Morgana Starveil tilted her head. \"Now this is interesting. That is not the look of two strangers meeting in battle.\"","Aurelian Lareth’s expression turned colder. Anything that revealed another hidden depth of Max made his mood worse, and Kaiden was not a weak opponent. If Max defeated Kaiden too, then his position in the final rankings would become even more terrifying.","At the Black Dragon Clan, the disciples erupted with excitement and nervousness.","\"Max is fighting Kaiden Voidmere!\"","\"Kaiden has not lost once!\"","\"He is from the Grand Void Sanctum. His void and space techniques are insane.\"","\"Max has space power too, right?\"","\"He used dimensional abilities before. Maybe this battle will show more of it.\"","Lady Virelia stood quietly before the giant screen, her eyes fixed on Max’s figure.","The seven family heads also grew solemn. They had seen Max use spatial power before, but Kaiden Voidmere was different from ordinary space cultivators. He had the backing of the Grand Void Sanctum, one of the most mysterious first-rate forces in the Divine Realm, and his control of space had looked effortless throughout the final stage.","At another distant viewing platform surrounded by folded space and silver-gray mist, the disciples of the Grand Void Sanctum watched with rare seriousness.","Kaiden was their pride.","He rarely spoke, rarely showed emotion, and rarely needed to use much strength against others. His victories were quiet, clean, and almost impossible to understand for anyone who did not cultivate space.","But now he had been matched with Max Morgan, the black dragon genius who had shaken the entire conference again and again.","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, Angelina Valerius raised her hand.","\"Max Morgan.\"","Her gaze shifted.","\"Kaiden Voidmere.\"","The transfer light began gathering above both pillars.","\"Enter the stage.\"","Two beams of light descended.","Max appeared on one side of the central stage, his white hair moving gently as the space around him settled.","Kaiden appeared opposite him, silver-gray robes fluttering softly, his calm eyes carrying a rare brightness. Unlike many other opponents, he did not immediately release oppressive aura. Instead, he looked at Max as if he was looking at someone familiar and unfamiliar at the same time.","For several breaths, neither of them moved.","Then Kaiden spoke first.","\"You have Void Genesis Art.\"","The words were quiet, but they struck like thunder among those who understood their meaning.","Max looked at him calmly.","\"I do.\"","Kaiden’s eyes became deeper. \"I sensed it before, but I was not completely certain. Now that we stand on the same stage, there is no mistake.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"I also sensed it from your techniques.\"","Kaiden nodded. \"Then you understand.\"","Max’s gaze sharpened slightly.","\"Yes. The master who gave me Void Genesis Art is the same master behind your path.\"","A wave of whispers spread across the participant pillars.","Same master.","Same path.","Same source.","The meaning behind those words was not small.","Kaiden looked at Max for a moment, then said, \"In the Grand Void Sanctum, very few people are allowed to approach that inheritance directly. Even among those who do, most only touch the outer shell. You are not from the sanctum, yet your foundation carries the core rhythm. That is why I called you junior brother before.\"","Max remembered that moment.","Kaiden had sensed it long ago.","He had not said everything then, but the meaning had been clear.","Max looked at him and asked, \"Then are you my senior brother?\"","Kaiden smiled faintly. \"Perhaps. Or perhaps we are both only people walking beneath the shadow of the same master.\"","Max’s smile grew slightly. \"That sounds more accurate.\"","Kaiden raised one hand slowly.","Space rippled around his fingers.","\"Still, same source does not mean same strength.\"","Max’s eyes brightened with interest.","\"Of course.\"","Kaiden’s silver-gray pupils shone faintly.","\"Then let us see how far your Void Genesis Art has gone.\"","Max raised his hand as well, and the space around him responded with a quiet hum.","The entire arena grew tense.","This was not a battle of brute strength like Max and Rakan.","This was not a clash of sword and divine light like Damian and Aurelian.","This was a battle between two cultivators walking the same mysterious space path, two people whose foundations echoed one another, and two undefeated geniuses whose collision could reveal the true depth of the Void Genesis Art.","Angelina Valerius looked down at them.","Her voice remained calm, but the Eternal Hourglass itself seemed to pay attention.","[Battle Begins.]","The space between Max and Kaiden folded.","And both of them vanished at the same time."]},{"number":1869,"title":"Chapter 1869: Pushing Kaiden!","paragraphs":["The space between Max and Kaiden folded, and both of them vanished in the same instant.","For a breath, the central stage looked empty. There was no explosion, no flash of golden light, no sword cry, no thunder, and no roaring dragon aura. Yet every true expert watching felt their skin tighten, because the battlefield had not grown calm. It had grown far more dangerous.","The danger had simply left the visible surface of the world and slipped into the hidden layers of space itself.","Then a line appeared in the air. It was not a sword mark. It was a spatial fracture.","Max and Kaiden appeared on opposite sides of that fracture at almost the same moment. Each had one hand raised, and each was using the same basic rhythm of the Void Genesis Art to twist the folded space between them.","The fracture expanded and then collapsed inward, disappearing before it could tear the stage apart. In the next instant, both of them vanished again.","Kaiden’s voice echoed from somewhere within the warped space.","\"Void Genesis Art, Empty Step.\"","His figure reappeared behind Max without disturbing the air. A palm shot forward carrying no visible energy, yet the space in front of it folded into seven sharp layers. Had it landed on an ordinary opponent, the blow would never have struck from the outside.","Their inner organs, bones, and energy pathways would have been compressed from several spatial layers at once.","Max did not turn around.","\"Void Genesis Art, Origin Fold.\"","The space behind him bent before Kaiden’s palm could arrive. The strike that should have landed on Max’s back folded past him and emerged three meters to his left instead.","At the same time, Max stepped backward through the folded space and appeared in front of Kaiden. His fingers were already pressing toward Kaiden’s chest.","\"Void Genesis Art, Space-Sealing Finger.\"","Kaiden’s eyes sharpened.","\"Void Genesis Art, Hollow Displacement.\"","His body blurred as the space around him shifted half a step away from reality, and Max’s finger passed through nothing but an afterimage. Yet Max’s eyes remained calm, and his finger did not stop. It dipped slightly downward, and the sealed space redirected itself.","Kaiden’s true body had only just emerged when the Space-Sealing Finger arrived before him once more. He raised his hand and blocked.","Boom!","There was no ordinary shockwave. Instead, the space between them sank, twisted, and shattered into countless mirror-like fragments before the laws of the Eternal Hourglass knitted it back together.","The two separated, or rather, the space between them expanded. Max stood on one side of the stage while Kaiden stood on the other. Both remained composed, but the expressions of everyone watching had already changed.","The battle had opened with high-level Void Genesis Art techniques from the very first exchange. Neither man had tested the other with weak moves, and neither had wasted time on ordinary attacks.","That alone marked the difference between this fight and most others. Max and Kaiden both understood that two people trained by the same master, walking the same path of space, had no need for shallow probing.","Kaiden regarded Max quietly. \"You handled Hollow Displacement on the first try.\"","Max replied calmly, \"It had the same root as Empty Step.\"","Kaiden nodded. \"Then I will not use the outer forms anymore.\"","The silver-gray ripples around him deepened.","Max smiled faintly. \"Good. I was about to say the same thing.\"","In the next instant, the entire central stage transformed into a battlefield of invisible folds.","Kaiden raised both hands.","\"Void Genesis Art, Thousand-Layer Spatial Cage.\"","The space around Max split into layer after layer, forming a transparent prison without walls. Each layer overlapped the next, and every overlap carried crushing pressure. The cage did not attempt to bind Max’s body directly. It tried to bind his position in space itself, pinning him to a fixed coordinate no matter how he moved.","Max lifted one finger.","\"Void Genesis Art, Origin Point Reversal.\"","The center of the cage shifted. For one brief instant, the fixed coordinate changed from Max’s position to Kaiden’s own shadow. The Thousand-Layer Spatial Cage collapsed inward, but it closed around the spot where Kaiden had stood a breath earlier rather than around Max.","Kaiden had already moved.","\"Void Genesis Art, Void Corridor Severance.\"","A long corridor of folded space opened beneath Max’s feet. It sought to sever the path between Max and the surrounding arena, isolating him from every direction at once. At the same moment, Kaiden appeared above him with his palm descending like a silent blade.","\"Void Genesis Art, Space Burial Palm.\"","The palm fell, and the space around Max sank as though a tomb had opened beneath him.","Max looked up, and his eyes remained perfectly calm.","\"Void Genesis Art, Genesis Void Axis.\"","A vertical line of invisible force ran through Max’s body. The Space Burial Palm struck that axis and instantly lost its direction. The folded space that had tried to bury him began rotating around the axis instead. It formed a spiral that dragged the burial force away from Max and scattered it harmlessly into the edges of the arena.","Kaiden’s expression shifted slightly, but before he could withdraw, Max stepped forward. There was no distance left between them. Max’s palm pressed toward Kaiden’s shoulder.","\"Void Genesis Art, Returning Void Palm.\"","Kaiden crossed his arms.","\"Void Genesis Art, Triple Hollow Shield.\"","Three layers of hollow space materialized before him. Max’s palm touched the first layer, and it collapsed. The second layer twisted, and then the third layer shattered. Kaiden was driven backward for the first time in the battle.","He slid several meters across the stage, though his feet never truly touched the ground, for space kept folding beneath him to soften the impact. Even so, the fact was plain for everyone to see. Max had seized the advantage.","The Grand Void Sanctum disciples watching from afar went silent, while the Black Dragon Clan disciples erupted with excitement.","\"He pushed Kaiden back!\"","\"Max is using space against Kaiden and still winning!\"","\"Kaiden Voidmere has never been pushed like this before!\""]},{"number":1870,"title":"Chapter 1870: Sovereign of Space!","paragraphs":["Inside the Eternal Hourglass, the top geniuses watched with grave expressions.","Damian Voss narrowed his eyes. \"Their techniques share the same foundation, but Max’s handling runs deeper.\"","Ervin’s gaze turned thoughtful. \"Kaiden’s moves are clean, but Max is reading their source before they fully form.\"","Rakan Thorne frowned. \"I hate fights like this. They are punching each other with the battlefield itself.\"","Orion Starfall smiled weakly from his pillar. \"That is exactly what makes it frightening.\"","On the stage, Kaiden studied Max for a few breaths before raising his hand once more. This time, the space around the entire stage grew unstable.","\"Void Genesis Art, Eightfold World Folding.\"","Eight enormous folds spread across the central arena. Each fold contained a partial reflection of the stage, and within every reflection stood another Kaiden. The attack was no illusion. Each reflected Kaiden occupied a temporary spatial layer, and any one of them could become real at the instant of attack.","Eight Kaidens moved as one.","\"Void Genesis Art, Eight Hollow Strikes.\"","Eight palms lashed toward Max from eight separate spatial layers.","Max stood in place, and he neither dodged nor defended. The first strike passed through his shoulder while the second passed through his ribs. The third struck his back, and the fourth struck his chest. The fifth, sixth, seventh, and eighth all landed from their own different layers of space.","Yet Max did not move. No blood appeared, and no wound opened anywhere on his body. His clothes fluttered slightly, but he remained completely unharmed.","Kaiden’s eyes widened, and the eight reflected figures faded away.","Max regarded him quietly. \"Those attacks will not work on me.\"","Kaiden’s expression grew more serious. \"Why?\"","Max raised one hand, and the space around his palm answered him like an obedient subject.","\"It’s a secret.\"","The words were quiet, yet they spread through the arena like a shockwave, and Kaiden’s pupils contracted.","Max continued calmly, \"Your attacks are strong. Against almost anyone else here, even many top geniuses, they would be extremely dangerous. But they are still space element attacks. They still rely on folding, cutting, compressing, burying, displacing, or isolating space.\"","The space around Max became still. It was not controlled and it was not forced. It was simply still, as though it had accepted him of its own accord.","Max looked at Kaiden and said, \"I am mostly immune to that.\"","A wave of shock rolled across the arena. Kaiden slowly lowered his hand, and for the first time in the battle, his calm face showed genuine disbelief.","\"Mostly immune to space attacks?\"","Max offered no further explanation. He could not reveal everything about the Dimensional Sovereign Body, and he had no intention of exposing its source. The truth itself was simple enough.","Space could bend around him, fold around him, and even attack through him, but wounding him with space itself was nearly impossible unless the attacker held power far beyond his current level. His body did not merely resist spatial force. It belonged to a deeper dimensional foundation altogether.","The Dimensional Sovereign Body made him the true sovereign of space, and turning ordinary space attacks against him was simply foolish.","Kaiden grasped part of it without needing another word, and his gaze deepened.","\"So that is why my strikes failed to damage you.\"","Max nodded lightly. \"Yes.\"","Kaiden closed his eyes briefly, and when he opened them again, his expression had changed. There was no anger in it. There was only understanding, along with a strange sense of clarity. Even so, he did not surrender yet.","Silver-gray light erupted around him, and the space behind him opened into a vast hollow expanse filled with countless shifting planes. The aura of the Void Genesis Art swelled beyond anything he had shown before, and for the first time, Kaiden drove his mastery to its absolute limit.","\"Void Genesis Art, Grand Void Convergence.\"","Every spatial layer around the stage began folding toward a single point above Kaiden’s palm, and the pressure became terrifying. Even though Max was largely immune to spatial attacks, the sheer mastery behind this technique set the whole arena trembling.","The Grand Void Convergence did not simply cut or compress space. It gathered every fold Kaiden could command and condensed them into one point, seeking to collapse the opponent’s very position within reality.","Kaiden looked at Max. \"If this still cannot touch you, then I will have my answer.\"","Max stood calmly. \"Then come.\"","Kaiden pressed his palm forward. The Grand Void Convergence descended, and the point of collapsed space drifted toward Max like a silent star of emptiness.","Max raised his hand as the Void Genesis Art circulated within him. His movement, however, differed from Kaiden’s in nature. Kaiden controlled space with precision, while Max commanded it with the authority of its origin.","\"Void Genesis Art, Genesis Returns To Void.\"","The moment Max spoke, the collapsed point before him trembled. Kaiden’s Grand Void Convergence did not explode. Instead, it began to unfold. Layer by layer, the space Kaiden had compressed was returned to its original state.","The killing pressure vanished and the collapsing coordinates stabilized. The distorted reality mended itself around Max’s palm, and the enormous attack Kaiden had condensed with everything at his disposal dissolved without harming a single strand of Max’s hair.","The Grand Void Sanctum viewing platform fell deathly silent.","Kaiden stared at the scene, and at last he understood. The gap between them did not come only from Max’s immunity to space attacks. That was merely one reason. The deeper reason was mastery, for Max’s command of the Void Genesis Art surpassed his own.","Kaiden’s techniques were refined, powerful, and difficult to counter, but Max had reached a level where he could touch the root rhythm behind them. Whenever Kaiden folded space, Max could return the fold to its origin.","Whenever Kaiden displaced a layer, Max could redirect its axis, and whenever Kaiden compressed space into a killing point, Max could unfold it before it turned fatal. Even if Kaiden had somehow landed a strike, the Dimensional Sovereign Body would have kept the spatial force from truly injuring him.","This was not a battle between equals walking the same path. It was a senior pathwalker meeting someone who had traveled deeper into the inheritance than he ever had.","Kaiden looked at Max for a long moment, and then he smiled faintly.","\"I understand now.\"","Max lowered his hand. Kaiden glanced at the space surrounding Max, and then at Max himself.","\"No wonder master chose you.\"","The words sent another wave of shock through the arena. Master chose you. To everyone else, that sentence could carry countless meanings, but to Max and Kaiden it carried only one. The person behind the Void Genesis Art had not passed it to Max by accident."]},{"number":1871,"title":"Chapter 1871: Divine Son vs Rakan!","paragraphs":["Kaiden drew a slow breath and lowered his hands.","\"I surrender.\"","The arena went silent once more. Angelina Valerius regarded Kaiden for a breath, and then she announced calmly, \"Kaiden Voidmere has surrendered.\"","[Winner: Max Morgan.]","[Kaiden Voidmere Defeated.]","The screen above the stage updated.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Max Morgan]","[Total Battles Fought: 18]","[Total Wins: 18]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Kaiden Voidmere]","[Total Battles Fought: 18]","[Total Wins: 17]","The result shone above the arena. Kaiden Voidmere, the supreme genius of the Grand Void Sanctum, had lost. He had not lost because he was weak, nor because his Void Genesis Art was flawed.","He had lost because Max Morgan’s mastery stood higher, and because Max’s body rendered space itself nearly incapable of harming him.","At the Black Dragon Clan, the disciples erupted into wild cheers yet again. At the Grand Void Sanctum, the atmosphere stayed silent and complicated. Some disciples looked unwilling to accept it, but the elders said nothing at all.","They had seen the truth with perfect clarity. Kaiden had not surrendered out of cowardice. He had surrendered because he understood the gap more deeply than anyone watching from outside.","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, Kaiden stood across from Max and bowed his head slightly. It was not the bow of a defeated man surrendering his dignity. It was the acknowledgment of someone who had glimpsed a higher level of his own path.","\"Junior brother,\" Kaiden said softly, \"walk far.\"","Max looked at him and nodded. \"I will.\"","The transfer light descended and carried Kaiden back to his pillar, and Max returned to his own a moment later.","The other participants watched him in silence. He had defeated Rakan in a contest of body strength, and he had forced Selene to surrender without ever fighting. Now he had defeated Kaiden Voidmere on the path of space itself.","After Max defeated Kaiden Voidmere, the atmosphere of the final competitive stage grew even heavier. Another undefeated name had fallen.","Kaiden’s defeat felt different from Rakan’s, different from Orion’s, and different from the loss Aurelian had suffered at Damian’s hands. He had not been overwhelmed by raw force, cut down by sword authority, or exhausted by a countering Pseudo Cosmic Path. He had lost on the very path he took the most pride in.","The Void Genesis Art had been matched against the Void Genesis Art, and Max had displayed higher mastery and deeper authority. On top of that, his body had rendered spatial attacks nearly meaningless.","The Grand Void Sanctum fell into thoughtful silence, while the Black Dragon Clan erupted yet again.","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, Max returned to his pillar calmly, and Kaiden sat down with a faint smile resting on his face. His loss had not crushed him. Instead, it seemed to have answered a question he had carried in his heart, and after acknowledging Max as someone chosen by the same master, his expression had grown much lighter than before.","Angelina Valerius waited until the screen finished updating the records, and then she raised her hand once more.","\"The next battle will now begin.\"","The giant screen above the arena began to rotate. At this stage of the tournament, every single name carried weight. Most participants had already fought eighteen or nineteen battles. The weaker among them had long dropped out of the upper race, while the true monsters kept carving out their positions through victories and rare defeats.","One loss could reshape the top five, and one major victory could restore a damaged reputation. A single bad matchup could ruin everything.","The names flashed past, among them Max Morgan, Damian Voss, Revona, Ervin, Aurelian Lareth, Rakan Thorne, Orion Starfall, Morgana Starveil, Rosaline Lunara, and Kaiden Voidmere.","The light slowed, and the first name stopped.","[Rakan Thorne]","Across the Divine Realm, the War God Palace disciples snapped to attention at once. Rakan had already suffered one crushing defeat against Max, but since then he had won battle after battle with fierce dominance.","He remained one of the strongest body cultivators in the conference, and most participants below the absolute peak still could not withstand even his First or Second Limit. His record remained excellent, and his fighting spirit had not dimmed in the least.","The second name kept spinning and then slowed further. Aurelian Lareth’s golden eyes narrowed.","The name stopped.","[Aurelian Lareth]","The screen enlarged both names.","[Final Competitive Stage]","[Rakan Thorne vs Aurelian Lareth]","The arena erupted immediately, for this was another major battle. Rakan Thorne, the first Warlord of the War God Palace, would face Aurelian Lareth, the Divine Son of the second elven faction. One of them represented the extreme of physical body cultivation and close combat war power.","The other represented divine light, royal bloodline authority, and long-range Heavenly Luminance suppression. Both men had already lost to someone at the peak, yet both remained terrifying enough to dominate nearly everyone beneath that level.","On his pillar, Rakan cracked his neck and grinned. \"So I finally get the shining prince.\"","Aurelian looked at him coldly. \"You should worry less about my title and more about whether your fists can reach me.\"","Rakan’s grin widened. \"If they reach you once, you will understand why people respect the War God Palace.\"","Aurelian’s expression did not change. \"Then try.\"","The War God Palace disciples began to roar.","\"Rakan!\"","\"First Warlord!\"","\"Crush the Divine Son!\"","\"Break through that light!\"","Inside the viewing halls of the second elven faction, the atmosphere ran colder but burned no less intensely. Aurelian had already lost to Damian, and the humiliation of that defeat had not faded. If he lost again to Rakan, his standing in the eyes of the Divine Realm would sink even further.","Several elders stared at the screen with sharp eyes.","\"The Divine Son cannot lose this.\"","\"Rakan’s close combat is frightening, but he has a clear weakness.\"","\"He must be kept away.\"","\"His fists are only meaningful if they reach the target.\"","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, Max watched the stage calmly. This battle would be a clash of styles. If Rakan dragged Aurelian into close combat, Aurelian would suffer, because even with the Crownless Divine King he would not want to trade blows against Rakan’s Third Limit for long.","But if Aurelian held his distance and used the Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion to suppress the battlefield, then Rakan would have to fight through layers of divine light before he could ever land a clean hit.","Angelina looked toward both participants. \"Rakan Thorne. Aurelian Lareth. Enter the stage.\"","Two beams of light descended. Rakan landed heavily on one side of the central stage, and the stone beneath his feet cracked slightly under the weight of his body. Aurelian appeared opposite him with golden-white light flowing around him like a sacred robe.","Compared to Rakan’s violent war aura, Aurelian’s presence felt colder, brighter, and more distant, like a divine sun hanging high above a battlefield.","Angelina raised her hand.","[Battle Begins.]","Rakan moved first. He did not hesitate, and he wasted no time on slow probing. The instant the battle began, the bronze markings on his arms lit up.","\"War God Body, First Limit, War Blood Awakening.\"","His blood roared like war drums.","Boom!","The stage shattered beneath his feet as he charged. In a single instant he crossed half the distance to Aurelian with his fist drawn back and battle intent blazing in his eyes."]},{"number":1872,"title":"Chapter 1872: Rakan Going All Out!","paragraphs":["Aurelian raised one hand.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Sacred Spear Rain.\"","Hundreds of golden-white spears formed in the air and rained down toward Rakan. Each spear carried divine light strong enough to punch through ordinary defenses, but Rakan did not slow.","He punched forward and the air burst apart, shattering dozens of spears before they could touch him. The remaining spears struck his body and left burning marks across his shoulders and arms, yet he pushed through them like a war beast breaking out of a storm.","Aurelian’s eyes narrowed slightly.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Sunwheel Descent.\"","A blazing golden wheel materialized above Rakan and dropped with crushing force. Rakan roared and punched upward to meet it.","\"War God Fist, Mountain-Breaking Drum.\"","His fist struck the sunwheel.","Boom!","The golden wheel cracked, but the impact forced Rakan’s charge to falter. That small pause was all Aurelian needed. He slid backward through radiant light and opened the distance between them once more.","Rakan clicked his tongue. \"Running already?\"","Aurelian replied coldly, \"Choosing distance is not running. It is understanding the battlefield.\"","He raised both hands.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Twelve Sacred Wings.\"","Twelve radiant wings spread open behind him, and countless feathers of light streaked toward Rakan from every direction. They did not simply aim for his body. They targeted his joints, his eyes, his throat, his knees, and his path of movement, forcing him to either block or waste precious time tearing through them.","Rakan’s grin vanished.","\"Second Limit.\"","The sound of divine metal being reforged rang out from his bones.","\"War Bone Reforging.\"","His body grew heavier and harder. He crossed his arms and bulled straight through the feather storm. Golden-white feathers exploded against his skin, carving shallow wounds and burning lines across his flesh, yet none of them managed to halt his advance.","Aurelian lifted one finger.","\"Divine Luminance Chain Edict.\"","Golden-white chains rose from the ground and dropped from the sky at the same time, coiling around Rakan’s arms, legs, waist, and neck. These were no ordinary bindings. They carried divine authority, and they sought to dull his physical power by suppressing the rhythm of war beating inside his body.","Rakan’s muscles tightened. \"Break!\"","The chains cracked, but before they fully shattered, Aurelian’s next attack was already falling.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Crowned Sun Judgment.\"","A crown of light appeared above the stage and unleashed a pillar of divine radiance directly onto Rakan. The attack caught him before he could completely tear free of the chains.","Boom!","Rakan was driven down to one knee.","The War God Palace disciples clenched their fists.","\"He is suppressing Rakan from a distance!\"","\"Break it!\"","\"First Warlord, break through!\"","On the stage, Rakan lowered his head for a moment, and then he laughed. \"Good. Annoying, but good.\"","His flesh began to rumble.","\"Third Limit.\"","The bronze markings across his body joined into a single pattern.","\"War Flesh Unbound.\"","Boom!","Rakan’s aura exploded upward. The Divine Luminance chains shattered, and the pillar of the Crowned Sun Judgment cracked apart from within. Rakan rose to his feet covered in blood and light burns, yet his battle intent had only grown more violent.","Aurelian’s face turned colder.","Rakan vanished from where he stood. With the Third Limit open, his speed was terrifying, and he appeared before Aurelian almost instantly with a punch driving toward his chest.","Aurelian’s pupils contracted.","\"Heavenly Luminance Battle Form, Divine Step.\"","He darted backward, but Rakan’s fist still grazed past his shoulder.","Boom!","The passing force alone tore through Aurelian’s radiant armor and sent him sliding several meters across the stage.","The entire arena shook with excitement.","\"He touched him!\"","\"Rakan almost landed a clean blow!\"","\"If that punch had connected properly, Aurelian would be badly injured!\"","Aurelian glanced at his torn shoulder armor, and his expression turned ugly.","Rakan grinned. \"You see? Distance is useful only until I cross it.\"","Aurelian’s golden-white light flared brighter. \"You are right.\"","He raised his hand toward the sky. \"That is why I will not let you cross it again.\"","Behind him, sacred halls, radiant pillars, a golden throne, and an endless sun took shape, and his Pseudo Cosmic Path descended with overwhelming pressure.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path, Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion.\"","Boom!","The entire stage was swallowed in divine light. Rakan’s body sank slightly beneath the pressure, but he refused to retreat. Instead he laughed loudly and clenched his fists.","\"Good. Use everything.\"","Aurelian’s eyes were cold.","\"Divine Dominion, Luminance Decree.\"","A golden-white decree unfurled above the stage and released countless sacred words that pressed down on Rakan. They slowed his blood, weakened his war rhythm, and smothered the explosive force of his three opened limits.","Rakan punched forward.","\"War God Fist, Battlefield Collapse.\"","His fist shattered dozens of radiant words, but more kept descending. He tried to charge, only to find the ground beneath him covered in sacred lines that locked onto his feet.","Aurelian raised his other hand.","\"Divine Dominion, Twelve Pillars of Sacred Judgment.\"","Twelve radiant pillars surrounded Rakan and fired golden-white beams from every direction. Rakan crossed his arms and weathered the first wave. Then he roared and slammed his foot down, cracking the stage beneath him.","He forced his way forward through the beams, but every step drained more of his strength. The Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion empowered Aurelian while it weakened Rakan, and it turned the entire battlefield hostile toward him. Even with the Third Limit open, closing the distance was no longer easy.","Aurelian gave him no room to breathe.","\"Divine Dominion, Royal Mandate of the Endless Sun.\"","The endless sun above the divine kingdom brightened, and golden-white light poured down onto Aurelian himself. His aura swelled, and every attack he made took on the weight of a divine execution.","Rakan fought his way through the Twelve Pillars of Sacred Judgment and finally reached striking range again.","\"War God Fist, Three-Limit Heaven Breaker!\"","His fist drew back as the power of War Blood Awakening, War Bone Reforging, and War Flesh Unbound gathered into one terrifying punch. The entire arena could feel that if this blow landed cleanly, even Aurelian’s sacred armor would break.","Aurelian’s expression turned sharp, but he did not block. He retreated upward instead.","\"Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion, Radiant Ascension Step.\"","His body rose into the air along a pillar of light, and Rakan’s fist tore through nothing but the space he had just abandoned. The punch detonated against the stage instead and shattered a massive portion of the battlefield.","Before Rakan could recover his stance, Aurelian struck from above.","\"Divine Dominion, Sacred Sun Spearfall.\"","Hundreds of massive divine spears formed around the endless sun and plunged down toward Rakan one after another. This was no longer the ordinary Sacred Spear Rain from the opening exchange. Every spear now carried the authority of a Pseudo Cosmic Path, and every one of them sought to pin Rakan to the stage before he could leap upward."]},{"number":1873,"title":"Chapter 1873: Divine Son Previals!","paragraphs":["Rakan looked up and grinned fiercely. He punched, and one spear shattered. He punched again, and another broke apart. He charged through the falling divine spears and smashed them one after another, but their numbers were simply too great. His body began collecting wounds. Golden-white light pierced his shoulder, another spear grazed his ribs, and a third struck his thigh and made him stumble for half a breath.","Aurelian’s voice descended from above.","\"Crownless Divine King.\"","The golden throne behind him shattered into fragments of light that flowed into his body. His aura condensed sharply, and the Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion contracted into a smaller but far more oppressive form. The divine sun at his back became a burning crown, and countless runes gathered around his hands.","Rakan’s eyes widened slightly.","Aurelian pointed downward.","\"Crownless Divine King, Light That Judges All War.\"","The divine runes fell like a rain of judgment. Rakan roared and pushed his physical power to its absolute limit. His three limits burned as one, and his body resembled a bronze war statue drenched in blood. He charged upward into the falling light, straining to reach Aurelian before the long-range suppression could grind him down completely.","For several breaths, the battlefield became a violent collision between golden judgment and bronze war power. Rakan broke through one layer, then another, and then another after that.","The War God Palace disciples screamed his name.","\"Rakan!\"","\"Break through!\"","\"First Warlord!\"","\"Reach him!\"","And Rakan did reach the edge of Aurelian’s defensive range. His fist rose once more.","\"Three-Limit Heaven Breaker!\"","Aurelian’s eyes turned to ice.","\"Crownless Divine King, Final Luminance Judgment.\"","A massive divine sword of golden-white light took form above him and came crashing down before Rakan’s fist could fully release.","Boom!","The fist met the divine sword, and for a moment Rakan actually held the blade in place. His muscles bulged, blood burst from the wounds across his body, and the stage cracked further beneath him as he forced his fist upward against the Final Luminance Judgment, inch by grinding inch.","Aurelian’s face darkened.","Rakan laughed through gritted teeth. \"Your light is strong, prince, but not heavy enough.\"","Aurelian raised his other hand.","\"Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion, Solar Execution Array.\"","The entire divine kingdom behind him released hundreds of smaller golden-white blades. They did not strike at random. They arranged themselves into a circular array around Rakan and began cutting at him from the sides, from behind, and from above, all while the Final Luminance Judgment kept his strongest fist occupied.","Rakan wanted to move, but he could not. If he withdrew his fist, the divine sword would fall on him. If he kept resisting, the Solar Execution Array would carve him apart piece by piece. Golden-white blades struck his body one after another.","His back split open, his shoulder bled, and his arms began to tremble. Even the Third Limit of the War God Body could not shrug off so many attacks empowered by the Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion.","Max watched the fight with narrowed eyes. Aurelian’s choice was plain to see. He had no intention of meeting Rakan fairly in close combat. He was using distance, altitude, suppression, and layered long-range attacks to deny Rakan any chance at a decisive blow.","It was not cowardice. It was simply the correct strategy. Rakan was stronger up close, Aurelian was more dangerous at range, and Aurelian was making certain the battle never left his range.","On the stage, Rakan roared one final time. The bronze light around his body surged violently, and he shattered the Final Luminance Judgment with a single desperate punch.","Crack!","The massive divine sword broke apart, but before Rakan could follow through, Aurelian’s Solar Execution Array condensed into one final spear above him.","\"Crownless Divine King, Sun-Piercing Verdict.\"","The spear descended. Rakan tried to raise his arms, but his body had taken too much damage under the relentless suppression. The spear crashed into his crossed guard and hammered him down into the stage.","Boom!","The central stage caved inward, and dust, light, and broken stone rose in every direction. When the glare faded, Rakan knelt inside a crater with both arms trembling and blood covering most of his body.","His War God Body still burned, but its bronze light had turned unstable. He tried to rise, only for the Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion to press down on him again while several golden-white spears formed overhead, poised to fall if he continued.","Aurelian hovered in the air, breathing hard. His face was pale, and his aura no longer held steady. The fight against Rakan had clearly cost him a great deal, and if Rakan had reached him cleanly even once, the outcome might have been very different. But Rakan had not.","Angelina Valerius looked down at the stage. \"Rakan Thorne is unable to continue.\"","Rakan clenched his teeth, and for a moment it seemed he might force himself up regardless. Then he looked at the golden-white spears above him, glanced at Aurelian, and finally laughed with open bitterness.","\"Fine. I lose.\"","Angelina announced the result calmly.","[Winner: Aurelian Lareth.]","[Rakan Thorne Defeated.]","The screen above the arena updated immediately.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Aurelian Lareth]","[Total Battles Fought: 19]","[Total Wins: 18]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Rakan Thorne]","[Total Battles Fought: 19]","[Total Wins: 17]","The Divine Realm erupted in mixed reactions. The second elven faction finally released a wave of cheering after the suffocating gloom that had followed Aurelian’s loss to Damian.","Their Divine Son had defeated the first Warlord of the War God Palace. Even if the victory had come through range and suppression rather than direct confrontation, a victory was still a victory, and in a round-robin stage every win mattered.","At the War God Palace, the disciples seethed with frustration, yet none of them could claim Rakan had fought poorly. He had charged through the Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion, shattered countless divine spears, and broken the Final Luminance Judgment itself. He had nearly reached Aurelian more than once.","But Aurelian’s long-range attacks had been too layered, too constant, and too perfectly suited to denying Rakan the close combat battle he craved.","On the stage, Aurelian descended slowly, while Rakan struggled to his feet once the pressure lifted, his body already being stabilized by the laws of the Eternal Hourglass.","He looked at Aurelian and snorted. \"If I had landed one clean punch, you would not be standing so neatly.\"","Aurelian regarded him coldly. \"But you did not.\"","Rakan stared at him for a breath, and then he laughed. \"That is true.\"","Aurelian offered nothing further. The transfer light descended and carried both of them back to their pillars.","Max watched Aurelian quietly. This victory had restored a measure of the Divine Son’s pride, but it had also revealed something important.","Aurelian could defeat Rakan so long as he kept his distance, suppressed the battlefield, and stacked long-range divine attacks without permitting a single clean exchange up close. Yet if Rakan had ever reached him properly, even Aurelian would have been in danger. Aurelian was strong, but he was not without weakness.","After Aurelian Lareth and Rakan Thorne returned to their pillars, the final competitive stage pressed onward, and Angelina Valerius did not slow the rhythm of the tournament.","By this point, audiences throughout the Divine Realm had already witnessed too many shocking battles, and everyone understood that showing every remaining match in full would only drag the stage out endlessly.","The records were approaching their final stretch, and the important names had begun colliding with one another more frequently.","Some battles still carried real weight, some were decided almost instantly, and some merely confirmed what many had already guessed about the gulf between the upper monsters and the rest of the top twenty-five."]},{"number":1874,"title":"Chapter 1874: Ervin vs Orion!","paragraphs":["The next significant match paired Ervin against Orion Starfall.","The moment their names appeared together, the arena fell quiet once again. Orion had already fought one of the most exhausting battles of the final competitive stage against Revona, and although the laws of the Eternal Hourglass had stabilized his injuries, no one believed he had fully recovered.","His aura remained weaker than before, and his face still carried a trace of pallor. The star marks on his body no longer shone with the effortless brilliance they had displayed at the start of the final round.","Even so, when he stepped onto the stage, he was still smiling. It was the same bright and almost careless smile that made him look as though nothing in the world could truly spoil his mood.","His armor bore faint cracks from his previous battle, and the wounds beneath it had only recently closed, yet his eyes were clear. He looked across the stage at Ervin and laughed softly.","\"I really wanted an easier opponent after fighting Revona,\" Orion said.","Ervin stood opposite him with his black spear in hand, his expression as calm as ever. \"Then your luck is poor.\"","Orion sighed with exaggerated helplessness. \"Clearly.\"","A few spectators laughed, but the laughter faded quickly, because everyone understood this would be no light battle. Orion was the strongest genius of the Nine Star Court and the man who had forced Revona to use Return To Nothing.","Ervin was the mysterious spear genius whose Abyssal Origin Descent had swallowed Selene’s Heavenly Luminance Genesis and defeated Rosaline’s Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary. Both had already proven themselves among the true monsters of the final stage.","Angelina Valerius raised her hand.","[Battle Begins.]","Orion did not bother testing him. The instant the battle began, all nine star marks across his body lit up together. A vast starry sky opened behind him, and nine ancient stars descended one after another. They entered his hands, his spine, his heart, his bones, his blood, and his flesh, transforming his entire body into a living vessel of celestial power.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path, Nine Star Sovereign Body.\"","Boom!","A majestic star palace materialized behind Orion, ringed by nine immense stars and crowned with an empty throne of starlight. The pressure pouring from his body climbed sharply, and his smile grew brighter as he stepped forward.","\"I already learned not to waste time against monsters.\"","The moment his voice fell, Orion vanished. He reappeared before Ervin like a falling star, his fist wreathed in blazing stellar heat.","\"Nine Star Sovereign Body, First Star Fist.\"","Ervin raised his spear, and the fist crashed into the shaft.","Boom!","Starlight burst outward in a circular wave, and Ervin’s feet slid backward for the first time. Before he could fully steady himself, Orion changed stars. The heat in his fist vanished, and heavy dead-star pressure flowed into his shoulder instead.","\"Sixth Star Pressure Strike.\"","Orion’s shoulder slammed forward. Ervin shifted his spear and blocked again, but the pressure drove him back another two steps. The audience grew restless at once. Orion’s injuries had weakened him, yet with the Nine Star Sovereign Body active, he remained terrifying.","Every part of his body could become a different star weapon, and every movement changed the nature of his attack.","Orion stepped to the left.","\"Second Star Step.\"","His body shifted like a comet changing orbit. Ervin’s spear thrust toward the place Orion had just occupied, but Orion had already appeared at his right side. His elbow carried the sharpness of a meteor as it dropped toward Ervin’s ribs.","\"Third Star Elbow.\"","Ervin’s eyes sharpened, and his spear turned.","\"Abyss Spear Art, Hollow Moon Guard.\"","A crescent of dark spear force rose between them and caught the elbow, but Orion’s fourth star had already entered his leg. He abandoned the elbow strike halfway and lashed out with a kick of terrifying speed.","\"Fourth Star Crescent Kick.\"","The kick hammered the side of Ervin’s spear guard.","Bang!","Ervin was forced back yet again.","Across the Divine Realm, the Nine Star Court disciples roared with excitement.","\"Senior Brother Orion!\"","\"He is still suppressing Ervin!\"","\"Even after fighting Revona, he is still this strong!\"","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, Rakan Thorne grinned. \"That star bastard still has plenty left.\"","Kaiden Voidmere nodded faintly. \"His injuries are affecting him, but his control remains excellent.\"","Max watched quietly. Orion’s condition was clearly below its peak, yet his battle sense had not dulled at all.","He knew Ervin was dangerous, so he refused to give him the space to slowly open his abyssal path. He kept changing stars and shifting rhythm, forcing close exchanges before Ervin could drag the battlefield into his own pace.","On the stage, Orion’s assault grew fiercer.","\"Nine Star Sovereign Body, Seven-Star Revolving Impact.\"","Seven star forces rotated through his body within a single breath. His fists, elbows, knees, shoulders, and palms struck one after another, and each blow carried a different celestial property.","Heat, weight, sharpness, speed, pressure, burning blood, and crown-like suppression flowed through his attacks so quickly that most opponents would have been overwhelmed on the spot.","Ervin retreated six steps, then nine, and then twelve. For the first time since revealing his strength, he looked as though he had been pushed into a corner. Yet no panic touched his expression, and his abyss-like eyes stayed calm. At the thirteenth step, his foot stopped.","Orion’s fist descended again.","\"Ninth Star Crown Fist.\"","The crown-shaped starlight above his head flashed, and the fist fell with majestic pressure. It did not equal Starfall Extinction, but it still carried enough force to crush most defensive techniques.","This time, Ervin moved differently. His spear tip lowered, and the air beneath Orion’s fist sank.","\"Abyss Spear Art, Deep Current Reversal.\"","The star force in Orion’s fist suddenly tilted downward, as if an invisible current had seized it. His punch missed Ervin’s shoulder by a hair’s width and struck the stage instead.","Boom!","The stage caved in, and in the same instant, Ervin’s spear rose from below. Orion’s eyes widened slightly. He twisted his body in midair and blocked with his forearm, but the spear force still grazed his side and tore a wound across his armor. Blood splashed onto the stage."]},{"number":1875,"title":"Chapter 1875: Orion Giving His All!","paragraphs":["Orion landed several meters away and looked down at the wound. Then he smiled.","\"So you were waiting.\"","Ervin raised his spear calmly. \"You were too fast to interrupt carelessly.\"","Orion laughed. \"That is a compliment, right?\"","\"Yes.\"","The moment Ervin answered, the air around him changed. It sank, the light sank, and even the sound sank with it. The invisible pressure that had shocked everyone during his battle with Selene returned, spreading across the central stage like the arrival of a bottomless sea.","A black sea appeared behind Ervin, vast and silent and impossibly deep. From within that sea rose the broken ancient gate, half submerged and covered in mysterious symbols that no one could fully read. The moment it appeared, the nine stars inside Orion’s body flickered.","Ervin’s voice rang across the stage.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path, Abyssal Origin Descent.\"","Boom!","The battlefield transformed completely. The star palace behind Orion still shone brightly, but the black sea behind Ervin seemed to drag at its light. The nine stars within Orion’s body remained powerful, yet now every movement he made had to fight against the pressure of descent.","His star force did not vanish the way it had against Revona’s Void Origin Realm. Instead, it sank. It grew heavier, harder to circulate, harder to release, and harder to change quickly.","Orion felt the difference at once, and his smile dimmed slightly.","\"This path really is unpleasant.\"","Ervin replied calmly, \"Your stars shine too brightly.\"","Orion clenched his fists. \"Then try swallowing them.\"","He rushed forward again, and the battle grew grander than before. Orion’s Nine Star Sovereign Body erupted with its full brilliance as he pushed all nine stars to their limit. He no longer relied on quick changes alone. Instead, he began combining several stars at once.","His First Star burned through the abyssal pull while his Second Star accelerated his movement. His Sixth Star deepened his pressure, and his Ninth Star anchored his authority. He crossed the sinking battlefield like a star refusing to fall.","Ervin answered with his black spear.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, First Depth Tide.\"","The black sea surged, and a wave of abyssal pressure rose from the ground to swallow half the stage. Orion strode through it with his body glowing brighter, though his speed visibly slowed. Ervin’s spear lanced out from within the wave, silent and precise. Orion blocked with his fist.","Boom!","Starlight and abyssal force detonated against each other. Orion was pushed back three steps, while Ervin gave up only one.","Orion’s eyes lit up again. \"Good.\"","He gathered five stars into his arm.","\"Nine Star Sovereign Body, Five-Star Heaven Breaker.\"","His fist shot forward, and Ervin raised his spear to meet it.","\"Abyss Spear Art, Gate Shadow Thrust.\"","The thrust carried the shadow of the broken gate. It collided with Orion’s fist, and the five-star force shuddered violently. For a moment the star power seemed on the verge of piercing through, but the gate’s shadow dragged part of it downward and the attack lost its stability.","Orion gritted his teeth and changed once more, driving the Ninth Star into his fist at the final moment.","Boom!","The unstable attack exploded, and both men were hurled backward.","Orion landed with one knee briefly touching the ground while blood ran from his lips. His old injuries had torn open again. Starlight leaked from the cracks in his armor, and the nine stars within his body flickered unsteadily. Even so, his smile returned brighter than before.","Ervin’s sleeve had been shredded, and a wound ran across his left shoulder. He regarded Orion with rare seriousness.","\"You are injured more than you show.\"","Orion rose slowly. \"And you are stronger than you look.\"","The audience was completely absorbed. No one dared call this an easy victory for either side. Orion was weakened, yet he was still forcing Ervin to fight in earnest.","Ervin’s Abyssal Origin Descent was terrifying, yet Orion’s Nine Star Sovereign Body refused to sink without a fight.","The black sea rose again, and the nine stars blazed in answer. Through the next several exchanges, the entire stage looked like a starry heaven straining to escape a bottomless abyss. Orion’s punches birthed brilliant starbursts while Ervin’s spear carved dark lines through the battlefield.","Each time Orion gathered his power, the broken gate pulled at it, and each time Ervin tried to bury the stars, Orion shifted his star force and erupted from a different angle.","At last, Orion stepped back. His breathing had turned rough, and blood ran down his chin once more. Yet his eyes shone with the same reckless brilliance he had shown against Revona.","\"I suppose I only have one move left that can trouble you.\"","Ervin’s grip tightened around his spear. \"Starfall Extinction.\"","Orion smiled. \"You saw it.\"","\"I did.\"","\"Then defend well.\"","The moment Orion spoke, the nine stars inside his body went still, and then they began to collapse inward. A terrible pressure radiated from his fist as the star palace behind him reappeared in a broken and desperate form.","The nine stars surrounding the palace shattered into streams of pure star essence and rushed into his arm. His body shook violently, several wounds reopened at once, and blood dripped onto the stage beneath his feet.","The Nine Star Court disciples fell silent. They knew what this technique had cost him against Revona, and now he was using it again while nowhere near fully recovered.","Orion’s smile did not waver.","\"This technique is still incomplete,\" he said. \"But if I wait until it is perfect, I will never know how far it can go.\"","The star essence compressed around his fist.","\"Starfall Extinction.\"","Orion vanished. He appeared before Ervin with his final fist already falling. The compressed star essence roared within that strike, layered and collapsing, with each layer built to erupt the moment the one before it was swallowed or broken.","This was the technique Orion had forged himself, the move that had driven Revona to use Return To Nothing. Even in his weakened state, it carried shocking destructive force."]},{"number":1876,"title":"Chapter 1876: Revona vs Rakan!","paragraphs":["Ervin’s Abyssal Origin Descent responded instantly. The black sea rose higher than it ever had, and the broken gate behind him began to open. It did not open slightly. It opened far wider than before. A soundless pressure spilled out from behind the gate, and for one brief instant, several of the top geniuses felt their hearts tighten.","Max’s eyes narrowed.","’That gate again.’","Ervin’s voice remained calm, but his aura had clearly grown heavier.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, Return To Depth.\"","The broken gate pulled, and Orion’s Starfall Extinction struck its edge.","Boom!","The star force exploded, but instead of spreading outward, it was dragged inward by the abyssal gate. The first layer of Starfall Extinction collapsed while still resisting. The second layer erupted and tore a crack across the gate’s shadow. The third layer burned like a dying star and forced Ervin back half a step.","Ervin’s expression shifted slightly. Orion roared and drove his fist deeper, and the star force pressed onward. For a moment it seemed that Starfall Extinction might pierce through the gate’s pull, but Orion’s body was no longer in peak condition.","The brilliance in his fist flickered and his arm trembled. The star essence within his body began breaking apart before the technique could reach its full eruption.","Ervin stepped forward as the black sea surged.","\"Endless Depth.\"","The broken gate swallowed. The remaining layers of Starfall Extinction sank one by one into the abyssal opening, their light dimming like a star falling beneath an endless sea.","Orion tried to force out one final burst, but his body could no longer sustain it, and the last star layer collapsed before it could fully detonate.","The gate closed partway, and the starlight vanished.","Orion stood before Ervin with his fist still extended and blood dripping from his arm. For a moment, neither of them moved. Then Orion sighed.","\"Again... not enough.\"","His body swayed. Ervin’s spear came to rest before his throat, but he did not thrust. Orion looked at the spear tip and laughed softly.","\"I surrender before I faint standing.\"","Angelina Valerius raised her hand.","[Winner: Ervin.]","[Orion Starfall Defeated.]","The arena stayed silent for a few breaths before the Nine Star Court disciples began cheering once more. They cheered not because Orion had won, but because he had fought with everything he had left.","Even wounded, exhausted, and far from his peak, he had forced Ervin to open the broken gate wider and use Return To Depth in earnest. That alone was enough to prove his strength all over again.","Ervin withdrew his spear. \"You would have been more dangerous at full strength.\"","Orion smiled tiredly. \"I will take that as comfort.\"","Ervin nodded. \"It was meant as one.\"","The transfer light descended and carried both of them back to their pillars. Orion sat down the moment he returned, laughing weakly to himself as the Eternal Hourglass began healing his injuries once again.","Ervin remained standing, though his gaze lingered on Orion a moment longer than usual. The battle had not been easy, and everyone who understood the clash could see it plainly.","Orion had lost, but he had not fallen cheaply. And Ervin’s Abyssal Origin Descent had once again proven itself one of the most mysterious and dangerous Pseudo Cosmic Paths in the entire final stage.","[Winner: Ervin.]","[Orion Starfall Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Ervin]","[Total Battles Fought: 20]","[Total Wins: 20]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Orion Starfall]","[Total Battles Fought: 20]","[Total Wins: 18]","The result drew sighs from many watchers. Orion was incredibly strong, and almost no one doubted that he belonged among the peak geniuses of the conference. Yet his repeated clashes against monsters like Revona and Ervin had left him in a punishing position.","His strength was real, his Pseudo Cosmic Path was majestic, and his self-created technique had shocked the Divine Realm. Even so, in this final stage, brilliance alone could still lose to a worse matchup.","The next major match arrived quickly.","[Damian Voss vs Morgana Starveil]","Morgana entered the arena wearing a bitter smile, fully aware that this was not a favorable fight. Her Star-Curse Labyrinth was extremely dangerous against most opponents, but Damian’s Sword Sovereign Heaven had already proven it could cut through the structure behind powerful Pseudo Cosmic Paths. She still fought with everything she had.","The Star-Curse Labyrinth opened, curse mirrors filled the stage, and countless witch symbols strained to twist Damian’s direction, his senses, and his sword rhythm.","Damian did not rush. He raised his sword and used \"Sword Sovereign Heaven, First Edict, All Blades Refuse Submission,\" then followed with \"Sword Sovereign Heaven, Third Edict, Blade Meets The Moonless Curse.\"","His blade carved through the curse mirrors one by one. When Morgana attempted to activate \"Star-Curse Labyrinth, Nameless Witch Burial,\" Damian answered with \"Sword Sovereign Heaven, One Sword Divides Heaven\" and split the burial curse before it could close around him.","Morgana surrendered with a sigh, though no shame showed on her face.","[Winner: Damian Voss.]","[Morgana Starveil Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Damian Voss]","[Total Battles Fought: 20]","[Total Wins: 20]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Morgana Starveil]","[Total Battles Fought: 20]","[Total Wins: 15]","\"Of course he won,\" Rakan muttered from his pillar, though his eyes stayed sharp.","Morgana returned to her pillar and looked at Damian with a smile that was half amused and half weary. \"Swordsmen are really unpleasant opponents.\"","Damian only nodded slightly, his expression as calm as ever.","Then another match seized everyone’s attention.","[Revona vs Rakan Thorne]","The moment those two names appeared together, the arena went quiet again, for this was no simple matchup.","Rakan Thorne possessed terrifying physical strength, and against most energy-based geniuses his War God Body was a walking nightmare. He could charge through attacks, break defensive formations with his bare fists, and drag opponents into close combat where very few could survive him.","Revona, however, was no ordinary long-range or energy-based fighter. Her Void Origin Eyes did more than block attacks. They erased force, nullified the structures of techniques, and dismantled the foundation of an enemy’s power before it ever fully reached her."]},{"number":1877,"title":"Chapter 1877: Max vs Divine Son!","paragraphs":["When the battle began, Rakan opened the First Limit of the War God Body at once and charged with brutal speed. Revona erased the pressure surrounding his first punch, but Rakan’s physical body kept coming regardless.","The fist did not fully vanish, because the body behind it remained real, heavy, and terrifying. The blow forced Revona to retreat for the first time, and many spectators immediately understood that Rakan truly was a dangerous opponent for her.","Rakan laughed and opened the Second Limit. His bones roared like divine metal, and his charge became even harder to stop.","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes erased the outer force of his punches, yet every strike still carried enough physical momentum to shake the space around her. Again and again Rakan forced his way closer, smashing through layers of void ripples with the stubbornness of a war beast that refused to stop moving.","But Revona stayed calm. She did not panic, and she did not spend her power recklessly. Instead, she studied the rhythm of Rakan’s body. She watched the moment his blood surged, the instant his bones locked, and the brief pause between one explosive step and the next.","Her Void Origin Eyes made no attempt to erase him whole. They targeted the most critical points of his physical release, weakening the link between his movement and the war power bursting out of his body.","Rakan opened the Third Limit with a roar.","\"War God Body, Third Limit, War Flesh Unbound.\"","His aura exploded, and the entire stage shook beneath him. For several breaths he truly seemed capable of smashing through everything. He drove Revona backward through sheer pressure, forcing her to weave movement and nullification together.","One of his punches nearly reached her shoulder, and its passing force tore a line through her sleeve and drew blood from her arm. The War God Palace disciples roared wildly, convinced that Rakan was about to overwhelm her.","Then Revona finally opened her Pseudo Cosmic Path.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path, Void Origin Realm.\"","The world behind her turned hollow. There was no sky, no ground, no sound, and no color. There was only origin-level emptiness.","The moment the Void Origin Realm spread, Rakan’s charge slowed. His War God Body still burned fiercely, but the force released by each step began disappearing before it could fully gather.","His fists remained dangerous, yet the explosive pressure around them was stripped away layer by layer. He tried to break through with \"Three-Limit Heaven Breaker,\" but Revona condensed the Void Origin Realm around his fist and hollowed out most of its force before the punch could land.","Even then, the battle was far from easy. Rakan was simply too strong to fall to ordinary nullification. He kept advancing beneath the Void Origin Realm even as his body bled and his aura flickered, and he laughed as he threw punch after punch, forcing Revona to retreat several times.","At one point he shattered a section of her void field through raw physical momentum and very nearly reached her true body.","But nearly was not enough.","Revona’s eyes shone with terrifying clarity.","\"Void Origin Realm, Return To Nothing.\"","The hollow world condensed into a single point before Rakan’s strongest punch, and his fist crashed into it.","For one brief moment, the War God Palace disciples believed he would break through. The bronze force of the War God Body roared violently as the Third Limit poured everything into that single strike.","But Return To Nothing did not try to withstand the punch the way a normal defense would. It folded the power inward, erased the gathered force, and returned the released war pressure to nothingness before any of it could touch her body.","Rakan’s fist stopped inches from her chest, and his eyes widened slightly.","Then Revona moved. A void ripple struck his chest, not to destroy his body directly, but to erase what remained of the War God Body’s released balance. Rakan’s bronze aura flickered wildly, and his knees sank into the cracked stage.","He tried to rise again, but his three limits had already been drained too far, and the Void Origin Realm pressed down around him like an invisible hollow sea.","For the first time, Rakan stopped smiling. Then he laughed bitterly.","\"Fine. I lose.\"","[Winner: Revona.]","[Rakan Thorne Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Revona]","[Total Battles Fought: 20]","[Total Wins: 20]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Rakan Thorne]","[Total Battles Fought: 20]","[Total Wins: 18]","The result set off another wave of discussion across the Divine Realm. Revona had defeated Orion in a battle that pushed her to the very edge, and now she had beaten Rakan despite his terrifying War God Body. It proved once again that she was no mere counter to long-range fighters.","She stood among the strongest geniuses of the entire final stage, and her Void Origin Eyes and Void Origin Realm could adapt even against close combat monsters.","Rakan returned to his pillar with a helpless grin, while Revona sat down quietly upon reaching hers. Her aura wavered unsteadily, and it was obvious that defeating Rakan had cost her dearly, but a victory was a victory. Her undefeated record remained intact.","The records kept shifting. The upper rankings were growing clearer, yet the final order had still not been decided.","Then Angelina Valerius raised her hand once more, and the giant screen above the arena began to spin. The names flashed rapidly past, and yet nearly everyone in the arena felt an invisible pressure before the result even appeared.","Among the rotating names were Max Morgan, Damian Voss, Aurelian Lareth, Ervin, Kaiden Voidmere, Rakan Thorne, Revona, Orion Starfall, Selene Vaeloria, and Rosaline Lunara.","The light slowed, and the first name stopped.","[Max Morgan]","The entire arena went silent. Then the second name continued spinning. It passed over Damian, over Ervin, over Kaiden, and over Rakan.","Then it stopped.","[Aurelian Lareth]","For one breath, not a single sound could be heard. Then the screen enlarged both names.","[Final Competitive Stage]","[Max Morgan vs Aurelian Lareth]","Angelina Valerius looked toward the two pillars and announced calmly.","\"Max Morgan. Aurelian Lareth. Enter the stage.\""]},{"number":1878,"title":"Chapter 1878: Same Attacks!","paragraphs":["Two beams of light descended from above the arena. One fell upon Max Morgan’s pillar, and the other fell upon Aurelian Lareth’s.","The moment both lights touched them, the entire Divine Realm seemed to grow still. This was not like Max’s battle against Rakan, where everyone had wondered whether his body could challenge the first Warlord of the War God Palace.","It was not like his battle against Kaiden, where the mystery of the Void Genesis Art had captured the attention of every space cultivator. This battle carried something much colder, much deeper, and far more personal.","Max Morgan stood against Aurelian Lareth. The black dragon genius faced the Divine Son of the second elven faction. The one who had risen like a monster through every stage of the Cosmic Ascension Conference now stood opposite the one who carried golden-white divine light and the prestige of a royal elven faction upon his shoulders.","Max appeared on one side of the central stage with his white hair falling around his face and his expression calm and unreadable.","No Emotion Severing Path appeared, and no Divine King Punishment rumbled above him. No dragon scales covered his skin, and no Draconic Essences roared through his body.","He looked almost ordinary compared to the terrifying pressure he had shown against Rakan and Kaiden, yet no one in the arena dared believe anymore that his calmness meant weakness.","Aurelian appeared opposite him. Golden-white light flowed around the Divine Son like a sacred robe. His pale golden hair drifted gently behind him, and his eyes shone with the cold pride of a man raised to stand above others.","Even after his loss to Damian Voss, his bearing remained noble, arrogant, and sharp. The Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline within him stirred faintly, and the moment it did, Max felt something inside his own body answer.","Aurelian felt it too, and his gaze turned colder.","Neither of them needed to speak the truth aloud. Aurelian already knew what he carried, for he had always known. He knew the source of his Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline had once belonged to Max, and he knew that Max had uncovered that truth.","That was why the tension between them had never been simple hatred. It was a silent war over ownership, over identity, and over the right to stand beneath the name of divine light.","By now, Max’s own Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline had almost fully reawakened. The wounds left behind by the theft had healed enough that his light could circulate through his body with stability and brilliance once more.","His Dimension of Light had also grown stronger, rendering most light-based attacks meaningless against him. Yet one thing was still missing. The source itself remained inside Aurelian, and only by reclaiming it could Max’s bloodline truly return to completeness and evolve toward its real peak as a true Divine Bloodline.","Across the stage, Aurelian regarded him with a faint, cold smile.","\"So it finally came to this.\"","Max looked at him calmly. \"Yes.\"","Aurelian’s smile deepened, and there was no ignorance in it. There was only arrogance, defiance, and a frigid refusal to bow his head before the original owner of the power he carried.","\"You have been waiting for this battle for a long time,\" Aurelian said.","Max’s eyes stayed calm. \"So have you.\"","Aurelian’s golden-white light burned brighter. \"Do not think that knowing the origin of something means you can take it back.\"","Max looked at the light surrounding him, and for a moment his expression turned cold enough to make even the air above the stage feel heavier.","\"It feels strange,\" Max said quietly.","Aurelian narrowed his eyes. \"What does?\"","Max raised one hand and watched a faint golden-white glow bloom in his palm. \"Feeling something inside me answer from across the stage.\"","The words were vague enough that the crowd could not grasp their true meaning.","To most spectators, it sounded like a mysterious resonance between two similar light-based powers. But Aurelian understood exactly what Max meant, and because he understood, his expression grew colder still.","\"You speak as though bloodline alone decides ownership,\" Aurelian said. \"Power belongs to the one who can wield it.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"Then prove that it listens to you.\"","Aurelian’s eyes sharpened. For the first time, a trace of anger surfaced beneath his noble expression. It was not because Max had exposed the truth. It was because Max had touched the one fear Aurelian never allowed himself to admit.","What if the stolen power had never truly accepted him? What if it obeyed only because the original owner had been absent? And what if, now that Max stood before him, the bloodline inside his body remembered?","Aurelian slowly raised one hand as golden-white light gathered in his palm.","\"Then watch carefully,\" he said coldly. \"I will show you who stands above this light now.\"","Angelina Valerius raised her hand.","[Battle Begins.]","Aurelian attacked instantly.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Sacred Spear Rain.\"","Hundreds of golden-white spears formed in the air and plunged toward Max like divine punishment.","Each spear carried brilliant sacred power, sharp enough to pierce defensive barriers and pure enough to burn away darkness, curses, and corrupted energy. Against most opponents, an opening like this would force an immediate defense.","Max did not move. He only raised his hand, and golden-white light gathered around his fingers.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Sacred Spear Rain.\"","The same attack materialized above Max. Hundreds of golden-white spears took shape in the air, nearly identical in structure, rhythm, and radiance to the ones Aurelian had summoned.","The only difference was that Max’s light felt quieter and purer. It was less domineering and less forced, and somehow it felt more natural.","The two spear rains collided in midair.","Boom!","Golden-white light exploded across the stage, and countless fragments of sacred radiance scattered like broken stars.","The arena froze.","\"He used the same technique?\"","\"That was Heavenly Luminance!\"","\"Max Morgan can use Heavenly Luminance power too?\"","\"How is that possible?\"","Aurelian stared at Max, and his expression shifted for the first time.","Max lowered his hand calmly. \"Surprised?\"","Aurelian’s golden eyes went colder. \"You copied my technique?\"","Max shook his head. \"No.\"","He raised his hand again.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Sunwheel Descent.\"","A golden-white sunwheel blazed into existence above Max and spun toward Aurelian with terrifying speed.","Aurelian’s face hardened, and he summoned his own wheel at once.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Sunwheel Descent.\"","The two wheels crashed together, and the impact rocked the stage. Both sunwheels shattered in the same instant.","Aurelian stepped back half a pace, not because he had truly been hurt, but because the shock in his heart had disturbed his rhythm. He could accept that Max was strong. He could accept Max wielding strange sword paths, dragon power, dimensional ability, and even the Void Genesis Art.","But watching Max command Heavenly Luminance techniques with such natural control struck at something far more fragile inside him. That light was supposed to be his symbol. It was his status, and it was his proof that he was the Divine Son.","Max watched him quietly. \"Try something stronger.\"","Aurelian’s face darkened.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Twelve Sacred Wings.\"","Twelve golden-white wings unfurled behind him, and countless feathers of light streaked toward Max from every direction, filling the stage with radiant blades. The attack was fast, dense, and oppressive, and every feather carried cutting force, burning heat, and purification power together."]},{"number":1879,"title":"Chapter 1879: What can a thief do with stolen light?","paragraphs":["Max stood still, and the feathers reached him. Or rather, they reached him and dissolved. The golden-white blades touched his body, but the light within them seemed to sink into an unseen luminous dimension surrounding him.","They could not pierce his skin, they could not burn his flesh, and they could not so much as disturb his breathing. They faded harmlessly away, as though returning to the place they had come from.","Aurelian’s eyes widened slightly.","Max watched the vanishing feathers and said calmly, \"Too light.\"","Aurelian’s face turned ugly, and the Divine Realm erupted in disbelief.","\"His attacks are not hurting Max!\"","\"He is not even defending!\"","\"The Twelve Sacred Wings vanished the moment they touched him!\"","\"What kind of light resistance is that?\"","Max took one step forward as golden-white radiance climbed around his body. He lifted his hand, and twelve wings of light opened behind him as well.","Compared to Aurelian’s wings, Max’s looked less ornamental and less royal, yet far more intimate with the essence of light itself. They did not resemble the decoration of a throne. They looked like something born directly from a living source.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Twelve Sacred Wings.\"","The feathers shot forward, and Aurelian raised his hand quickly.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Sacred Mirror Guard.\"","A golden-white mirror formed in front of him, and Max’s feathers struck it.","Crack!","The mirror split apart. Aurelian swept his arm and scattered the remaining feathers with a wave of divine light, but his expression had grown far colder than before.","He could no longer ignore what was happening. Max was not merely imitating the outer form of his techniques. He was wielding the Heavenly Luminance power with frightening compatibility.","Max looked at him and asked, \"Does it bother you?\"","Aurelian clenched his jaw. \"What?\"","\"That when you look at me, the power inside you answers,\" Max said quietly.","The words remained vague enough for the audience to misread, but to Aurelian they felt like a blade sliding beneath his ribs.","Aurelian’s light erupted.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Crowned Sun Judgment.\"","A crown of sacred light appeared above the stage and released a massive golden-white pillar straight down at Max. This attack carried far greater power than everything before it, enough to crush weaker Pseudo Cosmic Paths if wielded properly.","Max looked up as the pillar descended, and he did not dodge. The Crowned Sun Judgment struck him head-on.","Boom!","The stage around Max shattered beneath the force of the blow. Golden-white light swallowed his figure whole, and the arena barrier flared brightly from the impact.","Aurelian stared into the pillar with cold eyes. Then the light faded, and Max still stood there, entirely unharmed. His clothes had not even been singed. A faint golden-white glow flowed around him for a moment before sinking back into his body like water returning to the sea.","Max raised his eyes toward Aurelian. \"Again.\"","The word was soft, yet it made Aurelian’s expression stiffen. For the first time, something close to disbelief entered the Divine Son’s eyes.","\"No.\"","Max tilted his head slightly. \"No?\"","Aurelian’s aura surged violently.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Royal Sun Spear.\"","A massive spear of divine light formed in his hand and shot toward Max’s chest. Max opened his palm, and the spear struck him and dissolved.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Divine Flame Burial.\"","Golden-white flames rose from beneath Max’s feet and swallowed him, and then the flames simply disappeared.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Sacred Sun Cage.\"","A cage of radiant light closed around Max, every bar burning with sealing power. Max walked straight through it, and the cage shattered without offering the slightest resistance.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Sun King’s Execution.\"","Aurelian shaped a giant blade of sacred light and swung it down with both hands. Max raised one finger, and the blade struck that finger and broke.","This time, the entire arena went completely silent.","Aurelian stared at Max’s finger, and then at Max’s face. His breathing had grown heavy.","Max lowered his hand slowly. \"Do you understand now?\"","Aurelian’s eyes turned cold and furious. \"Understand what?\"","Max stepped closer. The stage beneath his feet glowed faintly with golden-white light, but unlike Aurelian’s light, Max’s radiance made no attempt to dominate the battlefield. It simply existed, calm and absolute, as though the light around him felt no need to prove itself.","\"You are trying to use light attacks that was never truly yours.\" Max said smiling.","Aurelian’s face changed. The sentence still was not open enough for the crowd to grasp the full truth, but it struck Aurelian directly.","The power he carried, the power he had treated as proof of his divinity, was failing against Max again and again. His attacks held enough force to injure other peak geniuses, yet against Max they collapsed as though they had lost their reason to harm him.","Max continued, his voice pitched low enough that only Aurelian could hear him clearly through the surrounding explosions of light. \"Because what you carry came from me.\"","Aurelian’s pupils shrank. For one breath, all his arrogance cracked, and then it returned as fury.","\"Shut up.\"","Golden-white light erupted behind him. Sacred halls appeared and radiant pillars rose, and a golden throne manifested beneath an endless sun. The Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion descended with overwhelming majesty, spreading across the central stage like a divine kingdom declaring judgment upon the world.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path,\" Aurelian said coldly, his voice trembling with anger he could barely suppress. \"Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion.\"","Boom!","The dominion swallowed the battlefield. This time, Aurelian held nothing back. The sacred halls poured out endless light while the radiant pillars locked onto Max. The throne beneath the sun blazed with oppressive authority, and the golden-white crown above Aurelian’s head grew nearly solid.","\"Divine Dominion, Luminance Decree.\"","A sacred decree unfurled above Max and released countless words of divine judgment. Max stood beneath it as the words struck him, and they dissolved.","Aurelian’s expression twisted.","\"Divine Dominion, Twelve Pillars of Sacred Judgment.\"","Twelve radiant pillars encircled Max and fired beams of Heavenly Luminance empowered by the Pseudo Cosmic Path from every direction. The beams struck him and faded against his body, like sunlight vanishing into a deeper light. Max slowly walked forward through the barrage, and his voice stayed calm.","\"You are using my own bloodline’s light against me.\"","Aurelian’s face paled slightly.","\"Divine Dominion, Royal Mandate of the Endless Sun.\"","The endless sun above the divine kingdom flared brighter than it ever had. A massive pillar of golden-white authority came crashing down, pouring all of its judgment, purification, and suppression onto Max.","Max stopped walking. The light struck him in full, the ground around him cracked, and the barrier trembled. Yet Max remained standing.","The Dimension of Light within him opened in silence, and the Heavenly Luminance power straining to injure him was drawn into that inner dimension, where it was scattered, absorbed, and rendered harmless.","It was not that Aurelian’s attack was weak. Against almost anyone else, it would have been terrifying. Against Max, however, light itself held almost no meaning as a weapon unless it was used as an attack by someone who was way too stronger than him.","Max looked at Aurelian through the pillar of radiance, and Aurelian stared back. For the first time, true anxiety surfaced in the Divine Son’s eyes. He could not understand it, and he could not accept it.","His Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion had injured Morgana, suppressed Rakan at range, and fought Damian’s Sword Sovereign Heaven to the very limit. Yet against Max, it felt as though he were throwing water into the ocean.","Max stepped forward again, and the Royal Mandate shattered around him.","\"You relied on something that was never truly yours,\" Max said softly. \"You built status on it. You built pride on it. You built your path on it.\"","Aurelian’s lips tightened, and Max’s gaze grew colder.","\"But when the owner stands before you, what can a thief do with stolen light?\""]},{"number":1880,"title":"Chapter 1880: Take Care of It!","paragraphs":["Aurelian’s expression finally broke.","\"Shut up!\"","The golden throne behind him shattered, and its fragments flew into his body. His aura condensed sharply into something unstable and terrifying.","\"Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion, Crownless Divine King.\"","The divine kingdom contracted around him. The sacred halls vanished, the radiant pillars compressed, and the endless sun became a burning crown at his back. All the authority of the dominion merged into his flesh, his spear, and his bloodline.","This was the state he had used against Damian, the form that turned him into a living weapon of divine judgment.","Aurelian appeared before Max in an instant.","\"Crownless Divine King, Light That Judges All Blades.\"","A spear of condensed divine light lanced toward Max’s throat. Max did not draw Dragonheart. He raised his hand and caught the spear. The light exploded between his fingers, and then it simply disappeared.","Aurelian froze.","Max regarded him from a distance of only a few steps. \"You still do not understand.\"","He squeezed, and the spear shattered. Aurelian stumbled back in shock, and Max followed calmly.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Sacred Palm Seal.\"","Max’s palm struck Aurelian’s chest.","Boom!","Aurelian flew backward with golden-white blood spraying from his mouth, and he crashed into one of the remaining radiant pillars of his own dominion.","The audience erupted.","\"Max used Heavenly Luminance to injure him!\"","\"Aurelian’s light cannot hurt Max, but Max’s light can hurt him!\"","\"What is happening?\"","\"Is Max’s Heavenly Luminance stronger?\"","Aurelian struggled to his feet, and his eyes were no longer calm. The arrogance still lingered, but now it was tangled with confusion, fear, and disbelief.","Max kept walking toward him. \"You were proud of this power,\" he said quietly. \"But every time you use it, you only remind me of what I will take back.\"","Aurelian’s breath caught, because this time he understood the meaning completely, and his face drained of color. Max had not spoken loudly, and he had not exposed the truth for the world to hear.","The surrounding storm of golden-white light hid his words from most people, and the distortion of the dominion kept anyone else from hearing clearly. But Aurelian heard every word, and each one struck his mind harder than any fist.","Take back. That meant Max knew. Max knew what had been done, and he knew where the source remained. Max knew that the bloodline inside Aurelian had never truly been his.","Aurelian’s hands trembled, and he forced them still.","\"No,\" he whispered.","Max’s eyes were cold. \"Yes.\"","Aurelian roared and raised both hands.","\"Crownless Divine King, Final Luminance Judgment.\"","The enormous divine sword of golden-white light took shape above him. This was the same attack Damian had cut apart, but this time Aurelian poured far more desperation into it.","His bloodline burned and his dominion shook, and the endless sun behind him dimmed as every scrap of its remaining authority flowed into the blade.","The divine sword descended.","Max looked up as golden-white light rose around his own body. He did not use a Pseudo Cosmic Path, for he did not yet possess a perfected light-based path of his own.","But he had the Dimension of Light, he had his almost fully reawakened Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline, and he held authority over the very light Aurelian was wielding.","Max raised his palm.","\"Heavenly Luminance, First Dawn Reversal.\"","A quiet golden-white light spread from his hand. It did not clash violently against the Final Luminance Judgment. Instead, it seeped into the descending divine sword and disturbed the bloodline rhythm within it.","The massive blade shuddered. Its outer layer remained powerful, but its inner structure began to loosen, as though something inside it had recognized Max and ceased obeying Aurelian completely.","Aurelian’s eyes widened in horror. \"No...\"","Max’s palm closed, and the Final Luminance Judgment shattered from within. Fragments of divine light rained down around Max like broken glass. Aurelian stumbled backward as the Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion flickered violently behind him.","Then Max appeared in front of him, and this time his palm stopped mere inches from Aurelian’s chest.","Aurelian froze, and the golden-white light around him shook uncontrollably.","Max looked into his eyes and spoke in a voice meant for him alone.","\"Take care of my bloodline until then.\"","Aurelian’s face lost every trace of color. Max’s eyes remained calm, but the killing intent buried beneath that calm was so cold that Aurelian felt his very soul tighten.","\"It will not be long before I come for it.\"","Aurelian’s lips parted, but no words emerged. In that moment, he no longer resembled the proud Divine Son who had stood above countless geniuses.","He looked like a man who had suddenly realized that the throne beneath him had been built over a pit, and that the owner of the pit had finally returned.","Max did not strike his heart. He could have, and he wanted to. But Angelina Valerius hovered above the stage, and the laws of the Eternal Hourglass tracked every movement.","If Max tried to kill Aurelian here, or attempted to extract the stolen bloodline source in front of everyone, Angelina would intervene at once.","Max was certain of it. Even if he could resist her for a moment, the risk was not worth taking. This was not the place, and this was not the time. He would wait until he had the right moment, the right ground, and the certainty to reclaim what was his without losing everything else.","So he did not kill him. He only pressed two fingers against Aurelian’s chest.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Dawn Break.\"","Boom!","A controlled burst of golden-white light slammed into Aurelian’s body. His remaining dominion shattered, and the Crownless Divine King state collapsed.","Aurelian was hurled backward and crashed into the ground, rolling across the cracked stage before coming to rest near the edge of the arena. Golden-white blood stained his lips while his aura guttered weakly.","He tried to lift himself, but his hands shook too badly to hold him.","Max stood where he was, calm and untouched.","Aurelian looked up at him from the ground, and no arrogance remained in his eyes. There was only silence, only disbelief, and only a fear he tried and failed to hide.","Angelina Valerius looked down at the stage for a moment, and then she announced the result calmly.","\"Aurelian Lareth is unable to continue.\"","The screen above the arena changed.","[Winner: Max Morgan.]","[Aurelian Lareth Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Max Morgan]","[Total Battles Fought: 19]","[Total Wins: 19]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Aurelian Lareth]","[Total Battles Fought: 20]","[Total Wins: 18]","The result shone above everyone, and the Divine Realm stayed silent. Aurelian Lareth, the Divine Son of the second elven faction, had lost yet again. But this defeat was different from the one Damian had handed him.","Damian had cut down his dominion with the sword. Max had rendered the very light he relied upon useless.","The viewing halls of the second elven faction went deathly still. Elders stared at the screen with rigid faces, unable to comprehend how Max could wield Heavenly Luminance power so naturally, or why Aurelian’s strongest light-based attacks had failed to harm him at all.","At the Black Dragon Clan, the disciples exploded into thunderous cheers.","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, Damian Voss studied Max with narrowed eyes, and Kaiden Voidmere’s expression turned thoughtful. Ervin watched in silence while Revona’s Void Origin Eyes flickered faintly.","Rakan Thorne let out a low laugh, though even he kept his voice down.","Max stood on the stage and looked at Aurelian one final time. Aurelian, sprawled on the cracked ground, stared back at him. No words passed between them this time, because none were needed.","The transfer light descended and carried the defeated Divine Son back to his pillar, and a moment later, Max returned to his own.","The battle had ended, but for Aurelian Lareth, something far worse than defeat had just begun. He now understood that the power he had treated as his divine proof was no shelter at all. It was a debt, and Max Morgan had come to collect it."]},{"number":1881,"title":"Chapter 1881: Ervin vs Kaiden!","paragraphs":["After Max Morgan defeated Aurelian Lareth, the entire final competitive stage stayed silent for a long while.","It was not because the battle had been the most destructive one so far.","In terms of pure destruction, Orion’s Starfall Extinction against Revona had shaken the arena just as fiercely, and so had Damian’s Sword Sovereign Heaven against Aurelian’s Divine Dominion, along with Rakan’s physical collision against Aurelian’s long-range Heavenly Luminance suppression.","What set Max’s victory apart was the manner in which he had won.","He had not cut Aurelian’s light apart the way Damian had. He had not tried to overpower the Divine Son with brute force the way Rakan had attempted, and he had not erased the attacks the way Revona would have.","He had simply stood there and let the Heavenly Luminance power collapse around him, as though Aurelian’s divine light had no right to harm him at all.","Then he had used that very same light to break Aurelian’s dominion, shatter his pride, and leave him silent on the ground.","The spectators across the Divine Realm could not grasp the full truth, but they could feel the humiliation buried inside that defeat. Aurelian Lareth had lost far more than a battle.","The symbol he carried had been challenged, and the authority of the second elven faction’s Divine Son had been shaken before every major force watching the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","Aurelian sat on his pillar with his head lowered slightly. He did not speak, and he did not look at Max. The golden-white light around his body had gone quiet, almost suppressed, and even the faint crown-like glow that usually hovered above him had vanished.","The laws of the Eternal Hourglass mended his injuries, but they could not mend the fear Max had planted inside his heart.","On another pillar, Max stood calmly with his expression unchanged, and he did not spare Aurelian another glance. The battle had ended, and he had already said everything that needed saying.","For now, the stolen bloodline source would remain inside Aurelian, because the Eternal Hourglass, Angelina Valerius, and the eyes of countless great powers made reclaiming it here impossible.","But the debt had been marked, and the warning had been delivered. It would not be long.","Angelina Valerius waited until the arena’s atmosphere settled somewhat before raising her hand again.","\"The final competitive stage will continue.\"","The giant screen above the stage began to spin once more, and the participants forced themselves to recover their focus. Max’s victory over Aurelian had been shocking, but the round-robin stage was not yet finished. The top rankings remained unsettled, and several major battles still lay ahead.","Damian Voss stood undefeated, Revona stood undefeated, and Max stood undefeated as well. Ervin was the same as well.","Kaiden Voidmere had fallen to Max, yet no one dared underestimate him on the strength of that single result. In fact, after watching Max’s battle with Kaiden, many people had begun to suspect that Kaiden’s true power had never been fully displayed.","That suspicion took on far greater weight when the screen stopped again.","The first name appeared.","[Ervin]","The arena immediately grew quieter. Then the second name slowed and came to rest.","[Kaiden Voidmere]","For a moment, the spectators seemed to draw breath as one. The screen enlarged both names.","[Final Competitive Stage]","[Ervin vs Kaiden Voidmere]","A wave of excitement rolled through the Divine Realm, because this was another major battle. Ervin’s Abyssal Origin Descent had defeated Selene, Rosaline, and Orion.","His broken gate had swallowed Heavenly Luminance Genesis, Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary, and Starfall Extinction in turn. Every time he fought seriously, watchers felt as though they were staring into a bottomless abyss whose true depth remained hidden.","Kaiden Voidmere, however, was no ordinary opponent. Against Max, his brilliance had been eclipsed, because Max’s mastery of the Void Genesis Art surpassed his own and the Dimensional Sovereign Body rendered spatial attacks nearly meaningless.","That battle had made Kaiden appear suppressed, but anyone with real judgment understood the truth. Kaiden had not been weak. He had simply drawn the worst possible opponent, a man who walked the same path at a higher level and stood almost immune to the very element Kaiden relied upon.","Against Ervin, no such restriction existed. Kaiden could finally show the true terror of the Grand Void Sanctum.","Angelina Valerius looked toward both participants.","\"Ervin.\"","\"Kaiden Voidmere.\"","\"Enter the stage.\"","Two beams of light descended. Ervin appeared on one side of the central stage with his black spear resting calmly in his hand. His aura remained quiet, but after so many battles, no one mistook that quietness for weakness anymore.","It was the silence of something lying deep beneath the surface, something that had no need to roar because everything above it would eventually sink.","Kaiden appeared opposite him in silver-gray robes, his expression calm and thoughtful. Unlike the aftermath of his battle with Max, no trace of helplessness lingered in his eyes now.","He regarded Ervin with genuine seriousness, and the space around him began to ripple before the battle had even begun.","Ervin studied him calmly. \"You held back against Max.\"","Kaiden shook his head. \"No. I simply had no chance to show more against him.\"","Ervin’s eyes deepened slightly.","Kaiden continued, \"Against him, all my attacks were useless but not against you.\"","Ervin raised his spear. \"Then show me.\"","Kaiden’s silver-gray pupils shone. \"I will.\"","Angelina raised her hand.","[Battle Begins.]","Kaiden moved first.","\"Void Genesis Art, Empty Step.\"","His body vanished, and at almost the same instant, dozens of spatial ripples bloomed around Ervin. They were neither afterimages nor illusions.","Each ripple was a folded path that could deliver Kaiden’s attack from a different angle, and each one carried enough distortion to tear an ordinary defense apart.","Ervin’s spear moved.","\"Abyss Spear Art, Hollow Moon Guard.\"","A dark crescent took shape around him. Kaiden appeared above the crescent and pressed one palm downward.","\"Void Genesis Art, Space Burial Palm.\"","The space around Ervin sank like a collapsing tomb. The Hollow Moon Guard trembled and then cracked beneath the pressure. Ervin stepped back once and thrust his spear upward.","\"Abyss Spear Art, Deep Current Thrust.\"","The spear lanced toward Kaiden’s palm, but Kaiden’s body slid sideways without his feet ever moving.","\"Void Genesis Art, Hollow Displacement.\"","The spear passed through the place where Kaiden should have been, and in the next instant, he appeared behind Ervin.","\"Void Genesis Art, Sevenfold Severing Line.\"","Seven invisible spatial lines slashed toward Ervin’s back. Ervin spun sharply and swept his spear behind him, but two of the seven lines still slipped through his defense and opened shallow wounds across his shoulder and waist."]},{"number":1882,"title":"Chapter 1882: Kaiden’s True Strength!","paragraphs":["The arena stirred at once.","\"He injured Ervin!\"","\"Kaiden is much sharper than he looked against Max!\"","\"Against Max his attacks seemed useless, but against Ervin every spatial cut is dangerous!\"","Kaiden did not pause. He raised both hands, and the entire central stage split into overlapping planes.","\"Void Genesis Art, Thousand-Layer Spatial Cage.\"","Ervin’s surroundings folded again and again. Transparent layers of space formed a prison around him, and every layer shifted to its own rhythm. If Ervin moved forward, the distance stretched away from him. If he moved backward, the ground folded beneath his feet, and if he thrust his spear, the attack was rerouted through another plane entirely.","Ervin’s expression grew more serious.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent.\"","The black sea appeared behind him, and the broken gate rose from its depths. The moment his Pseudo Cosmic Path descended, the pressure across the battlefield changed. The folded spatial cage began to sink, as though its layers had suddenly gained weight.","The black sea spread toward the transparent walls, pulling at them and dragging them downward, straining to collapse space itself into the abyssal current.","Kaiden’s eyes sharpened.","\"Grand Void Sanctum, Void Anchor Seal.\"","Silver-gray anchors materialized within the spatial layers. They pierced into the folded planes and pinned them in place, keeping the Thousand-Layer Spatial Cage from sinking entirely into Ervin’s abyssal pressure. The clash between the cage and the black sea set the arena trembling. Space fought to fold while the abyss fought to drag everything down.","Ervin lifted his spear.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, First Depth Tide.\"","The black sea surged upward, and Kaiden raised one hand to meet it.","\"Void Genesis Art, World-Folding Barrier.\"","The tide crashed into the folded barrier and split across several spatial planes. Rather than striking Kaiden directly, most of the abyssal wave was rerouted into empty layers of space. Yet the abyssal pressure was too strange to be fully contained. Even after redirection, part of it kept sinking down through the folds, and Kaiden was forced back half a step.","His expression grew even more focused as Ervin advanced.","\"Abyss Spear Art, Gate Shadow Thrust.\"","The shadow of the broken gate gathered around his spear tip, and the thrust crossed the distance between them like a black line drawn up from the bottom of the sea.","Kaiden did not block in any ordinary way. His hands moved, and the space in front of him twisted into a spiral.","\"Void Genesis Art, Spiral Exile Gate.\"","The spear thrust entered the spiral and vanished. For one brief moment, everyone believed Kaiden had exiled the attack into some distant spatial layer entirely. Then Kaiden’s head snapped around. The spear thrust had reappeared behind him, having forced its way back through the exile gate by riding the abyssal pull into the battlefield.","Kaiden’s eyes narrowed.","\"Void Genesis Art, Origin Fold Reversal.\"","The space behind him folded backward and barely diverted the thrust past his shoulder. Even so, the black spear force grazed him and tore a line through his silver-gray robe.","Kaiden and Ervin retreated at the same moment, and neither of them looked relaxed any longer.","Rakan Thorne’s eyes gleamed from his pillar. \"Now this is a fight.\"","Damian Voss watched quietly. \"Kaiden is showing far more than he did against Max.\"","Revona nodded faintly. \"Because Ervin cannot ignore spatial attacks.\"","Orion Starfall smiled weakly. \"And because Ervin’s abyss can drag space itself down. What a troublesome pair.\"","Max observed the battle calmly, and he understood Kaiden’s strength better than most. Against him, Kaiden had looked restrained only because the Dimensional Sovereign Body and a higher mastery of the Void Genesis Art had ruined the matchup entirely.","Now, against Ervin, Kaiden’s true power was finally coming into view. His spatial control ran anything but shallow. His techniques were layered, precise, and frighteningly difficult to predict, and even Ervin’s abyss could not swallow them casually.","On the stage, Kaiden drew a slow breath, and the space behind him opened. A vast silver-gray void unfolded, filled with countless corridors, mirrors, and broken spatial planes.","This was no ordinary field technique. It was the manifestation of his deepest spatial foundation, a terrifying maze of the void where every direction could be folded, severed, or exiled at his will.","Kaiden’s voice rang out calmly.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path.\"","The silver-gray void expanded.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth.\"","The moment the name appeared, the entire central stage shifted. The ground grew distant and the sky became layered. Ervin now stood at the center of a labyrinth built from folded space, where every wall was a passage, every passage was a blade, and every blade could become a prison.","Compared to Max’s sovereign command over space, Kaiden’s Grand Void Labyrinth was something different in nature. It did not attempt to rule space as a true sovereign would. Instead, it turned space into an endless battlefield of traps, routes, distortions, and points of exile.","This was Kaiden’s true power, a Pseudo Cosmic Path forged from the Void Genesis Art and the deepest spatial principles of the Grand Void Sanctum.","Inside the Grand Void Labyrinth, Kaiden’s aura climbed sharply.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth, Corridor of Ten Thousand Cuts.\"","The spatial corridors around Ervin opened, and invisible cuts poured in from every direction. Ervin spun his spear and released a deep abyssal ring, but the cuts did not all arrive within the same layer.","Some came through present space while others emerged from folded space. Some appeared only after a delay of half a breath, and some bypassed the spear ring entirely to materialize right beside his body.","Blood splashed, and several wounds opened across Ervin’s arms and shoulders.","The arena erupted.","\"Kaiden is suppressing Ervin!\"","\"This is his Pseudo Cosmic Path!\"","\"The Grand Void Labyrinth, what a terrifying path!\"","Ervin’s eyes grew darker, and the black sea behind him climbed higher.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, Gate of the First Depth.\"","The broken gate opened, and the pull of the abyssal origin surged outward to drag at the Grand Void Labyrinth. Several spatial corridors bent downward and began sinking toward the black sea. But Kaiden’s figure appeared at the end of one corridor with his hand already descending.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth, Exile Palm.\"","The palm struck the air, and Ervin’s left side vanished. It was not his body that disappeared, but rather the space around his left side, which was exiled for a brief moment and broke his balance. Kaiden pressed the advantage at once.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth, Mirror Burial.\"","Dozens of mirrored spaces bloomed around Ervin, each one reflecting a different version of him. Then all the reflections collapsed inward, seeking to bury his real body among the false spatial layers.","Ervin drove his spear into the ground.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, Second Depth Pressure.\"","The black sea deepened, and the mirrored spaces sank sharply and cracked beneath the pressure. Yet the Grand Void Labyrinth was too flexible to break so easily. The shattered mirrors simply reformed into new corridors, and from those corridors, Kaiden attacked again and again.","For the first time in the tournament, Ervin was being driven to the edge. Wounds accumulated across his body, and his spear movements grew heavier. The black sea remained terrifying, but every time it tried to swallow Kaiden’s path, the Grand Void Labyrinth shifted and opened a fresh route.","Kaiden never lingered in one place long enough to be dragged down. He fought like a master of endless distance, never striking from where Ervin expected and never allowing the abyss to fully claim his position.","The Grand Void Sanctum disciples finally erupted.","\"Senior Brother Kaiden!\"","\"Show them the Grand Void Labyrinth!\"","\"This is his true strength!\"","Even the elders of the Grand Void Sanctum looked satisfied. Against Max, Kaiden’s pride had been smothered by an impossible counter. Against Ervin, the Divine Realm could finally see why Kaiden Voidmere ranked among the strongest geniuses of the entire conference."]},{"number":1883,"title":"Chapter 1883: Mysterious Ervin!","paragraphs":["On the stage, Ervin took another wound across his chest, and his black spear dipped slightly. Kaiden appeared far above him through a folded corridor.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth, World Exile Coffin.\"","The entire labyrinth compressed. Six massive spatial walls formed around Ervin, closing in from above, from below, and from all four sides. Every wall contained countless folded planes leading away from the battlefield.","If they sealed completely, Ervin would suffer far worse than imprisonment. His very position would be exiled into the outer folds of Kaiden’s Pseudo Cosmic Path, and escape would be nearly impossible without breaking the labyrinth from within.","Ervin looked up, and his expression finally changed. It showed no fear and no panic. It showed complete seriousness.","\"You are strong,\" he said.","Kaiden’s voice answered from everywhere within the labyrinth. \"So are you.\"","Ervin closed his eyes briefly, and then the black sea behind him went utterly still. The broken gate ceased its trembling. The abyssal pressure no longer spread wildly, and instead it gathered inward, growing darker, deeper, and far more ancient.","The water of the black sea sank below the stage, yet its presence became more frightening rather than less, as though only the surface had disappeared while the true abyss awakened beneath everyone’s feet.","Ervin opened his eyes.","\"I did not want to use this unless I had to.\"","Kaiden’s gaze sharpened. Ervin raised his spear with both hands.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent.\"","The broken gate opened wider than it had against Selene, wider than it had against Rosaline, and wider than it had against Orion.","\"Gate of the Second Depth.\"","Boom!","A pressure far beyond the previous gate erupted across the stage. The World Exile Coffin stopped closing, and its six spatial walls shook violently. The corridors of the Grand Void Labyrinth twisted downward while the mirrors cracked.","Even the folded paths grew heavy, as though the very concept of distance had been dragged into a deeper layer of abyssal origin.","Kaiden’s expression changed for the first time. \"The Second Depth.\"","Ervin stepped forward, and the black spear in his hand seemed to merge with the gate at his back.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, Second Depth Spear, Sunken World.\"","He thrust, but the spear did not fly toward Kaiden. It struck the Grand Void Labyrinth itself. For a moment, the entire Pseudo Cosmic Path went silent, and then the silver-gray labyrinth began to sink. Corridor after corridor collapsed downward while mirror after mirror shattered.","The folded planes lost their routes and tumbled into the invisible depth opened by the Second Depth Gate.","Kaiden immediately fought to stabilize his path with both hands.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth, Infinite Corridor Rotation.\"","The surviving corridors began spinning rapidly, working to scatter the abyssal pull across countless spatial layers. For a moment it worked, and the sinking slowed. Kaiden’s control was astonishing, and many experts could see that he was resisting Ervin’s full-strength abyss through pure spatial mastery alone.","But Ervin stepped forward again.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, Second Depth Spear, Return Of The Sunken Path.\"","The spear moved a second time, and now the abyssal force followed the very routes Kaiden had created. It did not assault the labyrinth from outside. It entered the corridors themselves and dragged them down from within.","Kaiden’s face paled slightly as the Grand Void Labyrinth shuddered. He raised one hand and gathered every remaining spatial fold into a single point.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth, Final Corridor, Void Beyond Return.\"","A dark silver passage opened behind Ervin. This was no ordinary exile gate. It was the deepest corridor Kaiden could currently open, a path built to cast its target beyond the returning folds of the battlefield entirely.","If Ervin fell into it, even his Abyssal Origin Descent would need to burn enormous power just to find a way back.","The corridor opened beneath Ervin’s feet, and he sank halfway into it. The arena gasped.","Kaiden pressed both hands downward. \"Go.\"","The Void Beyond Return swallowed Ervin’s lower body. But Ervin’s spear struck the edge of the corridor, and the broken gate behind him released a terrifying and soundless pull.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, Return To Depth.\"","The black sea rose up through the corridor, and the abyss invaded the Void Beyond Return itself. Kaiden’s eyes widened.","The exile corridor should have led away from the battlefield, away from the current spatial layer, and away from anything easily reached. But the abyssal origin cared nothing for ordinary direction. It treated all depth as something that could be dragged lower still.","The Void Beyond Return began sinking backward, and Ervin stepped out of it. His face was pale and blood ran from several wounds across his body, yet his eyes remained calm and deep. He had been pushed to the absolute edge.","Had he hesitated for even a single breath, Kaiden’s final corridor might have sealed him away long enough to decide the battle. But he had not hesitated, and he had spent everything.","Ervin raised his spear one final time.","\"Second Depth Spear, Abyss Returns All Roads.\"","The spear descended, and the remains of the Grand Void Labyrinth collapsed. Silver-gray corridors shattered across the sky while the folded planes broke apart. The mirrors of space sank into darkness.","Kaiden tried to slip through one last fold, but the abyssal force traced the route and arrived before him in the same instant.","Ervin’s spear stopped at Kaiden’s throat, and the entire arena went silent.","Kaiden stood motionless with blood at the corner of his mouth, his silver-gray robes torn, and his aura flickering. His Grand Void Labyrinth had collapsed, yet his eyes stayed calm. There was no shame in them. There was only acceptance.","\"You really hid that deeply,\" Kaiden said.","Ervin’s breathing came slightly heavy. \"You forced me to.\"","Kaiden looked at the spear resting before his throat, and then he smiled faintly.","\"Then I have no complaints.\"","He lowered his hands.","\"I surrender.\"","Angelina Valerius announced the result calmly.","[Winner: Ervin.]","[Kaiden Voidmere Defeated.]","The screen above the arena updated.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Ervin]","[Total Battles Fought: 21]","[Total Wins: 21]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Kaiden Voidmere]","[Total Battles Fought: 21]","[Total Wins: 19]","The Divine Realm erupted. This time, no one dared claim that Kaiden’s loss to Max had made him look weak.","Against Ervin, he had unveiled his true power in the terrifying Grand Void Labyrinth, and he had pushed the Abyssal Origin Descent so far that Ervin was forced to open the Gate of the Second Depth and fight at full strength to win.","Kaiden had lost, but he had made one of the most mysterious geniuses of the final stage reveal a deeper layer of his Pseudo Cosmic Path.","On his pillar, Max gave Kaiden a faint nod. He had always known Kaiden was strong, and now everyone else knew it too.","Ervin returned to his pillar a moment later, his aura quieter than before yet visibly drained. The black spear in his hand still carried a trace of the Second Depth’s pressure, and several top geniuses regarded him with renewed caution.","Damian Voss narrowed his eyes slightly while Revona’s Void Origin Eyes flickered. Rakan Thorne grinned with open interest.","Orion Starfall laughed weakly from his pillar. \"So he had another gate after all. How unfair.\"","Kaiden sat down quietly as the Eternal Hourglass healed his injuries. He had lost again, but this defeat carried an entirely different meaning. Against Max, he had been countered.","Against Ervin, he had truly fought to his limit, and because of that, his strength had finally been witnessed by the entire Divine Realm."]},{"number":1884,"title":"Chapter 1884: Damian vs Rakan!","paragraphs":["Angelina Valerius let the uproar from Ervin and Kaiden’s battle settle for a short while before she raised her hand once more, and the giant screen above the arena began to spin.","By now, the final competitive stage had moved far past the point where ordinary matches could satisfy the crowd. Too many shocking battles had already taken place. Max had defeated Rosaline, Rakan, Kaiden, Selene, and Aurelian.","Revona had ground Orion down to exhaustion and had later beaten Rakan as well. Ervin had just forced Kaiden to unveil the full terror of the Grand Void Labyrinth before defeating him with the Gate of the Second Depth.","The remaining battles grew heavier with each round, and every new pairing between major geniuses seemed capable of reshuffling the rankings at the top.","The first name slowed and appeared.","[Damian Voss]","A wave of noise rolled through the arena, and the second name soon followed.","[Rakan Thorne]","This time the noise swelled even louder, because another major battle had arrived. It was another clash between monsters, pitting the strongest genius of the Sword God Palace against the first Warlord of the War God Palace.","The crowd inside the Eternal Hourglass came alive at once, and across the Divine Realm, countless watching forces straightened before their viewing screens.","At the Black Dragon Clan, many disciples who had just been dissecting Ervin and Kaiden’s battle turned their full attention back to the large screen.","At the War God Palace, the disciples who had felt both proud and frustrated during Rakan’s earlier matches leaned forward again.","Although Rakan had already suffered defeats in the final stage, no one there had lost faith in his power. After all, the ones who had beaten him so far were monsters among monsters.","Now he was about to face Damian Voss.","Above the arena, Angelina’s voice rang out calmly.","\"Damian Voss.\"","\"Rakan Thorne.\"","\"Enter the stage.\"","Two beams of light descended, and Damian appeared first. He stood in flowing sword robes with his long hair drifting slightly behind him, his expression as calm and cold as ever.","The sword in his hand rested quietly, yet no one who had watched him fight could overlook the terrifying sharpness hidden inside that stillness.","Damian’s sword was not loud like Rakan’s fists, nor majestic like Rosaline’s dawn kingdom. It was not strange like Morgana’s curses, and it was not immeasurable like Revona’s void. Even so, everyone present understood that once he drew it in earnest, it became one of the deadliest things in the entire conference.","Rakan appeared opposite him. The first Warlord of the War God Palace still carried that fierce and open battle aura around him. His body seemed carved from battle itself, broad-shouldered and sturdy and terrifyingly solid.","Even after so many punishing fights, he still looked like the sort of man who would rather collapse after spending everything than retreat a single step early. He rolled his shoulders once, looked at Damian, and grinned.","\"Well,\" Rakan said, \"we finally get a proper rematch.\"","Damian regarded him calmly. \"The first one ended too early.\"","Rakan laughed. \"That is true. Back then the first round ended before we could go all out.\"","He clenched both fists, and the air around his knuckles began to tremble. \"This time, no one is stopping us.\"","Damian’s sword tilted slightly downward. \"This time,\" he replied, \"I intend to finish it.\"","The moment those words fell, the atmosphere in the arena sharpened again. Even Max, standing on his pillar, narrowed his eyes slightly.","Rakan’s raw physical strength was terrifying, and the three broken limits of the War God Body had already placed him at the summit of body cultivators among the younger generation.","Against most opponents, that alone would have been enough to crush them outright. But Damian was not most opponents.","His sword had already brought down the Divine Son, one of the strongest geniuses of the elf race, and even top monsters like Orion and Kaiden treated him with caution.","Angelina raised her hand.","[Battle Begins.]","Rakan moved first. He did not test, he did not circle, and he did not waste a single breath on a probing exchange.","\"War God Body, First Limit.\"","Boom!","The first limit broke instantly. His body released a frightening pressure as the muscles across his arms and torso surged with explosive force. He took one step and the stage cracked beneath his feet. Then his fist shot forward.","\"War God Fist, Mountain-Breaker Rush.\"","The punch came on like a charging fortress, carrying overwhelming body force and battle aura together.","Damian drew his sword.","\"Falling River Cut.\"","A clean silver-white line appeared, and sword met fist.","Clang!","The shockwave exploded outward and swept across the arena in a ring of pressure. Rakan’s body did not retreat, and Damian’s sword did not bend. For a brief instant, the battlefield seemed caught between a mountain of flesh and a river of steel.","Then Rakan’s second fist came.","\"War God Fist, Iron Heaven Smash.\"","Damian’s sword turned.","\"Crosswind Return.\"","The blade redirected the strike rather than meeting it head-on, and Rakan’s punch slid past Damian’s left shoulder. In the same motion, Damian’s sword flashed upward toward Rakan’s ribs. Rakan twisted his body and caught the strike on his hardened forearm.","Sparks burst outward, and a thin line of blood appeared.","The crowd roared immediately, because Damian had drawn first blood.","Rakan only grinned wider. \"Good!\"","He stepped forward again and threw three punches in succession, each heavier than the last.","\"War God Fist, Shattering Drum.\"","\"War God Fist, Bonequake Burst.\"","\"War God Fist, Heaven-Hammer Drive.\"","Every punch came from a different angle, and each carried enough physical force to break apart the protective barriers of peak geniuses.","Damian’s sword moved swiftly through the storm of fists, sometimes blocking and sometimes diverting, and sometimes slipping around an attack to strike at Rakan’s weak points.","For a while, neither man seemed willing to reveal his deepest cards. Even so, this early exchange already burned hotter than most battles of the final stage.","The Sword God Palace disciples watched with shining eyes, while the War God Palace disciples shouted Rakan’s name, especially when his fists managed to force Damian back half a step."]},{"number":1885,"title":"Chapter 1885: Tyrant Heaven Shatter!","paragraphs":["But that half step only sharpened Damian’s gaze, and his sword style changed at once. Rather than continuing to meet Rakan’s ferocity head-on, his blade became cleaner, colder, and far more precise.","\"Thousand Thread Severance.\"","The silver-white sword light split into countless narrow lines. Each line targeted a different part of Rakan’s movement, cutting at the wrist, the shoulder joint, the knee, the waist, and the ankle.","It was not a technique built to overpower strength. It was a sword art designed to sever rhythm, structure, and continuity within an opponent’s body.","Rakan’s face grew more serious. He crossed both arms before him and took the attack head-on, but the lines of sword light still bit into his skin one after another. Several shallow wounds opened at once, and more importantly, his next forward burst lost its perfect rhythm.","Damian stepped in.","\"Silent Star Draw.\"","A vertical sword line fell straight toward Rakan’s chest.","Rakan roared. \"War God Body, Second Limit.\"","Boom!","The second limit broke. His aura surged wildly and his body force climbed to a new height. The sword strike still landed, but this time Rakan met it with both palms pressed together and caught the descending blade between them.","Blood spilled from his hands, yet he forced the sword aside and drove his knee toward Damian’s abdomen.","Damian stepped back, though not entirely, and the knee passed within inches of him. Rakan pressed forward immediately.","\"War God Fist, Battlefield Tyrant.\"","His whole body lunged behind the punch. This was no longer merely a fist technique. It was his full body weight, his second-limit War God Body, and the fury of a battle-crazed warlord compressed into one unstoppable blow.","Damian’s eyes narrowed.","\"Sword Guard, White Horizon.\"","A broad silver-white arc opened in front of him.","Boom!","The Battlefield Tyrant crashed into the White Horizon. The sword guard trembled violently, and the stage beneath Damian’s feet cracked under the pressure. For a moment, it looked as though Rakan might truly blast through on brute force alone.","Then Damian’s right hand shifted. The White Horizon guard folded inward and became a slanted current.","\"White Horizon, Turning Edge.\"","Rakan’s force was redirected to the side. His punch tore apart an entire section of the stage instead of Damian’s body, and before he could correct his posture, Damian’s sword slashed twice across his torso.","Blood sprayed, and the War God Palace disciples fell silent for a moment.","Rakan’s breathing grew heavier, but he refused to retreat. Instead, he laughed.","\"Good. Very good.\"","His body released a terrifying red-gold battle aura.","\"War God Body, Third Limit.\"","The instant the third limit broke, the entire arena trembled. This was the true peak of Rakan’s physical body. His muscles tightened like tempered divine metal, and veins of battle-red force ran across his skin.","The surrounding air seemed unable to bear the pressure radiating from his flesh. Compared to his first and second limits, the third was a complete leap, and it was the level that had earned him the title of first Warlord of the War God Palace.","Rakan bent slightly at the knees. Then he vanished.","The crowd gasped as he reappeared before Damian like a red-gold cannonball.","\"War God Fist, Worldsplitter.\"","The punch exploded forward, and Damian blocked.","Clang!","For the first time, Damian was driven back several full steps. Before he could steady himself, Rakan was already on him again.","\"War God Fist, Nine Battlefield Tremors.\"","Nine consecutive punches descended like falling war drums, and each strike landed heavier than the one before it.","Damian’s sword moved in a storm of silver-white brilliance as he blocked and redirected them one after another, yet even so, the pressure bearing down on him climbed sharply. On the ninth strike, the air burst apart and Damian slid backward across the stage.","The War God Palace erupted in cheers.","\"That is it!\"","\"Senior Brother Rakan!\"","\"Crush him!\"","Rakan lifted his chin with blood running from the cuts across his body, and his battle aura soared like wildfire.","\"This is the body of the War God Palace,\" he said. \"Can your sword cut through it?\"","Damian looked at him quietly, and then he raised his sword again.","\"It already has.\"","The words were calm, but in the next instant, his aura changed. The sky above the stage seemed to sharpen. The sword in his hand grew brighter, purer, and colder than before. The surrounding sword intent did not explode wildly.","It condensed instead, until it felt as though every strand of sharpness in the world had gathered around Damian’s blade.","Max watched carefully, and he understood at once that Damian had stopped merely fighting. Now he was beginning to cut in earnest.","Damian took one step forward.","\"Sword Path, Seven Line Clear Severance.\"","One slash came, and then another, and then a third. He did not attack with overwhelming visual force. He attacked with terrifying precision.","Each sword line cut into the exact flow of Rakan’s body force, landing where his joints transferred power, where his muscles chained explosive force together, and where the rhythm of his War God Body surged between its limits.","Rakan met him head-on. He punched through the first line, broke the second with his elbow, and destroyed the third with a downward smash. But the fourth line cut across his thigh while the fifth slashed his shoulder.","The sixth severed the rhythm of his next forward charge, and the seventh landed across his chest and drew a deep line of blood.","Rakan staggered, though only once. Then he roared and gathered everything he had into a final charge.","\"War God Body, Three Limits Unified.\"","His red-gold battle aura compressed fully around him.","\"War God Palace Secret Art, Tyrant Heaven Shatter.\"","This was Rakan’s strongest attack, and it was far more than a fist or a burst of body force. It was the complete union of his three broken limits, his battle will, and the entire ferocity of the War God Palace’s body-cultivating path.","When he launched the punch, it felt as though a whole battlefield of war spirits charged behind it.","The Divine Realm held its breath, and even the top geniuses on the pillars watched without blinking.","Damian looked at the incoming Tyrant Heaven Shatter, and at last his sword path truly rose.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path.\"","A vast sword heaven appeared behind him. Countless ancient swords floated in silence above a silver-white firmament, and at the very center stood one enormous sword shadow that seemed to rule over all the rest.","Unlike loud and crushing domains, Damian’s Pseudo Cosmic Path was frightening because of its purity. It carried no waste, no unnecessary flourish, and no unstable violence.","It was the kind of path that sent an instinctive chill through every swordsman watching, because it looked like a path created for the sole purpose of proving that the sword stood above all."]},{"number":1886,"title":"Chapter 1886: Damian Wins!","paragraphs":["\"Sword Sovereign Heaven.\"","The name alone made the arena feel colder. Rakan’s eyes widened, but he did not stop.","Damian’s voice stayed calm.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, First Edict.\"","The enormous sovereign sword behind him trembled.","\"All force beneath the sword shall be judged.\"","Then Damian slashed. The silver-white sword line descended and met Tyrant Heaven Shatter head-on, and for a moment the two attacks held. Rakan roared and poured every ounce of power from his three broken limits into the punch.","The battlefield spirits behind him shook wildly as they strained to push through the sovereign sword line.","Then Damian’s sword brightened, and the Sword Sovereign Heaven pressed down. The War God Palace’s secret art cracked, the battlefield spirits split apart, and Tyrant Heaven Shatter broke. The silver-white line continued forward and struck Rakan directly.","Boom!","Rakan was blasted backward across the stage. His huge body crashed and rolled, carving a long trench into the arena floor before finally coming to rest near the very edge of the battlefield. Blood ran from his mouth and chest while the battle aura around him flickered violently.","The three broken limits of his War God Body began collapsing one after another.","The War God Palace disciples fell silent.","Rakan forced himself to rise. He planted one knee into the shattered stage and pushed himself halfway up while breathing heavily. His fists still trembled with unwillingness, and the red-gold aura around him struggled to flare one last time.","Damian appeared before him, and his sword stopped at Rakan’s throat. The entire arena went silent.","Rakan looked at the blade, and then up at Damian. For a few breaths he said nothing. Then, slowly, he laughed. The sound was hoarse and pained, yet entirely sincere.","\"So this is the sword of the Sword God Palace.\"","Damian’s expression remained calm.","Rakan shook his head lightly. \"I gave it all.\"","\"I know,\" Damian replied.","Rakan exhaled slowly. The unwillingness drained from his eyes and was replaced by the clear acceptance of a warrior who had lost only after emptying himself completely.","\"Then I lose.\"","Angelina Valerius announced the result at once.","\"Winner, Damian Voss.\"","The giant screen above the arena changed.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Damian Voss]","[Total Battles Fought: 22]","[Total Wins: 22]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Rakan Thorne]","[Total Battles Fought: 22]","[Total Wins: 19]","The Divine Realm erupted once more. Damian Voss remained undefeated. Rakan Thorne had given everything, drawing on all three broken limits of the War God Body and even the War God Palace’s secret art, and Damian’s sword had still cut him down in the end.","At the Sword God Palace, countless disciples cheered with pride blazing across their faces. At the War God Palace, the disciples were disappointed, yet not one of them looked ashamed of Rakan.","Their first Warlord had not lost through weakness. He had lost after fighting at his absolute peak against one of the strongest swordsmen the Divine Realm had produced in generations.","Saint Reiner, still hidden in the shadows of the War God Palace, watched in silence. A faint glint crossed his eyes before he murmured to himself, \"Damian is indeed terrifying, but the one I truly want to watch is still that boy.\"","On the pillars of the Eternal Hourglass, the other top geniuses watched quietly, and Max’s eyes lingered on Damian a moment longer than the rest. That sword was truly dangerous, and dangerous in a way that demanded respect.","Rakan had been anything but weak. Among the body cultivators of the younger generation, he stood absolutely among the very best. Yet Damian had cut through all of it and won cleanly in the end.","The battle had ended, but the pressure gathering at the top of the rankings had only grown heavier.","Rakan returned to his pillar with his wounds still knitting under the laws of the Eternal Hourglass, though his eyes stayed bright. He had lost, yet no one could claim he had fallen cheaply.","He had opened all three limits of the War God Body, unleashed the War God Palace’s secret art, and driven his body to its edge before Damian’s Sword Sovereign Heaven finally cut through him.","It was a defeat, but it was equally proof of why Rakan Thorne was called the first Warlord.","Damian returned to his pillar in silence. His sword had been sheathed again, his expression calm and his aura restrained. Yet after that battle, everyone sensed his danger even more keenly.","He had remained undefeated through every match, and each time someone forced him to reveal a little more, his sword grew more frightening.","The Sword God Palace disciples across the Divine Realm were still cheering, while many great forces had fallen into solemn discussion about just how far his Sword Sovereign Heaven could truly reach.","Angelina Valerius waited until the stage restored itself. The shattered ground mended, the sword marks faded, and the bloodstains vanished beneath the golden flow of the Eternal Hourglass laws. Then she raised one hand again.","\"The next battle will now be selected.\"","The giant screen above the arena began spinning, and the names of the remaining participants flashed rapidly through the air. At this point, nearly every battle among the top names carried real importance.","Some participants had already lost their chance to reach the very summit, but pride, ranking, and future reputation still hung in the balance.","A victory over a major genius could reshape how the entire Divine Realm regarded them, while a crushing defeat could damage even an ancient faction’s prestige.","The light slowed, and one name appeared.","[Orion]","The arena stirred immediately.","Orion was still seated on his pillar, recovering from his previous brutal battles.","He had lost to Revona after forcing her to use Return To Nothing, and then lost to Ervin after pressing the Abyssal Origin Descent hard enough to make the broken gate open wider. His record was no longer perfect, yet no one dared underestimate him.","If anything, his defeats had painted his reputation in sharper colors.","Orion was not someone who lost through weakness. He was someone who lost only after burning everything he had against monsters of the highest tier.","Across the Divine Realm, the Nine Star Court disciples snapped to attention at once.","\"Senior Brother Orion again!\"","\"Who is his opponent?\"","\"He has already fought Revona and Ervin. Please do not let it be another terrible matchup.\"","\"He still has the Nine Star Sovereign Body. Even injured, he can fight anyone.\"","On his pillar, Orion looked up at his own name and sighed with a helpless smile. \"Again? The Eternal Hourglass really refuses to let me rest.\"","Rakan, still recovering nearby, laughed. \"Maybe it likes watching you suffer.\"","Orion turned his head and smiled at him. \"Coming from someone who just got cut down by Damian, that sounds strangely comforting.\"","Rakan grinned. \"At least I lost after punching everything I could reach.\"","Orion shrugged lightly. \"Then I shall try to punch something bright this time, depending on who appears.\"","As though answering his words, the second name slowed. The spinning light passed over Max Morgan, then over Damian Voss, then over Revona, and then over Ervin. Then it stopped."]},{"number":1887,"title":"Chapter 1887: Orion vs Divine Son!","paragraphs":["[Aurelian Lareth]","The moment the name appeared, the arena dropped into a sudden and sharp silence. Then the giant screen enlarged both names.","[Final Competitive Stage]","[Orion Starfall vs Aurelian Lareth]","The atmosphere changed instantly, because this was no casual match. It was a battle between the strongest genius of the Nine Star Court and the Divine Son of the second elven faction.","Orion Starfall, whose Nine Star Sovereign Body had shaken the arena and whose self-created Starfall Extinction had forced even Revona to reveal one of her deepest moves, would now face Aurelian Lareth, the proud Divine Son who carried the Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion and had already fought Damian, Rakan, Rosaline, and Max.","Both of them had suffered major defeats. Both of them still carried terrifying strength. And both of them needed this battle for entirely different reasons.","Orion needed to prove that even after losing to Revona and Ervin, he still belonged among the absolute peak. His body was not fully recovered, his star power had been drained again and again, and his strongest technique had been used repeatedly in battles where ordinary geniuses would have collapsed long before.","Yet the more he fought, the clearer one truth became. Orion’s brilliance had never come from an easy path. It came from his willingness to keep shining even while wounded.","Aurelian needed something entirely different. He needed restoration.","After losing to Damian, his pride had been damaged. After losing to Max, something far deeper than pride had been shaken.","The entire Divine Realm had watched his Heavenly Luminance attacks fail to harm Max, and although most people did not know the hidden truth behind that scene, everyone understood that something strange and humiliating had taken place.","The Divine Son of the second elven faction had returned to his pillar in silence, and since then he had not spoken a single unnecessary word.","Now he had been matched against Orion. For the second elven faction, this was a chance to recover some face. For the Nine Star Court, it was a chance to prove that their strongest genius could still challenge the highest tier even after terrible matchups and repeated exhaustion.","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, the top geniuses reacted one after another.","Rakan crossed his arms as his grin returned. \"This should be good. Orion’s stars against that fellow’s divine light.\"","Morgana Starveil smiled faintly. \"A battle between two people who desperately need a win. That usually turns ugly.\"","Kaiden Voidmere looked thoughtful. \"Orion’s Nine Star Sovereign Body will let him close the distance, but Aurelian’s long-range suppression is difficult to cross if he controls the field early.\"","Ervin’s gaze stayed deep. \"Orion is not at full strength.\"","Revona opened her eyes slightly. \"But his will is not weak.\"","Damian Voss looked between the two names without speaking. He had defeated Aurelian himself, and he had also witnessed Orion’s Starfall Extinction. His silence made the coming battle feel heavier still, because everyone knew Damian never wasted attention on fights that lacked meaning.","Max stood on his pillar calmly, and his gaze rested on Aurelian for a brief moment. The Divine Son’s expression was cold, but the arrogance he once wore had changed. Something in him had quieted after the battle with Max.","It was not humility, and it was not peace. It was a tightened, suppressed, dangerous kind of silence. He looked like a man trying to hold a cracked throne together with both hands while pretending no one could see the fractures.","Then Max looked toward Orion, who was smiling again. He was pale, injured, and exhausted, and he was smiling all the same.","Max’s eyes turned slightly thoughtful. Orion had been pushed hard throughout the final stage. He had fought Revona, Ervin, and many other dangerous opponents, yet his spirit had never dimmed. Even in defeat he carried no shame.","What he carried was hunger. He wanted to discover how far his stars could go, and every loss only seemed to sharpen his determination to refine them.","Outside, the Divine Realm boiled with discussion.","\"The Nine Star Sovereign Body against the Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion.\"","\"Can Orion break through Aurelian’s long-range light suppression?\"","\"He forced Revona to use Return To Nothing, but he has already burned through too much.\"","\"Aurelian lost terribly to Max, but he is still the Divine Son. Against anyone else, his Heavenly Luminance Dominion remains terrifying.\"","\"If Orion uses Starfall Extinction again, can Aurelian block it?\"","\"Or will Aurelian suppress him before he can gather enough star force?\"","At the Nine Star Court, the elders watched with solemn faces. They understood Orion’s current condition better than anyone. His body had been repaired by the Eternal Hourglass, but repair did not mean he had returned to his absolute peak.","The Nine Star Sovereign Body was powerful, yet it placed terrifying demands on his foundation. Starfall Extinction was worse still, being self-created, incomplete, and dangerous to use repeatedly. Orion’s will could carry him far, but no amount of will could erase every cost.","At the viewing halls of the second elven faction, the atmosphere had turned deathly cold. Aurelian had to win. No one spoke those words aloud, yet everyone understood them. He had already lost to Damian, and he had lost even more humiliatingly to Max.","If he fell to Orion as well, especially while the Divine Realm still questioned the authority of his Heavenly Luminance power, the Divine Son’s prestige would suffer another heavy blow. Even though Orion ranked among the strongest geniuses present, a defeat at this point would remain dangerous for Aurelian’s standing.","Inside the arena, Orion slowly rose to his feet. His body still looked a little unsteady, but his smile stayed bright. He looked toward Aurelian’s pillar and said, \"Divine Son, I hope you are not too angry today. Angry opponents are troublesome.\"","Aurelian looked down at him with cold golden eyes. \"You should worry about yourself.\"","Orion chuckled. \"I have been doing that since Revona nearly erased me and Ervin nearly drowned my stars. It has not helped much.\"","Aurelian’s expression did not move. \"Then this battle will end quickly.\"","Orion’s smile widened slightly, though his eyes turned sharper. \"That is what everyone says before it becomes difficult.\"","The tension between them thickened.","Angelina Valerius looked at both participants. Her silver-white robe stirred faintly as the laws of the Eternal Hourglass gathered around the central stage once more.","The arena had already finished repairing itself after Damian and Rakan’s battle, yet now, as Orion and Aurelian prepared to step forward, the barrier brightened more than usual. It was as though the Eternal Hourglass itself anticipated another large-scale collision.","Above the stage, the announcement still shone.","[Final Competitive Stage]","[Orion Starfall vs Aurelian Lareth]","Orion Starfall lifted his head as faint starlight began gathering around his body. Aurelian Lareth stood opposite him in the distance, and golden-white radiance rose slowly behind his figure like a sacred sun.","Angelina Valerius raised her hand.","\"Orion Starfall.\"","\"Aurelian Lareth.\"","\"Enter the stage.\""]},{"number":1888,"title":"Chapter 1888: A Good Match!","paragraphs":["The battle began the moment Orion Starfall and Aurelian Lareth landed on the central stage. There was no casual greeting this time, and there was no slow testing.","The instant Angelina Valerius’s hand lowered and the words appeared above the arena, both of them unleashed their power without a moment’s hesitation.","[Battle Begins.]","Orion’s smile remained on his face, but the starry light in his eyes turned sharp enough to make the air tremble.","He knew his body was not in perfect condition. He had already fought Revona to the edge and used Starfall Extinction against her, and then he had pushed himself against Ervin and lost after forcing the abyssal gate to open deeper.","The laws of the Eternal Hourglass had repaired his injuries, but some exhaustion could not be erased so easily. His foundation was still strained, his meridians still carried the echo of overdrawn star power, and his flesh still remembered the burden of converging the nine stars into himself again and again.","But he did not care.","Aurelian Lareth stood opposite him with a face colder than before. After losing to Max, the arrogance around him had hardened into something more dangerous.","He no longer looked like a proud prince waiting for others to kneel. He looked like a man whose throne had been cracked in front of the entire Divine Realm, and who now intended to bury the next opponent beneath enough light to make everyone forget that humiliation.","Golden-white radiance erupted behind him first.","\"Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion.\"","Aurelian opened his Pseudo Cosmic Path directly. Sacred halls rose behind him, and radiant pillars pierced the sky. A golden throne manifested beneath an endless sun, and the entire stage was swallowed in divine light before Orion had even taken his first step.","The pressure that descended ran far stronger than the openings he had used in most of his earlier battles. Aurelian had no intention of preserving strength, and he had no intention of showing mercy.","After Max had made his Heavenly Luminance power look useless, he needed to prove that against everyone else, the Divine Son’s light remained terrifying.","Orion’s smile widened slightly. \"Straight to the dominion. Good. I was afraid you might still be in a bad mood.\"","Aurelian’s eyes turned icy. \"You talk too much.\"","Orion lifted one hand, and nine ancient stars appeared behind him. \"Then I will fight more.\"","The nine stars descended at once.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path, Nine Star Sovereign Body.\"","Boom!","The stars entered Orion’s flesh, his bones, his blood, his spine, his heart, his arms, his legs, and his soul foundation. His aura erupted upward and pushed against the Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion with radiant celestial force.","Behind him a vast star palace appeared, cracked from previous burdens yet still majestic, surrounded by nine immense stars that turned like crowns of heaven.","The Divine Realm roared.","\"They both opened Pseudo Cosmic Paths immediately!\"","\"Aurelian is not holding back after his loss to Max!\"","\"Orion is injured, but he still activated the Nine Star Sovereign Body from the start!\"","\"This will be brutal!\"","Aurelian raised one hand.","\"Divine Dominion, Twelve Pillars of Sacred Judgment.\"","Twelve radiant pillars appeared around Orion and fired golden-white beams from every direction. Each beam carried the authority of a Pseudo Cosmic Path, and each one sought to purify the star power inside Orion’s body before it could fully circulate.","Orion vanished.","\"Second Star Step.\"","His body slid through starlight and crossed the first beam by a hair’s width. Then he twisted his torso, gathered burning star force into his fist, and punched the second beam directly.","\"First Star Fist.\"","Boom!","The beam shattered. A third beam struck toward his back, but Orion’s body spun in midair as the sixth star entered his shoulder.","\"Sixth Star Pressure Crash.\"","His shoulder slammed into the beam and crushed it apart with dead-star heaviness. Aurelian’s eyes narrowed slightly, and the twelve pillars adjusted their angles at once. The beams no longer fired at random. They locked onto Orion’s movement rhythm, trying to seal off every possible path before he could shift again.","Orion laughed softly. \"Not bad.\"","The third star entered his elbow.","\"Third Star Elbow, Meteor Break.\"","His elbow fell like a plunging meteor and smashed through the nearest radiant pillar. The fourth star entered his leg next, and he kicked through another pillar with a crescent arc of starlight.","\"Fourth Star Crescent Kick.\"","Two pillars shattered, but Aurelian’s dominion rebuilt them instantly. Golden-white light poured down from the endless sun, repairing the broken pillars and strengthening the divine kingdom. Aurelian’s expression stayed cold as his hand pressed downward.","\"Divine Dominion, Luminance Decree.\"","A golden-white decree unfolded above Orion. Sacred words descended and targeted his body, his star circulation, and the rhythm of his Nine Star Sovereign Body. The moment the words touched him, Orion felt the star power in his limbs grow heavier. The decree was straining to suppress the connection between the nine stars and his flesh.","His smile faded slightly. \"Annoying.\"","Aurelian’s voice was cold. \"Fall.\"","The decree brightened. Orion’s knees bent under the pressure, and the radiant pillars around him fired again.","Rakan Thorne frowned from his pillar. \"That decree is restricting his star changes.\"","Kaiden Voidmere nodded slightly. \"Aurelian is not giving him the chance to build rhythm.\"","Ervin watched calmly. \"Orion’s body is still not at full strength.\"","Revona’s eyes stayed fixed on the stage. \"But his will has not weakened.\"","On the stage, Orion drew a deep breath. The ninth star entered his spine, and his entire body straightened beneath the decree.","\"Ninth Star Crown Stabilization.\"","The star palace behind him trembled, and a crown of starlight appeared faintly above his head. The sacred words pressing down on him began cracking one after another. Orion clenched his right fist and poured three stars into his arm at once.","\"Three-Star Heaven Breaker.\"","He punched upward, and the punch tore straight through the Luminance Decree.","Crack!","The decree split apart, and Orion rushed through the falling fragments of sacred light. His speed climbed again, and in a single breath he arrived before Aurelian.","\"Five-Star Revolving Impact.\"","His fist, his elbow, his knee, his shoulder, and his palm struck one after another, and each carried a different star force. Aurelian formed a golden-white mirror with one hand and a sacred spear with the other.","\"Divine Dominion, Sacred Mirror Guard.\"","\"Heavenly Luminance, Royal Sun Spear.\"","The mirror blocked Orion’s fist while the spear thrust toward his chest. Orion shifted the second star into his waist, twisted around the spear, and drove his knee into the mirror.","\"Fifth Star Knee, Falling Orbit.\"","Boom!","The mirror shattered, and Aurelian retreated half a step. That half step made the Nine Star Court disciples erupt.","\"He pushed him back!\"","\"Senior Brother Orion!\"","\"Break the dominion!\"","Aurelian’s face darkened. After his loss to Max, being forced back by another opponent felt like a second blade scraping across his pride. His crown blazed brighter, and the golden throne behind him released a more oppressive radiance.","\"Divine Dominion, Royal Mandate of the Endless Sun.\"","The endless sun poured golden-white light into Aurelian’s body. His aura surged, and the dominion pressed outward in every direction. Orion’s star palace trembled beneath the pressure, and the nine stars around it flickered slightly.","Aurelian raised both hands.","\"Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion, Sacred Sun Spearfall.\""]},{"number":1889,"title":"Chapter 1889: Orion’s Grit and WIll!","paragraphs":["Hundreds of massive golden-white spears formed above the stage, and then they descended.","Orion looked up. The sky was gone, and only the divine spears remained. He grinned again, but this time blood had already appeared at the corner of his mouth. The pressure of the dominion was forcing his injuries to reopen, and every time he changed stars too quickly, his body screamed in protest.","Still, he stepped forward.","\"Seven-Star Revolving Body.\"","Seven stars lit up inside him at once, and he moved into the falling spearfield. The first spear grazed his shoulder, the second pierced through the starlight around his arm, and the third tore open a wound on his thigh.","Yet Orion kept moving. He punched one spear apart, kicked another aside, broke a third with his elbow, and smashed through the fourth with his shoulder. Starlight burst from his body over and over, and each time he should have slowed, he forced another star to rotate into position.","Aurelian’s eyes grew colder. \"Still moving?\"","Orion laughed through the blood. \"Unfortunately for you, yes.\"","He jumped. The second star pushed his speed beyond its previous limit, and the sixth star added crushing weight to his descent.","\"Second Star Step.\"","\"Sixth Star Falling Heaven Strike.\"","Orion dropped toward Aurelian like a collapsing star. Aurelian raised his palm.","\"Crownless Divine King.\"","The golden throne shattered, and its fragments flowed into his body as the dominion condensed instantly. The sacred halls vanished, the radiant pillars shrank, and the endless sun became a blazing crown behind him. Aurelian’s aura turned sharper and more unstable as all the dominion’s authority merged into his flesh.","He pointed upward.","\"Crownless Divine King, Light That Judges All Stars.\"","A beam of condensed golden-white judgment shot toward Orion. Orion did not dodge. The ninth star entered his fist.","\"Ninth Star Crown Fist.\"","His fist collided with the judgment beam.","Boom!","The explosion swallowed the center of the stage. Orion was thrown backward with blood spraying from his arm, but the judgment beam shattered as well. Aurelian stepped through the explosion, his speed far greater in the Crownless Divine King state.","\"Radiant Execution Step.\"","He appeared before Orion and thrust with a spear of condensed light.","\"Crownless Divine King, Sun-Piercing Verdict.\"","The spear drove toward Orion’s chest. Orion twisted aside, but his accumulated injuries left him half a breath too slow. The spear tore through the armor near his ribs and left a deep, bleeding wound. Aurelian followed with another attack at once.","\"Crownless Divine King, Solar Execution Array.\"","Dozens of golden-white blades formed around Orion and slashed toward him from every angle.","Orion’s face finally turned serious.","\"Nine Star Sovereign Body, Full Star Rotation.\"","All nine stars rotated through his body at terrifying speed, and he moved as though a star were being torn through nine different orbits at once. His fists broke the front blades, his knees shattered the lower ones, and his elbows destroyed the blades at his sides.","His shoulders smashed through two that came from behind. Even so, some still landed. Blood scattered across the stage, and Orion’s breathing grew heavier.","Aurelian pressed harder. He gave Orion no time to rest, and he gave him no room to speak. He attacked like a man trying to erase all memory of his own earlier humiliation.","\"Crownless Divine King, Final Luminance Judgment.\"","The enormous divine sword of golden-white light formed above the stage, and the spectators went silent. This attack had failed against Damian, and it had shattered uselessly against Max. But against Orion, it remained terrifying.","The divine sword descended, carrying the concentrated authority of Aurelian’s dominion, his bloodline power, and his Crownless Divine King state. The pressure was so heavy that even Orion’s star palace groaned beneath it.","Orion looked up. His body was wounded, his star power was strained, and his previous battles had taken too much from him. Yet his eyes were still bright.","He laughed softly. \"Good.\"","The nine stars inside his body began to gather, and the Nine Star Court elders watching from afar shot to their feet.","\"He cannot use that again.\"","\"His body will not hold.\"","\"Orion, do not force it.\"","But Orion could not hear them, and perhaps he would not have listened even if he could. He had fought Revona, and he had fought Ervin. He had been beaten down again and again by people whose paths were every bit as terrifying as his own.","Yet he had never accepted that his stars should stop shining simply because an opponent was stronger, stranger, or better rested.","He clenched his fist, and the nine stars collapsed inward.","\"Starfall Extinction.\"","The entire arena trembled.","This Starfall Extinction was different from the ones he had used against Revona and Ervin. It did not have the same fullness he could produce at his peak, and it did not have the same stable foundation.","It was rough, bloody, and dangerous to himself. Yet it carried something sharper than before. It carried will. Every star inside his body burned as though Orion were forcing them to shine even while cracked.","He rushed upward, and Starfall Extinction met Final Luminance Judgment.","Boom!","The collision split the stage in half. Golden-white divine light and collapsing star essence erupted together. Aurelian pressed both hands downward and poured more power into the divine sword, while Orion roared and drove his fist upward, the star essence layers within Starfall Extinction detonating one after another.","The first layer broke the outer divine light. The second layer cracked the judgment runes. The third layer forced the divine sword to tremble. The fourth layer shattered Orion’s own arm armor, and the fifth layer tore blood from his shoulder. But he did not stop.","Aurelian’s expression changed. \"How are you still pushing?\"","Orion looked up through the raging light, his teeth stained with blood and his smile fierce and bright. \"Because I am not done.\"","The sixth layer of Starfall Extinction erupted.","Crack!","Final Luminance Judgment split. The seventh layer followed, and the divine sword shattered.","Aurelian’s pupils contracted. Orion broke through the falling fragments of golden-white light and appeared before him, his fist still carrying the last remnant of collapsing star power.","Aurelian tried to retreat.","\"Radiant Ascension Step.\"","Orion’s left hand shot out and seized the edge of Aurelian’s radiant robe before he could fully escape. \"Not this time.\"","The eighth star entered Orion’s other fist.","\"Nine Star Sovereign Body, Eighth Star Collapse Fist.\"","The punch landed on Aurelian’s chest.","Boom!","Aurelian was blasted backward with golden-white blood spilling from his mouth. His Crownless Divine King state trembled violently, but he still did not fall. He raised both hands, his eyes filled with fury and disbelief.","\"Divine Dominion, Solar Execution Array.\"","The golden-white blades formed again. Orion staggered and nearly dropped to one knee. Then he stood.","Aurelian’s face twisted. \"Why do you refuse to fall?\"","Orion breathed heavily, and then he smiled. \"Because I already lost enough today.\"","He stepped forward as the nine stars behind him flickered. Not all of them were stable anymore, but they still answered him.","\"Because if I keep losing without taking one back, my master will laugh at me.\"","He stepped again, and the Solar Execution Array descended. Orion rushed straight into it. Blades cut his arms, light tore across his shoulder, and one radiant blade sliced across his side. But he kept moving.","\"Nine Star Sovereign Body, Final Orbit Break.\"","His body became a streak of unstable starlight, weaving through the execution array while taking every wound he could not avoid. The second star gave him speed, the fourth star changed his angle, and the sixth star added pressure. The ninth star stabilized his core just enough to keep him from collapsing.","Then he appeared before Aurelian again.","Aurelian’s eyes widened."]},{"number":1890,"title":"Chapter 1890: Orion Wins!","paragraphs":["Orion raised his fist. There was almost no star power left in him, so he gathered every last trace of it into a single point.","\"Nine Star Sovereign Body, Last Star Fist.\"","The fist struck Aurelian’s chest, and this time Aurelian’s remaining dominion broke. The burning crown behind him shattered, the Crownless Divine King state collapsed completely, and the Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion scattered into broken golden-white fragments.","Aurelian flew backward and crashed into the ground, carving a long trench across the stage before coming to rest near the edge.","Orion landed on one knee. His right arm trembled, and blood dripped from his chin. His aura flickered so weakly that many spectators wondered whether he would faint before the announcement could even arrive.","Aurelian tried to stand. His hand pressed against the cracked ground, and golden-white light flickered around him, but it shattered almost instantly.","He forced one knee beneath himself, only for his body to tremble and drop back down. His eyes were filled with humiliation, rage, and disbelief.","He had lost again. This time it had not been to Damian’s sword, and it had not been to Max’s strange immunity and hidden bloodline truth.","He had lost to Orion Starfall, a wounded opponent who had already been drained by earlier battles and still refused to fall until the very end.","Angelina Valerius looked down at the stage. \"Aurelian Lareth is unable to continue.\"","The screen above the arena changed.","[Winner: Orion Starfall.]","[Aurelian Lareth Defeated.]","For a moment, the Divine Realm was silent. Then the Nine Star Court erupted. Their disciples shouted so loudly that even the viewing formations trembled, and the elders who had been tense throughout the battle finally released long breaths.","Orion had not won cleanly, and he had not won easily. He had won while wounded, exhausted, bleeding, and nearly collapsing under the burden of his own technique. But he had won.","The screen updated.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Orion Starfall]","[Total Battles Fought: 22]","[Total Wins: 20]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Aurelian Lareth]","[Total Battles Fought: 21]","[Total Wins: 19]","On the stage, Orion slowly pushed himself up. He swayed once, then steadied himself with a laugh.","\"That was... harder than I wanted.\"","Rakan Thorne burst into laughter from his pillar. \"You look half-dead.\"","Orion turned his head slightly and smiled weakly. \"Only half. That means I can still brag.\"","Even Damian Voss’s eyes softened slightly as he looked at Orion. Revona watched in silence, though there was respect in her gaze. Ervin studied Orion a moment longer than usual as well.","He had defeated Orion before, but after witnessing this battle, he understood even more clearly that Orion Starfall’s greatest strength was not only his Nine Star Sovereign Body or his Starfall Extinction. It was the simple fact that he never truly stopped fighting.","Max stood on his pillar and looked at Orion with a faint smile.","Aurelian, by contrast, was carried back to his pillar by the transfer light in silence. The Divine Son’s face was pale and his aura unstable, and for the third time in this final stage, his pride had been broken in front of the entire Divine Realm.","The final competitive stage continued, but after this battle everyone understood one thing clearly. Orion Starfall might have lost before, and he might have been wounded and exhausted, yet as long as a single star inside him still burned, he remained dangerous enough to defeat even the Divine Son.","After Orion defeated Aurelian, the entire final competitive stage seemed to settle into a strange silence. It was not the silence of boredom. It was the silence that followed too many shocking results overturning expectation after expectation.","The Divine Son of the second elven faction had now suffered yet another defeat. Damian Voss had cut through his Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion. Max Morgan had made his light-based attacks look meaningless.","Now Orion Starfall, wounded and exhausted from his previous battles, had still forced his way through the full pressure of the Divine Son’s dominion and won through sheer refusal to fall.","Aurelian returned to his pillar in silence. His pale golden hair hung slightly across his face, and the golden-white radiance around his body flickered weakly as the laws of the Eternal Hourglass healed his injuries.","Yet no law could mend the damage done to his pride. His expression stayed cold, but that coldness had turned brittle. It no longer felt like the calm arrogance of a Divine Son who believed the world should kneel. It felt like the frozen surface of a lake concealing cracks beneath.","Orion, on the other hand, returned to his pillar and sat down at once with a tired laugh. His aura was unstable, his breathing was heavy, and several traces of golden-white light still clung to the wounds across his body.","Even so, his smile stayed bright. The Nine Star Court disciples across the Divine Realm were still cheering, and many who had watched him lose twice before now regarded him with renewed respect.","Orion Starfall had proven that his earlier defeats had never been proof of weakness. He had simply been fighting monsters from the very beginning.","Rakan Thorne looked at him from a nearby pillar and laughed loudly. \"You really do not know when to stay down.\"","Orion leaned back slightly and waved a weak hand. \"It was a fun battle.\"","Morgana Starveil smiled faintly. \"You say that after kneeling on it for half the battle?\"","Orion glanced at her and sighed. \"Witches should be more merciful to injured men.\"","Morgana’s smile deepened. \"Injured men should stop pretending they are heroic when they are half-dead.\"","Even a few tense participants could not help reacting to that exchange, but the light atmosphere lasted only a moment.","Everyone knew the final stage had not ended. The strongest names still had to finish their remaining battles, and some of the most important pairings had yet to appear. Max Morgan, Damian Voss, Revona, Ervin, and Kaiden Voidmere all still hung over the arena like mountains.","Angelina Valerius waited for the stage to finish restoring itself. The cracks left by Orion’s Last Star Fist closed, the burned marks from Aurelian’s Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion faded, and the final traces of star essence dissolved into the golden laws of the Eternal Hourglass. Then she raised her hand again.","\"The next battle will now be selected.\"","The giant screen above the arena began to spin, and the atmosphere tightened immediately. Names flashed across the screen, among them Max Morgan, Damian Voss, Revona, Kaiden Voidmere, Ervin, Rakan Thorne, Orion Starfall, Morgana Starveil, Rosaline Lunara, Selene Vaeloria, and Aurelian Lareth.","Each passing name carried its own weight, but by now the audience had grown especially sensitive to the top-tier pairings. Whenever the names of two monsters appeared close together, the whole Divine Realm held its breath.","The first name slowed, and then it stopped.","[Revona]"]},{"number":1891,"title":"Chapter 1891: Revona vs Kaiden!","paragraphs":["The arena went quiet at once. Revona opened her eyes on her pillar. Her face remained calm and pale, and the Void Origin Eyes carried their usual unfathomable stillness. She had already proven herself one of the strongest geniuses of the final stage.","She had defeated Orion after being pushed to the edge by Starfall Extinction, and she had defeated Rakan by adapting her Void Origin Realm against his terrifying War God Body. She had erased, nullified, hollowed, and returned attacks to nothing again and again, until even the top geniuses treated her with caution.","Her strength did not come from loud displays. It came from the terrifying certainty that no attack was guaranteed to matter once it entered the range of her eyes.","Across the Divine Realm, many spectators leaned forward.","\"Revona again.\"","\"Who will she fight this time?\"","\"She is still undefeated, right?\"","\"Yes. She defeated Orion and Rakan. Her Void Origin Eyes are simply monstrous.\"","\"Only Max, Damian, Ervin, and Kaiden might truly pressure her now.\"","As though answering that thought, the second name began to slow. The light passed over Damian Voss, then over Ervin, and then over Max Morgan. Then it stopped.","[Kaiden Voidmere]","For a breath, the entire arena fell silent. Then the giant screen enlarged both names.","[Final Competitive Stage]","[Revona vs Kaiden Voidmere]","A strange pressure descended over the Eternal Hourglass. This was not a battle of brute strength, and it was not a clash of light and star power. It was a confrontation between two of the most mysterious spatial and void-based geniuses in the entire conference. On one side stood Revona, the owner of the Void Origin Eyes.","On the other stood Kaiden Voidmere, the supreme genius of the Grand Void Sanctum. One of them could nullify, erase, and return power to nothing. The other could fold space, create endless corridors, exile attacks beyond return, and trap opponents inside the Grand Void Labyrinth.","The very nature of the battle felt difficult to predict. Would Revona’s Void Origin Eyes erase Kaiden’s spatial folds before they formed? Would Kaiden’s Grand Void Labyrinth split the battlefield into too many layers for her eyes to fully control?","Could the Void Origin Realm drag spatial attacks into nothingness before they reached her, or could Kaiden use exile routes and folded corridors to avoid being caught by her nullification entirely?","The Divine Realm erupted into discussion.","\"This might be one of the strangest battles so far.\"","\"Void Origin Eyes against the Grand Void Labyrinth.\"","\"Revona can erase attacks, but Kaiden’s attacks do not always come from the same space.\"","\"If Kaiden splits the battlefield into layered corridors, can her eyes erase all of them at once?\"","\"But if Revona opens the Void Origin Realm, even spatial layers might be dragged toward nothingness.\"","\"Do not forget that Kaiden pushed Ervin to reveal the Gate of the Second Depth.\"","\"And Revona defeated Orion and Rakan. She is not someone who can be handled with ordinary space tricks.\"","At the Grand Void Sanctum’s viewing platform, the disciples who had been disappointed after Kaiden’s loss to Ervin grew focused once more.","Kaiden had lost to Max because Max was nearly the worst possible opponent for him, a man who possessed deeper mastery of the Void Genesis Art and a body that could ignore most spatial attacks.","Against Ervin, however, Kaiden had revealed his true power. His Grand Void Labyrinth had driven the Abyssal Origin Descent to its edge and forced Ervin to open the Gate of the Second Depth. No one who had watched that battle could still treat Kaiden as inferior.","Now he would face Revona, and the elders of the Grand Void Sanctum looked solemn.","\"Her eyes are dangerous.\"","\"They do not merely defend. They erase the foundation of techniques.\"","\"Kaiden must not let her see the complete structure of the labyrinth too early.\"","\"Layered attacks. Delayed corridors. False routes. He must keep the battlefield changing.\"","Elsewhere in the Divine Realm, those connected to Revona watched with equal seriousness. Kaiden was not Rakan, whose strength could be dulled through careful nullification and rhythm disruption.","He was not Orion, whose star power could be erased when the timing was right. Kaiden’s power flowed through folded space, hidden layers, shifted positions, delayed routes, and exile corridors.","If Revona misjudged even one layer, an attack could appear from behind her, beneath her, or out of a space that had not existed a breath earlier.","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, the top geniuses grew serious as well.","Rakan Thorne crossed his arms and grinned. \"I hate both of their fighting styles.\"","Orion, still recovering, laughed weakly. \"That is because neither of them is polite enough to stand still and get punched.\"","Rakan snorted. \"Exactly. Very disrespectful.\"","Morgana Starveil looked at the names with interest. \"This one might be decided by perception. If Revona reads the labyrinth fast enough, Kaiden will suffer. If Kaiden hides the true route of his attacks well enough, Revona will be forced to defend blindly.\"","Ervin watched Kaiden quietly. \"His Grand Void Labyrinth is difficult to break. Even the Abyssal Origin Descent had to go deeper.\"","Damian Voss said nothing, but his eyes stayed fixed on the screen.","Max watched with interest as well. He understood Kaiden’s path better than most after their battle. Kaiden’s weakness against him had made that result look one-sided, but that weakness would not exist against Revona. Here, Kaiden could fully wield space as a weapon, a battlefield, a prison, and an escape route all at once.","At the same time, Max had seen Revona’s Void Origin Eyes bypass the very logic that should have protected other techniques. Her power was not ordinary defense. It came closer to denying the existence of an attack before it could fully become meaningful. This battle would not be simple.","On her pillar, Revona slowly stood. Her long hair drifted gently behind her, and her eyes remained calm, almost empty. She did not look excited, and she did not look nervous. Yet the void-like stillness around her deepened, and the space near her body seemed to grow quieter, as though even movement hesitated near her gaze.","Kaiden Voidmere stood as well, and silver-gray ripples spread from beneath his feet. His expression was composed, but his eyes carried the seriousness of a man with no intention of underestimating his opponent.","After battling Max and Ervin, his prestige had not fallen. If anything, people now understood how unfortunate his matchups had been. Against Revona, he had a chance to show a different side of his strength.","Kaiden looked toward Revona and spoke calmly. \"Your eyes are famous.\"","Revona looked back at him. \"Your labyrinth is troublesome.\"","A faint smile touched Kaiden’s face. \"Then this should be meaningful.\"","Revona’s eyes flickered slightly. \"Yes.\"","The brief exchange was calm, yet the tension beneath it was enough to silence even the loudest spectators.","Angelina Valerius looked toward the two of them. The laws of the Eternal Hourglass gathered around the stage, and the barrier brightened again. It was as though the arena itself was bracing for a battle that might not damage the stage in the usual way, but could twist, erase, fold, and hollow the space within it beyond recognition.","Above the stage, the announcement still shone.","[Final Competitive Stage]","[Revona vs Kaiden Voidmere]","Angelina raised her hand.","\"Revona.\"","\"Kaiden Voidmere.\"","\"Enter the stage.\""]},{"number":1892,"title":"Chapter 1892: Injuring Revona!","paragraphs":["The two beams of light descended at the same time.","Revona appeared on one side of the central stage, her posture quiet and her eyes calm. There was no grand pressure around her, no violent aura, and no obvious sign that she had already defeated monsters like Orion Starfall and Rakan Thorne.","Yet the stillness surrounding her carried a danger that made many spectators instinctively hold their breath. Her Void Origin Eyes were open, pale and unfathomable, as though every attack that entered her sight had already begun to vanish.","Kaiden Voidmere appeared opposite her. Silver-gray ripples spread beneath his feet, and the space around him folded softly, almost respectfully.","Compared to the calm he had shown against weaker opponents, his expression now was far more focused. After battling Max and Ervin, he had already suffered two defeats, yet neither had broken his confidence.","Against Max, he had been countered by a deeper mastery of the same path and a body almost immune to spatial attacks. Against Ervin, he had pushed the Abyssal Origin Descent all the way to the Gate of the Second Depth before losing.","Now he faced Revona, a different kind of monster entirely.","The entire Divine Realm watched closely.","Angelina Valerius raised her hand.","[Battle Begins.]","Kaiden moved first.","\"Void Genesis Art, Empty Step.\"","His body vanished from the stage without a ripple. Revona’s eyes shifted slightly, and a faint void light appeared in her pupils. Kaiden reappeared behind her with one palm already descending toward the space near her shoulder.","\"Void Genesis Art, Space Burial Palm.\"","The space around Revona sank instantly, as if an invisible tomb had opened around her body. The attack did not need to strike her flesh directly. It sought to bury her position in folded space, compressing the battlefield around her until movement became impossible.","Revona turned her head slightly, and the Void Origin Eyes brightened. The sinking space trembled, and then the buried region began to hollow out. Kaiden’s palm fell through emptiness. Revona stepped sideways, and the Space Burial Palm vanished, as though the foundation of the technique had been erased before it could close completely.","Kaiden did not look surprised.","\"Void Genesis Art, Sevenfold Severing Line.\"","Seven invisible spatial cuts appeared around Revona at once. They came from different angles, different distances, and slightly delayed spatial layers. Against most opponents, even perceiving one line would already be difficult, and perceiving all seven at once was nearly impossible.","But Revona’s eyes moved. One line vanished, then another, and then a third. The first three spatial cuts were erased before they reached her. The fourth and fifth dimmed and lost most of their cutting force.","The sixth was diverted by a hollow ripple around her body. Only the seventh slipped through her range at the last moment and grazed her sleeve, drawing a thin line of blood across her forearm.","The arena stirred.","\"He injured her.\"","\"Only a shallow wound, but he still reached her.\"","\"Kaiden’s attacks come from too many layers. Even Revona cannot erase everything instantly.\"","Revona looked at the blood on her arm, and then back at Kaiden. \"Good.\"","Kaiden’s eyes sharpened slightly. \"I will take that as praise.\"","The space beneath him opened into multiple corridors.","\"Void Genesis Art, Nine Hollow Routes.\"","Nine silver-gray paths appeared across the stage, each bending through a different spatial layer. Kaiden’s figure appeared at the end of all nine paths at once. Some were true projections, some were delayed positions, and some were future routes that had not fully formed. To ordinary eyes, it was impossible to tell which path carried the real attack.","Revona stood still as her Void Origin Eyes scanned the battlefield.","Kaiden attacked.","\"Grand Void Sanctum, Hollow Route Palm.\"","Nine palms descended from nine positions. Revona erased four, and two more collapsed under void ripples. But three reached her defensive range at the same time.","She raised her hand.","\"Void Origin Palm.\"","A hollow palm seal spread outward and weakened the three incoming attacks, but Kaiden’s true body slipped through the weakest route and appeared directly before her.","\"Void Genesis Art, Origin Fold Strike.\"","His palm struck toward her chest. Revona’s eyes narrowed. The attack began to disappear, but it did not vanish fully. Kaiden had hidden the real strike inside a folded route, so her eyes erased the outer technique first while the inner force continued forward. The palm struck her shoulder and pushed her back several steps.","The crowd gasped. Revona had retreated.","Kaiden stood where he was with silver-gray light around his hand. Revona’s shoulder trembled faintly, yet her expression stayed calm.","\"You hide your attack well.\"","Kaiden replied, \"Your eyes force me to.\"","The moment his words ended, the atmosphere changed. Kaiden raised both hands, and silver-gray light expanded behind him as the battlefield began splitting into countless folded planes. Corridors appeared in the air. Mirrors of space opened and closed.","The sky seemed to bend into several layers while the ground stretched and shrank at the same time. Every direction became unreliable.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path.\"","The silver-gray void expanded fully.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth.\"","Boom!","The entire stage transformed. Revona stood at the center of a labyrinth built from folded space, hidden passages, mirror routes, exile corridors, and delayed attack points. Every wall was also a doorway, every doorway was also a blade, and every blade could become a prison.","The Grand Void Labyrinth did not try to overwhelm an enemy with one massive attack. It turned the whole battlefield into a trap where an opponent could never be sure where the danger truly came from.","Kaiden’s voice echoed from every direction.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth, Corridor of Ten Thousand Cuts.\"","The spatial corridors opened, and invisible cuts poured toward Revona from every layer. Her Void Origin Eyes shone, and cut after cut vanished.","But the Ten Thousand Cuts did not all arrive together. Some came now, some came a breath later, and some appeared behind her only after being reflected through three folded corridors.","Some moved toward her, vanished, and reappeared beneath her feet. Revona erased dozens of them, and then hundreds, yet several still slipped through. Blood appeared on her shoulder, another wound opened near her waist, and a thin cut appeared across her cheek."]},{"number":1893,"title":"Chapter 1893: Kaiden’s Terrifying attack!","paragraphs":["The arena erupted in shock.","\"Kaiden is pushing her back!\"","\"The Grand Void Labyrinth is too difficult to read!\"","\"Even Void Origin Eyes cannot erase every attack if the structure keeps changing!\"","On the pillars, the top geniuses watched seriously.","Rakan Thorne grinned, though tension lived in his eyes. \"I still hate this kind of fight.\"","Orion Starfall smiled weakly. \"Because you cannot punch a corridor that is not there yet?\"","Rakan snorted. \"Exactly.\"","Damian Voss looked at the battlefield with narrowed eyes. \"Kaiden is forcing her to divide her perception.\"","Ervin nodded faintly. \"If she reads one layer, he attacks from another.\"","Max watched quietly. He had fought Kaiden himself and knew how dangerous the Grand Void Labyrinth became when the opponent could not ignore spatial attacks. Against him, Kaiden’s path had been suppressed by a cruel mismatch.","Against Revona, the labyrinth finally revealed its true terror. Revona could erase attacks, but she still needed to perceive the foundation of what she erased, and Kaiden kept shifting that foundation before her eyes could fully lock onto it.","On the stage, Revona raised one hand.","\"Void Origin Realm.\"","The world behind her became hollow. There was no sky, no ground, no sound, and no color. There was only origin-level emptiness.","The moment the Void Origin Realm appeared, the Grand Void Labyrinth trembled. Several spatial corridors lost their edges and faded into nothingness. Mirror routes dimmed, and delayed attack points collapsed before releasing their stored force.","Kaiden’s expression grew serious.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth, Infinite Corridor Rotation.\"","The labyrinth began rotating. Every corridor changed position, every wall became a different path, and every exile point moved away from Revona’s gaze before her Void Origin Realm could fully hollow it. The clash turned terrifyingly strange. Revona’s emptiness erased routes while Kaiden’s labyrinth created new ones faster than ordinary minds could follow.","Revona stepped forward.","\"Void Origin Realm, Hollowing Wave.\"","A silent wave spread from her, and the nearest corridors vanished. Kaiden appeared far above her through a mirror path.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth, Exile Palm.\"","His palm descended. The space around Revona’s left side disappeared for a breath. Her balance shifted, and three spatial cuts came from her blind angle. Revona turned her eyes sharply. Two cuts vanished, but the third landed, and blood splashed from her arm.","Kaiden pressed harder.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth, Mirror Burial.\"","Dozens of mirrored spaces appeared around Revona, each one reflecting her from a different angle. Then the mirrors collapsed inward, trying to bury her real position among false layers and seal her inside a distorted spatial grave.","Revona’s Void Origin Realm expanded. The first mirrors dissolved, then the second layer, and then the third. But Kaiden’s attack held five hidden layers. The fourth layer collapsed around her and forced her body half a step into folded space. The fifth layer appeared behind her as a silver-gray blade.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth, Backflow Severance.\"","The blade struck toward her back. Revona’s eyes widened slightly, and for the first time she moved quickly. Her body turned, and the Void Origin Eyes erased half the blade, but the remaining force still cut across her shoulder. Blood stained her clothes, and the impact drove her several steps forward.","A rare silence fell over the arena. Revona had been wounded several times. Kaiden had truly pushed her.","The Grand Void Sanctum disciples shouted loudly.","\"Senior Brother Kaiden!\"","\"Suppress her!\"","\"Break the Void Origin Eyes!\"","Kaiden did not celebrate. His breathing had grown heavier. Maintaining the Grand Void Labyrinth while constantly changing routes to escape Revona’s erasure consumed enormous energy.","He had wounded her repeatedly, but every failed corridor was erased completely, and each route lost to the Void Origin Realm could not be restored easily.","Revona stood at the center of the labyrinth with blood flowing from several wounds, yet her expression had not changed. She looked at Kaiden.","\"Your labyrinth is dangerous.\"","Kaiden replied calmly, \"Your eyes are worse.\"","Revona raised her head slightly. \"Then I should look more carefully.\"","The moment she spoke, the Void Origin Eyes changed. They grew deeper. The pale emptiness in her pupils no longer merely erased what came toward her. It began to trace the routes behind the attacks, following each spatial cut back through the folded corridors, mirror layers, and hidden paths that had created it.","Kaiden’s expression shifted slightly.","Revona lifted one hand.","\"Void Origin Eyes, Trace To Nothing.\"","A spatial cut flew toward her. She did not erase only the cut. Her eyes followed its route backward and hollowed the corridor that had produced it, and the corridor vanished. Another attack came from below. Revona’s gaze shifted, the attack disappeared, and the folded plane beneath it collapsed into nothingness.","Kaiden immediately changed tactics.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth, Thousand False Roads.\"","Thousands of narrow corridors appeared at once, spreading in every direction like a silver-gray web. Only a few held real attacks. The rest were false routes meant to overwhelm Revona’s perception and make her waste power erasing empty paths.","Revona stood still, and her eyes slowly turned.","\"Void Origin Realm, Silent Eye Field.\"","The hollow world behind her expanded into the labyrinth itself, and a strange silence spread. The false roads began disappearing on their own, not all at once, but steadily.","One by one, the corridors that held no true force faded under the pressure of origin emptiness, while the real routes grew clearer because they carried Kaiden’s intent. For the first time, the endless complexity of the Grand Void Labyrinth began to thin.","Kaiden’s face turned pale.","\"She is adapting,\" Morgana Starveil murmured from her pillar.","Damian Voss nodded slightly. \"That is what makes her dangerous.\"","Ervin’s gaze deepened. \"Kaiden pushed her to the edge, but now she has begun reading the labyrinth.\"","Max watched with clear focus. Revona had not won because Kaiden was weaker. She was learning the battlefield while wounded, and that was terrifying in its own way.","Kaiden raised his hands again, knowing he could not delay any further. The Grand Void Labyrinth condensed. Every remaining corridor, mirror, wall, and exile point began gathering into one enormous silver-gray passage behind Revona. Its edges were dark, unstable, and frighteningly deep.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth, Final Corridor.\"","The passage opened completely.","\"Void Beyond Return.\"","The deepest exile path Kaiden could currently create appeared beneath Revona’s feet. The moment it opened, the space around her body vanished downward, and Revona began to sink. Her Void Origin Realm pressed against it, but the Final Corridor was no ordinary attack.","It was an exile route built from the deepest layers of Kaiden’s Pseudo Cosmic Path, and it did not try to cut, crush, or pierce her. It tried to remove her from the battlefield entirely.","The spectators held their breath. Revona’s lower body sank into the corridor, then her waist, and then her chest."]},{"number":1894,"title":"Chapter 1894: Last few battles!","paragraphs":["Kaiden pressed both hands downward as blood appeared at the corner of his mouth from the strain. \"Go.\"","The Final Corridor pulled harder, and for a moment it looked as though Revona would truly be exiled. Then her eyes shone with a terrifying emptiness.","\"Void Origin Realm.\"","Her voice was calm.","\"Return To Nothing.\"","The hollow world behind her condensed into a single point, and that point appeared inside the Final Corridor itself.","Kaiden’s eyes widened. The Final Corridor did not shatter immediately. Instead, it began losing meaning. Its direction faded, its destination vanished, and its exile authority hollowed out from within. The path that was supposed to lead beyond return no longer had a place to return from, nor a place to send her to.","The corridor trembled violently. Revona stopped sinking. Then she stepped out. Her face was pale and blood flowed down her arm, but her gaze remained steady.","Kaiden tried to shift away. Revona looked at him.","\"Trace To Nothing.\"","The corridor beneath Kaiden’s feet vanished, and his escape route disappeared. He tried to open another, but Revona’s eyes followed the intent and erased the new route before it could form. Kaiden’s pupils contracted. For the first time in the battle, he had nowhere to move.","Revona raised her hand, and a hollow ripple spread from her palm.","\"Void Origin Realm, Hollow Return.\"","The ripple crossed the remaining distance and struck Kaiden’s chest. It did not explode, and it did not blast him away with force. It erased the spatial support around his body, hollowed the foundation of the Grand Void Labyrinth, and returned the last stable route beneath him to nothingness.","Kaiden’s Pseudo Cosmic Path trembled once, and then it collapsed.","The silver-gray labyrinth shattered. Corridors broke apart, mirrors faded, and exile points vanished. The stage returned to normal.","Kaiden stood in front of Revona with his aura unstable and his silver-gray robes torn. He tried to raise his hand one more time, but no corridor answered him quickly enough. Revona’s hand stopped before his chest, and the emptiness around her palm made the air between them disappear.","The entire arena fell silent.","Kaiden looked at her hand, and then at her eyes. After several breaths, he smiled faintly.","\"You learned the labyrinth faster than I hoped.\"","Revona’s voice was quiet. \"You almost exiled me.\"","\"Almost is not victory.\"","\"No.\"","Kaiden lowered his hand. \"I surrender.\"","Angelina Valerius announced the result calmly.","[Winner: Revona.]","[Kaiden Voidmere Defeated.]","The screen above the arena updated.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Revona]","[Total Battles Fought: 21]","[Total Wins: 21]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Kaiden Voidmere]","[Total Battles Fought: 22]","[Total Wins: 19]","The Divine Realm erupted. Kaiden Voidmere had lost again, but no one dared call him weak. He had pushed Revona closer to danger than almost anyone besides Orion. His Grand Void Labyrinth had wounded her, disrupted her Void Origin Eyes, and nearly sealed her inside the Void Beyond Return.","For a long stretch of the battle, it had truly looked as though Kaiden might hand Revona her first defeat. But Revona had adapted. She had traced his hidden routes, hollowed his false paths, survived the deepest exile corridor, and finally erased the foundation of the Grand Void Labyrinth itself.","On the pillars, Orion Starfall laughed softly despite his exhaustion. \"That woman is unreasonably strong.\"","Rakan Thorne snorted. \"Both of them are unreasonable.\"","Morgana Starveil smiled faintly. \"The difference is that Revona becomes more dangerous the longer she watches you.\"","Ervin nodded slightly. \"That is why she won.\"","Max watched Revona quietly. Her aura was clearly weaker than before, and the wounds across her body proved how close the fight had become, yet her eyes remained calm. Kaiden had almost pushed her to her limit, but he had not crossed it.","The transfer light descended and returned both fighters to their pillars. Revona sat down after arriving, her pale face showing the cost of victory. Kaiden also sat quietly, his expression calm despite the defeat.","The battle had ended. Revona remained undefeated, and the final competitive stage moved one step closer to its true climax.","After Revona defeated Kaiden Voidmere, the atmosphere of the final competitive stage grew even more complicated. Kaiden had lost, yet the way people looked at him had changed once again. Against Max, his spatial path had been suppressed before it could reveal its full danger.","Against Ervin, he had forced the Abyssal Origin Descent into the Gate of the Second Depth. Against Revona, he had pushed one of the strongest undefeated geniuses in the entire conference close to the edge, cutting through her defenses, forcing her to adapt, and nearly sending her into the Void Beyond Return.","He had lost in the end, but the Divine Realm now understood clearly that Kaiden Voidmere could not be judged by his record alone.","Revona returned to her pillar with her aura unstable and her face paler than before. The laws of the Eternal Hourglass began repairing her wounds, but everyone could see that the battle had cost her.","Her Void Origin Eyes remained calm, yet a faint exhaustion hid in their depths. She had defeated Orion, Rakan, and now Kaiden. Each victory had been real, and each one had proven her strength. But each had also drained her, and the final competitive stage still had not ended.","Angelina Valerius waited only until the stage restored itself before continuing, and the battles that followed moved faster.","Several lesser participants were matched against the top geniuses and were quickly defeated. Most of them no longer tried to force a miracle. By this point, everyone had seen enough to recognize when a gap was impossible to cross.","A spear genius from a hidden sect surrendered to Damian after three exchanges once his spear intent was cut apart before it could fully form. A beast-blooded warrior tried to challenge Max with raw strength, only to be stopped by one palm and pushed outside the fighting zone without Max using any special ability.","Morgana Starveil defeated a flame cultivator by placing a curse on his spiritual fire, and Rosaline Lunara used the Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary to suppress a poison-path genius and forced him to surrender before his poison mist could spread across the stage.","[Winner: Damian Voss.]","[Winner: Max Morgan.]","[Winner: Morgana Starveil.]","[Winner: Rosaline Lunara.]","The screen kept updating. The battle counts were approaching the end, and the pressure at the top grew sharper with every result.","Then another important match appeared.","[Ervin vs Fin Arclight]","Fin entered the stage with his Pale Eclipse Burial already stirring around him. He had lost several important matches, yet his strength remained dangerous. The moment the battle began, he opened the Pale Eclipse Field and tried to bury Ervin’s senses beneath moonless darkness. The pale eclipse spread in silence, dimming the stage until even the light of the Eternal Hourglass seemed to lose its warmth.","But Ervin’s response was direct. He summoned the Abyssal Origin Descent before the eclipse could fully close, and the black sea rose beneath the moonless field.","Fin’s eclipse was built to bury perception, sever rhythm, and suppress an enemy inside pale darkness, but Ervin’s abyss did not need ordinary sight. The moment the broken gate appeared, the Pale Eclipse Field began sinking from below.","Fin used \"Pale Eclipse Burial, Moonless Descent,\" trying to crush Ervin before the gate opened wider, but Ervin answered with \"Abyssal Origin Descent, Gate of the First Depth,\" and the moonless blade sank into the black sea.","Fin fought fiercely and changed angles again and again, yet his strongest eclipse power could not escape the pull of the abyss. In the end, Ervin’s spear stopped before his chest, and Fin surrendered with a grim expression."]},{"number":1895,"title":"Chapter 1895: Damian vs Kaiden!","paragraphs":["[Winner: Ervin.]","[Fin Arclight Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Ervin]","[Total Battles Fought: 21]","[Total Wins: 21]","After that came another matchup that drew attention.","[Rakan Thorne vs Morgana Starveil]","Morgana’s Star-Curse Labyrinth opened immediately, filling the arena with violet-black mirrors, starry curse threads, and witch symbols that tried to twist Rakan’s movement.","Against ordinary close-combat fighters, this would have been a nightmare, since every step forward would trigger another curse and every punch would be redirected or weakened by star-bound witchcraft.","But Rakan had already suffered too many losses against the top monsters, and his mood was clearly terrible. He opened the First Limit, then the Second Limit, and charged straight through the curse field.","Morgana tried to slow him with \"Star-Curse Labyrinth, Witch Mirror Binding,\" then followed with \"Nameless Star Misfortune,\" but Rakan’s War God Body burned so violently that he broke through the curse layers by brute force.","When Morgana finally tried to deepen the labyrinth, Rakan opened the Third Limit and crushed three curse mirrors with one punch.","Morgana clicked her tongue and surrendered before he could close the distance completely.","[Winner: Rakan Thorne.]","[Morgana Starveil Defeated.]","Rakan returned to his pillar with a grin, though the curse marks on his arms were still fading.","\"You witches are annoying,\" he said.","Morgana smiled faintly despite her loss. \"And you body cultivators are far too stubborn to be elegant.\"","Rakan laughed. \"Good. Elegance does not break bones.\"","The next notable match came soon after.","[Revona vs Rosaline Lunara]","Rosaline’s Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary unfolded with beautiful brilliance, filling the arena with rose-gold light, falling petals, radiant palaces, and sovereign seals. She did not hold back. She knew Revona’s Void Origin Eyes were dangerous, so she did not rely on one large attack.","Instead, she used layered suppression, spreading \"Dawn Edict, First Seal,\" \"Dawn Edict, Second Seal,\" and \"Dawn Edict, Third Seal\" across different points of the battlefield while using the sanctuary itself to rebuild whatever Revona erased.","For a short time, it worked. Revona erased one seal, and Rosaline created two more. Revona hollowed the petal chains, and the sanctuary formed new bindings from another direction. Rosaline had learned from her earlier defeats, and this time she did not try to overpower Revona with one decisive strike.","She tried to drown her in repeated sovereign control instead.","But Revona’s eyes stayed too calm. She allowed Rosaline to build the sanctuary wider, then opened the Void Origin Realm and erased the foundation of the sealing structure one layer at a time.","When Rosaline used \"Final Dawn Edict, Sovereign Rose Spear,\" Revona did not clash with it directly. She used \"Void Origin Realm, Return To Nothing\" in a far smaller form than the one she had used against Orion, hollowing the spear’s authority before it could fully pierce her defense.","Rosaline’s face turned pale, but she smiled bitterly and lowered her hands. \"I surrender.\"","[Winner: Revona.]","[Rosaline Lunara Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Revona]","[Total Battles Fought: 21]","[Total Wins: 21]","The undefeated records still belonged to only a few people. Max Morgan, Damian Voss, and Revona stood among them. Every time those names appeared on the ranking projection, the arena felt the same pressure.","Everyone knew the final stretch would eventually force some of them to collide. The round-robin stage allowed no hiding. There were no brackets to avoid a bad matchup, no luck to carry someone around an opponent, and no excuse once the names were called.","Then another powerful battle appeared.","[Orion Starfall vs Morgana Starveil]","Orion was still recovering from his battle with Aurelian, and Morgana tried to take advantage of that at once. She opened the Star-Curse Labyrinth and used curse threads to slow the circulation of Orion’s star power.","For several exchanges, Orion’s movement was restricted, and his Nine Star Sovereign Body flickered under the pressure of the curses.","But Orion had already fought too many strange paths to be caught so easily now. He smiled, opened the Second Star Step, shifted his star rhythm three times in a single breath, and broke the curse pattern by constantly changing which star powered which part of his body.","Morgana’s eyes narrowed when she realized he was using his own unstable condition as a weapon, making his star rhythm difficult to predict because even he was forcing it to move beyond its normal limit.","In the end, Orion used \"Nine Star Sovereign Body, Seven-Star Revolving Impact\" to break three layers of the labyrinth, then forced Morgana to surrender with \"Ninth Star Crown Fist.\" He did not use Starfall Extinction, and everyone could tell he was preserving what little recovery he had left.","[Winner: Orion Starfall.]","[Morgana Starveil Defeated.]","The next battle moved quickly as well.","[Max Morgan vs Fin Arclight]","Fin’s expression turned extremely ugly the moment he saw Max’s name beside his own. Still, he entered the stage and opened Pale Eclipse Burial directly. Pale darkness swallowed the arena, and the Moonless Descent blade formed above Max’s head with enough force to threaten most top geniuses.","Max did not draw Dragonheart, and he did not use the Emotion Severing Path. He simply raised one hand, and a seven-colored lightning glow flickered faintly around his fingers.","The destructive pressure of Divine King Punishment did not fully descend, yet even that faint trace was enough to make Fin’s pale eclipse tremble. Max flicked his finger, and the Moonless Descent blade shattered before it could fall.","Fin stared at him for one breath. Then he surrendered.","[Winner: Max Morgan.]","[Fin Arclight Defeated.]","No one mocked Fin for it. At this stage, surrendering before Max when the gap was so obvious was not cowardice. It was survival.","The records continued rising.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Max Morgan]","[Total Battles Fought: 20]","[Total Wins: 20]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Damian Voss]","[Total Battles Fought: 20]","[Total Wins: 20]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Revona]","[Total Battles Fought: 21]","[Total Wins: 21]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Ervin]","[Total Battles Fought: 21]","[Total Wins: 21]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Kaiden Voidmere]","[Total Battles Fought: 22]","[Total Wins: 19]","By now, the entire Divine Realm could feel that the final stage was approaching its climax. The easy battles had nearly disappeared. The ranking table had begun settling into a terrifying shape, though the top positions still depended on the remaining collisions among the strongest.","Max, Damian, Ervin and Revona remained undefeated. Kaiden had suffered more losses because his matchups were brutal, yet every battle he fought proved that his true strength still belonged among the highest tier.","Then Angelina Valerius raised her hand once again, and the giant screen above the arena began spinning. This time, the atmosphere grew tense even before the first name appeared.","The light slowed, and the first name stopped.","[Damian Voss]","The Sword God Palace disciples immediately went silent with expectation.","The second name continued rotating. It passed over Max Morgan, then over Revona, and then over Ervin. Then it slowed and stopped.","[Kaiden Voidmere]","For a breath, the Eternal Hourglass became completely still. Then the screen enlarged both names.","[Final Competitive Stage]","[Damian Voss vs Kaiden Voidmere]","A wave of excitement spread through the Divine Realm. Damian Voss, the undefeated sword sovereign of the Sword God Palace, would face Kaiden Voidmere, the supreme genius of the Grand Void Sanctum whose Grand Void Labyrinth had pushed both Ervin and Revona to reveal deeper strength.","This was another clash of two terrifying paths, sword against space, with Sword Sovereign Heaven set against the Grand Void Labyrinth. One path could cut through force, law, rhythm, and authority.","The other could fold the battlefield, create endless corridors, exile positions, and make distance itself meaningless.","On his pillar, Kaiden slowly opened his eyes. Damian Voss looked toward him calmly. Neither spoke at first, and the entire Divine Realm leaned closer to the screens.","Angelina Valerius looked at both of them and announced the next battle.","\"Damian Voss.\"","\"Kaiden Voidmere.\"","\"Enter the stage.\""]},{"number":1896,"title":"Chapter 1896: Damian vs Kaiden!","paragraphs":["Two beams of light descended from above the arena.","Damian Voss appeared on one side of the central stage with his sword resting quietly at his waist. His expression was still calm, almost too calm, as though the battle before him was not one of the most important matches left in the final competitive stage.","Yet everyone who had watched him fight already knew that Damian’s calmness was more frightening than most people’s rage. His sword did not need loud pressure to make others cautious. The moment he stood there, the air around the stage seemed to grow thinner and sharper.","Kaiden Voidmere appeared opposite him. Silver-gray ripples spread beneath his feet, folding and unfolding the space around him in quiet waves. He had already suffered defeats against Max, Ervin, and Revona, yet those losses had not damaged his reputation. Instead, they had revealed just how terrible his matchups had been.","Against Max, his space power had been countered by someone with deeper mastery and almost natural immunity to spatial attacks.","Against Ervin, he had forced the Abyssal Origin Descent into the Gate of the Second Depth.","Against Revona, he had almost exiled one of the strongest undefeated geniuses into the Void Beyond Return before she adapted and turned the battle around.","Now he stood before Damian Voss. It was sword against space, Sword Sovereign Heaven against the Grand Void Labyrinth.","The Divine Realm held its breath.","Kaiden looked at Damian and spoke first. \"I have been waiting for this battle.\"","Damian replied calmly, \"You can say the same for me.\"","Kaiden’s eyes narrowed slightly. \"Then this battle will depend on whether your sword can cut through my space.\"","Damian’s hand rested on the hilt of his sword. \"We will see.\"","Kaiden’s silver-gray aura deepened. \"You look confident?\"","Damian looked at him quietly. \"I have participated in this conference with only one goal, and that is to win this conference.\"","The words were simple, but the moment they fell, the atmosphere on the stage tightened.","Angelina Valerius raised her hand.","[Battle Begins.]","Kaiden moved first.","\"Void Genesis Art, Empty Step.\"","His figure vanished without disturbing the air. In the same instant, dozens of folded spatial ripples appeared around Damian. Some hovered above him, some waited beneath his feet, some lurked behind his shoulders, and some sat beside his sword arm. They did not attack immediately. They merely opened like hidden mouths, waiting for the exact moment to release their killing force.","Damian drew his sword.","\"Silent Sword Art, First Cut, Parting Wind.\"","A single slash swept outward. The slash looked simple, yet every ripple it touched was cut apart before it could fully unfold. Seven spatial folds broke at the same time, and the lines hiding within them vanished as though they had been severed from their source.","Kaiden appeared far to the left with one palm raised.","\"Void Genesis Art, Sevenfold Severing Line.\"","Seven invisible spatial cuts shot toward Damian from seven different layers. Unlike an ordinary blade attack, these lines did not travel through normal distance. They arrived by folding space around Damian and appearing directly beside his body.","Damian’s sword moved.","\"Silent Sword Art, Returning Thread.\"","His blade flashed in a narrow arc. Three severing lines were cut apart, two were redirected into the ground, and one passed by his shoulder without touching him. The final line reached his chest, but Damian’s sword tip struck it directly and shattered it into silver-gray fragments.","Kaiden’s eyes sharpened. He had expected Damian to defend, but he had not expected him to cut the spatial lines with such accuracy from the very first exchange.","Damian looked at him calmly. \"Again.\"","Kaiden did not answer. His hands rose, and the entire stage split into overlapping planes.","\"Void Genesis Art, Thousand-Layer Spatial Cage.\"","The space around Damian folded again and again, forming a transparent prison without walls. Each layer shifted at a different angle, and each angle changed the direction of movement inside the cage. If Damian stepped forward, the distance would stretch. If he stepped back, the ground would fold under him. If he slashed, the sword light would be redirected into an empty plane. This technique had trapped many opponents before they could understand what had happened.","Damian lifted his sword with both hands.","\"Sword God Palace, Falling Peak Sword.\"","The sword descended.","Boom!","A mountain-like sword force struck the Thousand-Layer Spatial Cage from within. The first dozens of layers trembled but did not break. The remaining layers turned the sword force sideways, trying to disperse it through folded planes, but Damian’s eyes remained still. His sword pressed deeper.","\"Falling Peak Sword, Second Descent.\"","Another wave of sword force fell, and then a third.","\"Falling Peak Sword, Third Descent.\"","Crack!","The spatial cage shattered layer by layer.","Kaiden’s expression grew more serious. \"You are not only cutting the surface.\"","Damian stepped out of the collapsing cage. \"The surface is meaningless.\"","The two vanished at the same time. Kaiden stepped through folded corridors while Damian advanced through straight sword movement. One moved by twisting space, and the other moved by cutting the shortest line through it. Their figures crossed the stage again and again, and the silver-gray spatial ripples and pale sword lights flashed so quickly that ordinary spectators could no longer follow their positions.","\"Void Genesis Art, Hollow Displacement.\"","Kaiden’s body shifted away from reality, and Damian’s sword passed through his afterimage.","\"Grand Void Sanctum, Reverse Corridor Palm.\"","A palm strike emerged from behind Damian instead of from Kaiden’s visible position. Damian’s eyes shifted slightly.","\"Crosswind Return.\"","His sword turned backward without his body turning, and the blade met the palm strike behind him.","Boom!","The impact spread in a ring of folded space and broken sword light.","Kaiden appeared above Damian next.","\"Void Genesis Art, Space Burial Palm.\"","The space around Damian sank like a tomb. Damian raised his sword upward.","\"Heaven-Cutting Ascension.\"","A straight sword light pierced through the burial field and split the sinking space from bottom to top. Kaiden retreated through a folded path, but Damian’s sword light followed the path for a short distance and cut open his sleeve. A thin line of blood appeared on Kaiden’s arm.","The Grand Void Sanctum disciples grew tense.","\"He wounded Senior Brother Kaiden.\"","\"Damian’s sword is following the folds.\"","\"That should not be easy.\"","At the Sword God Palace, the disciples watched with burning eyes.","\"Senior Brother Damian can cut space.\"","\"No, he is cutting the path hidden inside space.\"","\"That is even more terrifying.\"","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, the top geniuses grew serious.","Rakan Thorne crossed his arms and frowned. \"I hate this one too. I cannot even tell where Kaiden is standing.\"","Orion Starfall smiled weakly. \"That is the point. If you could tell, he would not be Kaiden.\"","Revona watched quietly, her Void Origin Eyes faintly glowing. \"Damian is not trying to understand every corridor. He is cutting the route that carries Kaiden’s intent.\"","Ervin nodded. \"That is why the sword is dangerous.\""]},{"number":1897,"title":"Chapter 1897: Damian Getting Pushed!","paragraphs":["Max stood on his pillar with focused eyes. He had defeated Kaiden with the Void Genesis Art, but Damian was approaching the battle from a completely different direction. Max’s advantage had been mastery and immunity. Damian had neither.","He was not immune to spatial attacks, and he did not understand the Void Genesis Art as Kaiden did. Yet his sword path was so pure and precise that it could cut through the meaningful line behind Kaiden’s movements. That made him frightening in another way entirely.","On the stage, Kaiden’s aura finally changed. Silver-gray light expanded behind him, and the entire battlefield began twisting into a vast spatial maze. Corridors rose from the ground, mirrors opened in the air, and walls of folded distance appeared and vanished. Exile points flickered at the edge of sight while hidden blades of space moved between planes.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path.\"","Kaiden’s voice rang across the arena.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth.\"","Boom!","The stage became a labyrinth of folded space. Damian stood within it, surrounded by countless corridors and mirror routes. Every direction looked real, and every path looked false. Even the sky above him had been divided into layers, and every layer could become an attack route, an escape route, or an exile route at any moment.","Kaiden’s figure appeared in a distant corridor. \"Damian Voss,\" he said calmly, \"if your sword can cut through this, then cut.\"","The Grand Void Labyrinth activated.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth, Corridor of Ten Thousand Cuts.\"","Countless invisible cuts emerged from all directions. Damian’s sword moved instantly.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, First Edict, All Blades Refuse Submission.\"","The sword world appeared behind him. An ancient sword altar rose within a vast sword heaven, and countless sword lights answered Damian’s blade. The first wave of spatial cuts was shattered before reaching him, but Kaiden’s attack did not end there.","The cuts arrived from delayed corridors, hidden mirrors, and folded paths that had not existed a breath earlier. One cut grazed Damian’s sleeve, another tore across his shoulder, and a third left a faint wound on his cheek.","Damian’s expression did not change.","Kaiden’s voice echoed again.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth, Mirror Burial.\"","Dozens of mirrored spaces appeared around Damian, each reflecting him from a different angle. Then the mirrors collapsed inward, trying to bury him inside false spatial layers. At the same time, Kaiden used the collapsing mirrors to hide his true attack.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth, Backflow Severance.\"","A silver-gray blade emerged from behind Damian’s reflection and struck toward his back. Damian’s eyes sharpened.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, Second Edict, One Sword Divides Heaven.\"","One sword light swept outward. The mirrors split, the false layers split, and the Backflow Severance blade split as well. The sword light continued through the labyrinth and cut open three corridors at once, forcing Kaiden to step out from a distant fold.","Kaiden looked down at the torn edge of his robe, and then he smiled faintly. \"As expected.\"","Damian lowered his sword slightly. \"Your labyrinth is impressive.\"","Kaiden’s eyes grew deeper. \"It is not finished yet.\"","The Grand Void Labyrinth began to rotate.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth, Infinite Corridor Rotation.\"","Every path around Damian changed position. The corridor behind him became the sky, and the mirror above him became the ground. The wall on his right became a blade, and the blade on his left became an exile gate. The entire labyrinth moved like a living spatial beast, constantly reshaping its own organs to confuse its prey.","Damian’s sword lights began missing, and for the first time, Kaiden started gaining a visible advantage. A spatial cut struck Damian’s arm. A folded palm force hit his shoulder.","An exile ripple brushed past his leg and nearly dragged him into a side corridor. Kaiden moved faster and faster within the Grand Void Labyrinth, no longer standing in one route long enough to be caught.","His attacks came from present space, delayed space, mirrored space, and reversed space. No single attack was enough to defeat Damian on its own, but together they began to pressure him heavily.","The Sword God Palace disciples grew tense.","\"Senior Brother Damian is being pushed.\"","\"Kaiden’s labyrinth changes too quickly.\"","\"Can even Sword Sovereign Heaven keep cutting if the path keeps moving?\"","Damian stopped in place. A silver-gray blade shot toward his throat, and he cut it apart. Another emerged from beneath his feet, and he stepped aside and severed it. A third appeared behind him, and he cut backward without turning.","Then ten more came, and then a hundred. Damian’s robe was cut in several places, and blood appeared on his arm and shoulder, yet his grip on the sword did not loosen at all.","Kaiden’s figure appeared above him through a folded corridor.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth, World Exile Coffin.\"","Six massive spatial walls appeared around Damian, closing in from above, from below, and from all four sides. Each wall contained countless folded planes leading away from the battlefield. If the coffin sealed completely, Damian would be exiled into a space where even his sword would have to cut through countless layers before returning.","Damian looked up as the walls closed.","Kaiden pressed both hands downward. \"Seal.\"","The World Exile Coffin descended. Damian finally raised his sword vertically before him, and the Sword Sovereign Heaven behind him changed. The ancient sword altar grew brighter. The sword palace above it appeared, and the empty throne within the palace released a faint glow.","Damian’s voice remained calm.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, Third Edict.\"","The sword in his hand hummed.","\"The sword does not follow distance.\"","He slashed, and a single straight line appeared within the World Exile Coffin. That line cut through the first spatial wall, then the second, and then the third. The fourth wall tried to fold the sword light away, but the sword light cut through the fold itself. The fifth wall opened an exile path, but the sword line severed the path’s destination. The sixth wall compressed inward, only to be split from its center.","Crack!","The World Exile Coffin shattered. Kaiden’s eyes widened slightly.","Damian stepped out with his aura sharper than before. \"Your space changes many paths,\" Damian said. \"But every path has a point where it begins.\"","Kaiden’s face turned solemn.","Damian raised his sword. \"I only need to cut that.\"","The pressure of Sword Sovereign Heaven rose. Kaiden realized that Damian had adapted. At the beginning, Damian had cut attacks. Then he had cut routes. Now he was starting to cut the origin points of the spatial changes themselves. If this continued, the Grand Void Labyrinth would lose its advantage entirely.","Kaiden drew a deep breath, and the entire labyrinth condensed. Every corridor, mirror, folded path, and exile point began gathering toward one final silver-gray passage. The space behind Damian darkened into a terrifying tunnel that seemed to lead beyond the battlefield, beyond the Eternal Hourglass, and beyond return.","The spectators grew silent, because they had seen this move before. It was the technique that had almost defeated Revona.","\"Grand Void Labyrinth, Final Corridor.\"","Kaiden’s hands trembled slightly as he formed the deepest route of his Pseudo Cosmic Path.","\"Void Beyond Return.\"","The final corridor opened beneath Damian’s feet, and the space around him vanished downward. Damian’s body began to sink.","The Sword God Palace disciples shouted in alarm.","\"Senior Brother Damian!\"","The Grand Void Sanctum disciples clenched their fists.","\"Seal him!\"","\"Void Beyond Return!\"","Even the top geniuses grew focused."]},{"number":1898,"title":"Chapter 1898: Max vs Orion!","paragraphs":["Damian sank to his knees, and then to his waist. The corridor tried to remove him from the battlefield entirely. It did not attack his body. It attacked his position, his presence, and the route connecting him to the stage. If it succeeded, even his Sword Sovereign Heaven would be forced to cut through endless folded exits to return.","Kaiden pressed harder. \"Go.\"","Damian looked down at the darkness below him, and then he closed his eyes. For a breath, the sword in his hand became silent, and the Sword Sovereign Heaven behind him fell silent as well. Then the single sword hanging before the empty throne descended, and the entire sword world seemed to hold its breath.","Damian opened his eyes.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven.\"","The sword before the throne dissolved into light and entered his blade.","\"Final Edict.\"","The labyrinth trembled.","\"Throne Of The Only Sword.\"","In that instant, every sword light vanished. The sword altar vanished, the sword mountains vanished, and the sword rivers vanished. Even the palace behind Damian dimmed. Only one sword remained, the sword in Damian’s hand, and because only one sword remained, every other direction lost its meaning before it.","Damian slashed downward. The slash entered the Void Beyond Return.","For a moment, nothing happened. Then the final corridor cracked.","Kaiden’s face changed. \"No.\"","The crack spread through the corridor. It did not spread along the surface. It spread along the hidden route of exile, cutting through the very connection that made the path lead away from the battlefield. The Void Beyond Return tried to deepen itself, but Damian’s sword had already found the line that mattered. The destination was cut, the returnless nature was cut, and the exile authority was cut. The corridor shattered.","Boom!","Damian stepped out of the collapsing void with his sword still lowered. The Grand Void Labyrinth shook violently. Kaiden tried to move, but Damian was already gone. A straight sword line crossed the labyrinth. No corridor delayed it, no mirror diverted it, and no folded plane swallowed it. The sword line cut through the center of the Grand Void Labyrinth and arrived before Kaiden.","Kaiden opened three emergency folds, and Damian cut through them. Kaiden formed a Hollow Displacement, and Damian severed the displaced position. Kaiden raised a World-Folding Barrier, and Damian’s blade pierced through it. Then the sword stopped at Kaiden’s throat.","The entire arena went silent. Kaiden stood still. His silver-gray robes were torn, his aura was unstable, and the Grand Void Labyrinth behind him cracked layer by layer before finally collapsing into countless fading fragments of space.","He had given everything. He had shown the full depth of his spatial path. He had trapped Damian, wounded him, nearly exiled him, and forced him to use the Final Edict of Sword Sovereign Heaven. But in the end, Damian’s sword had cut through space itself.","Kaiden looked at the blade before his throat, and then he looked at Damian. After a few breaths, he smiled faintly. \"You cut the Void Beyond Return.\"","Damian’s expression remained calm. \"Barely.\"","Kaiden shook his head lightly. \"Barely is still enough.\"","He lowered his hands. \"I surrender.\"","Angelina Valerius announced the result.","[Winner: Damian Voss.]","[Kaiden Voidmere Defeated.]","The screen above the arena updated.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Damian Voss]","[Total Battles Fought: 20]","[Total Wins: 20]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Kaiden Voidmere]","[Total Battles Fought: 22]","[Total Wins: 18]","The Divine Realm erupted. Damian Voss had completed all twenty-four battles with twenty-four victories.","The Sword God Palace fell into thunderous celebration. Countless swords rose from their sheaths, and their cries echoed through mountains, halls, and floating sword platforms. Their strongest genius had not merely won another battle. He had ended the full round-robin stage undefeated, cutting down divine light, body power, curses, and now the Grand Void Labyrinth of the Grand Void Sanctum.","At the Grand Void Sanctum, the disciples were silent, yet none of them lowered their heads in shame. Kaiden had fought beautifully. His space power had pushed Damian further than most opponents, and even in defeat he had proven once again that his place among the top monsters was unquestionable.","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, Damian lowered his sword and stepped back. Kaiden gave him a slight nod.","\"The Sword God Palace deserves its name.\"","Damian sheathed his blade. \"So does the Grand Void Sanctum.\"","The transfer light descended and returned both of them to their pillars.","Max watched Damian quietly. Twenty-four battles and twenty-four wins. Damian Voss had finished his round, and his sword still felt as though it had more to show.","After Damian defeated Kaiden and returned to his pillar with twenty-four victories to his name, the pressure inside the Eternal Hourglass rose to an even more frightening level. Everyone understood that the final competitive stage had entered its final stretch, and from this point onward, almost every battle that appeared on the screen would carry the weight to shake the entire Divine Realm.","Angelina Valerius gave the arena only a brief moment to settle. The broken traces of Kaiden’s Grand Void Labyrinth disappeared, the stage restored itself under the laws of the Eternal Hourglass, and then the great screen of light above the battlefield began to spin once more.","This time, even before the first name appeared, many spectators had already begun holding their breath. The top monsters remaining had grown too few, and any pairing among them was enough to make the blood of the crowd heat up.","The first name slowed and stopped.","[Max Morgan]","A wave of noise rose instantly. The second name continued rotating through the light, passing several surviving participants before finally slowing as well.","[Orion Starfall]","The moment both names appeared together, the Eternal Hourglass erupted.","[Final Competitive Stage]","[Max Morgan vs Orion Starfall]","All across the Divine Realm, countless viewing grounds, sect halls, clan plazas, floating platforms, mountain palaces, and inheritance chambers burst into excitement. The Black Dragon Clan disciples straightened immediately. The Nine Star Court fell unusually quiet for a moment before its disciples began watching with burning eyes.","Even many elders from the seven strongest first-rate forces leaned forward slightly, because everyone knew this was no ordinary battle.","Max Morgan, who had risen from the mortal world and continued shocking the Divine Realm without pause, was now facing Orion Starfall, the strongest genius of the Nine Star Court, a man who had proven again and again that even when injured or cornered, his will to fight only grew more terrifying.","On his pillar, Orion stood up immediately, and his bright smile returned at once. That smile carried no fear, no hesitation, and no trace of gloom from his previous battles. If anything, he looked more alive than before.","\"So it is finally my turn,\" Orion said with a laugh as he looked toward Max. \"I have been waiting for this battle for a long time.\"","Max met his gaze from across the arena and smiled faintly. \"I know,\" he said calmly. \"You have been looking at me with battle intent for quite a while now.\"","Orion jumped down from his pillar as the beam of transfer light descended around him. \"You are right,\" he replied, still smiling. \"Because among everyone here, you are one of the few who truly make me feel excited.\"","Max stepped into his own beam of light and appeared on the central stage opposite him. \"You should be excited,\" Max said. \"I am not easy to fight.\"","Orion laughed loudly. \"Good. If you were easy, I would be disappointed.\"","The crowd’s excitement only rose further at that exchange. Max stood with Dragonheart still sheathed, his white hair drifting lightly in the wind generated by the arena’s formations. Orion stood opposite him in dark-gold battle armor marked with stars, and even before the battle began, the air between them already felt heavy enough to crack."]},{"number":1899,"title":"Chapter 1899: Orion Going All Out!","paragraphs":["Angelina Valerius raised her hand.","[Battle Begins.]","The instant the battle started, Orion did not waste even a breath. He did not test Max, he did not throw a basic star attack, and he did not try to read the battlefield first. He went straight to his strongest state from the very beginning, because he knew better than most people here that anything less would be meaningless in front of Max Morgan.","\"Nine Star Sovereign Body.\"","The sky above the stage changed. Nine stars appeared at once, each shining in a different color and carrying a different pressure. Silver, gold, crimson, azure, white, violet, black, green, and deep blood-red all lit up together, and before the crowd could fully appreciate the scene, all nine stars descended into Orion’s body one after another.","Boom!","His aura exploded, and the ground beneath his feet cracked. The muscles in his body tightened, the star marks on his armor lit up violently, and his eyes shone with a dazzling stellar brilliance, as if miniature galaxies had been lit inside them.","But Orion still did not stop there. He raised both hands, and the phantom of an ancient star palace appeared behind him, majestic and endless, while all nine stars within his body began revolving at terrifying speed.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path,\" Orion said, and for the first time since the battle was announced, even his smile gained a solemn edge. \"Full Star Convergence.\"","The arena trembled. This was no simple technique, and it was not a single attack. The moment Full Star Convergence descended, the power of the nine stars no longer remained separate within Orion’s body.","It began fusing into his blood, his flesh, his bones, his veins, and his spirit, turning his already terrifying Nine Star Sovereign Body into something far more monstrous. In that moment, Orion no longer looked like a genius who specialized in long-range star techniques. He looked like a supreme close-combat tyrant carrying the power of an entire star court inside his body.","Rakan Thorne grinned from his pillar. \"Good. That idiot did not hold back.\"","Morgana Starveil narrowed her eyes slightly. \"Straight to the peak state from the start. He really has no intention of saving anything.\"","Revona watched in silence. Damian Voss also studied the stage carefully.","Max, however, only smiled. \"That is more like it.\"","The next moment, Orion vanished. He did not move like an ordinary body cultivator. He exploded.","\"First Star Impact!\"","His fist arrived before Max’s chest almost instantly, carrying the crushing weight of a falling star. Max’s right hand rose and blocked. He also directly opened the first Divine Vein - Vein of Origin.","Boom!","A heavy shockwave spread across the stage, and the arena barrier rippled. Before the force from the first impact had fully dispersed, Orion was already gone again.","\"Third Star Split!\"","This time his elbow descended from above with enough force to split a mountain range. Max took half a step back and let the elbow brush past his shoulder, but before he could counter, Orion’s knee had already risen from below.","\"Fifth Star Ascending Break!\"","Max blocked again, and another violent shockwave burst outward.","The crowd shouted in excitement. Orion allowed no breathing room. Fully aware that letting Max settle into rhythm would make the battle harder, he pressed on without pause and attacked from every angle with the power of converged stars.","His fists, elbows, knees, and shoulders all became terrifying weapons, and each movement carried the pressure of a different star. One was crushing, one was piercing, one was explosive, one was twisting, and one was suppressive. Together they formed a close-combat storm powerful enough to overwhelm most geniuses in only a few breaths.","Max blocked several strikes barehanded at first. He even matched Orion in close combat for a short stretch, and that alone shocked countless people, because after seeing Orion enter Full Star Convergence, most had expected him to force even Max onto the defensive immediately.","But then Max smiled a little more deeply. \"Not bad,\" he said.","Then Dragonheart came out. The sword cried once as it left its sheath, and in the next instant it met Orion’s descending fist.","Clang!","The metallic impact shook the stage.","Orion grinned brightly. \"Now it begins.\"","He pressed forward again.","\"Seventh Star Crushing Descent!\"","Max answered with a horizontal slash. The sword and fist collided, and sparks of sword light and star light exploded between them. Orion slid back a short distance before charging again, and this time his attacks no longer came as isolated moves. They came as a complete martial sequence empowered by all nine stars within him.","His left fist carried the First Star. His right knee shifted into the Fourth. His shoulder impact changed to the Eighth. His palm strike fused the Third and Seventh. The speed at which he changed star attributes throughout his body made him look like a celestial war machine.","Max’s sword began moving faster. He did not release any major external power yet. He simply used Dragonheart and pure swordsmanship to answer Orion’s storm of close-combat attacks, but even that made the crowd uneasy, because Max was doing far more than barely keeping up.","He was already reading Orion’s changes, blocking some, redirecting others, cutting through the force of several, and even counterattacking whenever he found a gap.","Still, Orion was too powerful to suppress with ordinary swordsmanship alone.","\"Starfall Spiral Fist!\"","He spun and drove a rotating star fist toward Max with enough force to blow apart the ground beneath them. Max blocked with Dragonheart, but the impact still pushed him a short distance backward.","Orion’s smile widened at once. \"Good!\" he shouted. \"You really can take it!\"","Max steadied his footing. Then the expression on his face slowly changed. The smile remained, but the atmosphere around him became deathly calm. Dragonheart lowered slightly, and a silent, eerie sword aura spread out from him.","The lively pressure created by Orion’s stars suddenly felt as though it had entered a much colder world, one where the air itself carried a severing edge that aimed not merely at flesh or force, but at the invisible connections behind them.","Max raised Dragonheart.","\"Emotion Severing Path.\"","The moment those words left his mouth, the noise around the arena seemed to dim for a breath.","Orion’s eyes sharpened immediately. He had seen this power before, and he had heard enough about it from others. But seeing it from the stage itself was different.","The Full Star Convergence inside his body was still raging, yet when Max’s Emotion Severing Path spread across the battlefield, Orion could feel a strange pressure touching not his flesh but the rhythm behind his power, as though that cold and silent sword aura wanted to cut the emotional force, intent, and momentum that allowed his star convergence to shine so fiercely.","Max stepped forward. One slash came, and it was silent. It was too silent.","Orion answered with \"Ninth Star Crown Fist,\" condensing all his gathered momentum into one direct collision.","Boom!","Sword and fist met. The stage beneath their feet shattered into a wide crater, and the arena shook violently. But while Orion’s fist remained terrifyingly strong, the star intent supporting the strike was clearly shaken. Max’s severing aura had not merely clashed with the outer power. It had bitten into the rhythm of the star force itself.","Orion retreated three steps, then laughed. \"So this is what it feels like directly.\"","He took another breath, then exploded forward again. This time he used everything.","\"First Star Impact!\"","\"Third Star Split!\"","\"Sixth Star Heaven Drive!\"","\"Eighth Star Ruin Break!\"","Each attack came stronger than the last, and Max answered each one with Dragonheart, sometimes blocking, sometimes cutting, sometimes redirecting, and sometimes meeting them with direct sword strikes that split even the air around them.","The battle grew fierce. Orion’s Full Star Convergence made him terrifying in close combat. He attacked like a man wearing the sky itself as armor and wielding the collapse of stars in every movement. Yet Max’s Emotion Severing Path made every collision dangerous for him in a different way."]},{"number":1900,"title":"Chapter 1900: Ervin vs Morgana!","paragraphs":["The more they clashed, the more Orion could feel that Max’s sword was not only attacking his body but also trying to cut apart the battle intent, momentum, and converged star rhythm that allowed him to chain one brutal attack into another.","Still, Orion refused to yield. His injuries from earlier battles, the strain of Full Star Convergence, and the pressure of the Emotion Severing Path all gathered together, but instead of weakening his spirit, they seemed to force him into an even more desperate brilliance.","He leapt back once and raised both hands.","\"Nine Star Sovereign Body, Starfall Extinction!\"","The ancient star palace behind him trembled, and all nine stars within his body burned to their peak. A massive stellar force gathered around his right arm, layer after layer and star after star, until his whole arm looked as though it carried the collapse of a miniature cosmos.","The crowd was stunned. He was using that technique again, and from the beginning state of Full Star Convergence.","Orion appeared before Max like a falling comet. \"Take this, Max!\"","The fist came down. Max looked at the incoming attack calmly, and then his eyes grew colder. The Emotion Severing Path around Dragonheart deepened. He gripped the sword with both hands and brought it down in a single decisive slash.","\"Sever.\"","The two attacks collided. For one breath, the arena went white with star light and dark-gray severing force. Then a crack appeared. It was not in the stage, and it was not in the barrier. It was in the star force itself.","Max’s Emotion Severing Path had cut into the converged will behind Orion’s Starfall Extinction, severing the furious upward battle spirit that held its star layers together. The moment that invisible support cracked, the immense stellar force began collapsing unevenly.","Orion’s eyes widened. Max’s slash continued. The star fist broke apart, the star layers shattered, and the stellar pressure split in two. Then Max’s figure passed through the broken light and appeared before Orion. Dragonheart stopped before his throat.","The entire arena fell silent. Orion stood frozen. The glow of Full Star Convergence around his body flickered once, then again, and then finally dimmed. He tried to steady himself, but the overuse of his Pseudo Cosmic Path and the destruction of Starfall Extinction had already drained too much of his strength.","For a few breaths, he simply stared at the sword before his throat. Then he laughed. It was not a bitter laugh. It was bright, honest, and filled with excitement even in defeat.","\"You really are ridiculous,\" Orion said, breathing heavily. \"I used my Full Star Convergence from the beginning, and you still cut through everything.\"","Max lowered Dragonheart slightly. \"You forced me to take out my sword and use the Emotion Severing Path seriously from the start,\" Max replied. \"That is enough to show your strength.\"","Orion shook his head and smiled helplessly. \"That sounds like comfort.\"","\"It is not.\"","Orion looked at him for a moment, then laughed again and finally raised both hands in surrender. \"I surrender.\"","Angelina Valerius announced the result calmly.","[Winner: Max Morgan.]","[Orion Starfall Defeated.]","The great screen above the arena changed immediately.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Max Morgan]","[Total Battles Fought: 21]","[Total Wins: 21]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Orion Starfall]","[Total Battles Fought: 22]","[Total Wins: 18]","The Divine Realm erupted once more. At the Black Dragon Clan, disciples shouted with excitement, some in pure joy, some in disbelief, and some with a pride that had long since surpassed their earlier expectations. Lady Virelia looked at the screen with bright eyes and a faint smile, while several elders exchanged astonished glances. Across the seven great families tied to the Black Dragon Clan, many leaders who had once only hoped Max would perform well in the Cosmic Ascension Conference now had no choice but to admit that he had become one of the most terrifying young geniuses in the entire Divine Realm.","At the Nine Star Court, the disciples were disappointed but not ashamed. Orion had gone all out from the beginning, and no one who watched that battle could say he had performed poorly. He had attacked with the courage and brilliance worthy of the strongest genius of the Nine Star Court.","On the stage, Orion let out a long breath. \"I lost,\" he said simply, though his smile never faded. \"But that was fun.\"","Max sheathed Dragonheart. \"You are one of the best opponents here.\"","Orion grinned. \"Good. Then next time, I will force even more from you.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"I will wait.\"","The transfer light descended and returned both of them to their pillars. The battle had ended. Max Morgan remained undefeated, and with each battle, the final competitive stage moved closer to its true deciding point.","After Max defeated Orion, the atmosphere inside the Eternal Hourglass remained heated for a long time. Orion returned to his pillar with a tired but satisfied smile, his star armor cracked, his aura unstable, and his body still trembling from the backlash of using Full Star Convergence and Starfall Extinction against Max.","Yet no one looked down on him. He had known from the beginning that anything below his Pseudo Cosmic Path would be useless, so he had burned everything from the first breath. He had forced Max to draw Dragonheart and use the Emotion Severing Path seriously, and for someone who had already suffered through battles against Revona, Ervin, and Aurelian, that result alone was enough to make the Nine Star Court proud.","Max returned to his own pillar calmly. His record now stood at twenty-four battles and twenty-four victories, the same as Damian Voss. But the final competitive stage had not truly ended.","The battle count and record projection above the arena began shifting, and several names continued rotating through the final remaining matchups. Some participants had already finished all their battles, while a few important names still had several pairings left. The Eternal Hourglass gave no one special treatment.","Those who had not yet crossed paths would still be matched, and only after every necessary result had been recorded would the final ranking become complete.","Angelina Valerius raised her hand again.","\"The final competitive stage will continue.\"","The next few battles came quickly.","[Revona vs Fin Arclight]","Fin Arclight stepped into the arena with a grim expression. He knew Revona was one of the worst possible opponents for him, but surrendering without trying would be too shameful for someone who had already reached this stage.","The moment the battle began, he opened Pale Eclipse Burial and tried to cover the entire stage in moonless darkness. Pale eclipse light spread outward, suppressing sight, sound, rhythm, and direction, while the Moonless Descent blade formed silently above Revona’s head.","Revona looked up once. The Void Origin Eyes opened fully, and the Moonless Descent blade faded before it could fall. Fin immediately shifted positions and used \"Pale Eclipse Burial, Eclipse Shadow Division,\" creating several pale afterimages that attacked from different angles, but Revona’s gaze followed the true source of each strike.","One by one, the pale shadows vanished. When Fin tried to compress the eclipse field and launch one final attack, Revona opened a small portion of the Void Origin Realm and hollowed the center of the field before it could collapse around her.","Fin lowered his blade and surrendered.","[Winner: Revona.]","[Fin Arclight Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Revona]","[Total Battles Fought: 21]","[Total Wins: 21]","The result caused little surprise. Revona’s strength had already been proven repeatedly, and after defeating Orion, Rakan, and Kaiden, no one expected Fin to be the one to break her undefeated record.","The next important match came after several faster results among the lower-ranked participants.","[Ervin vs Morgana Starveil]","Morgana entered the stage with a faint smile, but her eyes were extremely serious. Her Star-Curse Labyrinth was one of the most troublesome Pseudo Cosmic Paths among the top twenty-five, yet Ervin’s Abyssal Origin Descent had already swallowed too many different types of authority. She did not waste time with small curses.","The moment the battle began, the Star-Curse Labyrinth opened, and violet-black mirrors filled the stage, each one carrying a different misfortune, binding, or distortion curse."]}]);
